E["item:anaya-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Anaya's Pendant",z="darkshore",s="Across Ameth'Aran, Anaya's Pendant remains with the tormented spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner. Cerellean Whiteclaw still grieves for the love he lost when the Sundering shattered their world.",h="Across Ameth'Aran, Anaya's Pendant remains with the tormented spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner.",sec={{t="A Keepsake Across Millennia",b="Ten thousand years ago, the Well of Eternity was destroyed and the ancient kaldorei city of Ameth'Aran fell into ruin. Cerellean Whiteclaw believed his beloved Anaya had perished. He carried his grief into a long sleep beside Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage.\n\nAfter waking, Cerellean wandered Darkshore and found Anaya's tormented apparition drifting through Ameth'Aran with the pendant. He cannot raise a hand against her himself. So he asks travelers to free her spirit and recover the heirloom.",sp=0},{t="Parting and Peace",b="In Auberdine, Cerellean receives the pendant, and Anaya Dawnrunner's spirit briefly appears before him one last time. Freed from the anguish binding her to Ameth'Aran's haunted ruins, her ghost fades peacefully into the night. Cerellean is left alone with the pendant and the memory of their ancient love.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Anaya's Pendant come from?",a="Anaya's Pendant comes from the ghost of Anaya Dawnrunner, who wanders the ancient kaldorei ruins of Ameth'Aran in southern Darkshore.",al={"where to get anayas pendant","how do i get anaya pendant","who drops anaya pendant"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Anaya's Pendant?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw wants Anaya's Pendant. The grieving night elf lives in Auberdine, the coastal town in Darkshore.",al={"who do i give anayas pendant to","cerellean whiteclaw quest","turn in anayas pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why couldn't Cerellean retrieve the pendant himself?",a="Cerellean found his lost love's spirit roaming Ameth'Aran, but could not bear to raise his own hand against her, even after ten thousand years of sorrow.",al={"why didnt cerellean kill anaya","why does cerellean need help"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you return the pendant to Cerellean?",a="When you return the pendant to Cerellean in Auberdine, Anaya's spirit briefly appears to bid farewell, then fades into peace. Cerellean is left to grieve her memory.",al={"what happens to anaya","cerellean reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Anaya's Pendant?",a="Anaya's Pendant is an ancient keepsake belonging to Anaya Dawnrunner, a kaldorei who perished thousands of years ago during the destruction of Ameth'Aran. Carried by her restless spirit among the ruins, the pendant serves as a poignant physical token of her enduring love and the life she shared with Cerellean Whiteclaw before the Sundering tore their world apart.",al={"what is anayas pendant","anaya pendant lore","who does the pendant belong to"},it="identity",add="2379a09f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see in the pendant a reminder of the War of the Ancients and the many lives and loves torn apart in the Great Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Cerellean slept for millennia beside Shan'do Stormrage, hoping to escape his grief. He woke to ghosts lingering in the waking world."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","pendant","well of eternity"},rel={"quest:963","npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:shan-do"},src={"Anaya's Pendant","For Love Eternal"}}
E["item:ancient-moonstone-seal"] = {t="item",n="Ancient Moonstone Seal",z="darkshore",s="In Bashal'Aran, the Ancient Moonstone Seal holds Asterion captive among the ruins. The Highborne forged it long before the Sundering, binding his spirit with arcane magic.",h="In Bashal'Aran, the Ancient Moonstone Seal holds Asterion captive among the ruins.",sec={{t="A Prison of Highborne Sorcery",b="Athrikus Narassin, Asterion's former master, forged the Ancient Moonstone Seal to bind his soul to Bashal'Aran's pillars. The Highborne sorcerer made it an unbreakable anchor while the Well of Eternity still stood and Queen Azshara reigned. More than ten millennia later, Asterion remains a spirit bound by its magic. No strength or spell he commands can break the ward.",sp=0},{t="Destruction in Ameth'Aran",b="After the Great Sundering, the Deth'ryll satyrs took the seal into Darkshore's surrounding wilderness. Highborne enchanted stone yields to no ordinary force. To destroy the relic, it must meet the ancient blue flame still burning in Ameth'Aran's twin ruins to the south. That fire shatters Athrikus's binding ward and frees Asterion's spirit to enter the mortal realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Athrikus Narassin, a Highborne sorcerer, crafted the Ancient Moonstone Seal to bind Asterion's ghost to his shrine in Bashal'Aran.",al={"what is moonstone seal","seal of asterion","bashal'aran seal"},it="identity"},{q="Who possesses the seal before it is recovered?",a="Before anyone recovers it, a Deth'ryll satyr in the ruins around Bashal'Aran holds the seal. Its presence lets the satyr command lesser grell minions.",al={"who has the seal","where to find moonstone seal","who drops moonstone seal"}},{q="How can the seal be destroyed?",a="Ordinary weapons and present-day magic cannot harm the seal. It must be cast into the ancient flame still burning in Ameth'Aran's twin ruins to the south.",al={"how to break the seal","destroy moonstone seal","where do i destroy the seal"}},{q="What happens when the seal is destroyed?",a="The flame in Ameth'Aran destroys the seal and breaks the enchantments binding Asterion. After thousands of years in captivity, his spirit is free to roam the world.",al={"what does breaking the seal do","asterion freed"},sp=1},{q="Where does the Ancient Moonstone Seal come from, and who made it?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal was crafted millennia ago during the height of the kaldorei empire, prior to the Great Sundering. It was forged through the sorcery of one of the most powerful Highborne lords—Athrikus Narassin—to serve as a mystical binding mechanism.",al={"who made ancient moonstone seal","ancient moonstone seal origin","creator of ancient moonstone seal"},it="origin",add="bc236585"},{q="Why does Asterion want the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Asterion seeks the seal because it is the very anchor that keeps his spirit bound within the ruined shrine of Bashal'Aran. As long as it remains intact, he is trapped behind invisible bars, unable to leave his ancient prison or rest. By recovering the seal, he hopes to destroy it in the ancient flames of Ameth'Aran and finally gain his freedom.",al={"why does asterion want the seal","why find ancient moonstone seal","who wants ancient moonstone seal"},it="why_wanted",add="a13d6402"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you can see in the seal the Highborne's arcane power and their cruel enslavement practices before the Great Sundering.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how ancient elven abjuration magic held its binding field for more than ten thousand years in the moonstone."},kw={"ameth'aran","ancient moonstone seal","asterion","athrikus","bashal'aran","darkshore","deth'ryll","highborne","moonstone"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","subzone:ameth-aran","zone:darkshore","topic:highborne","topic:satyr"},src={"Ancient Moonstone Seal","Bashal'Aran (3)","Bashal'Aran (4)"}}
E["item:athrikus-narassin-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Athrikus Narassin's Head",z="darkshore",s="At the Tower of Althalaxx, Athrikus Narassin's Head proves the ancient warlock is dead. The coven's demonic work in northern Darkshore has been disrupted.",h="At the Tower of Althalaxx, Athrikus Narassin's Head proves the ancient warlock is dead.",sec={{t="Blight Upon Althalaxx",b="Athrikus Narassin led dark sorcerers from the Tower of Althalaxx. His coven practiced fel magic along the Darkshore coast and summoned demons that threatened the wilderness. Claiming his head breaks their leadership and drives back their foothold in the region. Yet corruption lingers, and the land will need watchful eyes.",sp=1,bt={"q954.5"}}},faq={{q="Who was Athrikus Narassin?",a="Athrikus Narassin was an ancient and powerful warlock who led the cultists in the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. From the spire's summit, he directed the coven's demonic rituals.",al={"who is athrikus","athrikus lore","who is the warlock"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q954.5"}},{q="Why is his head needed?",a="Alliance scouts watching the Tower of Althalaxx need proof that the master warlock is dead. His severed head confirms his death and the strike against the demonic forces.",al={"why take the head","athrikus head purpose","what is head for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Athrikus Narassin located?",a="Athrikus Narassin is at the summit of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. His devoted cultists and summoned demons guard him.",al={"where to find athrikus","athrikus location","tower of althalaxx top"},sp=1,it="place",gp=true,bt={"q954.5"}},{q="Does killing him eliminate the demonic threat completely?",a="Athrikus Narassin's death strikes hard at the dark ritualists and scatters their current operations. Yet the demonic forces may gather again, and Darkshore will still need defense.",al={"are demons gone","is the tower cleansed","did we beat the cult"},it="threat"},{q="What is Athrikus Narassin's Head?",a="It is the severed head of Athrikus Narassin, an ancient night elf warlock commanding the dark forces entrenched within the Tower of Althalaxx. You take it as irrefutable proof that the leader of the local cult has been slain.",al={"what is athrikus head","athrikus narassin head"},it="item",add="5ecacf9e"},{q="Where does Athrikus Narassin's Head come from?",a="It is claimed directly from the apex of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Athrikus Narassin resides at the pinnacle of the ruined structure, surrounded by his most dangerous warlocks and fel summoned minions until struck down.",al={"where did athrikus head come from","where to get athrikus head","who made athrikus head"},it="origin",add="639f8902"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you see Athrikus Narassin's death purge a demonic blight from ancient Kaldorei ruins along Kalimdor's northern shores.",["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you know Athrikus's mastery of fel powers made him formidable. His reckless visibility in Althalaxx proved his undoing."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus narassin","cultists","darkshore","fel","severed head","warlock"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","zone:darkshore","topic:warlock","quest:494"},src={"Athrikus Narassin's Head","The Tower of Althalaxx (8)"}}
E["item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Bottom of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, the bottom fragment lies among the remains of a shattered winding key. It belonged to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast, and reef crawlers scavenged it from the shore.",h="Along Darkshore, the bottom fragment lies among the remains of a shattered winding key.",sec={{t="Claimed by Crawlers",b="Threshadons sank Gelkak Gyromast's ship off Darkshore. The wreck cast the gnome and his belongings ashore, including the winding key that activated his mechanical first mate. Coastal rocks broke the key into three pieces, and local scavengers came upon the debris. Reef and tide crawlers seized the bottom fragment as they searched the tideline.",sp=0},{t="Reassembly",b="Gelkak needs the bottom fragment with the middle and top pieces to activate his mechanical crewman. Coastal murlocs dragged off the middle piece, while inland foreststriders took the top. The gnome pirate must pry this heavy fragment from the shoreline crabs' shells to restore his construct and seek vengeance for his ruined expedition.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Bottom of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="The Bottom of Gelkak's Key is one of three pieces needed to repair the winding key belonging to the stranded pirate Gelkak Gyromast. The repaired key can reactivate his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","purpose of bottom of gelkaks key","why do i need gelkak key bottom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this key piece come from?",a="Reef crawlers scavenged the key piece from Darkshore's coast. Encrusted Tide Crawlers and Raging Reef Crawlers search along the water's edge.",al={"where to find bottom of gelkak key","who drops bottom of gelkaks key","gelkak key bottom location"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the key broken into three pieces?",a="Threshadons wrecked Gelkak's ship, and the key struck the shoreline rocks as he washed ashore. It broke into fragments that scattered among the local wildlife.",al={"why did gelkaks key break","how did the key break"}},{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is a stranded gnome pirate on Darkshore's shores. Threshadons destroyed his vessel and scattered his gear.",al={"who is gelkak","gelkak gyromast lore"}},{q="What is the Bottom of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is the lowest fragment of a mechanical key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel foundered off the coast of Darkshore, the key shattered on the jagged rocks upon impact, and this piece was scavenged from the debris by the local shoreline crawlers.",al={"what is bottom of gelkaks key","bottom of gelkak key","what is this key piece"},it="identity",add="bb7c59d0"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize part of a specialized winding implement built to power complex clockwork automatons.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may appreciate that Gyromast relies on clockwork ingenuity instead of a flesh-and-blood crew, even while stranded on a hostile coast."},kw={"crawler","darkshore","first mate","gelkak","gyromast","key","retrieval","shipwreck"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key","item:top-of-gelkak-s-key","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate"},src={"Bottom of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:cliffspring-river-sample"] = {t="item",n="Cliffspring River Sample",z="darkshore",s="At Cliffspring River's waterfall in Darkshore, foul water gathers in a pool. Drawn for Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, the sample shows corruption moving toward the coast.",h="At Cliffspring River's waterfall in Darkshore, foul water gathers in a pool.",sec={{t="A Tainted Current",b="The Cliffspring River runs from Darkshore's eastern heights, past ancient stone bridges, and into the sea at Mist's Edge. Its clear water has turned foul and visibly corrupted. Thundris Windweaver, a night elf in Auberdine, fears the tainted flow will reach the settlement's shore and water supply. He sent travelers to draw water from the pool beneath the river's lower waterfall. The sample confirms that unnatural rot is moving downstream toward the coast.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of Felwood",b="Blackwood furbolgs live along the river upstream and suffer under its darkening influence. Thundris recognizes that the corruption comes from high above the cliffs to the east, in Felwood. Demonic sickness blighting the mountaintops is seeping into Darkshore's watersheds. Auberdine's defenders must prepare to respond.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Cliffspring River Sample collected?",a="The sample comes from the pool beneath the first Cliffspring River waterfall, north of Auberdine. Follow the river inland to the waterfall beneath an overhead bridge.",al={"where do i get the sample","cliffspring river location","waterfall pool sample"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver need this water?",a="Thundris fears the foul river water will contaminate Auberdine's coastal waters. A sample lets him study the taint and plan how to counter it.",al={"why gather the water","thundris river quest","purpose of river sample"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is causing the Cliffspring River to turn foul?",a="The true source lies east in Felwood, where lingering demonic blight is seeping into the mountain headwaters. Corrupted Blackwood furbolgs live along the river, too.",al={"what poisoned the river","why is the water corrupted","source of river corruption"},it="danger"},{q="Are the Blackwood furbolgs responsible for the poison?",a="The Blackwood furbolgs worsen the trouble along the riverbanks, but they are not its root cause. They have fallen prey to the wider corruption flowing from the blighted lands to the east.",al={"did furbolgs do it","blackwood furbolg taint","are furbolgs poisoning water"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Cliffspring River Sample?",a="It is a vial of foul, corrupted river water gathered in an empty sampling tube from the base of the waterfall along the Cliffspring River. It serves as tangible proof that a foul taint is washing downstream through Darkshore.",al={"cliffspring river sample","what is cliffspring river sample","cliffspring water sample"},it="identity",add="2e135e3b"},{q="Where does the Cliffspring River Sample come from?",a="The sample is collected from the pool beneath the first waterfall of the Cliffspring River, north of Auberdine. While you gather the natural water yourself using an empty sampling tube, its unnatural foulness originates from corrupting forces upstream flowing down from Felwood.",al={"where does cliffspring river sample come from","cliffspring river sample origin","who made cliffspring sample"},it="origin",add="57059c85"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, corruption in northern Kalimdor's waters is a grave sign of blight spreading from Felwood.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know that waterways must remain in balance. The Cliffspring sample's unnatural toxicity needs urgent study and cleansing."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","felwood","sample","thundris","tube","waterfall","windweaver"},rel={"quest:4762","quest:4761","item:empty-sampling-tube","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:mist-s-edge","topic:furbolg"},src={"Cliffspring River Sample","The Cliffspring River"}}
E["item:corrupted-kor-gem"] = {t="item",n="Corrupted Kor Gem",z="darkshore",s="Near Blackfathom Deeps, naga rites taint Kor gems. Sorcerers prize their arcane power, though the corruption must be cleansed before a gem can be used in righteous smithing.",h="Near Blackfathom Deeps, naga rites taint Kor gems.",sec={{t="Vessels of Tainted Power",b="Kor gems hold great stores of magic, making them useful to sorcerers and enchanted smiths. Near the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, naga oracles and tide priestesses claim the stones for their rites. Their enchantments corrupt each gem with magic from the sea. The taint leaves the stone's latent power intact, so those seeking a potent focus still look among the naga.",sp=0},{t="Purification and Smithing",b="Thundris Windweaver requires a Corrupted Kor Gem to be purified before it is taken to Jordan Stilwell. In Auberdine, the night elf cleanses the naga's evil magic. He assures the paladin that the gem's power remains intact for the blacksmith's ritual.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Kor Gem used for?",a="Kor gems hold arcane energy for spellcasters. Skilled blacksmiths can set them into enchanted weapons to channel magic.",al={"what are kor gems","purpose of kor gem","kor gem lore"},it="power"},{q="Where are Corrupted Kor Gems found?",a="Naga spellcasters carry Corrupted Kor Gems around Blackfathom Deeps, both within and outside its ancient ruins on the Ashenvale and Darkshore border. Blackfathom Tide Priestesses and Blackfathom Oracles bear them.",al={"where to find corrupted kor gem","kor gem location","who drops kor gem"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why must the gem be purified?",a="Naga rites fill the gems with foul magic. Before a gem can be worked into an arm, a master of nature or light such as Thundris Windweaver must purge the evil.",al={"cleanse kor gem","why purify kor gem","is the gem evil"},it="motive"},{q="Does cleansing the gem preserve its power?",a="Yes. Thundris Windweaver assures the paladin that cleansing leaves the gem's power intact for Jordan Stilwell's ritual.",al={"does purification ruin the gem","weaker after purification"}},{q="What is a Corrupted Kor Gem?",a="A Corrupted Kor Gem is a magical vessel originally meant to store raw arcane or spellcasting energy, but twisted by dark sorcery. Naga spellcasters have infused the stone with their own vile power, turning an otherwise neutral conduit into a tainted relic brimming with malevolent energy.",al={"what is corrupted kor gem","corrupted kor gem info","tell me about corrupted kor gem"},it="identity",add="114a4618"},{q="Where does a Corrupted Kor Gem come from, and who made it?",a="While Kor gems were originally crafted as conduits for spellcasters to store magical energy, these corrupted versions are held and altered by the naga dwelling around Blackfathom Deeps in northwestern Ashenvale. Naga priestesses and oracles have saturated the gems with their own foul magic, transforming them into tools of dark ritual.",al={"who made corrupted kor gem","corrupted kor gem origin","where did kor gem come from"},it="origin",add="1218ae71"},{q="Why does anyone want a Corrupted Kor Gem?",a="Holy paladins seek out the gem at the behest of the blacksmith Jordan Stilwell to aid in forging a weapon of righteousness, though it must first be cleansed of its evil magic by Thundris Windweaver. Its ability to hold magical energy makes it valuable for ritual craft once properly purified.",al={"why get corrupted kor gem","who wants corrupted kor gem","why do i need kor gem"},it="why_wanted",add="1d7ce70e"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you must recover and purify a Kor Gem to forge a sacred armament. In doing so, you prove you can face evil and cleanse darkness into righteous strength.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the danger naga relics bring to Darkshore. Scholars such as Thundris Windweaver preserve the knowledge needed to cleanse the ancient stones."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","corrupted kor gem","kor gem","naga","purification","thundris windweaver","tide priestess"},rel={"quest:1442","quest:1653","zone:blackfathom","topic:naga","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Corrupted Kor Gem","Seeking the Kor Gem"}}
E["item:crawler-leg"] = {t="item",n="Crawler Leg",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's misty coast, crabs lose legs most travelers have no use for. Their tough limbs can keep a gnome's communication device working.",h="Along Darkshore's misty coast, crabs lose legs most travelers have no use for.",sec={{t="Gnomish Ingenuity on the Coast",b="Darkshore's crabs leave sturdy legs along the shore, from pygmy tide crawlers to reef crawlers. The night elf sentinels pay them little mind. But gnome engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle has found a use for them.\n\nFrom Auberdine, he designed prototype long-distance communication devices called buzzboxes to work with improvised local parts. Crawler legs have segmented joints and durable chitin, giving the friction and leverage needed to repair Buzzbox 827 just south of town along the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are crawler legs used for?",a="Crawler legs help repair Buzzbox 827, an experimental communication station along the Darkshore coast just south of Auberdine. Gnome inventor Wizbang Cranktoggle placed it there.",al={"crawler leg purpose","why keep crawler legs","buzzbox crawler leg"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where do crawler legs come from?",a="Crawler legs come from crabs along Darkshore's beaches. These include Pygmy Tide Crawlers, Young Reef Crawlers, Encrusted Tide Crawlers, and Reef Crawlers.",al={"crawler leg source","which crabs drop crawler legs","where to find crawler leg"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does a mechanical buzzbox need crab legs?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle designed his machines to use parts from nearby wildlife for field repairs. Crawler legs have rigid joints and chitinous segments that fit the buzzbox's grinding gears and restore its mechanisms.",al={"why crabs for machine","buzzbox crab legs lore","how does crawler leg fix buzzbox"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Crawler Leg?",a="A Crawler Leg is a severed limb harvested from the various species of crawlers skittering along the mist-shrouded shores of Darkshore. With their rigid, chitinous shells and durable joints, these legs are surprisingly tough and suited for rugged, improvised mechanical repairs.",al={"what is crawler leg","crawler leg item","about crawler legs"},it="identity",add="bab31e79"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle uses crab legs as makeshift levers, showing how gnomes improvise in the field with nearby materials in place of standard metal linkages.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may see aggressive crustaceans on a beach and recognize their legs as possible parts for a delicate long-distance communication network."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 827","crawler leg","darkshore","reef crawler","tide crawler","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:983","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},src={"Crawler Leg","Buzzbox 827 (quest)"}}
E["item:curative-animal-salve"] = {t="item",n="Curative Animal Salve",z="darkshore",s="Across Darkshore and the Barrens, druids tend sick wildlife with Curative Animal Salve. Herbalists prepare it in both lands, while the Cenarion Circle reads the animals’ afflictions as signs of a wider blight.",h="Across Darkshore and the Barrens, druids tend sick wildlife with Curative Animal Salve.",sec={{t="Mending the Wilds",b="Druids use Curative Animal Salve on sick wildlife in Darkshore and the Barrens. Alanndarian Nightsong directs young druids to treat sick deer between the Cliffspring River and Ashenvale’s borders. In the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem brews the same remedy for sick gazelles north of the Crossroads.\n\nEach herbalist gathers local herbs and prepares the salve in batches of ten doses. Field druids apply it directly to the animals. Both herbalists work with local authorities to make larger supplies.",sp=0},{t="Symptoms of a Deeper Malaise",b="The salve eases the animals’ suffering, but the Cenarion Circle sees a wider disturbance. In Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze observes that the afflicted deer on the coast and the suffering gazelles on the savannah are no random casualties. They are unwitting victims of a blight spreading across Kalimdor from several directions.\n\nFor initiates, treating the animals tests their dedication to protecting nature and their skill at cleansing poison.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Curative Animal Salve used for?",a="Druids apply Curative Animal Salve directly to afflicted wildlife to ease their ailments. In Darkshore, they use it on sick deer; in the Barrens, they treat sick gazelles grazing north of the Crossroads.",al={"curative animal salve purpose","how to use curative animal salve","what does the salve do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who prepares the salve?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong prepares the salve from gathered herbs in Darkshore. In the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem brews it at the Crossroads for Horde druids.",al={"who makes the salve","where does the salve come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the deer and gazelles sick in the first place?",a="Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle says the wildlife are victims of a growing taint spreading across Kalimdor. The deer and gazelles are early casualties of an ecological blight.",al={"why are animals sickly","what is poisoning darkshore deer","barrens gazelle sickness"},it="motive"},{q="How many doses does a batch contain?",a="A standard batch contains ten doses, enough for ten applications.",al={"how many charges","how many uses on salve"},gp=true},{q="What is Curative Animal Salve?",a="Curative Animal Salve is an herbal remedy concocted to treat afflicted wildlife suffering from spreading unnatural sickness. Prepared by druidic allies using local reagents, it cleanses the malaise poisoning innocent creatures such as the deer of Darkshore and the gazelles of the Barrens.",al={"curative salve","what is animal salve","curative animal salve lore"},it="identity",add="a20a877c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, treating wildlife with this salve tests your dedication to the Cenarion Circle’s work across Kalimdor and your skill at cleansing poison.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, using the salve in the Barrens follows Cenarius’s teachings. Tauren druids work in harmony with ancestral circle rites to heal the earth."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","curative animal salve","curing the sick","power over poison","sickly deer","sickly gazelle","tonga runetotem"},rel={"quest:6124","quest:6125","topic:cenarion-circle","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:tonga-runetotem","zone:darkshore","zone:barrens"},src={"Curative Animal Salve","Curing the Sick (Alliance)","Curing the Sick (Horde)"}}
E["item:darkshore-grouper"] = {t="item",n="Darkshore Grouper",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Darkshore Grouper are a familiar catch, though murloc attacks have driven fishermen from their boats. The fish are prized for food and sport, and a good haul takes patience.",h="Along Darkshore, Darkshore Grouper are a familiar catch, though murloc attacks have driven fishermen from...",sec={{t="A Staple of the Shrouded Coast",b="In Darkshore’s cold waters, Darkshore Grouper are a welcome catch. Around Auberdine, anglers value them for the simple dishes they make. Travelers and residents alike enjoy those meals. A fishing line and basic gear are enough to bring one in. For many fishermen, catching a grouper is as pleasing as eating it.",sp=0},{t="The Murloc Menace",b="Fishermen such as Gubber Blump once rowed small boats into deeper waters and returned with grouper by the dozen. Now the coastal murlocs are more aggressive, and most boats around Auberdine stay ashore. Anglers fish from shore and dock instead. Locals suspect the murlocs are eating the grouper, so a good haul takes patience.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Darkshore Grouper be found?",a="Cast your line into Darkshore’s saltwater, including the waters around Auberdine, to catch Darkshore Grouper.",al={"where to fish grouper","darkshore grouper location","how to catch darkshore grouper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Darkshore Grouper in Auberdine?",a="Gubber Blump, a dwarven fisherman staying in Auberdine, asks travelers to catch Darkshore Grouper for him. He offers a prized Blump Family Fishing Pole in return.",al={"who needs grouper","gubber blump fish","grouper quest giver"},it="wants"},{q="Why aren't fishermen using boats to catch grouper?",a="Aggressive murlocs along Darkshore’s coast make boat trips too dangerous for local fishermen.",al={"why are boats stopped","auberdine fishing boats","murlocs grouper"},it="conflict"},{q="Do you need to be on a quest to catch a Darkshore Grouper?",a="No. Darkshore Grouper are ordinary saltwater fish, and any angler can catch them in Darkshore’s waters. Locals such as Gubber Blump may ask you to catch them.",al={"is grouper a quest item","can i fish grouper anytime"},gp=true},{q="What is Darkshore Grouper?",a="Darkshore Grouper is a local saltwater fish swimming off the misty coastline of Darkshore. Highly prized by local anglers like Gubber Blump, it is celebrated both as great sport to reel in from the surf and as versatile fare for home cooking.",al={"what is darkshore grouper","darkshore grouper fish","about darkshore grouper"},it="identity",add="bdb033c0"},{q="Where does Darkshore Grouper come from?",a="Darkshore Grouper is a wild saltwater fish native to the coastal ocean waters along Darkshore. It is not crafted or created by anyone, though catching it requires casting a line into the surf off the shore and docks.",al={"darkshore grouper origin","where does darkshore grouper come from","where is darkshore grouper from"},it="origin",add="97e4a4d8"},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Darkshore Grouper?",a="Gubber Blump simply loves catching and eating them, boasting that there are plenty of fine dishes you can cook up with a fresh catch. Because hostile murlocs have driven the local fishing boats out of the water, he relies on helpful travelers to pull them from the coast.",al={"why want darkshore grouper","why does gubber want grouper","what is darkshore grouper used for"},it="why_wanted",add="f987244e"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Darkshore Grouper make a handy ingredient for simple coastal recipes. They give traveling cooks a way to practice their trade along the shore.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize Gubber Blump. His fishing on Kalimdor’s shores carries on his family’s proud heritage. He rewards those who match his kin’s skill at catching fish."},kw={"auberdine","blump family fishing pole","darkshore","darkshore grouper","fishing","grouper","gubber blump","murloc"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","item:gaffer-jack"},src={"Darkshore Grouper","The Family and the Fishing Pole"}}
E["item:death-cap"] = {t="item",n="Death Cap",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Death Cap grows in a cave behind Cliffspring Falls. Night elf herbalists seek the scarce fungus, though the Grove of the Ancients warns against going near the falls.",h="In Darkshore, Death Cap grows in a cave behind Cliffspring Falls.",sec={{t="A Toxic Bloom in the Dark",b="Death Cap grows in a damp cave behind Cliffspring Falls, along Darkshore’s northeastern mountain ridges. Scaber stalks cover the cavern floor, but Death Cap is scarce. Night elf herbalists such as Barithras Moonshade value it for experimental brewing. To find even one, you must enter a cave the Grove of the Ancients warns against, where corruption is taking root.",sp=0},{t="Omen of Cliffspring",b="Guardians of the Grove of the Ancients warned local Kaldorei to stay away from Cliffspring Falls. They sensed a foul presence taking root in the darkness. Anyone who enters the cave for Death Cap must face whatever forces have claimed the damp hollow as their lair.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find a Death Cap?",a="Death Cap grows in a hidden cave behind Cliffspring Falls, against the mountain wall in northeastern Darkshore.",al={"death cap location","where is death cap","cliffspring cave mushroom"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this mushroom?",a="Barithras Moonshade, an alchemist in Auberdine, the coastal settlement, seeks Death Cap for a specialized potion.",al={"who needs death cap","barithras mushroom quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why didn't Barithras Moonshade collect it himself?",a="Guardians from the Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras to avoid the cave behind Cliffspring Falls. They sensed an encroaching evil there.",al={"why not get it himself","barithras warning"},it="motive"},{q="How does the Death Cap differ from a Scaber Stalk?",a="Scaber stalks are plentiful across the floor of the Cliffspring cave, while Death Cap is scarce and harder to find.",al={"death cap vs scaber stalk","difference between mushrooms"},it="item"},{q="What is a Death Cap?",a="The Death Cap is an exceedingly rare and potent mushroom found deep within the shadowy recesses of Darkshore. Unlike ordinary woodland fungi, it thrives only in specific, hidden caverns, such as the cavern tucked behind Cliffspring Falls. Its ominous name reflects both its rarity and its potential danger, making it a prized specimen for alchemists and herbalists studying the unique flora of the region.",al={"what is death cap","death cap mushroom","what kind of mushroom is death cap"},it="identity",add="508b05a0"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Gathering Death Cap for Barithras calls for no special sickle. Herbalists know the danger of seeking rare fungi in damp, corrupted caves.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can bring Death Cap to Barithras in Auberdine and heed the Grove of the Ancients’ warning."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","grove of the ancients","scaber stalk"},rel={"quest:947","npc:barithras-moonshade","subzone:cliffspring-falls","item:scaber-stalk","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:952"},src={"Death Cap","Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["item:electropeller"] = {t="item",n="Electropeller",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Electropeller parts lie scattered through freshwater after a night outing went wrong.",h="In Darkshore, Electropeller parts lie scattered through freshwater after a night outing went wrong.",sec={{t="Mishaps along the Riverbank",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle built the electropellers to propel an experimental exploding duck decoy. The gnome inventor works out of Auberdine. After too many drinks, he went scouting along Darkshore's waterways and blacked out. Hours later, he woke with singed hair and an empty pack. His electropellers had tumbled into the freshwater currents, where they remain scattered through rivers and lakes until patient anglers recover them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an electropeller used for?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle designed electropellers to propel an experimental, self-propelled, exploding duck decoy he was developing in Darkshore.",al={"electropeller purpose","what does an electropeller do","why duck decoy"},it="purpose"},{q="How did these parts end up in the rivers of Darkshore?",a="After too many drinks, Wizbang Cranktoggle went scouting in Darkshore at night and blacked out. Hours later, he woke with singed hair and an empty pack. His electropellers had tumbled into the freshwater currents.",al={"why in the water","how did electropellers get lost","cranktoggle mistake"},it="origin"},{q="Where can electropellers be recovered?",a="Anglers can recover electropellers from Darkshore's freshwater bodies, including the Cliffspring River and the Wildbend River.",al={"where to fish electropellers","electropeller locations","cliffspring river fishing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these components returned?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome in Auberdine, wants twelve electropellers returned so he can continue his decoy research.",al={"who needs electropellers","who is cranktoggle","auberdine gnome quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is an electropeller?",a="An electropeller is a specialized mechanical propulsion component crafted by gnome engineering. These motorized parts are designed to drive aquatic devices, specifically the eccentric inventions conceived by Wizbang Cranktoggle, such as his motorized duck decoys.",al={"what is electropeller","electropeller item","what are electropellers"},it="identity",add="3f720660"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, the electropeller shows the ambition and hazards of gnomish engineering. Wizbang Cranktoggle designed it to propel an exploding duck decoy, but it ended up in the river before a proper test.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Wizbang Cranktoggle's bold technical ambition. He asks passing anglers to salvage the results of his late-night experiments."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","duck decoy","electropeller","electropellers","wildbend river","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1580","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","item:gaffer-jack","quest:1579","subzone:wildbend-river","quest:4762"},src={"Electropeller","Electropellers"}}
E["item:empty-cleansing-bowl"] = {t="item",n="Empty Cleansing Bowl",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, the Empty Cleansing Bowl carries moonwell water against the Blackwood corruption. Mixed with food samples, the water makes a meal that briefly breaks the satyrs’ demonic hold over the furbolgs.",h="In Auberdine, the Empty Cleansing Bowl carries moonwell water against the Blackwood corruption.",sec={{t="A Vessel of Purification",b="In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver gives adventurers the Empty Cleansing Bowl to carry sacred water from the local moonwell. The night elves have learned that satyrs use enchanted talismans to drive the northern Blackwood furbolgs into demonic madness. Dip the bowl in the moonwell, then mix its water with nuts, grains, and fruits gathered from the furbolgs. The blessed meal briefly restores the afflicted creatures’ sanity and reveals the satyr overseer behind their madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What do I do with the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="Take the bowl to the Auberdine moonwell and dip it in the blessed waters to make a Filled Cleansing Bowl. Then gather grain, nut, and fruit samples from the northern Blackwood furbolg camp to mix with the water.",al={"empty cleansing bowl use","how to use empty cleansing bowl","where to fill cleansing bowl"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why do the night elves need this bowl to fight the furbolg corruption?",a="Satyr talismans bind the Blackwood furbolgs with dark magic. Thundris Windweaver uses the bowl to hold a sanctified mixture that briefly breaks their frenzy and draws out their hidden controller, Xabraxxis.",al={"why cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl purpose"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Who provides the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="Thundris Windweaver, a night elf scholar in Auberdine, gives you the bowl when he asks you to uncover the source of the Blackwood corruption along the Cliffspring River.",al={"who gives cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl questgiver"},it="origin"},{q="What happens once the mixture is prepared?",a="Set the prepared mixture near the northern camp’s bonfire. It cleanses nearby furbolgs long enough to draw Xabraxxis’s fury, letting you slay the satyr and claim his Talisman of Corruption.",al={"cleansing bowl bonfire","place cleansing bowl"},sp=1},{q="What is the Empty Cleansing Bowl?",a="The Empty Cleansing Bowl is a ritual vessel entrusted to you by Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. Crafted to hold the sanctified waters of a moonwell along with wild foodstuffs, it serves as the essential component for preparing a purifying offering capable of lifting the demonic taint afflicting the local wildlife and furbolgs.",al={"what is empty cleansing bowl","cleansing bowl lore","empty cleansing bowl purpose"},it="identity",add="2a179129"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see how Elune’s moonwells can undo demonic taint. The cleansing offers hope that your old furbolg allies may be saved.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you use moonwell waters to break unnatural afflictions. It reflects your calling to mend nature’s wounded balance across Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cleansing bowl","darkshore","empty cleansing bowl","moonwell","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4763","quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","item:talisman-of-corruption","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore","quest:4762"},src={"Empty Cleansing Bowl","The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["item:empty-cliffspring-falls-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler",z="darkshore",s="At Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore, young druids gather water to investigate a poison killing local wildlife. The Cenarion Circle gives them empty samplers for water from the cave mouth.",h="At Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore, young druids gather water to investigate a poison killing local wildlife.",sec={{t="Investigating the Tainted Waters",b="Cliffspring Falls feeds northern Darkshore. Poison in its headwaters puts the local wildlife at risk. When a wasting poison began killing the region’s deer, Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle gave empty samplers to young druids from Moonglade. They must gather water at a cave entrance by the falls, overrun by hostile naga.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for a Cure",b="Alanndarian Nightsong receives the filled sampler in Auberdine. The polluted water confirms that foul agents are poisoning the water table. By studying the contamination, Alanndarian and the Cenarion druids can formulate an antidote. They can also teach the initiate basic druidic healing rites.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this sampler?",a="Druids use the empty sampler to gather tainted water from the cave mouth at Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. The sample helps Cenarion herbalists diagnose and cure the poison affecting local wildlife.",al={"sampler use","what is cliffspring sampler for","empty sampler purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the water sample taken?",a="The water is gathered at the mouth of the cave near Cliffspring Falls, high in Darkshore’s northeastern hills. Hostile naga overrun the entrance.",al={"where to fill sampler","cliffspring sampler location","fill sampler spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who receives the filled container?",a="The filled sampler goes to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. She is a night elf healer and a Cenarion representative there.",al={"who gets the filled sampler","where to turn in sampler","alanndarian sampler"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls being sampled instead of other rivers?",a="Cliffspring Falls is the main freshwater source for northern Darkshore. Dendrite Starblaze traced the illness killing the region’s deer to these headwaters, so a direct sample is needed to develop a remedy.",al={"why cliffspring falls","what is poisoning darkshore","cliffspring poison"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler?",a="It is a specialized vessel provided to Cenarion Circle druids to collect an uncontaminated sample of water from Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Because the falls are thought to be tainted, having a sterile, dedicated container is essential for studying the toxic liquid without contaminating the sample or harming the bearer.",al={"what is cliffspring falls sampler","cliffspring sampler item"},it="identity",add="0413bdcd"},{q="Where does the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler come from, and who made it?",a="The sampler is supplied by the Cenarion Circle druids in Moonglade, specifically through Dendrite Starblaze. Sensing that something unnatural had begun poisoning Darkshore's wildlife, the Circle prepared these containers so trusted initiates could secure pure samples directly from suspected contamination sites.",al={"who gave me cliffspring sampler","who made sampler","sampler origin"},it="origin",add="dccecdc8"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you gather water at the naga-held cave as a rite of passage, then learn Cure Poison.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know that naga threaten the wildlife and Auberdine by tainting Darkshore’s forest water."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","cure poison","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","sampler"},rel={"item:filled-cliffspring-falls-sampler","quest:6122","quest:6125","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle"},src={"Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler","The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["item:empty-sampling-tube"] = {t="item",n="Empty Sampling Tube",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver gives you an Empty Sampling Tube to test the Cliffspring River. Night elf scholars study the taint threatening Darkshore.",h="In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver gives you an Empty Sampling Tube to test the Cliffspring River.",sec={{t="Testing the Waters",b="Darkshore's waterways are turning foul as blight spreads through the wilderness. In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver investigates the change. He gives you an empty glass tube for water from the Cliffspring River. Take the sample from the pool beneath the first waterfall north of town. Night elf naturalists will examine it to learn about the corruption flowing toward Mist's Edge.",sp=0},{t="Tracing the Source",b="Blackwood furbolgs live in camps along the riverbanks. Windweaver suspects they suffer from the rot and spread it, rather than cause it. The sample confirms that contamination flows from Felwood's tainted heights to the east. It may help shape a cure and guide a direct response to the blight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Empty Sampling Tube?",a="Use the Empty Sampling Tube to collect water from the corrupted Cliffspring River north of Auberdine. Bring the sample to Thundris Windweaver, who studies the foul substances spreading through Darkshore.",al={"why do i have this tube","what does the sampling tube do","tube purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the water sample supposed to be taken?",a="Fill the tube at the first waterfall on the Cliffspring River, north of Auberdine. The pool lies beneath an overhead bridge, before the water spills into Mist's Edge.",al={"where to fill tube","cliffspring river location","sampling tube spot"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who provided this tube?",a="Thundris Windweaver gives you the tube. He is a night elf naturalist studying threats to the land around Auberdine.",al={"who gives the tube","tube quest giver","thundris windweaver"},it="origin"},{q="What is polluting the Cliffspring River?",a="Blackwood furbolgs live along the riverbanks and add to the filth. Yet the taint flows from Felwood's corrupted woodland, high in the mountains to the east.",al={"why is the river green","what corrupted the water","cliffspring taint"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What is the Empty Sampling Tube?",a="It is a clean, specially prepared glass vial given to you to collect water from the Cliffspring River. Thundris Windweaver needs an uncontaminated vessel to secure a pure specimen of the foul wash currently flowing down into the sea north of Auberdine.",al={"what is empty sampling tube","empty tube lore","about empty sampling tube"},it="identity",add="54012ea9"},{q="Why does Thundris want a sample collected in this tube?",a="Darkshore's waters are rapidly sickening, and Thundris suspects the foul taint washing down the Cliffspring River reaches Auberdine's coast. By inspecting a fresh sample drawn in this vessel, he hopes to determine whether local Blackwood furbolgs or darker corruptions from the eastern highlands of Felwood are responsible, giving the night elves a basis for their counter-measures.",al={"why is empty sampling tube wanted","why collect cliffspring water","thundris sample why"},it="why_wanted",add="b354763d"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can help uncover how Felwood's taint reaches Darkshore's rivers and sickens local wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Auberdine, you can help test the Cliffspring River and keep its corrupting runoff from poisoning your coastal haven at Mist's Edge."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","empty sampling tube","mist's edge","thundris windweaver","water sample"},rel={"quest:4762","item:cliffspring-river-sample","quest:4761","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","topic:furbolg"},src={"Empty Sampling Tube","The Cliffspring River"}}
E["item:empty-water-tube"] = {t="item",n="Empty Water Tube",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, the Empty Water Tube is ready to gather sacred moonwell water for the red crystal on Darkshore’s eastern cliffs.",h="In Auberdine, the Empty Water Tube is ready to gather sacred moonwell water for the red crystal on...",sec={{t="A Vessel for Blessed Waters",b="Sentinels and scholars seek pure lunar essence to study the mysterious red crystal along Darkshore’s eastern ridge. Ordinary glass or flasks can taint consecrated water, so investigators visiting Auberdine’s moonwell receive this sealed vial. They carry the filled vessel up the mountain slopes to learn how the alien mineral responds to Elune’s magic.",sp=0},{t="Probing Felwood's Shadow",b="Felwood lies beyond the mountains east of Darkshore, poisoned by demonic corruption. Auberdine’s defenders suspect the ominous crimson monolith near the cliffs may be linked to that ruined forest. Researchers hope moonwell water cascading over its lattice will reveal the crystal’s inner structure without triggering a catastrophic release of the power trapped inside.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Empty Water Tube?",a="In Auberdine, you receive the empty container to draw moonwell water for analyzing the bizarre red crystal on Darkshore’s eastern heights.",al={"empty water tube purpose","why do i have empty water tube","what do i do with water tube"},it="purpose"},{q="Where should the tube be filled?",a="Dip the tube into the moonwell in Auberdine to fill it. The filled vessel becomes a Moonwell Water Tube.",al={"where to fill water tube","where do i fill empty water tube","fill water tube location"},gp=true},{q="Why is moonwell water needed for the crystal?",a="Moonwell water carries Elune’s potent, purifying magic. Scholars believe pouring it over the red crystal will reveal clues about its origin and composition.",al={"why moonwell water","what does moonwell water do to crystal","red crystal moonwell water"}},{q="Why are Auberdine's residents worried about the crystal?",a="The crystal rests near the high ridge overlooking Felwood, a forest badly corrupted by the Burning Legion. Local watchers fear a link to that tainted wilderness could threaten Darkshore.",al={"is the crystal dangerous","crystal danger darkshore","why investigate red crystal"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Empty Water Tube?",a="It is a simple, empty glass vial provided to you in Auberdine so you can gather water from the village's moonwell. Once filled, you will use its blessed contents to test the mysterious, alien red crystal resting against the mountains of Darkshore.",al={"what is empty water tube","empty water tube","vial for moonwell water"},it="identity",add="8160d8ef"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you treat handling consecrated moonwell water as a sacred duty. The Kaldorei revere moonwells as holy reservoirs blessed by Elune.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold moonwells in deep reverence. You rely on their untainted waters to study anomalies and cleanse strange disruptions from corrupted lands like Felwood."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","moonwell","moonwell water tube","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","item:moonwell-water-tube","quest:4811","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},src={"Empty Water Tube","As Water Cascades"}}
E["item:filled-cliffspring-falls-sampler"] = {t="item",n="Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler",z="darkshore",s="Near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore, the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler holds foul water drawn from the headwaters. The Cenarion Circle needs it to study the sickness striking local deer.",h="Near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore, the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler holds foul water drawn from the...",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Cliffspring Falls carries water from the eastern highlands through much of Darkshore. Now local deer are falling ill with an unnatural sickness. At Dendrite Starblaze’s request in Moonglade, druidic initiates draw water from a cave mouth where hostile naga dwell. The vial holds visibly foul water, proof that the fresh supply is tainted.",sp=0},{t="Path to a Remedy",b="Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine receives the foul water for the Cenarion Circle to study. Rather than discard it, Alanndarian examines its poison. By learning the sludge’s properties, the druids can make a curative salve. That is an essential step toward a rite that gives practitioners power over poison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler?",a="The sampler holds contaminated water drawn from a cavern mouth near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. The water is visibly discolored and carries the poison sickening local deer.",al={"sampler contents","what water is in the vial","what is in the sample"},it="identity"},{q="Who asks for this water sample?",a="Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle asks young druids to collect the sample. Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine receives it to study the poison and formulate a cure.",al={"who wants the water sample","who do i give the sampler to","who needs the filled sampler"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important?",a="Cliffspring Falls is Darkshore’s principal source of drinking water. Corruption in the falls spreads through local waterways and harms the wilderness.",al={"why cliffspring falls","importance of cliffspring falls"},it="purpose"},{q="What is causing the water to turn foul?",a="Hostile naga have overrun a cave near the headwaters, where the water is drawn. Their presence coincides with fouled water and sickness among local animals.",al={"who poisoned the water","why is the falls poisoned","naga cliffspring falls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler come from, and who made it?",a="The empty glass sampling tube is provided to young druids by Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. It becomes the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler once you take it to the mouth of the naga-infested cave beside Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore and draw water directly from the tainted stream.",al={"origin filled cliffspring falls sampler","who made cliffspring sampler","where do you get cliffspring sampler"},it="origin",add="57552b8f"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, retrieving and studying this tainted water gives you a proving trial. It also lays the groundwork for mastering Cure Poison.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Darkshore, you help secure the Cliffspring headwaters and protect Auberdine’s ecology from foul foreign corruption."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","poisoned water","sampler"},rel={"quest:6122","item:empty-cliffspring-falls-sampler","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:cliffspring-falls","quest:6125","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},src={"Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler","The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["item:fine-crab-chunks"] = {t="item",n="Fine Crab Chunks",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers yield Fine Crab Chunks. Gubber Blump seeks them for his cooking.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers yield Fine Crab Chunks.",sec={{t="Fruit of the Sea",b="Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers roam Darkshore's shores. By the water, travelers may find them pests or dangers, while cooks prize their meat. The chunks can be boiled, broiled, fried, or stirred into stews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers along Darkshore's rocky beaches and tidal shallows yield Fine Crab Chunks.",al={"where do fine crab chunks drop","which crabs drop chunks","crab meat source"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants Fine Crab Chunks in Darkshore?",a="Gubber Blump, a fisherman on Auberdine's docks, seeks Fine Crab Chunks for his crab dishes.",al={"who needs fine crab chunks","who turns in crab chunks","gubber blump crab"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Can you prepare these into actual meals?",a="Gubber Blump collects these raw chunks rather than using them directly in a recipe. Crab meat can be baked, barbecued, boiled, broiled, fried, or mixed into salads and stews.",al={"can you cook fine crab chunks","what can you make with fine crab chunks","crab recipes"},gp=true},{q="What are Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Fine Crab Chunks are prime cuts of meat carved from the sturdy crabs along Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast. Prized for their tenderness and versatility, they are considered by local enthusiasts to be the true fruit of the sea, suitable for nearly any preparation imaginable.",al={"what are fine crab chunks","fine crab chunks lore","what is fine crab meat"},it="identity",add="a1097ca6"},{q="Where do Fine Crab Chunks come from?",a="These choice morsels are harvested directly from the wild crustaceans prowling Darkshore's coastline, particularly the Reef Crawlers and Encrusted Tide Crawlers. They are not crafted by mortal hands, but butchered fresh from the creatures that thrive in the cold surf.",al={"where do fine crab chunks come from","source of fine crab chunks","fine crab chunks origin"},it="origin",add="09afcf23"},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Gubber Blump, an eccentric fisherman stationed at the Auberdine docks, is utterly obsessed with crab meat. Stranded with his fishing rod, he relies on travelers to gather fresh chunks so he can whip up an endless assortment of crab-based recipes, from baked and broiled dishes to crab salads and stews.",al={"why does gubber want crab chunks","who wants fine crab chunks","why collect fine crab chunks"},it="why_wanted",add="1943045a"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber Blump knows many ways to cook crab, from soups and salads to pepper rubs and Ironforge surprise crab.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supplying the residents on Auberdine's docks helps sustain the Alliance outpost in Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","crab","darkshore","encrusted tide crawler","fine crab chunks","fruit of the sea","gubber blump","reef crawler"},rel={"quest:1138","npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},src={"Fine Crab Chunks","Fruit of the Sea"}}
E["item:fine-moonstalker-pelt"] = {t="item",n="Fine Moonstalker Pelt",z="darkshore",s="In southern Darkshore, Terenthis seeks the hides of mature moonstalkers. Their thick, healthy pelts can help make an enchanted cloak for those searching for Volcor.",h="In southern Darkshore, Terenthis seeks the hides of mature moonstalkers.",sec={{t="Hides of the Pack Leaders",b="Moonstalker sires and matriarchs have coats dense and healthy enough to yield a fine pelt. They keep territory along the Wildbend River and farther south toward Ashenvale’s borders. There, they hunt with patience. Common moonstalkers roam Darkshore’s forests, but their hides are not fine enough.",sp=0},{t="A Cloak of Deception",b="Terenthis needs five intact pelts to make a cloak for travelers searching for the missing night elf Volcor. Nature magic binds the hides into an illusion that dulls the wearer’s presence to Darkshore’s wildlife. The cloak works only while its wearer avoids aggressive acts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What creatures yield a Fine Moonstalker Pelt?",a="Moonstalker sires and matriarchs yield Fine Moonstalker Pelts. Common and younger moonstalkers lack hides of sufficient quality.",al={"what drops fine moonstalker pelt","where to get moonstalker pelt","which cats have pelts"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Where can the mature moonstalkers be found?",a="Mature moonstalkers live in southern Darkshore, especially along the Wildbend River and farther south toward Ashenvale.",al={"where are the sires and matriarchs","moonstalker sire location","moonstalker matriarch location"},gp=true},{q="Why does Terenthis need these pelts?",a="Terenthis needs five pelts to make an enchanted cloak for travelers searching for the missing night elf Volcor. Its magic conceals the wearer from predatory beasts.",al={"what are pelts used for","why collect moonstalker pelts","terenthis pelt quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Does the finished cloak make you completely invisible?",a="The cloak does not make you completely invisible. Its natural illusion deters beasts, but actions beyond speaking to others can break the enchantment and dispel the disguise.",al={"how does the cloak work","cloak illusion limits","cloak break stealth"},gp=true},{q="What is a Fine Moonstalker Pelt?",a="A Fine Moonstalker Pelt is the prime hide harvested from the mature moonstalker sires and matriarchs roaming the wilds of Darkshore. These formidable night saber cats possess thick, supple fur capable of holding delicate natural enchantments, making their pelts far more prized and durable than the scruff of younger specimens.",al={"fine moonstalker pelt","what is moonstalker pelt","fine pelt"},it="identity",add="399f6830"},{q="Where does a Fine Moonstalker Pelt come from?",a="These pelts come naturally from the largest adult moonstalkers stalking the coasts and forests of Darkshore, particularly near the Wildbend River and farther south toward the Ashenvale border. Only fully grown moonstalker sires and matriarchs yield hides thick and healthy enough to be considered fine pelts.",al={"where to get fine moonstalker pelt","moonstalker pelt source","who drops fine moonstalker pelt"},it="origin",add="e53e751f"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking sires and matriarchs near the Wildbend River tests your skill against some of coastal Kalimdor’s fiercest predators.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you respect the moonstalkers’ sacred ferocity. Their hides are taken only in dire need, to aid fallen kin such as Volcor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fine moonstalker pelt","matriarch","moonstalker","sire","terenthis","volcor","wildbend river"},rel={"quest:986","npc:terenthis","npc:volcor","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Fine Moonstalker Pelt","A Lost Master"}}
E["item:flagongut-s-fossil"] = {t="item",n="Flagongut's Fossil",z="darkshore",s="At the Wetlands dig, Flagongut seeks answers in an ancient fossil. The Explorers' League keeps the specimen. Flagongut believes the Stone of Relu can help him decipher its secrets.",h="At the Wetlands dig, Flagongut seeks answers in an ancient fossil.",sec={{t="Excavation and Study",b="Prospector Whelgar keeps the fossil at his excavation site in the southern hills of the Wetlands. Dwarven expeditions across Khaz Modan unearthed it. Archaeologist Flagongut believes the ancient stone holds forgotten powers, and sees a kinship with artifacts found across the sea in Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Relic",b="Flagongut found the Stone of Relu and knew it could help decipher the fossil. Mottled raptors ambushed him on the road, and the stone was lost. Now he needs the fossil from Whelgar's dig and the stone recovered from Wetlands wildlife to unlock the specimen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Flagongut's Fossil?",a="Flagongut's Fossil is an ancient specimen recovered from the Wetlands. The dwarven Explorers' League keeps it to study the world's ancient past.",al={"what is the fossil","flagongut fossil lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the fossil located?",a="The fossil lies in a cave at the top of Whelgar's Excavation Site in the southern mountains of the Wetlands. Mottled raptors that overran the dig guard it.",al={"fossil location","where is flagongut fossil","whelgar fossil cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Flagongut need it returned?",a="Flagongut believes the Stone of Relu can help him decipher the fossil's hidden magical secrets. He also wants to compare it with similar findings in Kalimdor.",al={"why does flagongut want it","what will flagongut do with it"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is it connected to Darkshore?",a="Flagongut sees a parallel between the Wetlands specimen and the fossil Prospector Remtravel found in Darkshore. He believes the Stone of Relu might unlock the power in both relics.",al={"darkshore connection","remtravel fossil"},it="ties"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see fossils such as Flagongut's as links to the ancient past. The Explorers' League is dedicated to unearthing them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help secure artifacts from Whelgar's ruined dig site before wild beasts destroy them or hostile forces scavenge them in the marsh."},kw={"excavation","explorers' league","flagongut","fossil","relu","stone of relu","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:prospector-whelgar","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","item:stone-of-relu","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore","quest:729"},src={"Flagongut's Fossil","The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["item:gaffer-jack"] = {t="item",n="Gaffer Jack",z="darkshore",s="Off Auberdine, Gaffer Jack parts lie beneath Darkshore's waves. Wizbang Cranktoggle lost a crate during his voyage across the sea.",h="Off Auberdine, Gaffer Jack parts lie beneath Darkshore's waves.",sec={{t="Lost at Sea",b="Gnome tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle booked passage to Auberdine for quiet away from Ironforge's forge-works and taverns. During the voyage, he drank too much and fumbled a whole container of gaffer jacks over the railing. The small fasteners sank into Darkshore's coastal waters. Without them, Wizbang could not tune his stintle pegs.",sp=0},{t="Sunken Salvage",b="Gaffer jacks sank in the surf along Darkshore's shore, where patient fishermen sometimes catch them on their hooks. Recovering the parts lets Wizbang assemble his strange contraptions. Finding tiny metal hardware in the open sea takes patience and luck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Gaffer Jack used for?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle needs gaffer jacks to tune the stintle pegs in his experimental inventions.",al={"gaffer jack purpose","what does a gaffer jack do","gaffer jack use"},it="purpose"},{q="How did these end up in the ocean around Auberdine?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle sailed from the Eastern Kingdoms seeking quiet away from Ironforge. He drank too much during the voyage and accidentally sent his crate of gaffer jacks overboard into Darkshore's waters.",al={"why are gaffer jacks in the water","who dropped gaffer jacks","gaffer jack lost"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Gaffer Jacks recovered?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, an eccentric gnome inventor staying in Auberdine, wants eight gaffer jacks returned so he can keep building his strange inventions.",al={"who needs gaffer jacks","gaffer jack turn in","who takes gaffer jacks"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Gaffer Jacks be found?",a="Gaffer jacks lie submerged along Darkshore's coast. Anglers sometimes catch them while fishing the coastal surf.",al={"where to get gaffer jacks","how to find gaffer jacks","gaffer jack location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Gaffer Jack?",a="A Gaffer Jack is a specialized engineering component used by tinkerers like Wizbang Cranktoggle. Specifically, Wizbang relies on them to properly tune his stintle pegs, making them an indispensable part of his invention toolkit.",al={"what is gaffer jack","gaffer jacks lore","what are gaffer jacks"},it="identity",add="1164a7e3"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know how frustrating it is to lose specialized hardware like gaffer jacks. Without them, delicate mechanisms such as stintle pegs cannot be calibrated.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may find leaving Ironforge for a quiet life in Auberdine unorthodox. Losing a crate of essential parts over a ship's rail after drinking too much is another matter."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fishing","gaffer jack","ironforge","stintle pegs","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:1579","quest:1580","item:electropeller","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1141","npc:gubber-blump"},src={"Gaffer Jack","Gaffer Jacks"}}
E["item:glowing-soul-gem"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Soul Gem",z="darkshore",s="In Ordil'Aran, the Glowing Soul Gem serves the Cult of the Dark Strand's work in northern Ashenvale. Shadow sorcery fills the stone, which holds the spirit of an unwitting victim.",h="In Ordil'Aran, the Glowing Soul Gem serves the Cult of the Dark Strand's work in northern Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Vessel of Dark Sorcery",b="Northeast of Maestra's Post, the ruins of Ordil'Aran shelter the Cult of the Dark Strand and its shadowy masters. The cult's operatives carry Glowing Soul Gems, enchanted vessels that trap and torment the souls of the dead. The stones channel magical energy and bind spirits to the cult's ends.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Ordil'Aran",b="At Maestra's Post, Delgren the Purifier studies the gems to weaken the Dark Strand's influence across northern Kalimdor. Their enchantments hold dark arcane formulas and an imprisoned soul crying out from within. The formulas reveal experiments linking the cultists in Ashenvale to their kin at the Tower of Althalaxx.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Soul Gem?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand uses the Glowing Soul Gem as an enchanted soulstone. Shadow magic traps spirits inside, letting the cult harness their essence for sorcery.",al={"what is soul gem","soul gem darkshore","glowing soul gem lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this soul gem come from?",a="Members of the Cult of the Dark Strand carry the gem from the ruins of Ordil'Aran in northern Ashenvale. Its bearers include cultists, assassins, enforcers and adepts.",al={"who drops soul gem","glowing soul gem location","ordil'aran gem"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this soul gem and why?",a="At Maestra's Post, Delgren the Purifier seeks the gem. He believes its enchantments will reveal the secret source of the cult's power and what they are plotting.",al={"delgren soul gem","why delgren wants soul gem","maestra's post soul gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when the soul gem is deciphered?",a="Deciphering the gem's enchantments frees the ghost trapped within. The tormented soul is released, and the Dark Strand's practices are exposed.",al={"what is inside soul gem","ghost in soul gem"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you know the art of trapping spirits in soulstones. The Dark Strand's gem is a cruder, necromantic form of soul manipulation.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you can sense the agony of the spirit imprisoned in the gem. The artifact must be cleansed so the soul can find peace."},kw={"althalaxx","cult of the dark strand","dark strand","delgren the purifier","glowing soul gem","maestra's post","ordil'aran","soul gem"},rel={"quest:965","zone:ashenvale","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore"},src={"Glowing Soul Gem","The Tower of Althalaxx (4)"}}
E["item:grell-earring"] = {t="item",n="Grell Earring",z="darkshore",s="In Bashal'Aran, Grell Earring bears traces of the seal that binds Asterion.",h="In Bashal'Aran, Grell Earring bears traces of the seal that binds Asterion.",sec={{t="Traces in the Brass",b="Wild Grells and Vile Sprites gather scraps among Bashal'Aran's ruins and shape them into earrings. Most mortals see only trinkets without worth. But Asterion, an ancient night elf bound there as a tormented phantom, studies the magic they retain. He hopes those traces will lead him to the ancient seal that imprisons him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Grell Earrings come from?",a="Wild Grells and Vile Sprites carry the earrings through the ruins of Bashal'Aran, a night elven settlement in Darkshore.",al={"grell earring drop","where to get grell earrings","who drops grell earrings"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Asterion want these earrings?",a="Asterion is an ancient spirit held captive in Bashal'Aran by potent magic. He seeks traces of the seal that has bound his soul for centuries.",al={"asterion earrings","why collect grell earrings","grell earring use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How do the earrings help Asterion search for the seal?",a="Asterion hopes to cast a spell over the earrings and trace the seal that imprisons his spectral form in Bashal'Aran.",al={"are the earrings magic","do grells know magic"}},{q="Does Asterion find what he needs from the earrings?",a="The earrings do not hold the seal itself. Their traces show that the creatures have recently been near it, guiding Asterion deeper into the ruins.",al={"did the earrings work","asterion seal location"}},{q="What is a Grell Earring?",a="A Grell Earring is a simple piece of adornment worn by the wild grells and vile sprites infesting the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. While mundane trinkets on their own, these scavenged earpieces have absorbed subtle magical emanations from the ruins and whatever relics the creatures have handled.",al={"what are grell earrings","grell earring lore","what is grell earring"},it="identity",add="f6dd1a4f"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how metal may keep traces of the ambient magic from ancient warding seals over time.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see sacred ruins overrun by sprites wearing scavenged brass. The sight recalls how far the once-grand estates of ancient Kalimdor have fallen."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","darkshore","grell earring","seal","vile sprite","wild grell"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","zone:darkshore"},src={"Grell Earring","Bashal'Aran (2)"}}
E["item:grizzled-scalp"] = {t="item",n="Grizzled Scalp",z="darkshore",s="South of Auberdine, grizzled thistle bears roam Darkshore’s forests, and their thick hides find a use with Wizbang Cranktoggle.",h="South of Auberdine, grizzled thistle bears roam Darkshore’s forests, and their thick hides find a use with...",sec={{t="A Peculiar Fermentation",b="South of Auberdine, grizzled thistle bears roam the road, their rough pelts sought by hunters. Four scalps brought to Buzzbox 525 reveal their purpose. Wizbang Cranktoggle uses hidden buzzboxes scattered across Darkshore as stills. Night elves frown on illicit brewing in their settlements, so Wizbang relies on adventurers to gather bear scalps and other strange ingredients for his beloved thistle bear beer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Grizzled Scalps?",a="Grizzled thistle bears and their matriarch, the Den Mother, roam the forests south of Auberdine along Darkshore’s main trail.",al={"grizzled scalp location","who drops grizzled scalps","thistle bear scalp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are Grizzled Scalps used for?",a="Deposit the scalps in Buzzbox 525, a mechanical terminal hidden in the bushes beside the road far south of Auberdine.",al={"grizzled scalp use","what do i do with grizzled scalps"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Buzzbox 525 need bear scalps?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle uses his hidden buzzbox network to distill liquor away from night elf eyes. The scalps go into his thistle bear beer.",al={"why does wizbang want scalps","buzzbox 525 purpose"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Wizbang hiding his brewing in Darkshore's wilderness?",a="Wizbang hides his stills in the wilderness brush because the night elves of Auberdine object to unauthorized, noisy brewing in their sacred groves. The hidden contraptions keep his moonshine operation out of sight.",al={"why hide buzzbox","wizbang liquor darkshore"},sp=1},{q="What is a Grizzled Scalp?",a="A Grizzled Scalp is the thick, furred crown harvested from the rugged bears wandering the wilds of Darkshore. These seasoned beasts endure the harsh northern climate, developing resilient, bristled hides that trappers and curious inventors prize for their unique density.",al={"what is grizzled scalp","grizzled scalp info","tell me about grizzled scalps"},it="identity",add="903811df"},{q="Where does a Grizzled Scalp come from?",a="These scalps come from the mature thistle bears native to Darkshore, primarily the Grizzled Thistle Bears and the ferocious Den Mother. Rather than crafted goods, they are raw trophies taken directly from the wild beasts roaming south of Auberdine.",al={"where do grizzled scalps come from","grizzled scalp source","who drops grizzled scalps"},it="origin",add="e940f924"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how gnomish skill disguises automated brewing stills as field repair communication arrays.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you protect Darkshore’s wildlife and look askance at wanton poaching and gnomish stills hidden in the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 525","darkshore","grizzled scalp","grizzled thistle bear","thistle bear beer","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1003","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Grizzled Scalp","Buzzbox 525 (quest)"}}
E["item:highborne-relic-classic"] = {t="item",n="Highborne Relic (Classic)",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, spirits still clutch Highborne Relics, and night elf scholars seek to destroy them. Their dormant magic may bring further harm.",h="In Darkshore, spirits still clutch Highborne Relics, and night elf scholars seek to destroy them.",sec={{t="Remnants of the Sundering",b="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne caste brought ruin to ancient Kalimdor with reckless arcane magic. Across Darkshore, their estates lie in shattered ruins. At Ameth'Aran, wailing apparitions wander among crumbling columns, still clutching the tools of their old sorcery. Arcane taint binds the relics to these spirits, who will not let go of the objects tied to their undoing.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Arcane Taint",b="After the Great Sundering, most night elves turned away from arcane magic. Their scholars now see the relics as a grave hazard. Reports from the Sentinels reached Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, who sends travelers to wrest the relics from the cursed spirits. Once gathered, the relics are destroyed, so the Highborne's ancient evils and catastrophic mistakes cannot be repeated.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Highborne Relics come from?",a="In southern Darkshore, the spirits haunting Ameth'Aran carry Highborne Relics among the ancient ruins east of the main road. The wailing ghosts clutch them among the stones.",al={"where do i find highborne relics","who drops highborne relics","relic location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want these relics?",a="Thundris Windweaver fears the arcane corruption clinging to the relics. He gathers them for destruction so no one can revive the dangerous Highborne sorcery.",al={"why collect relics","what happens to the relics","windweaver goal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Highborne spirits still in Ameth'Aran?",a="The spirits are ancient Highborne nobility who perished when the world shattered ten thousand years ago. Their restless souls remain bound to the ruins of their former city, cursed by their hubris and attachment to arcane magic.",al={"why are ametharan ghosts there","who are the cursed highborne","why ghosts in darkshore"},it="history"},{q="Are Highborne Relics safe to use?",a="No. Night elves consider the relics tainted by the unchecked arcane practices that triggered the Great Sundering. Their dormant magic is hazardous, so scholars demand their destruction instead of study.",al={"can i use highborne relics","are relics dangerous"},it="power"},{q="What is a Highborne Relic?",a="A Highborne Relic is an ancient magical implement crafted by the Highborne sorcerers of ancient Kalimdor. These enchanted tools survive in the hands of the restless spirits haunting the shattered ruins of Ameth'Aran, bearing the lingering taint of the arcane sorcery that precipitated the Great Sundering.",al={"what is highborne relic","highborne relics lore","what are these relics"},it="identity",add="9b193d00"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, these relics recall the arcane arrogance that tore their ancient civilization apart.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may find the relics' arcane craftsmanship fascinating. The local night elf authorities insist they be destroyed."},kw={"ameth'aran","arcane","darkshore","highborne","highborne relic","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:968","subzone:ameth-aran","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:highborne","topic:sentinels","quest:4761"},src={"Highborne Relic (Classic)","Tools of the Highborne"}}
E["item:horn-of-awakening"] = {t="item",n="Horn of Awakening",z="darkshore",s="On the road to Ashenvale, Kerlonian Evershade carries the Horn of Awakening. It stirs him whenever sleep overtakes him.",h="On the road to Ashenvale, Kerlonian Evershade carries the Horn of Awakening.",sec={{t="A Remedy for Drowsy Druids",b="Kerlonian Evershade has only lately awakened from centuries in the Emerald Dream. Still, wakefulness weighs on him. The Druid of the Claw travels south toward Maestra's Post and entrusts the horn to travelers willing to escort him.\n\nWhen exhaustion takes Kerlonian on the wilderness trail, a clear blast jolts him awake. He gets back on his feet before wild beasts or cultists can reach him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Horn of Awakening found?",a="The horn rests inside Kerlonian's Chest beside Kerlonian Evershade's campsite in southern Darkshore, near the Ashenvale border.",al={"horn location","where is horn of awakening","kerlonians chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Kerlonian need the horn to stay awake?",a="After long ages asleep within the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian struggles with mortal wakefulness. Sudden, deep naps often overtake him while he travels.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","why does he fall asleep","emerald dream slumber"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Kerlonian trying to go?",a="Kerlonian is trying to reach Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale to meet Liladris Moonriver.",al={"kerlonian destination","where is he walking","maestras post escort"}},{q="What is the Horn of Awakening?",a="The Horn of Awakening is a personal instrument belonging to the night elf druid Kerlonian Evershade. Having recently emerged from the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian suffers from bouts of deep, untimely slumber on his travels. He keeps this horn secured in his chest specifically so an escort can sound it to rouse him whenever he collapses along the road.",al={"horn of awakening","what is this horn","kerlonian horn"},it="identity",add="061d2ee3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Druids of the Claw spent generations asleep in the Barrow Dens, communing with the Emerald Dream. Returning to wakefulness can leave them dazed and disoriented.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see in Kerlonian's drowsy journey how difficult it can be for your druids to wake after their long slumber in the Emerald Dream."},kw={"ashenvale","darkshore","druid of the claw","emerald dream","horn of awakening","kerlonian evershade","maestra's post"},rel={"npc:kerlonian-evershade","quest:5321","subzone:maestra-s-post","topic:emerald-dream","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:druid"},src={"Horn of Awakening","The Sleeper Has Awakened (Classic)"}}
E["item:ilkrud-magthrull-s-tome"] = {t="item",n="Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome",z="darkshore",s="At Fire Scar Shrine, Delgren the Purifier turns his attention to Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome. Its pages link the warlock to the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx.",h="At Fire Scar Shrine, Delgren the Purifier turns his attention to Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome.",sec={{t="A Grimoire of Corruption",b="At Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale, Ilkrud Magthrull holds ground poisoned by demonic influence. The formidable orc warlock is surrounded by summoned minions. His personal tome records foul rituals and shadowy communications. Delgren the Purifier, an Argent Dawn paladin, has long known Magthrull is there. The book is urgent to recover because it links the warlock to the dark cultists gathering at the Tower of Althalaxx.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling the Cult",b="After Magthrull is slain, his tome is brought to Delgren at Maestra's Post. Delgren studies the warlock's writings to understand the network coordinating demonic activity across the borders of Darkshore and Ashenvale. The text offers vital intelligence on the shadowy conspirators directing the corruption spreading through northern Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who owns this tome?",a="Ilkrud Magthrull owns the tome. The powerful orc warlock is established among the demonic ruins of Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale.",al={"who is ilkrud magthrull","who wrote the tome","ilkrud magthrull"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the tome found?",a="The tome is recovered from Ilkrud Magthrull at Fire Scar Shrine, south of the Shrine of Aessina in Ashenvale.",al={"tome location","how to get the tome","where to find ilkrud"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want the book?",a="Delgren seeks to study Magthrull's writings and uncover the ties between local demon-worshipers and the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"why delgren wants the tome","what is in the tome","delgren book purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens after the tome is recovered?",a="At Maestra's Post, Delgren examines the text to decipher Magthrull's demonic communications and learn how to dismantle the cult's network.",al={"turn in tome","what does delgren do with the book"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome come from, and who made it?",a="The book contains the personal writings and dark research of Ilkrud Magthrull, a powerful orc warlock dwelling amidst the demonic corruption of Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Penned by the warlock himself, the volume compiles his dark spells and notes, kept close at hand until his downfall.",al={"who wrote ilkrud magthrull tome","ilkrud tome origin","where did the tome come from"},it="origin",add="5352c240"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you help Brother Delgren, a fellow warrior of the Holy Light who opposes shadow and corruption in Ashenvale's wilderness.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can study Magthrull's grimoire, which records dark bindings and the subjugation of voidwalkers and succubi at the tainted Fire Scar Shrine."},kw={"ashenvale","delgren the purifier","fire scar shrine","ilkrud magthrull","maestra's post","tome","tower of althalaxx","warlock"},rel={"quest:965","npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:fire-scar-shrine","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:ashenvale","topic:warlock"},src={"Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome","The Tower of Althalaxx (5)"}}
E["item:insane-scribbles"] = {t="item",n="Insane Scribbles",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, cultists carry Insane Scribbles torn from the Twilight Tome, a fragment of dark literature. The dancing script and warped designs unsettle the mind. Ancient forest protectors study the pages to learn the Twilight's Hammer's purpose.",h="In Darkshore, cultists carry Insane Scribbles torn from the Twilight Tome, a fragment of dark literature.",sec={{t="A Maddening Manuscript",b="The Twilight Tome can put a mortal's sanity at risk. Its script writhes across the parchment, and graceful scrollwork warps into grotesque images before the reader's eyes. Even one torn sheet, called Insane Scribbles, leaves its bearer lightheaded and disoriented. The writing makes little sense, yet the parchment hums with primal, deeply ancient magic tied to dark powers buried beneath Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Clues for the Ancients",b="Onu, the ancient who presides over the Grove of the Ancients, studies the scribbles for signs of what blights Darkshore. Onu recognizes the chaotic energy clinging to the parchment as the work of the Old Gods. So the defenders of Kalimdor seek to piece the scribbles together and learn why the Twilight's Hammer has gathered along the mist-shrouded shores.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens if you try to read these scribbles?",a="The text resists easy translation. As you look at the parchment, its letters swim and the designs around them twist into horrifying shapes. Soon, dizziness and mental exhaustion set in as you try to decipher them.",al={"reading insane scribbles","what does the text say","can you read the scribbles"},it="danger"},{q="Where were these scribbles torn from?",a="The scribbles were torn from the Twilight Tome, a foul grimoire kept by Twilight's Hammer cultists operating in Darkshore.",al={"where do scribbles come from","twilight tome origin"},it="origin"},{q="Who can understand or study the scribbles?",a="Onu, the Ancient of Lore, examines the recovered parchment. Drawing on centuries of knowledge, Onu senses the ancient, primal magic binding the ink and seeks to learn the cult's purpose in the region.",al={"who wants the scribbles","onu scribbles"},it="purpose"},{q="What kind of power radiates from the parchment?",a="The parchment pulses with chaotic, primal magic tied to the Old Gods, the dark deities worshipped by the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"what magic is in the scribbles","magic type"},it="power"},{q="What are the Insane Scribbles?",a="They are a single, maddening page torn from the dark text known as the Twilight Tome. The writing upon it swims, dances, and twists into grotesque shapes before your eyes, radiating a chaotic and primal magical aura that threatens to overwhelm your senses if you stare too long.",al={"what are insane scribbles","insane scribbles lore","what is this parchment"},it="identity",add="12486380"},{q="Why does Onu want the Insane Scribbles?",a="The ancient Onu senses the chaotic touch of the Old Gods woven into the parchment. He seeks to study these recovered writings in hopes of deciphering what the secretive Twilight's Hammer cult is plotting within the forests and shores of Darkshore.",al={"why does onu want insane scribbles","who wants the scribbles","why bring scribbles to onu"},it="why_wanted",add="b40c7e7e"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you may recognize the twisting script as a perilous assault of madness, set against the Light's clarity.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know relics of the Twilight's Hammer threaten Darkshore's ancient peace and sacred lands."},kw={"darkshore","insane scribbles","madness","old gods","onu","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:950","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Insane Scribbles","Return to Onu"}}
E["item:laird-s-response"] = {t="item",n="Laird's Response",z="darkshore",s="Along Teldrassil's shore, Laird sends Nessa Shadowsong a curious report. The fish there are larger and more plentiful than those along mainland Darkshore.",h="Along Teldrassil's shore, Laird sends Nessa Shadowsong a curious report.",sec={{t="A Matter of Scales and Roots",b="Laird compares the catches from both sides of the Veiled Sea. Fish from Teldrassil's coast are larger and more plentiful than those from Darkshore's mainland beaches.\n\nIn his reply to Nessa Shadowsong, Laird of Auberdine wonders if the newly planted World Tree's unusual presence and vitality are changing the sea life nearby. Travelers carry his letter across the water to Rut'theran Village, where the fisherfolk meet the news with wonder and quiet curiosity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Laird's Response?",a="Laird's Response is Laird's reply to Nessa Shadowsong's inquiry in Teldrassil. Laird is a fish merchant and curer in Auberdine.",al={"what is this item","lairds response letter","what is lairds response"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Laird writing to?",a="Laird writes to Nessa Shadowsong, a night elf who lives in Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil's southern base.",al={"who receives lairds response","who gets this letter","nessa laird letter"}},{q="What does the letter say about the fish?",a="Laird reports that fish from Teldrassil's shores are larger and more plentiful than those from mainland Darkshore. He suspects the World Tree may influence the nearby sea life.",al={"why are the fish big","fish difference darkshore teldrassil","what did laird find"}},{q="How does the message travel back to Rut'theran Village?",a="A carrier can take the regular ferry from Auberdine's docks or arrange a hippogryph flight with Caylais Moonfeather, the flight master.",al={"how to get back to nessa","ruttheran boat darkshore","auberdine ferry to nessa"},gp=true},{q="Where does Laird's Response come from, and who wrote it?",a="This written reply is penned by Laird, a resident of Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore. He writes it to address questions sent across the sea from Rut'theran Village regarding the local marine life.",al={"who wrote laird's response","where does lairds response come from","laird response origin"},it="origin",add="aee914ad"},{q="Why does Nessa want Laird's Response?",a="Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village eagerly awaits Laird's observations on how mainland catches compare to Teldrassil's waters. The strange, oversized fish around the great boughs of the World Tree have puzzled fishermen, and Laird's notes confirm that mainland Darkshore sees nothing like them, suggesting Teldrassil itself is transforming the local wildlife.",al={"why does nessa want lairds response","why is laird's response wanted","who wants laird's response"},it="why_wanted",add="fb1c817f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf tending Teldrassil's shores, you may find Laird's notes intriguing and unsettling. The young World Tree may already influence the nature around it."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fishing","laird","laird's response","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:6343","npc:laird","quest:6344","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Laird's Response","Return to Nessa"}}
E["item:letter-to-delgren"] = {t="item",n="Letter to Delgren",z="darkshore",s="Balthule Shadowstrike sends word from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. His letter warns Delgren the Purifier of the Dark Strand cult's demonic work and must reach Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",h="Balthule Shadowstrike sends word from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Warning Sent South",b="At the Tower of Althalaxx ruins, Balthule Shadowstrike watches the Dark Strand cult gather. He cannot destroy them alone, so he writes to Delgren the Purifier, his tutor in the Holy Light, and asks for aid. Their foul rites threaten more than Darkshore's coast. The letter must travel south through Darkshore into western Ashenvale. There, Delgren works with night elf Sentinels against demonic and undead threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Letter to Delgren?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike's sealed letter warns Delgren the Purifier of the Dark Strand cult's growing activity at the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"what is this letter","letter to delgren","balthule's letter"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin at Maestra's Post in western Ashenvale. He serves the Holy Light and aids the night elf Sentinels against demons and undead in the ancient forests. He also mentors Balthule in holy warfare.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","where is delgren"}},{q="Why is Balthule sending the letter so far away?",a="Balthule is Delgren's pupil and seeks his mentor's skill against demonic corruption. At Maestra's Post, Delgren can draw on his combat prowess and the local Sentinel forces to oppose the Dark Strand's dark rituals.",al={"why send to ashenvale","why not tell auberdine"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this letter need to be delivered?",a="Carry the letter south through Darkshore and across the border into Ashenvale. Maestra's Post lies along the western road.",al={"where do i take the letter","letter delivery location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where does the Letter to Delgren come from, and who wrote it?",a="The letter was penned by Balthule Shadowstrike, a night elf stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx. Seeking to purge the demonic corruption taking root in the ancient ruins, Balthule wrote this urgent missive to summon the aid and counsel of his mentor, the paladin Delgren the Purifier.",al={"who wrote letter to delgren","where did letter to delgren come from","who sent letter to delgren"},it="origin",add="8fccd45f"},{q="Why is the Letter to Delgren so important?",a="The missive contains critical intelligence exposing the Dark Strand cult's sinister operations at the Tower of Althalaxx. Delgren the Purifier has dedicated himself to helping the night elves cleanse demons and undead from the forests, and Balthule needs his mentor alerted immediately so they can confront the growing threat.",al={"why does delgren need the letter","why want letter to delgren","importance of letter to delgren"},it="why_wanted",add="99aa1720"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see a human paladin teaching a night elf the Holy Light. Their bond joins Kaldorei lands with the martial faith of the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see human champions and night elf Sentinels working together against demonic cults in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","delgren the purifier","letter to delgren","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:paladin","topic:sentinels"},src={"Letter to Delgren","The Tower of Althalaxx (3)"}}
E["item:lunar-fungus"] = {t="item",n="Lunar Fungus",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore's caves, druids gather Lunar Fungus to help heal sick deer. Mixed with Earthroot and water, it strengthens a healing salve.",h="In Darkshore's caves, druids gather Lunar Fungus to help heal sick deer.",sec={{t="Properties and Ecology",b="Lunar Fungus grows from Lunar Fungal Blooms in Darkshore's underground caverns. The Cenarion Circle values its power to strengthen remedies. Mixed with soothing water and common Earthroot, it lends strength to a salve that counters debilitating afflictions. Territorial moonkin frequent the damp caves, so gathering the fungus takes care.",sp=0},{t="A Lesson in Healing",b="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong has young druids gather Lunar Fungus as they study nature's healing arts. They learn how physical ingredients such as the fungus can counter poisons in local deer. By studying herbal remedies, initiates prepare to channel natural antidotes through shapeshifting and spiritual power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lunar Fungus used for?",a="Lunar Fungus strengthens a healing salve. Alanndarian Nightsong mixes it with Earthroot and clean water to treat sick deer in Darkshore.",al={"lunar fungus purpose","what does lunar fungus do","why collect lunar fungus"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Lunar Fungus grow?",a="Lunar Fungus grows from Lunar Fungal Blooms in caves east of Auberdine, in Darkshore. Irritable moonkin share these caverns and defend their territory from intruders.",al={"lunar fungus location","where to find lunar fungus","lunar fungus blooms"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who requires this fungus in Auberdine?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong asks students of the wild to gather Lunar Fungus as part of their training. The fungus goes into remedies for ailing forest animals.",al={"who needs lunar fungus","auberdine herbal quest"},it="target"},{q="Why do druid initiates have to gather physical herbs to cure poison?",a="Learning how physical antidotes work is a fundamental part of druidic education. Gathering herbs such as Lunar Fungus and seeing how they counter toxins teaches students the principles of healing before they learn to purge poison through spiritual magic.",al={"why druids gather herbs","druid poison cure training"}},{q="What is Lunar Fungus?",a="Lunar Fungus is a potent medicinal mushroom native to Darkshore. It flourishes inside dark caverns east of Auberdine, harvested from larger clusters known as lunar fungal blooms. Druids prize the fungus for its natural potency, utilizing its properties as an essential ingredient when brewing alchemical salves to treat poisoned wildlife.",al={"what is lunar fungus","lunar fungus info","about lunar fungus"},it="identity",add="2a41e7eb"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a young druid, you seek Lunar Fungus in Darkshore's caves as part of your early training in curative magic and healing poisoned wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you help tend corrupted woodland creatures around Auberdine with native remedies such as Lunar Fungus."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cure poison","darkshore","earthroot","lunar fungal bloom","lunar fungus"},rel={"quest:6123","quest:6125","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Lunar Fungus","Gathering the Cure (Alliance)"}}
E["item:mathystra-relic"] = {t="item",n="Mathystra Relic",z="darkshore",s="In northern Darkshore, Mathystra's ancient relics still bear traces of magic. The Twilight's Hammer has taken an interest in them.",h="In northern Darkshore, Mathystra's ancient relics still bear traces of magic.",sec={{t="Remnants of a Fallen Bastion",b="Mathystra once stood on the Kalimdor coast as a city and bastion of elven civilization. Before the Great Sundering, it was a proud place. Now toppled columns and cracked stones lie half-swallowed by brush and sea mist. Restless spirits and lurking beasts move among them.\n\nRelics from that age lie scattered through the ruins. Ten thousand years of neglect have worn them, yet traces of elven arcane craft remain. In careless hands, these relics are dangerous.",sp=0},{t="A Looming Peril",b="Onu, the ancient tree of lore, seeks Mathystra's relics. He learned that the Twilight's Hammer cult is trying to weaponize forgotten elven writings found at the Master's Glaive. The cult wants to wield ancient Kaldorei magic and hasten the return of its dark masters.\n\nOnu and Darkshore's guardians study the scattered remnants to learn the cult's intentions. They seek to keep Mathystra's fading power from serving dark ends.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Mathystra Relics?",a="The Mathystra Relics are fragments and artifacts from the ancient night elven city. They still bear traces of elven magical craft from before the Sundering, though thousands of years have passed.",al={"what is mathystra relic","elven relics mathystra","what are these relics"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these relics found?",a="The relics lie scattered among broken stones, fallen pillars, and tall grasses in the Ruins of Mathystra, in northern Darkshore.",al={"mathystra relic location","where to find relics","relic locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Mathystra Relics?",a="Onu, an Ancient of Lore, asks travelers to gather the relics for study. He lives at the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore.",al={"who needs relics","who do i bring relics to","onu relics"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer interested in them?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult studies ancient elven texts found at the Master's Glaive. It seeks to twist the elves' old magic and use it to summon its shadowy masters into the world.",al={"why twilight hammer wants relics","twilight's hammer mathystra"},it="motive"},{q="Where do the Mathystra Relics come from, and who made them?",a="These artifacts hail from the ancient night elven city of Mathystra, crafted long ago during an era when the great bastion shone across northern Darkshore. Left behind after the ancient settlement crumbled into ruin, they still hold lingering shards of elven magic.",al={"origin of mathystra relics","who made the mathystra relics","where are mathystra relics from"},it="origin",add="bddb4f1c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, recovering these relics helps guard dangerous ancient magic from the Twilight's Hammer. It also honors a city lost to the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you work with ancients like Onu to protect Darkshore's balance. You help keep forgotten magic from aiding dark summonings."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","mathystra","mathystra relic","onu","ruins of mathystra","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:951","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","zone:darkshore","quest:952","topic:twilight-s-hammer","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:944"},src={"Mathystra Relic","Mathystra Relics"}}
E["item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Middle of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="Off Darkshore, threshadons sank Gelkak Gyromast’s ship and scattered his key in three pieces. Greymist murlocs took the middle fragment.",h="Off Darkshore, threshadons sank Gelkak Gyromast’s ship and scattered his key in three pieces.",sec={{t="A Fragment in the Silt",b="Gelkak Gyromast’s winding key broke when threshadons dragged his ship beneath the waves. The gnome pirate came ashore with his belongings shattered on the rocky shoals. His specialized key was made for his mechanical first mate, but the wreck split it into three pieces scattered along the strand. Coastal beasts carried off the top and bottom pieces. Greymist murlocs prowling the Darkshore surf took the middle piece and kept it in their camps and among the wreckage they hold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Middle of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="Gelkak Gyromast needs the Middle of Gelkak's Key as one of three pieces. Joined to the top and bottom, it makes the key that reactivates his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","middle of gelkaks key use","why do i need this key"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did this key piece end up?",a="Greymist murlocs scavenged the middle fragment. It can be taken from raiders, oracles, netters, tidehunters, and other tribe members along Darkshore’s beaches and shipwrecks.",al={"who has the middle key","where to find middle of gelkak key","middle key dropped by"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was the key broken in the first place?",a="Aggressive threshadons sank Gelkak’s ship just offshore. The key broke into three pieces against the coastal rocks as the gnome washed ashore, and local scavengers carried the pieces away.",al={"how did the key break","why is it in pieces"},it="history"},{q="What is the Middle of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is the central section of a three-piece key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome pirate Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel sank off Darkshore's coast and he washed ashore, the key shattered on the jagged rocks, leaving this fragment among the wreckage.",al={"middle of gelkaks key","gelkaks key middle piece","what is this key piece"},it="identity",add="d3714d13"},{q="Where does the Middle of Gelkak's Key come from, and who made it?",a="The key belongs to Gelkak Gyromast, brought aboard his vessel before it was destroyed by threshadons off the coast of Darkshore. While Gelkak owned the key to operate his mechanical first mate, its precise maker is unknown.",al={"who made gelkaks key","origin of middle key piece","where did the key come from"},it="origin",add="55a592b4"},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast want the middle key piece?",a="Gelkak Gyromast needs this central piece alongside the other two fragments to reassemble the entire key. Without the complete key, he cannot wind up and reactivate his mechanical first mate to exact revenge on the local shoreline beasts.",al={"why does gelkak want this key","who wants gelkaks key","why is the key needed"},it="why_wanted",add="7cf04b1b"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how this custom mechanical component winds and operates a clockwork first mate, a display of gnomish ingenuity in pirate hands."},kw={"clockwork","darkshore","gelkak gyromast","greymist","middle of gelkak's key","murloc","shipwreck"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","quest:2078","item:top-of-gelkak-s-key","item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","topic:pirate"},src={"Middle of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:mist-veil-s-lockbox"] = {t="item",n="Mist Veil's Lockbox",z="darkshore",s="Off Darkshore, coastal murlocs ambushed the Mist Veil and sank it. The night elven vessel now rests beneath the waves with the captain’s log and personal effects in its lockbox.",h="Off Darkshore, coastal murlocs ambushed the Mist Veil and sank it.",sec={{t="Lost to the Depths",b="The night elven vessel Mist Veil sank while sailing toward Auberdine. Coastal murlocs overwhelmed it and its sister ship, the Silver Dawning. The captain perished, and the logbook and personal effects remain sealed in the lockbox in the flooded hold. Murlocs still surround the wreck.",sp=0},{t="Rest for the Crew",b="Surviving sailors reached Auberdine, but they still grieve for their lost vessel and commander. Gorbold Steelhand seeks Mist Veil's Lockbox so the captain's final effects can be honored and laid to rest. Recovering it from the flooded wreck may bring solace to the survivors on the mainland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Mist Veil's Lockbox?",a="Mist Veil's Lockbox holds the captain's log and personal effects. The captain perished when the ship sank, and the surviving crew in Auberdine want the mementos returned to honor their fallen leader.",al={"contents of mist veil lockbox","what does the lockbox hold","what is in the box"},it="item"},{q="How did the Mist Veil sink?",a="Coastal murlocs ambushed Mist Veil while it sailed toward Auberdine. They overwhelmed it and its sister ship, the Silver Dawning, and both vessels sank.",al={"why did the ship wreck","who sank mist veil","what happened to the mist veil"},it="history"},{q="Where is the lockbox found?",a="The lockbox lies underwater off Darkshore, north of Auberdine, in the flooded hull of the sunken Mist Veil. Murlocs fill the wreck.",al={"where is mist veil's lockbox","mist veil location","lockbox location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the lockbox recovered?",a="Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine seeks the lockbox for the surviving crew. He hopes to honor the fallen captain and bring them peace.",al={"who takes the lockbox","who gives the quest","gorbold lockbox quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Mist Veil's Lockbox?",a="It is the captain's chest recovered from the sunken vessel Mist Veil, resting beneath the waves off the coast of Darkshore north of Auberdine. Kept secure aboard the vessel until murlocs brought the ship down, it preserves the late night elf captain's logs, journals, and private effects from the ruined voyage.",al={"what is mist veil lockbox","mist veils lockbox","what is the lockbox"},it="identity",add="fab3edd7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can help return the fallen captain's logbook and lay their spirit to rest in the waters off Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can honor the fallen crew and help Auberdine's maritime community."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"quest:982","item:silver-dawning-s-lockbox","npc:gorbold-steelhand","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc"},src={"Mist Veil's Lockbox","Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["item:moonstalker-fang"] = {t="item",n="Moonstalker Fang",z="darkshore",s="Near Auberdine, travelers collect Moonstalker Fang for Wizbang Cranktoggle's sampling devices. The teeth come from Darkshore's moonstalkers.",h="Near Auberdine, travelers collect Moonstalker Fang for Wizbang Cranktoggle's sampling devices.",sec={{t="A Grinding Mechanism",b="Moonstalker Fangs come from saber cats that hunt along Darkshore’s forest fringes. Their long teeth can shear flesh and bone. Wizbang Cranktoggle, an eccentric gnome tinkerer, puts them to another use. North of Auberdine near the bridge, Buzzbox 323 grinds the durable fangs to dust for his ecological surveys.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Moonstalker Fangs come from?",a="Moonstalker Fangs come from Darkshore's moonstalkers, from runts and adults to sires, matriarchs, and the prowler Shadowclaw.",al={"where to get moonstalker fangs","who drops moonstalker fangs","fang source"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Moonstalker Fangs?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle needs six Moonstalker Fangs for Buzzbox 323, his automated monitoring device north of Auberdine near the river bridge.",al={"who needs fangs","what quest uses fangs","buzzbox 323 turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens to the fangs inside the machine?",a="Buzzbox 323's gears grind the hard fangs into fine dust for Wizbang's field experiments.",al={"what does buzzbox 323 do","why grind fangs"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Moonstalker Fang?",a="A Moonstalker Fang is a sharp, predatory canine tooth taken from the predatory moonstalkers roaming the misty forests of Darkshore. These nocturnal saber cats use their formidable fangs to hunt woodland prey, making them prized trophies and surprisingly durable material for peculiar local contraptions.",al={"moonstalker fang","what are moonstalker fangs","moonstalker teeth"},it="identity",add="fbcb9ad4"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Wizbang Cranktoggle's remote communication devices as gnome engineering. His slurred speech and unusual sampling choices still raise eyebrows.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need sharp senses to face moonstalkers, ambush predators that blend into Darkshore's dark canopy."},kw={"buzzbox 323","darkshore","moonstalker","moonstalker fang","shadowclaw","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1002","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},src={"Moonstalker Fang","Buzzbox 323 (quest)"}}
E["item:moonwell-water-tube"] = {t="item",n="Moonwell Water Tube",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, moonwell water carries purifying nature magic. The tube is used to test a mysterious red crystal among Darkshore’s eastern ridges.",h="In Auberdine, moonwell water carries purifying nature magic.",sec={{t="A Vessel of Purifying Waters",b="Water from Auberdine’s moonwell fills the tube. The sacred pool is tied to Elune and holds restorative, purifying magic. Even a little can be used against corruption or to test strange mystical forces.",sp=0},{t="Investigating the Red Crystal",b="Researchers prepared the tube to test a huge red crystal that appeared along Darkshore’s eastern cliffside. Felwood’s corrupted heights loom above the mountain wall, so they feared the crystal shared that dark origin. When blessed water runs over its facets, the opaque stone briefly turns transparent and reveals the mysteries within.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the water drawn from?",a="The water comes from the sacred moonwell in Auberdine, the night elf haven on Darkshore’s western coast.",al={"where do i fill the tube","water tube source","auberdine moonwell water"},it="origin"},{q="Why use moonwell water on the red crystal?",a="Moonwell water carries concentrated nature and lunar magic. Poured onto the strange red crystal, it tests the stone’s mystical nature and briefly clears its opaque surface.",al={"why moonwell water","purpose of the water tube","what does the water do"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the researchers concerned about the crystal?",a="The crystal lies beneath the eastern mountains that border Felwood. Its deep demonic taint has led scholars to fear the alien formation carries corruption down into Darkshore.",al={"why test the crystal","red crystal danger","felwood connection"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Moonwell Water Tube?",a="The Moonwell Water Tube is a simple glass vial filled with blessed water drawn directly from the moonwell in Auberdine. Moonwells hold potent, sacred magic nurtured by night elf druids and priestesses, making the liquid inside far more than ordinary spring water. Carrying it allows researchers to bring a small, concentrated measure of Elune's purifying power into the field to test unknown phenomena.",al={"what is moonwell water tube","moonwell water tube item","what is this tube of water"},it="identity",add="f51af5d3"},{q="Why is the Moonwell Water Tube needed?",a="Investigators in Auberdine need the Moonwell Water Tube to analyze an ominous red crystal embedded along Darkshore's eastern mountains. Because the crystal is suspected of sharing a dark connection to corrupted Felwood high above, the researchers believe pouring the moonwell's pure, potent magic over its surface will safely react with the stone and reveal its inner composition.",al={"why do i need moonwell water tube","why want moonwell water","purpose of moonwell water tube"},it="why_wanted",add="21e1d317"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, using blessed moonwell water to probe foreign corruption reflects their reliance on Elune’s grace to reveal hidden truths.",["class:Druid"]="Druids know moonwell water as a vital vessel of nature’s balance, suited to counter unnatural corruption."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","moonwell water tube","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","item:empty-water-tube","quest:4811","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},src={"Moonwell Water Tube","As Water Cascades"}}
E["item:mysterious-fossil"] = {t="item",n="Mysterious Fossil",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, Prospector Remtravel uncovers the Mysterious Fossil. The Explorers' League sends it across the sea for study.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, Prospector Remtravel uncovers the Mysterious Fossil.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="Prospector Remtravel uncovers an unusual fossil along Darkshore's wild coast. He arranges for dwarven scholars to receive it rather than leave it in the wilderness. In Darnassus, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sees an extraordinary find among the stones of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Ties Across the Ocean",b="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sees a likeness to a rare fossil once shown at an Explorers' League gathering in Ironforge. Archaeologist Flagongut studied that fossil and suspected it held power waiting to awaken. To confirm the new fossil's origins and learn what it may hold, Greywhisker sends it across the sea to Flagongut. Flagongut waits at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where was the Mysterious Fossil found?",a="Prospector Remtravel found the Mysterious Fossil while working along Darkshore's ancient northern coast.",al={"fossil location","where is it found","origin of fossil"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Explorers' League want this fossil?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sees a link between the fossil and Archaeologist Flagongut's research. Flagongut suspects such fossils may hold power that can be awakened.",al={"why do dwarves want it","explorers league interest","what does the fossil do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut researches for the Explorers' League and has studied similar petrified relics. He is staying at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor while awaiting an escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands.",al={"who is flagongut","flagongut location","where is flagongut"},it="people"},{q="Who is Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker is the Explorers' League's senior representative in Darnassus. Greywhisker oversees dwarven research and archaeological work across northern Kalimdor.",al={"greywhisker","who is greywhisker","darnassus dwarf archaeologist"},it="people"},{q="What is the Mysterious Fossil?",a="The Mysterious Fossil is an ancient relic unearthed in the wilderness of Darkshore by the dwarven Prospector Remtravel. Unlike mundane petrified remains, this specimen bears a striking resemblance to an extraordinary artifact previously showcased to the Explorers' League in Ironforge. Its peculiar nature suggests it holds dormant secrets or power waiting to be unlocked by an experienced archaeologist.",al={"mysterious fossil lore","what is this fossil","mysterious fossil info"},it="identity",add="dc519f37"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the fossil as another missing piece in the Explorers' League's search for ancient titan heritage and forgotten mysteries.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can trace the relic's route from field scouts in Darkshore to scholars in Darnassus and Menethil Harbor."},kw={"darkshore","explorers league","flagongut","greywhisker","menethil harbor","mysterious fossil","remtravel"},rel={"quest:729","npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","npc:archaeologist-flagongut","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern"},src={"Mysterious Fossil","The Absent Minded Prospector (3)","The Absent Minded Prospector (4)"}}
E["item:nessa-s-collection"] = {t="item",n="Nessa's Collection",z="darkshore",s="At Rut'theran Village, Nessa's Collection is bound for Laird in Auberdine, carrying proof of the great fish near Teldrassil's roots.",h="At Rut'theran Village, Nessa's Collection is bound for Laird in Auberdine, carrying proof of the great fish...",sec={{t="Bounty of the World Tree",b="Nessa Shadowsong lives in Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil's base. She gathered fish bones and scales to compare island sea life with mainland Kalimdor. Catches from the waters around the Great Tree grow to striking size. So Nessa sent proof across the sea to Laird, a fish merchant along Auberdine's docks. The parcel travels through Vesprystus, Rut'theran's hippogryph master, and shows Teldrassil's growing vitality.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Comparison",b="In Darkshore, Laird finds that these specimens far outsize their mainland counterparts. The collection holds jawbones nearly twice the size of those from fish native to the Darkshore coast. Its scales are as large as a clenched fist. For coastal night elves, the package shows how greatly Teldrassil's waters differ from northern Kalimdor's somber shores.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Nessa's Collection?",a="The collection holds fish bones and scales. Its jawbones are nearly twice the size of those from fish native to the Darkshore coast, and its scales are as large as a clenched fist. The fish came from the waters around Rut'theran Village.",al={"nessas collection contents","what is in the package","fish bones parcel"},it="item"},{q="Who is the collection being sent to?",a="Nessa sends the collection to Laird, a night elf fish vendor along Auberdine's docks in Darkshore.",al={"who gets nessas collection","who is laird","delivery destination"},it="target"},{q="Why did Nessa gather these fish specimens?",a="Nessa gathered the specimens to compare the large fish thriving around Teldrassil with marine life on mainland Kalimdor.",al={"why send fish bones","nessa fish comparison","bounty of teldrassil reason"},it="motive"},{q="How does the collection reach Auberdine?",a="You carry the package to Vesprystus, Rut'theran's hippogryph master. He arranges its passage across the water to Auberdine for delivery to Laird.",al={"how is it delivered","vesprystus delivery","hippogryph parcel"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is Nessa's Collection?",a="Nessa's Collection is a package of fish bones and scales gathered from the waters around Rut'theran Village. It represents the unusual marine bounty thriving at the base of the World Tree Teldrassil, packed securely for transport across the sea to the Kalimdor mainland.",al={"what is nessa's collection","nessas collection","nessa collection item"},it="identity",add="6bde19ac"},{q="Where does Nessa's Collection come from, and who made it?",a="The collection was assembled by Nessa Shadowsong, a night elf residing in Rut'theran Village at the southern base of Teldrassil. Drawing from the remarkably large catches brought in by the local island fishermen, she gathered choice specimens to send overseas.",al={"who made nessa's collection","where does nessa collection come from","nessa collection origin"},it="origin",add="eb414ab6"},{q="Why does anyone want Nessa's Collection?",a="A fish vendor named Laird in Auberdine awaits the specimens so he can study them. Nessa hopes to compare the astonishing size and vigor of Rut'theran's catches with mainland fish, and Laird is eager to examine jawbones twice their normal size and scales as large as a fist.",al={"why does laird want nessas collection","why deliver nessas collection","nessas collection purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="d01c5154"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see how the waters around Teldrassil differ from those of the mainland."},kw={"auberdine","fish bones","laird","nessa shadowsong","nessa's collection","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"quest:6341","quest:6342","npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Nessa's Collection","The Bounty of Teldrassil","Flight to Auberdine"}}
E["item:phial-of-scrying"] = {t="item",n="Phial of Scrying",z="darkshore",s="Across Darkshore, scouts reach Onu from perilous ground. Onu provides the Phial of Scrying, whose enchanted waters form a bowl for divination across the corrupted woodlands.",h="Across Darkshore, scouts reach Onu from perilous ground.",sec={{t="A Lens Across Darkshore",b="Scouts deep in Darkshore use the Phial of Scrying for long-distance divination. Its mystical waters form a temporary bowl on the ground. From perilous places such as the Master's Glaive, they can speak with Onu without returning to his grove.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cult",b="Onu gives scouts the phial to watch the Twilight's Hammer cultists. At the place where an ancient fallen master lies impaled by an enormous glaive, a scout opens a scrying link. The vision confirms that dark cultists gather around the ancient remains, seeking slivers of forgotten power that linger even in death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does the Phial of Scrying do?",a="Uncork the Phial of Scrying and a magical bowl forms on the ground. From the field, you can use it to contact Onu and speak with him across vast distances.",al={"use phial of scrying","scrying bowl function","what is this phial for"},it="power"},{q="Who provides the Phial of Scrying?",a="The ancient treant Onu gives the phial to scouts in Darkshore when he sends them south to reconnoiter the Master's Glaive.",al={"who gives phial of scrying","where do i get the phial"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the phial is lost or exhausted?",a="If you lose the phial or use it before finishing your mission, Onu can give you another while he meditates in Darkshore.",al={"lost phial of scrying","get another phial","replace phial"},gp=true},{q="Why is Onu scrying into the Master's Glaive?",a="Onu knows an old lord fell at the Master's Glaive, and asks you to search there for Twilight's Hammer cultists. Their purpose becomes clear as the investigation continues.",al={"why scry master's glaive","onu glaive mission"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Phial of Scrying?",a="The Phial of Scrying is an enchanted vessel containing mystical waters provided by the ancient of lore, Onu. When poured out in the field, it creates a temporary Scrying Bowl that serves as a magical conduit, allowing you to establish a direct spiritual link with the ancient across vast distances.",al={"what is phial of scrying","phial of scrying lore","scrying phial explained"},it="identity",add="92e56a99"},{q="Why does Onu want you to use the Phial of Scrying?",a="Onu asks you to search the Master's Glaive for Twilight's Hammer cultists. The phial lets you create a scrying bowl and speak with him after searching the site, without first returning to his grove.",al={"why use phial of scrying","why does onu want phial","why need phial of scrying"},it="why_wanted",add="16c85a4e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Darkshore, you know scrying waters help keep watch over holy woodlands encroached upon by alien cults.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you recognize scrying bowls as a blend of natural water and communion magic. They let the forest's wardens exchange whispers across corrupted ground."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","quest:960","subzone:master-s-glaive","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Phial of Scrying","The Master's Glaive (quest)"}}
E["item:scaber-stalk"] = {t="item",n="Scaber Stalk",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Barithras Moonshade seeks Scaber Stalks from a cave behind Cliffspring Falls.",h="In Darkshore, Barithras Moonshade seeks Scaber Stalks from a cave behind Cliffspring Falls.",sec={{t="A Rare Fungal Specimen",b="Behind Cliffspring Falls, Scaber Stalks grow in a cave among Darkshore's northeastern mountains. The pale mushrooms thrive in its damp, secluded passages, far from the forest growth above. Few gather them from so remote a place. Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine sends scouts into the darkness for the rare stalks.",sp=0},{t="A Shadow in the Falls",b="The Grove of the Ancients warned local night elves away from the cave where Scaber Stalks grow. Its tree-spirits sensed a dark, growing evil taking hold within Cliffspring Falls. Alchemists prize the stalks alongside rare Death Caps for experimental draughts. Those who seek them may encounter the malice gathering beneath the mountains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do Scaber Stalks grow?",a="Scaber Stalks grow in a damp cave behind Cliffspring Falls, among Darkshore's northeastern mountains.",al={"scaber stalk location","where are scaber stalks","scaber stalk cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Scaber Stalks?",a="Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine seeks Scaber Stalks and a Death Cap to brew a specialized potion.",al={"who uses scaber stalk","barithras moonshade mushrooms","who needs scaber stalks"},it="target"},{q="Why didn't Barithras Moonshade collect the stalks himself?",a="The Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras away after its spirits sensed a dangerous new evil taking refuge in the cave behind the waterfall.",al={"why not get them himself","barithras warning","cliffspring cave warning"},it="motive"},{q="What else grows alongside Scaber Stalks?",a="The cavern also shelters the lethal Death Cap mushroom, another rare specimen Barithras needs for his alchemical research.",al={"other mushrooms in the cave","death cap and scaber stalk","cliffspring mushrooms"},gp=true},{q="What is a Scaber Stalk?",a="A Scaber Stalk is a rare species of cave mushroom native to the shadowy cavern tucked behind Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. While subterranean fungi are common throughout northern Kalimdor, this particular variety flourishes in damp, dark grottos that harbor sinister energies.",al={"what is scaber stalk","scaber stalk info","scaber stalk mushroom"},it="identity",add="f5b84e96"},{q="Why does anyone want Scaber Stalks?",a="Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine seeks Scaber Stalks as a vital ingredient for brewing specialized potions. Because these potent fungi only grow in the secluded cave near Cliffspring Falls, herbalists and alchemists must rely on adventurous travelers to harvest them.",al={"why gather scaber stalk","scaber stalk use","what are scaber stalks for"},it="why_wanted",add="053fa90e"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="These underground stalks are not a commonly traded herb. They offer insight into how unusual cavern climates and encroaching shadows affect local fungi.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you heed the Grove of the Ancients' warning and approach these cave mushrooms with care. A corrupting presence festers near Cliffspring Falls."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","scaber stalk"},rel={"quest:947","item:death-cap","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:barithras-moonshade","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:952"},src={"Scaber Stalk","Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["item:sea-creature-bones"] = {t="item",n="Sea Creature Bones",z="darkshore",s="On Darkshore, Sea Creature Bones wash ashore with the bodies of massive sea creatures. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde gathers samples for the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where the cause of the strandings is under investigation.",h="On Darkshore, Sea Creature Bones wash ashore with the bodies of massive sea creatures.",sec={{t="A Portent on the Shore",b="Massive sea creatures now fling themselves onto Darkshore’s shallows and perish there. Giant threshers among them are far larger than those native to these waters. To the night elves, this sudden increase is an ominous portent. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde was sent by the Temple of the Moon to Auberdine to gather bones from the beached creatures. Hippogryphs carry the specimens to Darnassus for close examination.",sp=0},{t="Carrion and Scavengers",b="The immense carcasses draw local scavengers. Greymist murlocs gather to feed on the dead and dying creatures, then fiercely defend their feeding grounds. They are too weak to hunt beasts of this size. So investigators and adventurers must fight through their packs along Mist's Edge to recover bone fragments for study.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these creatures washing ashore?",a="The exact cause remains unknown. Occasional strandings are a natural hazard, but the sudden, dramatic increase alarms the priestesses of Elune, who consider it unnatural and have begun a formal investigation.",al={"why are threshers beaching","darkshore dead whales","why do creatures strand darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="Who wants these bones?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde gathers the bones in Auberdine for the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. Scholars and priestesses there hope to learn what is disturbing the sea.",al={"who takes the bones","who turns in sea creature bones","gwennyth darkshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Did the murlocs kill these giant beasts?",a="No. The Greymist murlocs are too weak to bring down marine beasts of that size. They gather in numbers to feed after the creatures wash ashore.",al={"did murlocs kill the thresher","greymist murlocs killed sea monster"}},{q="Where are the bones recovered from?",a="The bones come from massive carcasses stranded along Darkshore, especially on the sands south of Auberdine and along Mist's Edge.",al={"where to find sea creature bones","beached sea creature locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are these Sea Creature Bones?",a="They are skeletal remnants scavenged from the massive carcass of a beached sea beast—specifically an unusually large thresher—stranded along the misty coastline of Darkshore. Scavenged by local Greymist murlocs, these massive remains serve as vital physical evidence for researchers trying to understand why the ocean's behemoths are perishing on shore.",al={"what are sea creature bones","sea creature bones lore","giant bones darkshore"},it="identity",add="90a4db20"},{q="Where do the Sea Creature Bones come from?",a="These bones come from a colossal thresher, far larger than any expected in Darkshore's waters, that inexplicably hurled itself onto the beaches of Mist's Edge south of Auberdine. Rather than being crafted or slain by local predators, the bones belong naturally to deep-sea beasts that mysteriously drove themselves ashore to die.",al={"where do sea creature bones come from","origin of sea creature bones","beached sea creature origin"},it="origin",add="cb40613a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know these sudden mass strandings deeply trouble your people, who revere harmony in the natural world. They see the beachings as a dark omen that calls for the Temple of the Moon’s attention.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the inexplicable deaths of ancient marine predators as a sign of deep disturbance in the waters off Kalimdor. Such a disturbance troubles any guardian devoted to ecological balance."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","greymist murlocs","gwennyth bly'leggonde","mist's edge","sea creature bones","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","quest:4723","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc"},src={"Sea Creature Bones","Washed Ashore","Beached Sea Creature (1)"}}
E["item:sea-turtle-remains"] = {t="item",n="Sea Turtle Remains",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Sea Turtle Remains gather on the coast and beneath the waves. Researchers in Auberdine study the growing number of dead sea turtles.",h="Along Darkshore, Sea Turtle Remains gather on the coast and beneath the waves.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Strand",b="Giant sea creatures wash ashore along Darkshore, while others lie beneath the water near sunken wrecks. In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde gathers bone fragments and tissue from their bodies. The Temple of the Moon in Darnassus urgently asks for these samples. Its scholars and priestesses fear the creatures are fleeing an unnatural disturbance in the waters around Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="Recovering the remains is dangerous. Murloc tribes along the coast gather around the huge carcasses, picking their bones clean and nesting beside them. Scholars need fresh bone fragments and tissue before the scavengers destroy evidence that might explain the creatures' fatal migration.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are these remains used for?",a="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects remains for the scholars and priestesses at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. They seek to learn why so many ocean creatures are dying along Darkshore.",al={"why collect turtle remains","turtle bones use","sea turtle quest darkshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are sea turtles beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="Researchers have not found the cause, but they fear marine life is fleeing an unsettling presence in the waters around Teldrassil. These strandings point to widespread distress among marine life.",al={"why are turtles dying","turtle strandings darkshore","beached sea creatures"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these carcasses found?",a="Giant sea turtle carcasses lie along Darkshore's coast. Some rest in shallow water near sunken ships west of Auberdine, while others litter beaches surrounded by murloc encampments.",al={"turtle remains locations","where to find skeletal sea turtle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is studying these remains?",a="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects the remains and sends detailed reports to the Sisterhood of Elune at the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"who wants the remains","gwennyth blyleggonde"},it="people"},{q="What are these Sea Turtle Remains?",a="These remains are skeletal samples recovered from giant sea turtles that have washed ashore along Darkshore's coastline or died in its shallow waters. Though scavenged by local predators and murlocs, salvageable bones and tissue linger, offering physical clues about the creatures' final moments.",al={"what are sea turtle remains","sea turtle remains lore","what is sea turtle remains"},it="identity",add="dfe0d6c5"},{q="Where do the Sea Turtle Remains come from?",a="They are gathered directly from massive skeletal carcasses lying along the shores and coastal waters of Darkshore, including specimens near Auberdine. They are natural remains of marine beasts rather than crafted objects, left behind when dying turtles swim aground and perish.",al={"where do sea turtle remains come from","origin of sea turtle remains","source of sea turtle remains"},it="origin",add="be90da46"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The mass stranding of sea life off your ancestral coast is an ominous sign. The suspected cause lies in the waters encircling Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="The unnatural deaths of great sea creatures point to a deeper corruption disturbing nature's balance along the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea turtle","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea turtle remains","teldrassil","temple of the moon","washed ashore"},rel={"quest:3524","npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","quest:940","topic:murloc"},src={"Sea Turtle Remains","Washed Ashore (2)","Beached Sea Turtle (1)"}}
E["item:silver-dawning-s-lockbox"] = {t="item",n="Silver Dawning's Lockbox",z="darkshore",s="Off the Darkshore coast, Silver Dawning's Lockbox lies in a wreck north of Auberdine. Coastal murlocs sank the ship, and the box holds its captain's personal effects and ship log.",h="Off the Darkshore coast, Silver Dawning's Lockbox lies in a wreck north of Auberdine.",sec={{t="Sunken Remnants",b="The Silver Dawning was sailing toward Auberdine when coastal murlocs attacked. They drove the ship beneath the waves north of the harbor, and the captain died in the assault. The flooded hull still holds the captain's lockbox, with the ship's log and private belongings inside. Recovering them may bring some peace to the surviving crew ashore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Silver Dawning's Lockbox located?",a="The lockbox rests inside the submerged wreck of the Silver Dawning, on the ocean floor north of Auberdine off the Darkshore coast.",al={"lockbox location","where is silver dawning box","silver dawning wreck"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Silver Dawning?",a="Coastal murlocs attacked the Silver Dawning as it sailed toward Auberdine. They overwhelmed the ship, and it sank beneath the waves with its captain.",al={"why did silver dawning sink","silver dawning backstory","how did ship wreck"},it="history"},{q="What is inside the lockbox?",a="The lockbox holds the Silver Dawning captain's personal effects and sea log.",al={"silver dawning contents","what is in the box"},it="item"},{q="Who is seeking the lockbox?",a="Gorbold Steelhand, a dwarf stationed in Auberdine, asks swimmers to retrieve the lockbox from the wrecks so the fallen captain's surviving crew can honor their memory.",al={"who wants the lockbox","who gives the quest","turn in lockbox"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Silver Dawning's Lockbox?",a="It is the personal chest belonging to the late captain of the Silver Dawning. When the vessel was overrun and sunk by murlocs off the northern coast of Darkshore, the lockbox went down with the wreck. It holds the captain's log and surviving personal effects, resting deep underwater amidst the prowling creatures.",al={"what is silver dawnings lockbox","silver dawning chest lore","captain lockbox silver dawning"},it="identity",add="9cc39920"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The lockbox holds the final writings and belongings of a kaldorei captain who died defending their vessel off the shores of northern Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Gorbold Steelhand takes it upon himself to honor the fallen captains and return their belongings to their surviving mates."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"quest:982","npc:gorbold-steelhand","item:mist-veil-s-lockbox","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},src={"Silver Dawning's Lockbox","Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["item:stone-of-relu"] = {t="item",n="Stone of Relu",z="darkshore",s="In the Wetlands, Stone of Relu is lost after raptors ambush Archaeologist Flagongut. He believes it can unlock secrets within ancient fossils.",h="In the Wetlands, Stone of Relu is lost after raptors ambush Archaeologist Flagongut.",sec={{t="A Key to Ancient Relics",b="The Explorers' League uncovered Stone of Relu. Archaeologist Flagongut believes the artifact can decipher prehistoric fossils gathered from Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. He plans to study his Wetlands specimens and the fossil Prospector Remtravel unearthed in Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Lost in the Marshes",b="On a Wetlands road, Archaeologist Flagongut was traveling to meet Prospector Whelgar when mottled raptors ambushed him. In the scramble, the relic was lost, then swallowed by one of the beasts. Now the League seeks the marsh raptors, hoping to cut the ancient stone from their gullets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Stone of Relu?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut seeks Stone of Relu, an ancient artifact he believes can unlock the hidden mysteries and power within prehistoric fossils.",al={"stone of relu","what is this stone","relu artifact"},it="identity"},{q="How did the stone end up inside a raptor?",a="Mottled raptors attacked Archaeologist Flagongut on a Wetlands road as he traveled to meet Prospector Whelgar. In the chaos, one beast swallowed the lost stone.",al={"why do raptors have it","who dropped the stone","how was it lost"}},{q="What is Flagongut planning to do with the stone?",a="Flagongut plans to use Stone of Relu on his recovered fossil and the fossil Prospector Remtravel found in Darkshore. He hopes to decipher and release their latent magical secrets.",al={"what does flagongut want","stone of relu purpose"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the Explorers' League, Stone of Relu may help piece together the origins of ancient life and the world's forgotten legacy.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance expeditions in Menethil Harbor rely on recovered artifacts like Stone of Relu to justify difficult excavations across the perilous marshlands."},kw={"archaeologist flagongut","explorers league","fossil","mottled raptor","prospector whelgar","stone of relu","wetlands"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","quest:729","item:flagongut-s-fossil","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore"},src={"Stone of Relu","The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["item:strangely-marked-box"] = {t="item",n="Strangely Marked Box",z="darkshore",s="On Darkshore, Strangely Marked Box runes point toward naga cargo washed ashore on dead sea turtles. Their presence hints that the turtles did not come ashore by chance.",h="On Darkshore, Strangely Marked Box runes point toward naga cargo washed ashore on dead sea turtles.",sec={{t="Trophies of the Deep",b="Dead sea turtles and other sea creatures wash onto Darkshore’s beaches. Some bear broken harnesses and carriages strapped to their shells. Among the wreckage lie sealed boxes marked with foreign, winding runes. Greymist murlocs shelter in hollow ribs and broken wagons, feeding on the carcasses and guarding what remains.",sp=0},{t="Evidence of Naga Expansion",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a researcher for the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine, recognizes the markings. The script and carriages belong to the naga, who use giant turtles to carry supplies and war equipment onto land. The boxes place naga along the northern shores and suggest they may be driving their mounts south toward Ashenvale. Auberdine's priesthood sends the relics to Darnassus for study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Strangely Marked Box found?",a="The box lies in an abandoned carriage strapped to a dead sea turtle on Darkshore's coast. Greymist murlocs feed near the carcasses and guard what remains.",al={"where to find strangely marked box","box location","turtle carriage box"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who made the Strangely Marked Box?",a="The naga made the box and its inscriptions. They strap carriages to living sea turtles to carry provisions, arms, and equipment from the ocean depths to Kalimdor's shores.",al={"who made the box","markings on box","box runes","what are the markings"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this box in Auberdine?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a researcher for the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine, collects the box to study the strange beachings and the naga threat.",al={"who do i turn this in to","box turn in","who wants the box"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Why were the sea turtles carrying these boxes?",a="The naga use giant sea turtles to carry supplies and war equipment onto land, with harnesses and carriages strapped to their backs. Gwennyth suspects one turtle was killed while heading south, perhaps toward Ashenvale.",al={"why do turtles have boxes","turtle carriages","why are turtles strapped"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens to the box after giving it to Gwennyth?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde sends the box and coastal survey findings to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where the night elf leadership can study the naga's reach.",al={"where does the box go","box sent to darnassus"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Strangely Marked Box?",a="It is a piece of cargo discovered inside a buckled carriage strapped to the shell of a beached sea turtle along Darkshore's coastline. Marked with peculiar runes, the crate serves as physical evidence of organized maritime transport along the coast, abandoned after the carrying creature perished and was subsequently overrun by scavengers.",al={"what is the marked box","what is strangely marked box","strangely marked box item"},it="identity",add="981461f5"},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the Strangely Marked Box?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde seeks the box on behalf of the Temple of the Moon to investigate why massive sea creatures are beaching themselves upon Darkshore. Deciphering the markings confirms that the turtles were harnessed and used as beasts of burden by hostile naga transporting supplies inland, clues she forwards directly to scholars in Darnassus.",al={"why does gwennyth want the box","why deliver strangely marked box","marked box purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="b4ce745f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Naga supply boxes lashed to native sea turtles along Darkshore warn the kaldorei that their ancient, mutated kin are pushing ashore from the Great Sea.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you help the Temple of the Moon's scholars in Auberdine secure shore relics as they work to protect the coast from marine corruption."},kw={"auberdine","carriage","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","naga","sea turtle","strangely marked box"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:4722","topic:naga","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Strangely Marked Box","Beached Sea Turtle (2)","Beached Sea Turtle (4)"}}
E["item:talisman-of-corruption"] = {t="item",n="Talisman of Corruption",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Xabraxxis turns the Blackwood furbolgs against their former allies with the Talisman of Corruption. He keeps it in his personal pouch, and its magic binds the tribe to fel madness.",h="In Darkshore, Xabraxxis turns the Blackwood furbolgs against their former allies with the Talisman of...",sec={{t="A Conduit of Madness",b="In Auberdine, the night elves seek the cause of the Blackwood furbolgs’ turn against their former allies. Thundris Windweaver found that satyrs brought about the tribe’s fall. Talismans like this carry corrupting sorcery through the wilderness. They taint food and twist peaceful forest spirits into frenzied beasts. Their fel magic grips the minds and wills of local tribes.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Grip",b="To draw out Xabraxxis, you cleanse samples of furbolg food with blessed moonwell water. The purification enrages the overseer. When Xabraxxis is slain, his demon bag yields the talisman. You bring it to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, where the Kaldorei can neutralize its foul emanations and study how to undo the demonic affliction in the forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Talisman of Corruption?",a="Xabraxxis uses the Talisman of Corruption to channel foul magic through the Blackwood furbolgs’ food and minds in Darkshore.",al={"what is talisman of corruption","talisman purpose","what does the talisman do"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries the talisman?",a="Xabraxxis, the satyr overseeing the northern Blackwood furbolg camp near the Cliffspring River, carries the talisman in his demon bag.",al={"who drops talisman of corruption","where to find talisman of corruption","how to get talisman"},it="origin"},{q="How do you draw out the owner of the talisman?",a="You gather the furbolgs’ fruit, grain, and nuts, then mix them with moonwell water in a cleansing bowl. Place the offering by the bonfire near the river. The cleansing enrages Xabraxxis until he attacks.",al={"how to summon xabraxxis","how to find xabraxxis","summon satyr darkshore"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the talisman after it is recovered?",a="You bring the talisman to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. He secures it for disposal and studies how to free the furbolgs permanently from demonic corruption.",al={"who do i give the talisman to","turn in talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver talisman"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei of Auberdine, recovering the talisman helps free your ancestral furbolg allies from demonic degradation and heal the land.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see devices like the talisman as a perversion of the natural order. They twist sacred beasts into feral pawns of the Burning Legion’s leftover minions."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","furbolg","satyr","talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4763","topic:satyr","topic:furbolg","item:empty-cleansing-bowl","quest:4761","quest:4762","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},src={"Talisman of Corruption","The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["item:tharnariun-s-hope"] = {t="item",n="Tharnariun's Hope",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Tharnariun Treetender seeks a cure for the sick thistle bears. His trap calms them long enough to bring them to his camp.",h="In Darkshore, Tharnariun Treetender seeks a cure for the sick thistle bears.",sec={{t="A Gentle Snare",b="Tharnariun Treetender made a trap to calm the sick thistle bears. A mysterious affliction has made them more and more frenzied and violent across Darkshore. He hopes to cure them instead of seeing them killed. Set on the ground, Tharnariun's Hope shines with a soothing light. A rabid thistle bear that crosses it grows calm for a time and can follow a traveler back to Tharnariun's camp for treatment.",sp=0},{t="The Elusive Remedy",b="Tharnariun Treetender's healing magic cannot save a captured bear. The trap quiets the maddened animal without harming it, but the corruption is more vicious than he expected. When he directs his healing into the bear, his magic clashes with the infection. The animal collapses and dies. Though his first attempt ends in heartbreak, Tharnariun remains determined to learn the true nature of the forest's sickness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Tharnariun's Hope do?",a="Tharnariun's Hope calms a rabid thistle bear for a time. Set on the forest floor, it casts a field of light that lets a traveler lead the bear peacefully back to Tharnariun Treetender.",al={"tharnariuns hope use","how does the trap work","what is this trap"},it="power"},{q="Why does Tharnariun want a live bear captured?",a="Tharnariun believes the sickness afflicting Darkshore's wildlife can be cured instead of answered with slaughter. He needs a living bear to test his cleansing remedies.",al={"why capture thistle bear","why catch a rabid bear","what does tharnariun want"},it="motive"},{q="Can you get another trap if you lose it?",a="Yes. Tharnariun says his hope is eternal. If the trap is triggered in vain or lost in the wild, return to him for another.",al={"lost tharnariuns hope","failed trap","trap disappeared"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the bear once it is brought back?",a="When the bear reaches Tharnariun, he casts healing magic to purge the corruption. The sickness overwhelms the beast, and it dies within moments.",al={"does the bear survive","can tharnariun cure the bear","bear dies at tharnariun"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Tharnariun's Hope?",a="Tharnariun's Hope is an enchanted snare devised by Tharnariun Treetender. When laid upon the ground, it radiates a calming light capable of temporarily pacifying the afflicted, rabid thistle bears wandering Darkshore. The soothing enchantment makes a frenzied beast gentle and willing to follow you back to Auberdine.",al={"what is tharnariuns hope","tharnariun hope item","tharnariun trap"},it="identity",add="820181a1"},{q="Where does Tharnariun's Hope come from, and who made it?",a="The trap was crafted and enchanted by Tharnariun Treetender, a night elf naturalist stationed in Darkshore. Horrified by the mysterious sickness driving the forest's wildlife into madness, he fashioned this device using gentle magic to subdue infected beasts without causing them further harm.",al={"who made tharnariuns hope","origin of tharnariun's hope","tharnariun trap creator"},it="origin",add="88ba9e19"},{q="Why does anyone want Tharnariun's Hope?",a="Tharnariun needs the trap used to capture a living, rabid thistle bear so he can study the corruption ravaging Darkshore. Ordinary hunting would only slay the beast, but this snare pacifies the animal long enough for you to lead it safely into his care in hopes of discovering a cure.",al={"why use tharnariun's hope","why need tharnariun trap","purpose of tharnariuns hope"},it="why_wanted",add="c80e933b"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see Tharnariun's trap as a choice to preserve corrupted beasts while there is still a chance to redeem them.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the thistle bears are beloved in Darkshore. Their sickness makes Tharnariun's trap a sign of desperate compassion."},kw={"darkshore","plagued lands","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun","tharnariun's hope","thistle bear","trap"},rel={"quest:2118","npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2139","zone:darkshore"},src={"Tharnariun's Hope","Plagued Lands"}}
E["item:thresher-eye"] = {t="item",n="Thresher Eye",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Wizbang Cranktoggle needs Thresher Eyes for his Buzzboxes. He uses them to repair Buzzbox 411, a communication machine on the beach north of Auberdine.",h="Along Darkshore, Wizbang Cranktoggle needs Thresher Eyes for his Buzzboxes.",sec={{t="Ecological Samples for Gnomish Gadgets",b="Darkshore Threshers hunt the surf and outer shallows off Darkshore. They threaten local fishermen and travelers, and their large eyes have drawn the interest of Wizbang Cranktoggle. The gnome engineer is stationed nearby and fond of crawler wine. He needs the eyes to repair Buzzbox 411, a communication machine on the beach north of Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="The Purpose of the Eyes",b="Wizbang does not explain how slimy eyes repair delicate machinery. They might serve as crude lenses, chemical agents, or biological gears. Whatever the method, three eyes placed in Buzzbox 411's maintenance hatch restore its communication link. Wizbang then sends supplies through transmissions choked with static.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Thresher Eyes come from?",a="Thresher Eyes come from Darkshore Threshers and Elder Darkshore Threshers in the ocean off Darkshore, especially near Auberdine.",al={"where do thresher eyes drop","how to get thresher eye","thresher eye source"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Thresher Eyes?",a="Wizbang wants Thresher Eyes for his Buzzboxes. He uses them to repair Buzzbox 411, a gnomish communication machine on the shoreline north of Auberdine. Placing the eyes in its hatch restores the machine's systems.",al={"why need thresher eyes","buzzbox 411 eyes","what are thresher eyes for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does an eye fix a machine?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle does not explain how an eye repairs a machine. Buzzbox 411 accepts the eyes and powers back on, though whether he uses their retinas for focusing or builds with their organic parts remains unclear.",al={"why eyes for a machine","gnome machine biological parts"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Buzzbox 411?",a="Buzzbox 411 is one of several communication and monitoring devices Wizbang Cranktoggle placed across Darkshore. When loaded with requested materials, it lets him communicate remotely and dispense supplies.",al={"buzzbox 411 purpose","who built buzzbox 411"},it="target"},{q="What is a Thresher Eye?",a="A Thresher Eye is the ocular organ harvested from the predatory threshers swimming in the coastal waters off Darkshore. While mundane biological matter to most, the eccentric tinkerer Wizbang Cranktoggle finds bizarre mechanical or chemical utility for them in repairing his far-speaking buzzbox machines.",al={"what is thresher eye","thresher eyes"},it="identity",add="eb2ee385"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizbang's use of animal parts to mend mechanical relays is an unusual example of gnomish engineering.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see a wilder edge of gnomish ingenuity in Wizbang Cranktoggle. He tinkers with field machinery in Kalimdor's wilderness between cups of crawler wine."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 411","darkshore","darkshore thresher","thresher eye","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1001","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:983","topic:gnome"},src={"Thresher Eye","Buzzbox 411 (quest)"}}
E["item:top-of-gelkak-s-key"] = {t="item",n="Top of Gelkak's Key",z="darkshore",s="A giant foreststrider bears the Top of Gelkak's Key into the woods near Darkshore. The piece broke from a mechanical key that belongs to the shipwrecked gnome Gelkak Gyromast.",h="A giant foreststrider bears the Top of Gelkak's Key into the woods near Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Shattered Mechanism",b="Threshadons struck Gelkak Gyromast's ship off Darkshore and dragged it beneath the waves. Gelkak washed ashore with the winding key for his mechanical first mate. The coastal rocks broke the key into three pieces.\n\nBefore the dizzy pirate could gather his wits, beasts scavenged the wreckage. A giant foreststrider carried the ornate upper piece into the woods.",sp=0},{t="Restoring the First Mate",b="Gelkak Gyromast needs the key to wind and activate his mechanical first mate. He means to use the construct against the local wildlife. Shore murlocs took the middle piece, and reef crawlers took the bottom one. With all three fragments, Gyromast can mend the key and bring his construct to life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Top of Gelkak's Key used for?",a="The Top of Gelkak's Key is one of three broken pieces Gelkak Gyromast needs to repair his mechanical winding key. Once assembled, the key can reactivate his mechanical first mate.",al={"what does gelkaks key do","use of top of gelkaks key","gelkak key purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did a foreststrider get this piece of the key?",a="When Gelkak was shipwrecked off Darkshore, the key broke against the rocks. Beasts scavenged the wreckage, and a giant foreststrider carried the upper brass piece into the woods northeast of the shore.",al={"why do tallstriders have the key","who took gelkak key top","how did foreststrider get key"}},{q="Where are the other pieces of the key?",a="Greymist murlocs near the shipwreck took the middle section. Crabs scouring the tideline carried off the bottom section.",al={"where are other key parts","middle and bottom of gelkak key","gelkak key fragments"},gp=true},{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is a gnome pirate marooned on Darkshore after threshadons wrecked his vessel. Stranded and furious, he plots revenge against the coastal creatures.",al={"who is gelkak","gelkak gyromast lore"},it="people"},{q="What is the Top of Gelkak's Key?",a="It is one of three broken fragments of a specialized key belonging to the shipwrecked gnome Gelkak Gyromast. When his vessel was brought down off the coast of Darkshore, the key shattered upon the rocky shoreline. This particular upper segment was scavenged by the local giant foreststriders wandering the nearby woods.",al={"top of gelkaks key","what is gelkaks key top","gelkaks key fragment"},it="identity",add="7697c1f6"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The key winds and activates a clockwork automaton. Its sturdy design shows the ingenuity of gnome tinkers.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may find a fellow gnome surviving a shipwreck through eccentricity and clockwork contraptions familiar and endearing."},kw={"darkshore","first mate","foreststrider","gelkak","gyromast","key","pirate","retrieval"},rel={"quest:2098","npc:gelkak-gyromast","item:middle-of-gelkak-s-key","item:bottom-of-gelkak-s-key","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate","topic:murloc"},src={"Top of Gelkak's Key","Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["item:worn-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Worn Parchment",z="darkshore",s="At the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, cultists gather and leave scraps of worn parchment in their belongings.",h="At the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, cultists gather and leave scraps of worn parchment in their...",sec={{t="Fragments of a Sinister Plot",b="North along Darkshore’s mist-shrouded coast, dark spellcasters and their followers have seized the ruined Tower of Althalaxx. Dark Strand Fanatics patrol the grounds and carry scraps of worn parchment among their belongings. One scrap holds only scattered writing and strange symbols. Gathered together, the fragments reveal an organization called the Cult of the Dark Strand.",sp=0},{t="Unmasking the Cult",b="From a nearby overlook, scout Balthule Shadowstrike watches the tower. He uses the gathered parchments to assess the threat for Delgren the Purifier and the sentinels in Auberdine. The texts confirm that the warlocks are organized under a cult, not independent outcasts. What the cult plans remains unknown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who carries these worn parchments?",a="Dark Strand Fanatics carry the parchments among their belongings. They are cultist foot soldiers encamped around the perimeter of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore.",al={"who drops worn parchment","where to get worn parchment","worn parchment source"},it="people"},{q="What is written on the parchments?",a="Each parchment holds cryptic fragments of ritual notes and orders. Gathered and deciphered by Balthule Shadowstrike, they reveal the name and existence of the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"what does worn parchment say","worn parchment text","parchment meaning"},it="item"},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike collecting them?",a="Delgren the Purifier tasked Balthule with watching the Tower of Althalaxx. Balthule needs the writings to learn why warlocks have gathered at the ruins, assess the danger to Darkshore, and report back.",al={"who wants worn parchment","balthule quest","why collect parchments"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Cult of the Dark Strand?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand is a secretive gathering of cultists and warlocks based in the ruins of Althalaxx. Even seasoned scouts like Balthule Shadowstrike had never encountered the order before finding these writings.",al={"dark strand cult","who are dark strand","cult of dark strand"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Worn Parchment?",a="These worn parchments are written scraps and scrolls carried by the Dark Strand cultists camped around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. When pieced together, their contents reveal the shadowy dealings and presence of a warlock sect known as the Cult of the Dark Strand.",al={"what is worn parchment","worn parchment lore","worn parchment info"},it="identity",add="83151644"},{q="Where does the Worn Parchment come from, and who made it?",a="The parchments originate from the Dark Strand Fanatics and warlocks who have congregated around the ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx. The cultists carry these written scraps as part of their communications and mysterious rites, though the exact author of each scroll remains unknown.",al={"where does worn parchment come from","who made worn parchment","who wrote worn parchment"},it="origin",add="4385c03d"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you read of the Dark Strand’s organized coven operating in secret on night elf lands. They wield fel and shadow beyond the gaze of both the Alliance and Horde.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know dark spellcasters and demonic corruption near ancient ruins like Althalaxx desecrate Darkshore’s sacred wilderness."},kw={"althalaxx","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","fanatics","worn parchment"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","quest:965","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:warlock"},src={"Worn Parchment","The Tower of Althalaxx (2)"}}
E["npc:alanndarian-nightsong"] = {t="npc",n="Alanndarian Nightsong",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong tends to Darkshore's sickened wildlife. She works with travelers to ease the afflictions spreading through the region, especially among its deer.",h="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong tends to Darkshore's sickened wildlife.",sec={{t="A Caretaker in Auberdine",b="From the coastal settlement of Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong watches over Darkshore's wildlife. Taints in the soil and water have left creatures of the ancient woods sick and strangely aggressive. She seeks ways to ease their suffering and restore their strength.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Stricken and Sick",b="Alanndarian Nightsong searches for what is making Darkshore's animals ill. She gathers plants and studies the region's water sources, then prepares salves and healing draughts. Travelers help her apply these cures to ailing creatures, hoping to stop the corruption from overtaking the wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong cares for Darkshore's afflicted wildlife from Auberdine. She seeks herbal cures for the unnatural sickness spreading along the coast.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","alanndarian nightsong lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Alanndarian Nightsong be found?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong lives in Auberdine, the main night elf settlement on Darkshore's foggy coast.",al={"alanndarian location","where is alanndarian","find alanndarian nightsong"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does she ask adventurers to perform?",a="Alanndarian asks travelers to find sources of sickness, gather healing ingredients, and give remedies to ailing animals such as the sickly deer.",al={"alanndarian quests","auberdine sick animal quests","what does alanndarian want"},it="purpose"},{q="Is she related to other Nightsongs?",a="Other night elves share the Nightsong name, but no known tie confirms Alanndarian is related to them. She devotes her days to Darkshore's wilderness.",al={"nightsong family","master nightsong relation","falara nightsong"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the creatures in Darkshore sick?",a="Polluted water from Cliffspring Falls, Darkshore's main drinking water source, has sickened deer across the region. Alanndarian suspects a greater taint is at work as well.",al={"why are darkshore animals sick","corrupted striders darkshore","darkshore blight"},it="threat"},{q="Can she train tallstrider pets?",a="Though rumor credits her with great knowledge of striders, Alanndarian does not train hunters' tamed pets. Her attention remains on wild populations.",al={"tallstrider trainer","strider training auberdine","train my strider"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Alanndarian Nightsong on?",a="She stands firmly with the night elves of Darnassus and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, she works directly to protect the wildlife of Darkshore and assists travelers loyal to the Kaldorei cause.",al={"alanndarian nightsong faction","alanndarian nightsong alliance or horde"},it="side",add="04324614"},{q="What does Alanndarian Nightsong want?",a="Alanndarian is dedicated to understanding and reversing the strange afflictions plaguing the local fauna. She seeks aid in uncovering the source of these sicknesses and gathering the necessary ingredients to craft remedies that will heal Darkshore's corrupted creatures.",al={"alanndarian nightsong goal","what is alanndarian trying to do"},it="wants",add="d3838107"},{q="Why is Alanndarian Nightsong in Darkshore?",a="She makes her home in the port town of Auberdine to watch over the wilderness of Darkshore. From here, she keeps a close eye on the creeping corruption unsettling the region's wildlife and coordinates efforts to restore balance to the land.",al={"why is alanndarian in auberdine","alanndarian darkshore reason"},it="why_here",add="209c0886"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving in Auberdine, Alanndarian helps explain the fragile state of northern Kalimdor's wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Alanndarian's care for the forest and its corrupted wildlife reflects kaldorei ideals of preservation.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Alanndarian's search for taints in the water and her work to heal poisoned creatures across Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can help Alanndarian track wild striders and distressed game by reading the beasts' signs."},kw={"alanndarian","auberdine","cure","darkshore","kaldorei","nightsong","strider","wildlife"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6124","quest:6123","quest:6122","quest:2178","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},src={"Alanndarian Nightsong"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-flagongut"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Flagongut",z="darkshore",s="At Menethil Harbor, Archaeologist Flagongut keeps in touch with field researchers across the Great Sea. The dwarven scholar of the Explorers' League is staying at the Deepwater Tavern on his way to the Whelgar Excavation Site.",h="At Menethil Harbor, Archaeologist Flagongut keeps in touch with field researchers across the Great Sea.",sec={{t="A Scholar in Port",b="Archaeologist Flagongut rests over a mug at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Like many members of Ironforge's Explorers' League, he traveled west across Khaz Modan to aid discoveries near the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. Far from the high halls of the library, he keeps ties with field researchers, studying lost relics and reports brought across the Great Sea from distant expeditions.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Field",b="Dwarven curiosity reaches beyond one continent. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus sends Flagongut a mysterious fossil unearthed in Darkshore by the absent-minded Prospector Remtravel. Flagongut is amazed. He once brought a similar fossil to the Explorers' League's annual conference in Ironforge, convinced its power could somehow be unlocked.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Flagongut is a dwarven researcher with the Explorers' League, staying at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. He reviews excavation reports there and keeps in touch with dig sites.",al={"who is flagongut","flagongut npc","archaeologist flagongut lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Flagongut at the Deepwater Tavern?",a="Flagongut came to Menethil Harbor on his way to the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. While in port, he uses the tavern as a base for mail, incoming artifacts, and correspondence from abroad.",al={"why is flagongut in menethil","flagongut location","what is flagongut doing here"},it="why_here"},{q="How is Flagongut connected to Darkshore?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus sends Flagongut Prospector Remtravel's mysterious fossil from Darkshore. It resembles one Flagongut brought to an Explorers' League conference, and he believes such fossils hold a power that can be unlocked.",al={"flagongut darkshore connection","why darkshore quest in wetlands"},it="ties"},{q="What organization does he belong to?",a="Flagongut belongs to the Explorers' League, King Magni Bronzebeard's royal society. It seeks the ancient origins, relics, and history of the dwarven race across Azeroth.",al={"flagongut faction","flagongut explorers league"},it="allies"},{q="Whose side is Archaeologist Flagongut on?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is aligned with Ironforge and the Alliance. As an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League, his loyalties lie with his kin and their scholarly mission to excavate and catalog ancient relics across the known world.",al={"flagongut faction","who does flagongut work for","flagongut allegiance"},it="side",add="c473457f"},{q="What does Archaeologist Flagongut want?",a="Flagongut wants to unlock the secrets of his fossils. On the road to Whelgar's Excavation Site, raptors swallowed the Stone of Relu, the relic he believes is the key, and he needs help recovering it along with his original fossil, now held by Prospector Whelgar, so he can study them beside Remtravel's fossil from Darkshore.",al={"flagongut goal","what does flagongut need","why talk to flagongut"},it="wants",add="af05d80a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see the Explorers' League's reach in Flagongut's work at a seaside tavern, where he studies Titan secrets.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Flagongut linking the night elf lands of Darkshore with the eastern Alliance strongholds of Khaz Modan."},kw={"archaeologist","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","flagongut","menethil harbor","remtravel","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","quest:729","zone:wetlands","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Flagongut"}}
E["npc:archaeologist-hollee"] = {t="npc",n="Archaeologist Hollee",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Archaeologist Hollee follows dwarven research across Darkshore. Ancient ruins draw Ironforge scholars to the coast, where she keeps in touch with prospectors seeking relics and unusual geological formations.",h="In Auberdine, Archaeologist Hollee follows dwarven research across Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Scholar in Kaldorei Lands",b="Archaeologist Hollee works from Auberdine, among the night elves who guard and settle Darkshore. She is a regional contact for surveyors and expedition teams crossing the wilderness. The Explorers' League sends its people across the sea to uncover traces of ancient history, and Darkshore's ruins give them ground to study.",sp=0},{t="Keeping Tabs on Remtravel",b="Prospector Remtravel is one of the field researchers Hollee keeps track of. He has important surveys along the wild coast, yet often wanders far from his work and misses his reporting schedule. Hollee asks travelers passing through Auberdine to find him, recover missing survey data, and keep the research safe from local wildlife and other threats.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is a dwarf in Auberdine who conducts and oversees field research for dwarven archaeological efforts on Kalimdor's western coast.",al={"who is hollee","hollee darkshore","dwarf in auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Hollee be found?",a="Hollee can be found in Auberdine, the coastal port town on Darkshore's western shore.",al={"hollee location","where is archaeologist hollee"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are dwarves conducting research in Darkshore?",a="After the Third War, closer ties between Ironforge and the night elves brought dwarven researchers to Kalimdor. They study ancient relics, geological formations, and buried history that may shed light on dwarven ancestry.",al={"why are dwarves in darkshore","ironforge in kalimdor"},it="why_here"},{q="What trouble does she need help with?",a="Hollee is concerned about Prospector Remtravel, an absent-minded surveyor who wandered into southern Darkshore and failed to report his findings.",al={"hollee quests","absent minded prospector quest"},it="wants"},{q="What is the relationship between Hollee and Prospector Remtravel?",a="Hollee and Prospector Remtravel are colleagues in Darkshore's excavation and survey work. Remtravel studies ruins in the field, while Hollee coordinates reports and speaks with travelers in Auberdine.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel and hollee"},it="ties"},{q="Does Hollee belong to the Explorers' League?",a="Hollee represents dwarven archaeological and prospecting expeditions allied with Ironforge. Such expeditions are typically organized under the Explorers' League, which operates from the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"explorers league hollee","hollee faction"},it="side"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, seeing a compatriot across the sea in Darkshore's misty woods recalls Ironforge's drive to uncover ancient history.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Hollee's work as cooperation between the Eastern Kingdoms and the night elves, with Auberdine as a base for studying Kalimdor's past."},kw={"archaeologist hollee","auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","ironforge","prospector remtravel","the absent minded prospector","trouble in darkshore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:729","quest:730","topic:dwarf"},src={"Archaeologist Hollee"}}
E["npc:asterion"] = {t="npc",n="Asterion",z="darkshore",s="At Bashal'Aran, Asterion remains bound to a moonstone seal. The ancient Highborne once served governor Athrikus Narassin, and now his spirit waits among the ruins for release.",h="At Bashal'Aran, Asterion remains bound to a moonstone seal.",sec={{t="A Servant of Ancient Splendor",b="Before the Great Sundering, Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities blessed by Queen Azshara. She appointed Athrikus Narassin to govern them, and Asterion served as his right hand. Renowned for physical combat and arcane sorcery, Asterion lived among Bashal'Aran's people. He often traveled between the sister cities to see to their citizens' needs.",sp=0},{t="The Moonstone Prison",b="For reasons lost to time, Asterion fell out of favor with Athrikus Narassin. His master fashioned a powerful moonstone seal, an inescapable magical cage meant to confine him in Bashal'Aran. The centuries of confinement brought Asterion agony. Even death offered no release: his spirit remained bound to the ruined shrine after the world cracked open and demons overran the settlement.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Grave",b="Vile satyrs and grells roam Bashal'Aran, feeding on its lingering arcane power, yet they shun the shrine where Asterion's ghost lingers. An Alliance adventurer can take the moonstone seal from the satyrs and shatter it in Ameth'Aran, breaking Asterion's spectral chains at last. Freedom brings no peace. With Athrikus Narassin still enduring, Asterion turns from ten thousand years of despair toward vengeance.",sp=1,bt={"q954.5"}}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient Highborne ghost at the ruins of Bashal'Aran in Darkshore. Before the Sundering, he was an accomplished mage and the second in command to governor Athrikus Narassin.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","ghost elf darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Asterion imprisoned?",a="Athrikus Narassin bound Asterion with a magical moonstone seal. The reasons for their falling out are unknown, but the powerful enchantment held Asterion's spirit for millennia, even after death.",al={"why is asterion trapped","asterion prison","why did athrikus trap asterion"},it="why_here"},{q="Why don't the satyrs in Bashal'Aran attack him?",a="Satyrs and grells feed on the lingering arcane energies in Bashal'Aran, but keep away from the shrine where Asterion is bound. The satyrs possess the moonstone seal that anchors his captivity, rather than meddling with his spirit.",al={"do satyrs attack asterion","why demons leave asterion alone"}},{q="Where did Asterion live in life?",a="Asterion lived among the people of Bashal'Aran. He often traveled south to its twin city, Ameth'Aran, to tend to civic affairs under Queen Azshara's governor.",al={"asterion home","where was asterion from"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after you free him?",a="Asterion hopes that breaking the moonstone seal will end the imprisonment that continued beyond his death. What follows is told in the hidden passage.",al={"what happens to asterion","does asterion move on","asterion vengeance"},sp=1},{q="Is Asterion hostile to modern night elves?",a="No. Though Asterion is an ancient Highborne from Queen Azshara's court, he is peaceful toward Alliance travelers and seeks their help to break his ancient magical bondage.",al={"is asterion friendly","asterion alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Asterion want?",a="Asterion seeks release from the ancient magical prison that has trapped his spirit for ten thousand years. Athrikus Narassin bound him to Bashal'Aran using a moonstone seal, leaving Asterion to suffer even beyond physical death. He desperately needs you to recover this seal from the satyrs and shatter it in Ameth'Aran, ending his long torment and allowing his thoughts to turn toward retribution against his former master.",al={"asterion goal","what does asterion need","asterion motives"},sp=1,it="wants",add="0f52734c",bt={"q954.5"}},{q="Who is Asterion tied to?",a="In ancient times, Asterion served directly under Athrikus Narassin, the Highborne lord appointed by Queen Azshara to govern Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. As second-in-command, Asterion tended to the needs of both settlements. Despite his loyal service, Athrikus used his dark craft to bind Asterion in an arcane moonstone prison for reasons lost to history, turning their ancient bond into a legacy of betrayal.",al={"asterion master","who imprisoned asterion","athrikus narassin asterion"},it="ties",add="98a0ebe3"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Asterion is a tragic relic from before the Sundering. His story shows the cruel internal politics among the Highborne before Azshara invited the Burning Legion into their lands.",["class:Mage"]="In life, Asterion was celebrated for his command of the arcane and his skill in physical combat. His story offers a glimpse of early Kaldorei spellcraft.",["faction:Alliance"]="Asterion is one of the rare Highborne spirits willing to trust and aid Alliance adventurers. He seeks their help to break his prison of ten thousand years."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone","narassin","satyr"},rel={"quest:954","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","zone:azshara"},src={"Asterion"}}
E["npc:balthule-shadowstrike"] = {t="npc",n="Balthule Shadowstrike",z="darkshore",s="Near the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike keeps watch over northern Darkshore. He scouts for Delgren the Purifier, watching the dark practitioners in ancient elven ruins.",h="Near the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike keeps watch over northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Scout in the Shadows",b="West of the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike keeps watch alone. Restless spirits haunt northern Darkshore, and shadowed ruins fill its coast. Yet the tower poses a special danger. Under Delgren the Purifier’s direction, Balthule watches the dark casters who have entered the ancient Highborne ruins.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cult",b="The sorcerers and cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx practice forbidden magic. They harvest artifacts and souls from nearby ruins. Balthule calls on traveling Alliance champions to strike at their leaders. He also seeks parchment and talismans that reveal how far their summoning efforts reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike scouts northern Darkshore for Delgren the Purifier. He watches the cultists there.",al={"who is balthule","balthule role","balthule shadowstrike npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is just west of the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, near the coastline.",al={"where is balthule","balthule location","find balthule shadowstrike"},gp=true},{q="What is his mission at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Balthule was sent to spy on the dark spellcasters and cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx. He gathers intelligence and coordinates strikes against their rituals.",al={"why is balthule here","what does balthule want","althalaxx quest guy"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. He coordinates the campaign against the dark forces in northern Darkshore, with Balthule as his forward eyes and ears.",al={"who is delgren","balthule superior","delgren connection"},it="ties"},{q="What kind of enemies occupy the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="Dark cultists and sorcerers occupy the Tower of Althalaxx and its grounds, along with summoned demonic or shadowy minions. They seek to use ancient Highborne power for sinister ends.",al={"who is in the tower","althalaxx enemies","tower of althalaxx cultists"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in these ruins?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven structure. Foul sorcery and demonic activity so near elven lands threaten Darkshore and the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"why care about the tower","alliance darkshore presence"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Balthule Shadowstrike on?",a="Balthule serves the Alliance and his fellow night elves. He works directly as a scout and operative for Delgren the Purifier, keeping watch over threats rising in northern Darkshore.",al={"balthule faction","who does balthule serve","is balthule alliance"},it="side",add="d382c05d"},{q="What does Balthule Shadowstrike want?",a="Balthule wants to uncover the dark rituals taking place within the Tower of Althalaxx. By spying on the cultists holding the ruin, he seeks to gather enough intelligence for Delgren the Purifier to cleanse the corruption taking root along the coast.",al={"what does balthule want","balthule goal","what is balthule trying to do"},it="wants",add="67352a1e"},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike here?",a="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze of Auberdine sent Balthule to keep vigil outside the Tower of Althalaxx. Perched in hiding nearby, his duty is to observe the hostile occupants and enlist capable travelers to disrupt their dark schemes.",al={"why is balthule in darkshore","why is balthule here","what brought balthule here"},it="why_here",add="d4776665"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see the cultists’ desecration of ancient Kalimdor ruins as an outrage. Balthule seeks to avenge it before corruption spreads farther into your lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member sent north from Auberdine, you can find Balthule as a forward contact against the dark cultists around the Tower of Althalaxx.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the patience and vigilance it takes to work deep in hostile territory under dangerous spellcasters’ noses. Balthule shows those qualities as an elven scout."},kw={"althalaxx","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","mathystra","purifier","scout","shadowstrike"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","npc:delgren-the-purifier","quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","topic:night-elf","topic:highborne"},src={"Balthule Shadowstrike"}}
E["npc:barithras-moonshade"] = {t="npc",n="Barithras Moonshade",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Barithras Moonshade seeks travelers to gather rare plants from Darkshore’s shadowed wilds.",h="In Auberdine, Barithras Moonshade seeks travelers to gather rare plants from Darkshore’s shadowed wilds.",sec={{t="Resident of Auberdine",b="Barithras Moonshade watches over Auberdine and helps the night elves study and care for Darkshore. He sends travelers into nearby caverns to gather fungi for study and use, including death cap mushrooms.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Ancients",b="Barithras also guides capable travelers south to meet Onu. The ancient works to heal Darkshore’s tainted soil and soothe its restless natural spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Barithras Moonshade?",a="In Auberdine, Barithras Moonshade asks travelers to investigate local plants and contact guardians in the region.",al={"who is barithras","barithras moonshade","who is this night elf"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Barithras Moonshade?",a="You can find Barithras Moonshade in Auberdine, the port settlement on Darkshore’s shore.",al={"barithras location","where is barithras","barithras moonshade location"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Barithras give?",a="Barithras sends travelers into nearby caverns to gather fungi, including death cap mushrooms, then points them south to meet Onu.",al={"barithras quests","what quests does barithras give","cave mushrooms quest"},gp=true},{q="Is Barithras related to the other Moonshades?",a="No relatives of Barithras are recorded, so any tie to other night elves named Moonshade is unknown.",al={"moonshade family","other moonshades","is barithras related to sentinel moonshade"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Barithras Moonshade on?",a="Barithras Moonshade stands firmly with the night elves of Auberdine and the wider Alliance. Stationed in Darkshore, he looks out for the settlement's well-being and aids travelers who work to protect the surrounding wilderness.",al={"barithras moonshade faction","who does barithras serve","barithras alliance"},it="side",add="1a832bfc"},{q="What does Barithras Moonshade want?",a="Barithras seeks assistance with local matters around Darkshore, dispatching capable adventurers to gather resources such as cave mushrooms and directing them onward to consult with ancient allies like Onu in the groves to the south.",al={"barithras moonshade goal","what does barithras need","barithras moonshade quests"},it="wants",add="e41cf5ef"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can help your kin in Auberdine safeguard Darkshore by watching its plants and keeping ties with ancient forest guardians like Onu.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As one attuned to plant life, you may appreciate Barithras’s interest in Darkshore’s unusual cavern fungi."},kw={"auberdine","barithras","cave mushrooms","darkshore","death cap","moonshade","onu"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:947","topic:night-elf"},src={"Barithras Moonshade"}}
E["npc:cerellean-whiteclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Cerellean Whiteclaw",z="darkshore",s="Near Auberdine’s docks and inn, Cerellean Whiteclaw mourns the love he lost. The Sundering’s memory still haunts him, and he longs to bring Anaya’s restless spirit peace.",h="Near Auberdine’s docks and inn, Cerellean Whiteclaw mourns the love he lost.",sec={{t="A Love Torn asunder",b="Before the War of the Ancients, Cerellean Whiteclaw shared his life with Anaya Dawnrunner. Ten thousand years ago, the demonic invasion shattered ancient Kalimdor. Anaya died when her city, Ameth'Aran, fell in the destruction. Grief-stricken, Cerellean followed Malfurion Stormrage into the long druidic slumber.\n\nThe Emerald Dream brought little peace from his memories. Millennia later, Cerellean awoke and wandered Darkshore in grief. There he found Anaya's ghost still bound to the stones where she fell.",sp=0},{t="A Plea for Release",b="Cerellean longs to give Anaya peace, but cannot bring himself to strike down her tormented shade. So he asks passing travelers to go south to the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, lay her spirit to rest, and recover her pendant.\n\nOnce freed, Anaya's shade visits Cerellean briefly on Auberdine's docks. She assures him her love endures and promises they will reunite one day in the afterlife.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Near Auberdine’s docks and inn in Darkshore, Cerellean Whiteclaw mourns Anaya Dawnrunner. She died during the War of the Ancients ten thousand years ago.",al={"who is cerellean","cerellean whiteclaw","auberdine docks elf"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner shared her life with Cerellean Whiteclaw in the ancient city of Ameth'Aran. She died when the city was destroyed during the War of the Ancients, and her tormented spirit lingered among its ruins for thousands of years.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean's love","cerellean lover"},it="ties"},{q="Why doesn't Cerellean lay Anaya's spirit to rest himself?",a="Cerellean is too heartbroken to confront and destroy Anaya's ghost himself. He asks sympathetic travelers to give her spirit its final release.",al={"why doesn't cerellean fight anaya","why need adventurer"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the ruins of Ameth'Aran?",a="The ruins of Ameth'Aran lie in southern Darkshore, east of the main road. Ghosts of ancient kaldorei who died during the Great Sundering haunt the area.",al={"where is ameth'aran","anaya location","where is anaya"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Cerellean Whiteclaw on?",a="Cerellean is a kaldorei citizen aligned with the night elves and the Alliance. He stands peacefully in Auberdine, consumed by his personal grief rather than political or military ambition, seeking help from any traveler willing to aid him.",al={"cerellean whiteclaw faction","who does cerellean serve","cerellean alliance or horde"},it="side",add="20d93eae"},{q="What does Cerellean Whiteclaw want?",a="Cerellean wants to grant eternal peace to the spirit of his lost love, Anaya Dawnrunner. Tormented by the sight of her ghost bound to the ruins of Ameth'Aran, he seeks someone with the strength to destroy her spectral form and return her pendant to him, freeing her from her ancient agony.",al={"cerellean goal","what does cerellean need","cerellean whiteclaw quest goal"},it="wants",add="f9b8a3f3"},{q="Why is Cerellean Whiteclaw in Darkshore?",a="After awakening from millennia in the Emerald Dream alongside Malfurion Stormrage, Cerellean wandered Kalimdor in a grief-stricken daze. His sorrow drew him back toward the ruins of Ameth'Aran, where Anaya perished, leaving him lingering near the docks of Auberdine, unable to move on.",al={"why is cerellean in auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw location reason","why is cerellean here"},it="why_here",add="838b08c5"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Cerellean's grief reflects the deep, lasting scars the War of the Ancients and Great Sundering left upon the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share the long slumber Cerellean entered alongside Malfurion Stormrage. The Emerald Dream could not wash away his earthly heartbreak."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","ghost","sundering"},rel={"quest:963","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:war-of-the-ancients","topic:night-elf"},src={"Cerellean Whiteclaw"}}
E["npc:elder-starweave"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Starweave",z="darkshore",s="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Starweave rests in Auberdine as a night elf ancestral spirit. Along Darkshore’s coast, she shares ancient wisdom with pilgrims.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Starweave rests in Auberdine as a night elf ancestral spirit.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="In Auberdine, Elder Starweave appears as an ethereal shade among the coastal dwellings. The Cenarion Circle and the peoples of Kalimdor honor her as an ancestor. Travelers pass through the port on their way inland or across the sea, yet those who pause before her receive an ancestral blessing.\n\nElder Starweave speaks of the stars. Their paths in this age differ from those of old, yet she sees them as beacons of hope and fortitude for generations to come.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Starweave appears in Auberdine as a night elf ancestral spirit. She greets travelers, shares ancient wisdom, and offers Coins of Ancestry.",al={"elder starweave lore","who is starweave","starweave the elder"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Elder Starweave be found?",a="Elder Starweave can be found near Auberdine, along the shoreline of Darkshore.",al={"where is elder starweave","elder starweave location","starweave spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does she appear as a spirit?",a="Elder Starweave is an honored ancestor who appears in spiritual form during the Lunar Festival. The living may then pay respects to those who shaped the night elves’ distant past.",al={"why is starweave a ghost","is starweave dead","why ghost"},it="origin"},{q="Can Horde players speak to her?",a="Yes. Ancestral elders honored during the Lunar Festival welcome travelers of every affiliation. Horde adventurers must cross Auberdine, an Alliance-friendly port, with care.",al={"can horde visit starweave","horde elder starweave"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Starweave on?",a="Elder Starweave takes no side in the wars of the living. As an honored night elf ancestor resting in Darkshore, she offers her celestial blessings and wisdom to any traveler, Alliance or Horde, who seeks her out.",al={"is elder starweave alliance","elder starweave faction","who does elder starweave serve"},it="side",add="2e80733d"},{q="Why is Elder Starweave here in Darkshore?",a="Elder Starweave lingers in Darkshore as an ancestral spirit to observe the world and guide younger generations. She watches the shifting constellations, reading the signs of the heavens as beacons of hope and strength for the trials of the coming ages.",al={"why is elder starweave in darkshore","why is starweave here","elder starweave purpose"},it="why_here",add="d8911fea"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf adventurer in Darkshore, you meet Elder Starweave and connect with your long lineage of forebears. They looked to Elune and the stars through ancient cataclysms.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid observing the festival, you may hear Starweave’s thoughts on the stars echo Cenarion teachings of renewal, memory, and harmony with the natural world."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","coin of ancestry","darkshore","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:night-elf","quest:8721"},src={"Elder Starweave"}}
E["npc:gelkak-gyromast"] = {t="npc",n="Gelkak Gyromast",z="darkshore",s="Along Mist's Edge in northern Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast waits for his mechanical first mate to work again. Threshadons sank his ship, leaving him stranded on the coast.",h="Along Mist's Edge in northern Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast waits for his mechanical first mate to work again.",sec={{t="Castaway on Mist's Edge",b="West of the Ruins of Mathystra, Gelkak Gyromast is stranded on Darkshore's northern coast. The gnome calls himself captain and talks like an old sea dog. Threshadons sank his ship just offshore, and he washed up on the misty shore.\n\nThe key to his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, broke on the rocks. Crawlers, foreststriders and murlocs rummaging through the wreckage carried off its pieces.",sp=0},{t="The Threshwackonator Malfunction",b="Once travelers recover the key, Gelkak sends them to switch on the Threshwackonator 4100 and lead it back to him. He hopes to set the machine against the murlocs and beasts along the coast.\n\nThe Threshwackonator follows obediently, then malfunctions and turns hostile as it reaches its captain. The travelers must destroy it.",sp=1,bt={"q2098.3"}}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is stranded on Mist's Edge, the northern beach of Darkshore just west of the Ruins of Mathystra. The gnome talks like a pirate captain.",al={"gelkak","who is gelkak","gyromast"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gelkak stranded in Darkshore?",a="Threshadons sank Gelkak's ship just offshore. He washed up on Darkshore's northern coast with the broken key to his mechanical first mate.",al={"why is gelkak here","gelkak darkshore"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Threshwackonator 4100?",a="The Threshwackonator 4100 is Gelkak's mechanical creation and self-proclaimed first mate. He wants it working again so it can take revenge on the murlocs and beasts along the coast.",al={"threshwackonator","gelkak machine","robot"}},{q="What help does Gelkak need from travelers?",a="Gelkak asks travelers to recover the three pieces of his broken key from the coast's crawlers, foreststriders and murlocs. Then they can start the Threshwackonator 4100 and lead it back to him.",al={"gelkak quests","gyromast quests"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Gelkak Gyromast on?",a="Gelkak is a gnome aligned with the Alliance, though out here on the lonely strands of Darkshore he acts strictly on his own behalf. Stranded far from any major settlement, he welcomes any friendly Alliance traveler willing to lend a hand with his mechanical mishaps.",al={"gelkak gyromast faction","is gelkak alliance","who does gelkak serve"},it="side",add="77810e79"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, seeing one of your own stranded at Kalimdor's edge shows how far your adventures can carry you from home.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see Gelkak's hopes of revenge rest on his impressive device, the Threshwackonator 4100."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak gyromast","gnome inventor","mathystra","mist's edge","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"subzone:mist-s-edge","quest:2098","quest:2078","subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","zone:darkshore","topic:gnome"},src={"Gelkak Gyromast"}}
E["npc:gorbold-steelhand"] = {t="npc",n="Gorbold Steelhand",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Gorbold Steelhand keeps trade moving along Darkshore’s coast. The dwarven merchant brings goods across the Great Sea for travelers, crafters, and night elves.",h="In Auberdine, Gorbold Steelhand keeps trade moving along Darkshore’s coast.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Trader in Kalimdor",b="Gorbold Steelhand carries Ironforge trade to Auberdine. Night elves live across much of northern Kalimdor, and Alliance outposts rely on merchants who cross the Great Sea. Gorbold works alongside the kaldorei, selling trade goods, reagents, crafting supplies, and tools. Travelers visit him before exploring Darkshore’s dangerous shores and forests.",sp=0},{t="Maritime Ventures",b="Gorbold Steelhand keeps watch on the perilous waters off Auberdine as well as his stock. Reefs along Darkshore have swallowed Alliance vessels, and their lost cargo interests the merchant. Travelers who dive into the deep ocean may find him eager to hear of salvage and lost logs from sunken wrecks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarven merchant in Auberdine, Darkshore’s coastal port.",al={"gorbold","who is gorbold steelhand","dwarf in auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="What does Gorbold Steelhand sell?",a="Gorbold Steelhand sells trade supplies, crafting ingredients, gathering tools, and reagents such as vials and thread to tradesfolk passing through Auberdine.",al={"what does gorbold sell","gorbold trade goods","gorbold vendor list"},gp=true},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf living in Darkshore?",a="Auberdine links Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms as an Alliance transit hub. Dwarves travel there for commerce, exploration, and to support allied night elf operations.",al={"why is a dwarf here","why is gorbold in darkshore","ironforge in auberdine"},it="why_here"},{q="Does Gorbold offer any quests?",a="Yes. Gorbold Steelhand sends adventurers to recover lost ship cargo from wreckage off Darkshore in 'Deep Ocean, Vast Sea'.:contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}",al={"gorbold quest","deep ocean vast sea quest giver"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gorbold Steelhand on?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is firmly allied with the Alliance. As an Ironforge dwarf doing business in the night elf haven of Auberdine, he maintains friendly relations with local kaldorei and welcomes travelers loyal to the Alliance who pass through Darkshore.",al={"gorbold steelhand faction","is gorbold steelhand alliance","gorbold allegiance"},it="side",add="59afaf53"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Gorbold Steelhand in Darkshore’s misty, nocturnal surroundings may remind you of home in Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Gorbold Steelhand helping eastern Alliance races and night elves keep trade flowing across the Great Sea."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold","ironforge","merchant","steelhand","vendor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:982","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gorbold Steelhand"}}
E["npc:gubber-blump"] = {t="npc",n="Gubber Blump",z="darkshore",s="Along Auberdine’s shore, Gubber Blump fishes, teaches angling, and seeks fresh crab meat.",h="Along Auberdine’s shore, Gubber Blump fishes, teaches angling, and seeks fresh crab meat.",sec={{t="The Angler of Auberdine",b="Gubber Blump fishes on the Darkshore coast between Auberdine’s flight master and ferry pier. Most dwarves favor stone halls or forges, but Gubber chooses the shore. He teaches fishing and sells simple angling gear to travelers. Crab meat is a favorite, so he often depends on travelers to bring catches from the dangerous coast or recover his family fishing tackle.",sp=0},{t="Family Ties and Ocean Favors",b="Gubber Blump speaks freely about his family, especially his cousin Graun Blump. Graun has a beard and an unusual odor. Travelers may help with coastal work by gathering crawler legs or finding Gubber’s family pole. For their help, they may receive a handwritten thank-you letter and a shiny fishing lure for their next cast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump fishes and teaches angling on Auberdine’s beach, between the village docks and the hippogryph master.",al={"who is gubber blump","gubber blump npc","where is gubber blump"},it="identity"},{q="What does Gubber Blump teach or sell?",a="Gubber Blump teaches fishing and sells basic angling gear, including fishing poles and shiny baubles.",al={"what does gubber sell","gubber blump trainer","darkshore fishing trainer"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does Gubber Blump give out?",a="Gubber Blump asks travelers to find his family fishing pole and gather fine crab meat from the coast.",al={"gubber blump quests","fruit of the sea","the family and the fishing pole"},gp=true},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun Blump is Gubber Blump’s dwarven cousin. Gubber says Graun has a beard and an unusual smell.",al={"graun blump","gubber blump cousin"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Gubber Blump on?",a="Gubber Blump is an Alliance-aligned dwarf stationed peacefully alongside the night elves of Auberdine. While he mostly minds his own business and focuses on his craft, he openly welcomes Alliance travelers to trade, train, and share in coastal catches.",al={"is gubber blump alliance","gubber blump faction","who does gubber blump serve"},it="side",add="0ab58c9b"},{q="What does Gubber Blump want?",a="Gubber is passionate about fishing and culinary delicacies, holding a particular fondness for fresh crab meat harvested from the local waters. Above all, he wants to enjoy the bounties of the sea, recover his family's lost tackle, and teach fellow anglers the finer points of the trade.",al={"what is gubber blumps goal","what does gubber blump need","gubber blump motives"},it="wants",add="09bb4e46"},{q="Why is Gubber Blump in Darkshore?",a="Gubber has made his home along the shoreline of Auberdine, nestled between the docks and the flight master. The misty coast provides ample fishing grounds and a steady harvest of reef crabs, making it an ideal post for a dwarven angler looking to fish in peace.",al={"why is gubber blump here","why is a dwarf in darkshore","why is gubber in auberdine"},it="why_here",add="77301056"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber Blump favors coastal food, especially fresh reef crawler meat. Cooks gathering food from Darkshore’s waters prize it as an ingredient.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you seldom find Gubber Blump settled on a foggy Kalimdor shore instead of Khaz Modan. His frank talk about kin still carries his Ironforge roots."},kw={"auberdine","blump","darkshore","fishing","graun blump","gubber","reef crawler","shiny bauble"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1141","quest:1138","topic:dwarf"},src={"Gubber Blump"}}
E["npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde"] = {t="npc",n="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde watches the tides and what they leave behind. From Auberdine, the night elf sends travelers to examine strange sea creatures and massive turtles found dead on the northern beaches.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde watches the tides and what they leave behind.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Shifting Sands",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde keeps watch over the coast from her home in Auberdine. While others in town tend to the forest or shipping across the Veiled Sea, she follows the shoreline. Lately, the tides have carried the remains of huge sea creatures onto the sands.\n\nShe asks travelers to search the beaches and bring back skeletal samples. With them, she hopes to learn what is happening in the waters offshore.",sp=0},{t="The Stranded Giants",b="North and south of Auberdine, more sea creatures and ancient sea turtles are washing ashore. Gwennyth asks travelers to inspect the bodies and bones. She hopes to learn what drove the creatures onto the beaches or killed them, and to understand the danger in the waters off northern Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf in Auberdine who studies strange changes along Darkshore's shore. She sends travelers to survey the beaches and investigate what the sea has cast ashore.",al={"who is gwennyth","gwennyth auberdine","gwennyth lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="You can find Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, near the beach and docks on Darkshore's mist-shrouded coast.",al={"where is gwennyth","gwennyth location","find gwennyth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is she interested in beached creatures?",a="The dead sea turtles and other strange sea creatures may point to an imbalance or an unseen predator in the waters off Darkshore. Gwennyth studies the remains to find the cause.",al={"why beached turtles","why does she want bones","washed ashore quest"},it="wants"},{q="What quests does Gwennyth offer?",a="Gwennyth sends travelers to investigate the sea creatures and turtles washing ashore along Darkshore's coast, then receives their discoveries.",al={"gwennyth quests","what does she give"},gp=true},{q="Is she part of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?",a="Gwennyth is a Priestess of the Moon who serves the Sisters of Elune in Auberdine. She is neither a Cenarion druid nor a Sentinel commander, though she shares her kin's concern for Darkshore's natural balance.",al={"gwennyth faction","is gwennyth a druid"},it="side"},{q="What does her name mean?",a="Gwennyth's surname, Bly'Leggonde, is an anagram of 'Leggy Blonde', a playful touch from the world's creators.",al={"bly leggonde meaning","gwennyth name easter egg"},it="name"},{q="Why is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth makes her home in the coastal port of Auberdine, keeping watch over Darkshore's mist-shrouded beaches. Disturbed by the unnatural blight washing up on the coast, she monitors the shoreline for stranded marine wildlife and enlists passing travelers to investigate beached sea creatures and turtles suffering from the strange corruption afflicting the waters.",al={"why is gwennyth here","gwennyth bly'leggonde auberdine why","why is gwennyth in darkshore"},it="why_here",add="9c9d3ff5"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the unnatural deaths of great sea beasts off Darkshore are a troubling sign of imbalance in their ancestral lands. Gwennyth's watch on the beaches matters deeply to them.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see Gwennyth's reports of stranded sea life as an alarming sign of disturbance in Kalimdor's natural harmony.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on Auberdine as the primary coastal port in northern Kalimdor. Safe waterways and beaches matter to all allied races traveling through."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","beached sea turtle","blyleggonde","darkshore","gwennyth","kaldorei","veiled sea","washed ashore"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:3524","quest:4722","quest:4723","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde"}}
E["npc:kerlonian-evershade"] = {t="npc",n="Kerlonian Evershade",z="darkshore",s="At the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, Kerlonian Evershade has just awakened from a long sleep in the Emerald Dream. The night elf Druid of the Claw needs help through the troubled wilds on his way to Maestra's Post.",h="At the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore, Kerlonian Evershade has just awakened from a long sleep in the...",sec={{t="Awakening in Darkshore",b="For centuries, Druids of the Claw slept in barrows and communed with the Emerald Dream. They were called from their slumber during the Third War. Now Kerlonian Evershade rests beneath the ancient trees of the Grove of the Ancients, still shaking off the supernatural grogginess of his long sleep. He must cross Darkshore's troubled forests to reach Maestra's Post on the Ashenvale border.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Journey",b="The road from the Grove of the Ancients is dangerous. Blackwood furbolgs prowl the Twilight Vale, and Dark Strand cultists lurk along the road into Ashenvale. Sleep has weakened Kerlonian, and sudden bouts of exhaustion still trouble him. So he depends on sympathetic Alliance travelers for protection as he journeys south to rejoin his fellow night elves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kerlonian Evershade?",a="Kerlonian Evershade is a night elf Druid of the Claw near the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore. He recently woke from the Emerald Dream and needs help crossing the woods safely.",al={"who is kerlonian","kerlonian evershade lore","druid in grove of the ancients"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Kerlonian fall asleep while walking?",a="Like many Druids of the Claw who slept for centuries in barrow dens, Kerlonian still suffers from the lingering stupor of the Emerald Dream. Sudden spells of drowsiness overtake him before his body and mind have fully adjusted to waking.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","sleeper has awakened quest druid","kerlonian sleepy"}},{q="Where is he trying to go?",a="Kerlonian seeks safe passage south to Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale, where he can recuperate safely.",al={"kerlonian destination","where does kerlonian go","grove of the ancients escort destination"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Druid of the Claw?",a="Druids of the Claw are night elf druids who take the shape of the great bear. They channel strength, resilience, and feral might. Traditionally, they guard barrows and night elf lands while spending ages asleep in the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is druid of the claw","druids of the claw lore"}},{q="Whose side is Kerlonian Evershade on?",a="Kerlonian is a night elf Druid of the Claw aligned with the Cenarion Circle and the Darnassian night elves of the Alliance. His devotion lies with nature, the Emerald Dream, and his fellow druidic brethren who safeguard the ancient groves across Kalimdor.",al={"kerlonian faction","is kerlonian alliance","kerlonian evershade side"},it="side",add="62482562"},{q="What does Kerlonian Evershade want?",a="Having recently stirred from his long slumber in the Emerald Dream, Kerlonian desires nothing more than safe passage back to the fellowship of his fellow night elves at Maestra's Post. His deep trance leaves him groggy, making simple travel through Darkshore treacherous.",al={"kerlonian goal","kerlonian evershade what does he want","kerlonian purpose"},it="wants",add="9e991c8a"},{q="Why is Kerlonian Evershade here?",a="Kerlonian stopped at the Grove of the Ancients for a short nap while traveling to meet Liladris Moonriver at Maestra's Post. He is still sleepy after waking from the Emerald Dream and asks for help reaching her safely.",al={"why is kerlonian in darkshore","kerlonian grove of ancients","why is kerlonian asleep here"},it="why_here",add="4cb7152a"},{q="Who is Kerlonian Evershade tied to?",a="Kerlonian belongs to the Druids of the Claw, an order within the Cenarion Circle devoted to the bear spirit and tasked with guarding the wild. He is also bound in kinship and duty to the night elves stationed at Maestra's Post along the Ashenvale border.",al={"kerlonian order","kerlonian ties","who does kerlonian serve"},it="ties",add="0418b012"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you know the toll deep communion with the Emerald Dream can take on Cenarion Circle disciples.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you help safeguard one of your ancient defenders, freshly returned to a world changed since the Third War."},kw={"darkshore","druid of the claw","emerald dream","evershade","grove of the ancients","kerlonian","the sleeper has awakened"},rel={"quest:5321","quest:952","quest:2561","zone:darkshore","topic:druid"},src={"Kerlonian Evershade"}}
E["npc:laird"] = {t="npc",n="Laird",z="darkshore",s="At Auberdine's inn, Laird sells fish and cooking supplies to travelers along Darkshore's coast.",h="At Auberdine's inn, Laird sells fish and cooking supplies to travelers along Darkshore's coast.",sec={{t="A Harbor Merchant",b="Inside Auberdine's inn, Laird sells fish and supplies. Sailors, locals, and travelers come to him as Darkshore's waters churn with dangers greater than those along Teldrassil's sheltered shores. Yet anglers willing to cast from the misty beaches can earn a handsome profit from the local catch.",sp=0},{t="Ties Across the Water",b="Laird keeps in touch with fishing operations across the channel in Teldrassil. His fellow fisher Nessa Shadowsong sends shipments from Rut'theran Village, linking it with the mainland port and keeping coastal trade moving.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laird?",a="Find Laird on the ground floor of Auberdine's inn. Auberdine is the main Alliance settlement on Darkshore's coast.",al={"laird location","where is laird","laird auberdine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Laird sell?",a="Laird sells caught fish and cooking ingredients. He also teaches how to prepare a Fillet of Frenzy.",al={"laird vendor","what does laird sell","laird wares"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Laird?",a="Laird receives a delivery from Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village. Then he asks adventurers to carry word back across the sea.",al={"laird quests","auberdine fish quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Laird think Darkshore fishing is worthwhile despite the danger?",a="Darkshore's misty shoreline is more dangerous than Teldrassil's tranquil waters. Yet its abundant and exotic sea life can make fishing more profitable for enterprising fishers.",al={"laird gossip","is darkshore good for fishing"}},{q="Who is Laird?",a="Laird is a night elf fisherman and fish vendor who makes his living in Darkshore. Based inside the bustling inn at Auberdine, he trades with travelers and fishers who ply the misty waters along the coastline, offering cooking recipes and fresh fish to those passing through.",al={"who is laird","laird auberdine","laird identity"},it="identity",add="47d7af55"},{q="Whose side is Laird on?",a="Laird is allied with the night elves and the Alliance. Residing peacefully within Auberdine, he welcomes Alliance adventurers and local fishermen to rest at the inn and browse his goods.",al={"laird faction","is laird alliance","who does laird serve"},it="side",add="f4a4a12e"},{q="Why is Laird here?",a="Laird remains at the Auberdine inn to buy and sell coastal catches. Although Darkshore's coastline carries perils absent from Teldrassil, he recognizes that daring fishers can reap substantial profits from the local waters, making the port a prime location for his trade.",al={"why is laird in auberdine","laird purpose darkshore"},it="why_here",add="90f5a883"},{q="What does Laird want?",a="Laird seeks a thriving coastal fish trade. He encourages local fishing ventures despite the dangers of Darkshore's shores and is glad to supply hungry travelers with seafood and culinary recipes.",al={"what does laird want","laird goals","laird motives"},it="wants",add="d47e4f81"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="If you travel through Darkshore to cook, Laird teaches you to fillet and cook the fierce frenzy fish found in Kalimdor's waters.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see how your people trade along Kalimdor's mainland shores and support the growing coastal network through Laird."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","fillet of frenzy","fish vendor","laird","nessa shadowsong"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6342","quest:6343","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Laird"}}
E["npc:prospector-remtravel"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Remtravel",z="darkshore",s="In southern Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel leads the Explorers' League dig among ancient relics. His scattered focus and the dangers around camp make the work perilous.",h="In southern Darkshore, Prospector Remtravel leads the Explorers' League dig among ancient relics.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Dig in Elven Lands",b="The Explorers' League sent Prospector Remtravel across the sea to establish a dig in southern Darkshore. Night elves guard their ancestral lands, yet the League's search for Azeroth's origins brings its prospectors into forgotten places. Remtravel uncovers fossils and ancient stones. Aggressive wildlife and hostile local threats make the camp hard for one scatterbrained dwarf to manage.",sp=0},{t="The Absent-Minded Scholar",b="Prospector Remtravel loses himself in thought and research notes. When he wanders from camp in search of fossils or lost artifacts, predators and hostile creatures can corner him. Those who find Remtravel in the wild often must protect his fragile discoveries and rescue him from Darkshore's dangers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is an archaeologist and surveyor from Ironforge, sent by the Explorers' League. He seeks ancient relics and fossils at his small excavation camp in southern Darkshore.",al={"who is remtravel","remtravel lore","who is the dwarf in darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an Ironforge dwarf digging in Darkshore?",a="The Explorers' League searches the known world for titan artifacts, lost history, and ancient fossils. Darkshore's ruins and ties to the distant past draw dwarven scholars there.",al={"why is a dwarf in darkshore","what is the explorers league doing in darkshore","why dig here"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is he called absent-minded?",a="Remtravel loses track of his surroundings and equipment when absorbed in scholarship. He often wanders into danger without noticing nearby predators and beasts.",al={"why absent minded","is remtravel crazy","what happened to remtravel"}},{q="Is Prospector Remtravel related to anyone in the League?",a="Prospector Remtravel is believed to be the adventurous uncle Karna Remtravel mentions. She credits him with inspiring her passion for discovery and the wider world.",al={"remtravel family","karna remtravel uncle","who is karna remtravel"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Prospector Remtravel on?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a loyal subject of Ironforge and an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League. Because Ironforge stands alongside Darnassus in the Grand Alliance, he operates openly within night elf lands, counting on friendly travelers to aid his research and keep the local perils at bay.",al={"prospector remtravel faction","who does remtravel serve","remtravel alliance"},it="side",add="a4e27c5f"},{q="What does Prospector Remtravel want?",a="Like many in the Explorers' League, Remtravel seeks ancient relics and geological curiosities buried in unfamiliar soil. He is determined to uncover the history beneath Darkshore's surface, though his absent-minded focus on his findings often blinds him to the immediate dangers prowling around his dig site.",al={"what is remtravel looking for","remtravel goal","why is remtravel digging"},it="wants",add="a325ae20"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Remtravel shows the Explorers' League's resolve to piece together dwarven origins, even in Kalimdor's cold, damp woods.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may find the League's noisy digging and disturbed ancient soils testing the patience of local sentinels and druids."},kw={"absent minded prospector","darkshore","explorers league","fossils","ironforge","prospector remtravel","remtravel","remtravels excavation"},rel={"subzone:remtravel-s-excavation","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","topic:dwarf","topic:night-elf"},src={"Prospector Remtravel"}}
E["npc:ranger-glynda-nal-shea"] = {t="npc",n="Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea",z="darkshore",s="Near Auberdine, Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea keeps watch over Darkshore. She sends travelers against dangers on the coast and to investigate strange signs.",h="Near Auberdine, Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea keeps watch over Darkshore.",sec={{t="Guardian of Auberdine",b="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea directs scouts from Auberdine as corruption grows and hostile forces press into Darkshore. She watches the wilderness around town and calls on capable travelers to guard the perimeter. Their aid helps protect night elf holdings along the coast.",sp=0},{t="Threats Along the Coast",b="Glynda watches the shore for danger, especially the bolder murlocs south of town. She oversees bounties on threats such as Murkdeep and sends scouts to examine strange finds. One report speaks of a crimson crystal near Darkshore's eastern mountain range.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea is a night elf stationed in Auberdine. She organizes scout patrols and defenses across Darkshore.",al={"glynda nal'shea","who is glynda","ranger glynda"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Glynda Nal'Shea be found?",a="Glynda Nal'Shea can be found in Auberdine, Darkshore's main Alliance settlement. She is near the sentinel watch and the town entrances.",al={"glynda location","where is glynda","where to find glynda"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea offer?",a="Glynda offers work against dangers in the region, including a bounty on Murkdeep and an investigation of the red crystal along Darkshore's cliffs.",al={"glynda quests","what does glynda give"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is Glynda concerned about Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is a vicious murloc chieftain whose attacks threaten the southern coast and Auberdine's security. His targets include night elf outposts and travelers.",al={"who is murkdeep","why kill murkdeep"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Red Crystal quest line?",a="Glynda begins the Red Crystal investigation by sending scouts up Darkshore's eastern cliffs. They examine a strange, pulsing crystal and retrieve fragments for study.",al={"red crystal darkshore","the red crystal quest"}},{q="What faction does Glynda Nal'Shea serve?",a="Glynda Nal'Shea serves the night elves of Darnassus. She commands an Alliance military outpost in Darkshore.",al={"glynda faction","who does glynda work for"},it="side"},{q="Why is Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea here in Darkshore?",a="Stationed in Auberdine, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea helps guard Darkshore against the countless dangers pressing in on the night elf settlement. Between encroaching murlocs along the coast and strange relics such as the red crystal on the cliffs, she keeps watch over local threats and directs capable adventurers to neutralize them before Auberdine is overwhelmed.",al={"why is glynda here","ranger glynda purpose darkshore","why is glynda in auberdine"},it="why_here",add="83e5dc60"},{q="What does Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea want you to do?",a="Glynda seeks to secure the safety of Darkshore and unravel the unnatural disturbances troubling the region. She enlists your aid in hunting down dangerous threats like the infamous murloc Murkdeep and investigating mysterious relics such as the large red crystal on the mountainside.",al={"what does glynda want","glynda nalshea tasks","ranger glynda goals"},it="wants",add="0a51f57f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Glynda Nal'Shea shows the vigilance needed to protect Kalimdor's sacred shores from aggressive beasts and ancient corruption.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may recognize Glynda's sharp instincts and direct way of dealing with wild beasts and shoreline predators.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler arriving by boat from Teldrassil or the Eastern Kingdoms, you can take Glynda's bounties and help secure Darkshore's perimeter."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda","murkdeep","nal'shea","night elf","ranger","red crystal","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:4740","quest:4811","quest:4812","quest:4813","quest:954"},src={"Ranger Glynda Nal'Shea"}}
E["npc:sentinel-aynasha"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Aynasha",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore’s wild borders, Sentinel Aynasha scouts dangers threatening night elven lands. She watches enemy movements and carries urgent intelligence across the frontier.",h="Along Darkshore’s wild borders, Sentinel Aynasha scouts dangers threatening night elven lands.",sec={{t="On the Front Lines",b="Sentinel Aynasha scouts and fights with the Sentinels where night elven lands meet hostile incursions. She carries urgent messages across rough country and watches for enemy patrols. Her skill with a bow and knowledge of survival help her cross contested ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Sentinel Aynasha scouts and fights as an archer with the night elven Sentinels. They defend northern Kalimdor and its borders.",al={"who is aynasha","aynasha role","sentinel aynasha lore"},it="identity"},{q="What threats does she monitor in Darkshore?",a="Along Darkshore’s edges, Sentinel Aynasha watches hostile camps, rogue furbolg tribes, and foreign incursions that threaten the night elf wilderness.",al={"aynasha enemies","darkshore threats","who is she fighting"},it="threat"},{q="Why is she often isolated on the road?",a="Sentinel Aynasha and other Sentinels often travel alone or in small pairs. They carry urgent intelligence between posts without drawing unwanted attention from hostile forces.",al={"why is she alone","aynasha solo mission","sentinel scout duties"},it="why_here"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see in Sentinel Aynasha a watchful defender of the ancient woods. She guards them from foreign powers and wild corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in Kalimdor, you may find Sentinel scouts like Aynasha along dangerous wilderness roads. They are vital contacts there."},kw={"archer","aynasha","darkshore","kaldorei","night elf","scout","sentinel"},rel={"zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:5713"},src={"Sentinel Aynasha"}}
E["npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",z="darkshore",s="Across the bridge from Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze watches over Darkshore's coast. From an upper floor, she tracks dangers in the wilderness and guides travelers toward them.",h="Across the bridge from Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze watches over Darkshore's coast.",sec={{t="A Vigilant Eye in Auberdine",b="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze directs Auberdine's defenses from across the bridge. Other Sentinels patrol Darkshore's coast and woodlands, while she keeps watch from the upper floor of a building northeast of the town inn. She stays alert for disturbances across the region. Her directions send travelers as far north as the Tower of Althalaxx, so threats in the shadows do not take Auberdine by surprise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Cross the small bridge northeast of Auberdine's inn, then go to the second floor of the building there. Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is on duty inside.",al={"elissa starbreeze location","where is elissa starbreeze","auberdine starbreeze"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is her duty in Darkshore?",a="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze helps guard Auberdine by watching for dangers across Darkshore. She directs scouts and adventurers toward distant outposts and strange threats, including the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"what does elissa do","elissa starbreeze role"},it="purpose"},{q="Does she have family among the night elves?",a="Nothing is recorded about Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze's kin. In Auberdine, she watches over the town and guides travelers toward the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"starbreeze family","who is elissa related to"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf guard serving the Sentinels in the coastal port of Auberdine. Stationed in Darkshore, she watches over the settlement and directs capable travelers toward pressing troubles throughout the surrounding wilds, including investigations near the enigmatic Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"who is elissa starbreeze","elissa starbreeze night elf","sentinel starbreeze identity"},it="identity",add="eef8e9fa"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze on?",a="She is completely loyal to the Sentinels, the night elves of Darnassus, and the broader Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, she works to safeguard night elven settlements and interests across the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"what faction is elissa starbreeze","is elissa starbreeze alliance","elissa starbreeze loyalty"},it="side",add="73c7acf2"},{q="Why is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze here in Auberdine?",a="Elissa is posted in Darkshore as part of the regional Sentinel detachment guarding Auberdine. From her outpost above the village, she coordinates scouts and recruits adventurers to monitor sinister activities unfolding along the coastline and inland ruins.",al={"why is elissa starbreeze in auberdine","elissa starbreeze location darkshore","what brought elissa starbreeze here"},it="why_here",add="650c6447"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see the Sentinels' watchful discipline at northern Kalimdor outposts such as Auberdine.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler from Teldrassil, you can look to Sentinel Starbreeze for directions to dangers deeper in Darkshore."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","night elf","sentinel"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","npc:elanaria","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze"}}
E["npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's road, Sentinel Tysha Moonblade keeps watch over a troubled coast. West of Ameth'Aran, she guides travelers and seeks help against the restless spirits haunting the ruins.",h="Along Darkshore's road, Sentinel Tysha Moonblade keeps watch over a troubled coast.",sec={{t="Watch upon the Road",b="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade watches the road through Darkshore. East of her, cursed Highborne ghosts and malevolent banshees haunt Ameth'Aran's ancient stone pillars. Auberdine's defenses are stretched thin by dangers along the coast. Tysha asks capable travelers to uncover how Ameth'Aran fell and put its restless dead to rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade patrols the main road in central Darkshore, just west of Ameth'Aran. She guards the route from wandering beasts and restless specters.",al={"who is tysha","tysha moonblade lore","sentinel tysha"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="You can find Sentinel Tysha Moonblade beside Darkshore's north-south road, directly west of Ameth'Aran.",al={"tysha moonblade location","where is tysha","where is sentinel tysha"},gp=true},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="Tysha sends travelers to Ameth'Aran to investigate the tragedy that ruined the ancient night elf settlement and quiet the tormented ghosts among its fallen columns.",al={"tysha moonblade quests","fall of ametharan quest giver","what does tysha want"},gp=true},{q="Is she related to anyone else in Darkshore?",a="No relatives of Tysha are known. She keeps watch alone on the road west of Ameth'Aran, guarding the way by the haunted ruins.",al={"tysha moonblade family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade on?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade serves the Sentinels of the night elves and stands firmly with the Alliance. As a guardian of Kalimdor's sacred wilderness, she watches the trails of Darkshore to protect her kin and their ancient lands from encroaching perils.",al={"tysha moonblade faction","who does tysha moonblade serve","is tysha moonblade alliance"},it="side",add="73e42ede"},{q="Why is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade here?",a="Stationed along the road just west of the haunted ruins of Ameth'Aran, Sentinel Moonblade patrols this thoroughfare to monitor the nearby ancient grounds. Darkshore is rife with agitated spirits and lurking enemies, requiring vigilance to keep passing travelers and nearby elven settlements secure.",al={"why is tysha moonblade in darkshore","tysha moonblade post","why is tysha near ameth'aran"},it="why_here",add="d8373493"},{q="What does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade want?",a="Moonblade seeks competent Alliance adventurers to uncover the tragic history haunting the ruins of Ameth'Aran. By directing allies to investigate the shattered relics and ancient accounts of the city's fall, she hopes to bring clarity and rest to the restless spirits lingering in the wilderness.",al={"what does tysha moonblade need","tysha moonblade mission","why does tysha need help"},it="wants",add="d2f2f0b1"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can help the Sentinels keep peace in lands scarred by the ancient Sundering. Lay your cursed ancestors to rest.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler heading south from Auberdine toward Ashenvale, you can find one of the few friendly outposts along a perilous road filled with monsters."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","night elf","sentinel","tysha moonblade"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:953","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Tysha Moonblade"}}
E["npc:terenthis"] = {t="npc",n="Terenthis",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Terenthis tracks corruption spreading into Darkshore. The Cenarion Circle sent the night elf druid from Teldrassil to learn how far it has reached and seek help from travelers and local allies.",h="In Auberdine, Terenthis tracks corruption spreading into Darkshore.",sec={{t="Investigating the Taint",b="Terenthis searches Darkshore for Fel Moss and other signs of corruption. The Cenarion Circle sent him to Auberdine to follow the blight spreading from Teldrassil. Night elves fear it may break the balance of northern Kalimdor. He seeks the rot's cause and a way to stop it before it consumes the forests.",sp=0},{t="A Plea from Grimclaw",b="Grimclaw reaches Auberdine wounded and alone, seeking Terenthis's help. Terenthis recognizes that the bear's master, Volcor, is in grave trouble. Bound to his post, Terenthis sends travelers into the wilderness to find Volcor. Aggressive furbolg tribes have pinned the druid down after an ambush.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis serves the Cenarion Circle as a night elf druid stationed in Auberdine, Darkshore.",al={"terenthis lore","who is terenthis","terenthis auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Terenthis in Auberdine?",a="The Cenarion Circle sent Terenthis to Auberdine to investigate Fel Moss and magical corruption spreading from Teldrassil into Darkshore. He seeks a way to stop it.",al={"what is terenthis doing","terenthis purpose","why is terenthis here"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the bear beside Terenthis doing there?",a="Grimclaw came to Terenthis in Auberdine wounded and alone. His master, the druid Volcor, was ambushed and pinned down by aggressive furbolgs.",al={"terenthis bear","grimclaw","why is there a bear in auberdine"},it="ties"},{q="What organization does Terenthis belong to?",a="Terenthis belongs to the Cenarion Circle, a druidic order that works to preserve balance and protect nature across Kalimdor.",al={"terenthis faction","is terenthis cenarion circle"},it="side"},{q="What threats is Terenthis most concerned with?",a="Terenthis fears Fel Moss corruption and the growing hostility of furbolg tribes, which threaten travelers and druids.",al={"darkshore corruption","fel moss threat","terenthis concerns"},it="threat"},{q="Does Terenthis offer any tasks to adventurers?",a="Yes. Terenthis sends travelers to gauge threats along the coast, aid local allies, and help Volcor.",al={"terenthis quests","what does terenthis want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What does Terenthis want?",a="Terenthis wants to determine the full extent of the Fel Moss corruption creeping into Darkshore and discover why Teldrassil and its surrounding wilderness are falling to taint. Ultimately, he seeks to purge this creeping blight and restore balance to the forest before the corruption permanently takes root.",al={"terenthis goal","what is terenthis trying to do","terenthis motive"},it="wants",add="ba1c722a"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you stand with Terenthis against corruption spreading from Teldrassil into the mainland.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share Terenthis's concern for purifying your sacred lands of fel taint and protecting innocent forest life."},kw={"auberdine","cenarion circle","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:986","quest:984","quest:4761","quest:994","quest:995","topic:furbolg"},src={"Terenthis"}}
E["npc:tharnariun-treetender"] = {t="npc",n="Tharnariun Treetender",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Tharnariun Treetender watches for sickness in Darkshore’s wilds. The night elf naturalist studies the corruption spreading through plants and animals, seeking ways to protect them.",h="In Auberdine, Tharnariun Treetender watches for sickness in Darkshore’s wilds.",sec={{t="A Guardian in Auberdine",b="Tharnariun Treetender watches the woods beyond Auberdine’s port. Satyrs and foul shoreline washaways threaten the village, yet his work is with the natural world around it. He believes neglecting nature invites ruin. So he studies the decline of the local woods and seeks ways to fight the sickness spreading across the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="Healing the Afflicted",b="Plagues and corrupted blights have driven Darkshore’s creatures mad. Peaceful animals have become rabid threats. Tharnariun seeks a remedy instead of killing them out of fear. He uses cleansers and targets the worst of the contagion, hoping to save what remains of the wilderness from decay.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker in Auberdine, on Darkshore’s coast. He watches the forest and studies the unnatural afflictions troubling its wildlife.",al={"who is tharnariun","tharnariun lore","tharnariunreetender"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tharnariun Treetender?",a="You can find Tharnariun in Auberdine, the night elf village on Darkshore’s western edge.",al={"where is tharnariun","tharnariun treetender location","tharnariun map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What problems is Tharnariun investigating in Darkshore?",a="Tharnariun investigates the corruption and plagues spreading through Darkshore’s land and wildlife. He sends adventurers to cleanse infected beasts and stop the blight.",al={"what does tharnariun want","tharnariun purpose","why help tharnariun"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Tharnariun care so much about diseased animals?",a="Tharnariun believes neglecting nature brings consequences for the night elves. He works to cleanse sick creatures rather than abandon the forest to corruption.",al={"why save the beasts","tharnariun animal quest"},it="motive"},{q="What quests does Tharnariun Treetender offer?",a="Tharnariun directs adventurers to address blighted land and wildlife through 'Plagued Lands', 'Cleansing of the Infected', and 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"tharnariun quests","tharnariun treetender tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Is Tharnariun a druid?",a="The entry does not name Tharnariun a druid outright. His concern for preserving beasts and plants echoes the Cenarion Circle, and he cares for Darkshore’s wilderness.",al={"is tharnariun druid","tharnariun class"}},{q="Whose side is Tharnariun Treetender on?",a="Tharnariun Treetender stands firmly with the night elves and the Alliance. Stationed in Auberdine, his loyalties lie with the preservation of Kalimdor's natural heritage and his kaldorei kin, welcoming travelers of the Alliance who are willing to aid in protecting the wilderness from encroaching blight.",al={"tharnariun treetender faction","is tharnariun alliance","who does tharnariun serve"},it="side",add="8905307a"},{q="What does Tharnariun Treetender want?",a="Tharnariun seeks to protect and cleanse the fragile ecosystem of Darkshore. Troubled by strange afflictions twisting the local fauna, he devotes his efforts to uncovering the root causes of the corruption and finding remedies to heal or mercifully put down the infected wildlife before nature completely unravels.",al={"tharnariun goal","what is tharnariun trying to do","tharnariun treetender purpose"},it="wants",add="3ad5bd13"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you may feel the weight of Tharnariun’s warnings. Your people have an ancient duty to watch over the natural balance of northern Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Tharnariun’s concern for blighted wildlife and the work of restoring harmony to corrupted lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="Auberdine is the Alliance’s main coastal gateway in northern Kalimdor. Tharnariun’s defense of the surrounding woods helps protect the outpost."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","corruption","darkshore","infected","kaldorei","plagued lands","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:2118","quest:2138","quest:2139","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tharnariun Treetender"}}
E["npc:volcor"] = {t="npc",n="Volcor",z="darkshore",s="Deep in southern Darkshore, Volcor lies wounded in Blackwood Den. The night elf scout depends on his bear Grimclaw and Auberdine's defenders to escape the hostile furbolgs.",h="Deep in southern Darkshore, Volcor lies wounded in Blackwood Den.",sec={{t="Trapped in the Den",b="Volcor, a wounded night elf scout, lies inside Blackwood Den. He was tracking the corrupted Blackwood tribe through its underground lair when the furbolgs ambushed him and badly hurt him. Unable to fight his way past them, he sent Grimclaw, his loyal bear companion, into the wilds of Darkshore to seek help in Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="A Way to Freedom",b="Volcor offers his rescuer two ways out of the den. After scouts reach him with word from Terenthis, you can fight through the cave's defenders or move quietly past the sentries.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Volcor located?",a="Volcor lies deep inside Blackwood Den in southern Darkshore, near the Ashenvale border and not far from the road south of Auberdine.",al={"volcor location","where is volcor","find volcor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Volcor trapped in Blackwood Den?",a="Volcor was scouting the Blackwood furbolgs when they attacked and wounded him. Cut off from the cave entrance, he could not get past the hostile sentries without help.",al={"why is volcor in a cave","what happened to volcor"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor's loyal bear companion. When Volcor was trapped, he sent Grimclaw to find help in Auberdine, alerting the druid Terenthis.",al={"who is the bear","volcor bear","grimclaw lore"},it="ties"},{q="How can you help Volcor escape?",a="Volcor lets you choose how to rescue him. You can fight through the cave's furbolg guards or use stealth to slip past them.",al={"escape through force or stealth","volcor escort quest","rescue volcor"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sent you to find Volcor?",a="Terenthis, a night elf druid in Auberdine, sends you to find Volcor after Grimclaw is found wandering without his master.",al={"who gave the volcor quest","terenthis connection"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What tribe of furbolgs attacked him?",a="The Blackwood tribe attacked Volcor. These furbolgs are native to Darkshore and have fallen to corruption, madness, and hostility.",al={"which furbolgs","blackwood furbolgs"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf explorer and wanderer of Darkshore. Accompanied by his loyal bear companion, Grimclaw, he ventured deep into the forests until he ran afoul of the hostile Blackwood furbolgs, leaving him wounded and stranded within their den.",al={"who is volcor","volcor identity","volcor night elf"},it="identity",add="fe864757"},{q="Whose side is Volcor on?",a="Volcor is allied with the night elves of Darnassus and the Alliance. His trusted contacts reside in the coastal haven of Auberdine, where friends like Terenthis look after his safety and welcome travelers who aid him.",al={"volcor faction","is volcor alliance","volcor allegiance"},it="side",add="77334435"},{q="What does Volcor want?",a="Trapped and weakened deep inside Blackwood Den, Volcor simply wants to escape alive and make his way back to the safety of Auberdine. Having sent Grimclaw ahead to find help, he now relies on passing allies to guide him past the hostile furbolgs.",al={"what does volcor want","volcor goal","volcor motive"},it="wants",add="a5845558"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you can see the danger facing the Kaldorei in Darkshore as once-peaceful furbolg allies fall to corruption.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you know the bond between Volcor and Grimclaw reflects the connection druids share with nature's beasts. Their rescue touches nature's balance.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can slip quietly past the Blackwood guards through tactical finesse."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood den","darkshore","escape through force","escape through stealth","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"quest:986","subzone:blackwood-den","npc:terenthis","subzone:auberdine","quest:994","quest:995","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},src={"Volcor"}}
E["npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"] = {t="npc",n="Wizbang Cranktoggle",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Wizbang Cranktoggle keeps Darkshore’s buzzboxes working. The eccentric gnome engineer lives upstairs at the inn, far from the halls of Gnomeregan and Ironforge.",h="In Auberdine, Wizbang Cranktoggle keeps Darkshore’s buzzboxes working.",sec={{t="An Engineer in Auberdine",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle brings Alliance ingenuity to Auberdine. The gnome engineer works on the inn’s upper floor, among tools and spare parts. The night elves here seek harmony with nature and follow ancient customs. Wizbang tackles practical mechanical problems instead, far from Kalimdor’s solemn druidic traditions.",sp=0},{t="The Buzzbox Network",b="Along Darkshore’s rugged coast, Wizbang maintains a network of buzzboxes. The devices send automated reports and carry messages over long distances. Coastal weather and hostile wildlife often damage them. So Wizbang asks travelers to find parts, salvage tools such as gaffer jacks, and recover electropellers to keep the network working.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle lives on the upper floor of the inn in Auberdine, the night elf settlement in Darkshore.",al={"wizbang location","where is wizbang","auberdine gnome location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Wizbang Cranktoggle doing in Darkshore?",a="Wizbang is an Alliance engineer working to establish and maintain buzzboxes across the Darkshore wilderness.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","wizbang purpose","what does wizbang do"},it="why_here"},{q="What are buzzboxes?",a="Buzzboxes are Wizbang Cranktoggle’s mechanical devices for monitoring and sending information over long distances across Darkshore. Wildlife and harsh weather often damage them.",al={"what is a buzzbox","buzzbox lore","buzzbox purpose"},it="item"},{q="Is Wizbang related to any other gnomes?",a="Wizbang shares a surname with Delber Cranktoggle, suggesting they may belong to the same family of tinkerers.",al={"cranktoggle family","who is delber cranktoggle","wizbang relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Why do the night elves tolerate his tinkering in Auberdine?",a="The night elves and gnomes belong to the Grand Alliance. Auberdine offers lodging and refuge to allied races, though gnomish machines contrast with elven harmony with nature.",al={"night elves and gnomes","why allow engineering in auberdine"},it="conflict"},{q="What tasks does Wizbang give to adventurers?",a="Wizbang asks travelers to help repair and configure his buzzboxes by searching the shore for parts such as electropellers and gaffer jacks.",al={"wizbang quests","what quests does wizbang offer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an enterprising gnomish engineer currently staying on the upper floor of the inn in Auberdine. While night elves generally prefer nature over clanking machinery, Wizbang has set up shop along the coast to deploy and maintain his network of mechanical contraptions known as buzzboxes.",al={"who is wizbang","wizbang cranktoggle identity","who is the gnome in auberdine"},it="identity",add="97312084"},{q="Whose side is Wizbang Cranktoggle on?",a="Wizbang is loyal to Gnomeregan and the Grand Alliance. He operates openly out of Auberdine under the hospitality of the night elves, offering his technical expertise and tasks to Alliance travelers passing through Darkshore.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle faction","is wizbang alliance","wizbang cranktoggle allegiance"},it="side",add="a9ee7ecd"},{q="What does Wizbang Cranktoggle want?",a="Wizbang wants to establish and maintain an automated surveillance and communication network across Darkshore using his buzzbox inventions. Because the local wilderness is perilous and machinery frequently breaks down, he seeks adventurers to gather native materials, creature parts, and mechanical components to keep his network operational.",al={"what does wizbang want","wizbang cranktoggle goals","why does wizbang need parts"},it="wants",add="be17225f"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, seeing one of your people run an experimental communication network along Kalimdor’s rugged coast recalls Gnomeregan’s relentless inventiveness.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can recognize the gnomish habit of solving logistical problems in uncharted lands with custom tools such as gaffer jacks and electropellers.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know sentinels and druids rely on wisps, messengers, and bonds with nature. Wizbang brings loud, whirring gears and metal boxes into Darkshore’s sacred woods."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","cranktoggle","darkshore","electropellers","engineer","gaffer jacks","gnome","wizbang"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:983","quest:1579","quest:1580","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Wizbang Cranktoggle"}}
E["quest:1001"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 411",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Buzzbox 411 waits for thresher eyes to bring it back into service. Wizbang Cranktoggle, an eccentric and intoxicated gnome inventor, reaches it through a mechanical relay network.",h="Along Darkshore, Buzzbox 411 waits for thresher eyes to bring it back into service.",sec={{t="Voice Through the Static",b="After you repair Buzzbox 827 farther south, Wizbang Cranktoggle's voice crackles through the transmitter again. Hidden from sight, the gnome inventor directs you north along Darkshore's beach to the damaged Buzzbox 411. His words break with hiccups and praise for crawler wine. He says local aquatic predators carry what his coastal apparatus needs to work.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Beneath the Surf",b="Thresher eyes must go into Buzzbox 411's hatch to restore the machine. Darkshore threshers prowl the shallows off Auberdine, and Wizbang says their eyes can recalibrate the device. Feed the eyes to the apparatus, and it jolts back to life. Then the line opens for another assignment, delivered in an even slurrier voice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Buzzbox 411?",a="Buzzbox 411 is a mechanical transmitter on the Darkshore shore, north of Auberdine. It belongs to an experimental listening and research network maintained by Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome engineer.",al={"buzzbox 411","what is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 purpose"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnome tinkerer who speaks remotely through the Buzzbox network. He enjoys crawler wine during field research and relies on passing adventurers to gather animal parts in dangerous places.",al={"wizbang","who is wizbang","who made buzzbox"},it="people"},{q="Why does a machine need Thresher Eyes?",a="Wizbang says thresher eyes are vital to repairing Buzzbox 411. Gnomish engineering sometimes joins organic matter with machines for unusual work, from optical sensors to biological research.",al={"why thresher eyes","thresher eyes for machine","buzzbox eyes"},it="item"},{q="Where is Buzzbox 411 located?",a="Buzzbox 411 is on the beach in Darkshore, north of the night elf settlement of Auberdine.",al={"where is buzzbox 411","buzzbox 411 location","find buzzbox 411"},gp=true},{q="Where do I find Darkshore Threshers?",a="Darkshore threshers swim in the coastal waters off Auberdine and along nearby shores. Swim beyond the surf to find them.",al={"where are threshers","thresher eye source","thresher location"},gp=true},{q="What happens after Buzzbox 411 is fixed?",a="Once Buzzbox 411 hums back to life, Wizbang Cranktoggle thanks you through the static, drinks again, and asks you to fix his next machine, Buzzbox 323.",al={"next buzzbox","what comes after buzzbox 411","buzzbox chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Buzzbox 411 repaired?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is working down the Darkshore coastline to restore his network of automated communication devices. While he maintains the machines remotely, he relies on passing adventurers to supply local organic components—allowing him to keep his contraptions operational across the wilderness without interrupting his drinking back at camp.",al={"wizbang motive","why repair buzzbox 411","why does wizbang need this"},it="motive",add="e6ddd018"},{q="What are Darkshore threshers?",a="Darkshore threshers are predatory marine beasts that prowl the chilly coastal waters off Auberdine. Equipped with sharp senses and multiple ocular lenses suited for murky depths, their biological parts happen to provide the unusual optical properties Wizbang needs to calibrate the mechanisms of Buzzbox 411.",al={"darkshore threshers","who are threshers","what are threshers"},it="target",add="b4fb6bd9"},{q="Why does Wizbang need you instead of doing this himself?",a="Wizbang is an eccentric tinkerer who clearly prefers the comfort of his workshop and a steady supply of crawler wine over braving the freezing ocean surf. With dangerous threshers prowling the coastal waters, outsourcing the hunting and field repairs to capable adventurers lets him expand his network without leaving his stool.",al={"why me buzzbox 411","why doesnt wizbang do it","why wizbang needs adventurer"},it="why_me",add="5ee0d229"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Wizbang Cranktoggle shows an eccentric gnomish approach to fieldwork: bold invention, peculiar components, and leaving dangerous swimming to whoever happens by.",["profession:Engineering"]="Using thresher eyes to calibrate a mechanical transmitter shows how far unconventional tinkerers will push their methods.",["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine's sentinels watch Darkshore's waters, though they usually leave peculiar gnomish contraptions on the shore to their own devices."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 411","crawler wine","darkshore","gnome","thresher eyes","tinkering","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:983","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 827",["end"]="Buzzbox 411",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1001,ri={"Thresher Eye"}},src={"Buzzbox 411 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1002"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 323",z="darkshore",s="Wizbang Cranktoggle’s fieldwork now reaches the third Buzzbox along Darkshore’s coast. You gather six Moonstalker fangs and feed them to the machine north of Auberdine.",h="Wizbang Cranktoggle’s fieldwork now reaches the third Buzzbox along Darkshore’s coast.",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="After you operate Buzzbox 411 farther south, Wizbang Cranktoggle’s voice crackles through the speaker. Drink has muddled his directions, but he points you north of Auberdine, to Buzzbox 323 near a road bridge. His research calls for six Moonstalker fangs from the fierce hunters roaming Darkshore’s forests.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Field Machinery",b="Before you begin, Buzzbox 323 chatters with static and faint muttering. Place the requested fangs in its intake hopper, and the machine rattles as it grinds the teeth to dust. Then Wizbang’s boozy voice returns through the transceiver, pleased with your delivery. He points you toward the next machine in his scattered network.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 323 located?",a="Buzzbox 323 sits beside the main road north of Auberdine, near the bridge over the local river in Darkshore.",al={"buzzbox 323 location","where is buzzbox 323","find buzzbox 323"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, a gnome inventor elsewhere in Darkshore, speaks through the remote transmitters while drinking ale.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox gnome","wizbang cranktoggle"},it="identity"},{q="What does Buzzbox 323 do with the fangs?",a="Place the Moonstalker fangs inside, and Buzzbox 323’s gears grind them into fine powder for Wizbang’s automated biological sampling.",al={"what happens to the fangs","why moonstalker fangs","buzzbox grinding"},it="item"},{q="Where can I find Moonstalkers in Darkshore?",a="Moonstalkers and their runts prowl the shaded woodlands and hills along the road north and south of Auberdine.",al={"where are moonstalkers","moonstalker fang farm","moonstalker location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quest comes before and after Buzzbox 323?",a="Buzzbox 323 follows Buzzbox 411, where you gathered thresher eyes. It comes before Buzzbox 525, which sends you south along the road to collect grizzled scalps from thistle bears.",al={"buzzbox quest chain","what follows buzzbox 323","buzzbox order"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang sound so incoherent?",a="Wizbang is thoroughly intoxicated as he gives directions. He pauses to search for his ale and takes loud gulps between sentences.",al={"why is wizbang drunk","buzzbox voice slurring"}},{q="Why does Wizbang want Moonstalker Fangs placed in Buzzbox 323?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is working his way through maintaining his network of automated Buzzbox sampling machines scattered across Darkshore. Each contraption is designed to process parts from the local wildlife, and Buzzbox 323 specifically requires six moonstalker fangs to calibrate its internal grinding mechanisms and continue its mysterious field work.",al={"why buzzbox 323","wizbang buzzbox motive","why moonstalker fangs"},it="motive",add="c1fdd18c"},{q="What are the Moonstalkers you are sent to hunt?",a="Moonstalkers are stealthy saber cats native to the shadowed forests of Darkshore. They prowl among the ancient ruins and tangled woodlands, hunting prey under the cover of perpetual dusk and preying upon travelers who wander too far from Auberdine's guarded roads.",al={"what are moonstalkers","darkshore moonstalkers","who are the targets"},it="target",add="78de9795"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you hear Wizbang’s remote voice network at work. It shows gnomish engineering flair, despite his poor personal discipline.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the fierce Moonstalkers call for reverent caution. Gnomish science grinds their lethal fangs to dust.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how the Buzzboxes join automated material processing with long-range voice relay, despite their rough operation."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox","buzzbox 323","cranktoggle","darkshore","fangs","moonstalker","wizbang"},rel={"quest:1001","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Buzzbox 411",["end"]="Buzzbox 323",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1002,ri={"Moonstalker Fang"}},src={"Buzzbox 323 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1003"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 525",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, Wizbang Cranktoggle's scattered machines await the last of his strange requests. Buzzbox 525 calls for animal remnants and stranger materials.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, Wizbang Cranktoggle's scattered machines await the last of his strange requests.",sec={{t="A Slurred Transmission",b="Once Buzzbox 323 is serviced, its rattling speakers carry Wizbang Cranktoggle's garbled instructions. His words slur through drunken chuckles and rambling directions. He sends his helpers far south along Darkshore's main road. There, he asks them to hunt grizzled thistle bears and place four thick scalps in Buzzbox 525's compartment. The machine is concealed behind a fence in the brush beside the road.",sp=0},{t="The Distiller's Secret",b="Raucous singing drowns the machinery's hum as Wizbang Cranktoggle speaks through Buzzbox 525. When the grizzled bear scalps go into the receptacle, Wizbang admits what his machines are for. They carry messages, but they also brew and distill liquor. Night elves do not welcome his trade in their towns, so he hid the machines in the wilds. The bear scalps feed the brewing of potent thistle bear beer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Buzzbox 525 located?",a="Buzzbox 525 lies far south along the main road from Auberdine, just off the path near a rustic fence and partly hidden beneath bushes.",al={"buzzbox 525 location","where is buzzbox 525","buzzbox 525 find"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang want grizzled scalps?",a="Wizbang says grizzled scalps are needed to repair Buzzbox 525, as earlier machines needed crawler legs, thresher eyes, and moonstalker fangs. A drunken song about thistle bear beer hints at another use for them.",al={"why grizzled scalps","buzzbox bear scalps","what are scalps for"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="Why does Wizbang hide the Buzzboxes out in the wilderness?",a="Wizbang placed the machines outside Auberdine and depends on travelers to reach them. Night elves do not welcome his liquor trade in their towns, so he hid the machines in the wilds.",al={"why are buzzboxes hidden","why hide buzzbox","wizbang secret"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="Who is speaking through the Buzzbox?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle, an enterprising gnome tinkerer, speaks through the voice transmitters he installed in his Buzzboxes across Darkshore.",al={"who talks in buzzbox","buzzbox voice","wizbang identity"},it="identity"},{q="Can Wizbang speak through the machine without the scalps?",a="Yes. Wizbang speaks through Buzzbox 525 before the scalps are added. He explains why he asked for them once the work is done.",al={"is the buzzbox broken","did wizbang lie"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="What song does the Buzzbox sing?",a="Before you add the scalps, the speaker repeats a drunken limerick: “Though crawler wine's sweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine is grand. There's nothing so dear, as a thistle bear beer, and soon I shall have some on hand!”",al={"buzzbox singing","thistle bear beer song"}},{q="What are you sent to hunt for Buzzbox 525?",a="Wizbang requires grizzled scalps to keep his Buzzbox working.",al={"what do i kill for buzzbox 525","buzzbox 525 target","grizzled thistle bears darkshore"},it="target",add="7fe06fd4"},{q="Why does Wizbang ask you instead of the sentinels to collect bear scalps?",a="Wizbang relies on travelers who can reach his secluded machines and gather the requested animal parts. He explains his choice of locations when the work is complete.",al={"why not ask sentinels","why does wizbang need me buzzbox","why ask adventurer buzzbox"},sp=1,it="why_me",add="4f91b84e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Darkshore's strict stewardship leaves little patience for reckless gnomish tinkering.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can recognize Wizbang's ambition in machines that mix complex engineering with questionable practical priorities."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 525","darkshore","grizzled scalp","thistle bear","thistle bear beer","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1002","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Buzzbox 323",["end"]="Buzzbox 525",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=1003,ri={"Grizzled Scalp"}},src={"Buzzbox 525 (quest)"}}
E["quest:1138"] = {t="quest",n="Fruit of the Sea",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Auberdine fisherman Gubber Blump asks you to gather crab meat. He keeps to the docks and dreams of dishes for his catch.",h="Along Darkshore, Auberdine fisherman Gubber Blump asks you to gather crab meat.",sec={{t="A Passion for Crustaceans",b="Gubber Blump fishes from Auberdine's long wooden piers, thinking of crab meat. He calls crabs the ocean's true bounty and imagines them baked, barbecued, or boiled. His recipes include whipper root crab and Ironforge surprise crab.",sp=0},{t="Combing the Tidepools",b="Gubber cannot leave his fishing rod, so he asks you to gather ingredients from Darkshore's beaches. Reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers move among the breakers, offering meat for a coastal cook. Mind their claws as you gather the fine crab chunks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Fruit of the Sea?",a="Gubber Blump, an Alliance fisherman on Auberdine's docks in Darkshore, asks you.",al={"fruit of the sea quest giver","who gives fruit of the sea","gubber blump quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="What creatures drop the Fine Crab Chunks?",a="Reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers along Darkshore's shores and shallow surf yield Fine Crab Chunks.",al={"where do fine crab chunks drop","what drops crab chunks","which crabs drop fine crab chunks"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Gubber gather the crab meat himself?",a="Gubber is busy fishing from Auberdine's piers and cannot leave his line to hunt crabs on the beach.",al={"why doesn't gubber get his own crab","why does gubber need help"},it="why_me"},{q="What dishes does Gubber want to make?",a="Gubber names crab salad, soup, stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and a regional dish he calls Ironforge surprise crab.",al={"gubber crab recipes","what recipes does gubber mention","crab dishes"},it="motive"},{q="Is Gubber Blump's speech referencing something?",a="Yes. Gubber's list of crab dishes echoes Benjamin Buford 'Bubba' Blue from the film Forrest Gump, whose speech about shrimp is described as identical.",al={"gubber blump pop culture reference","forrest gump bubba reference"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="It begins and ends in Auberdine, a port village, while you hunt along the shores of Darkshore in northern Kalimdor.",al={"where is fruit of the sea","what zone is fruit of the sea in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the Fine Crab Chunks for?",a="Gubber Blump intends to use them in an endless variety of culinary dishes. To him, crabs are the fruit of the sea, perfect for baking, barbecuing, boiling, broiling, frying, and mixing into soups, stews, and salads.",al={"fine crab chunks use","why fine crab chunks","what does gubber do with crab chunks"},it="item",add="cf4b2535"},{q="What are the crawlers along Darkshore's coast?",a="Reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers are native crustaceans that scavenge Darkshore's long, misty coastlines and shallow tide pools. While dangerous to careless beachcombers, their meat is prized by fishermen and cooks like Gubber Blump for rich coastal feasts.",al={"what are reef crawlers","encrusted tide crawlers darkshore","darkshore crabs"},it="target",add="82492fa1"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Gubber's eager list of crab dishes may inspire you to make the most of local coastal catches.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may hear a familiar note of home when an outsider in northern Kalimdor dreams of Ironforge surprise crab. You travel as a Khaz Modan mountaineer.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can reach Kalimdor through Auberdine, a landing hub for Alliance explorers, and help local fishermen settle in."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","encrusted tide crawlers","fine crab chunks","fruit of the sea","gubber blump","reef crawlers"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=1138,ri={"Fine Crab Chunks"}},src={"Fruit of the Sea"}}
E["quest:1140"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="From Maestra's Post, Delgren's crusade reaches its sixth chapter. He deciphers Orcish writings recovered from the cult's emissaries and learns Athrikus Narassin hid two trapped Highborne soulgems in satyr strongholds deep in Ashenvale. Champions are sent to Night Run and Satyrnaar to shatter the vessels, free the tormented spirits, and weaken Athrikus's power.",h="From Maestra's Post, Delgren's crusade reaches its sixth chapter.",sec={{t="Deciphering the Scribblings",b="After Ilkrud Magthrull, an orcish courier, is cut down, Delgren the Purifier puts his study of Orcish to use. His peers in the Holy Light often scoffed at learning an adversary's tongue. Yet Delgren's practical wisdom lets him decipher notes recovered from the cult's emissaries. They reveal that Athrikus Narassin hid two potent soulgems containing ancient Highborne essences far to the northeast, in the defiled groves of Night Run and Satyrnaar.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Alliances",b="The soulgems in satyr camps reveal a foul alliance between Athrikus's cabal and demonic scions of the Burning Legion. Bound above circles of imprisonment, ancient spirits endure endless torment to fuel dark spellcraft. Blood-soaked satyr altars hold wild demonic corruption. Hidden satyr stalkers sworn to guard these arcane conduits wait in the shadows.",sp=1},{t="Weakening Athrikus",b="Shattering the crimson stones and freeing the Highborne souls from their circles of agony deals a devastating blow to Athrikus's mystic strength. Delgren says the leader of the Althalaxx cult is severely weakened without the soulgems. Yet the deed leaves the holy crusader unsettled by the night elves' quiet unease about the satyrs. He resolves to bring the lingering demonic blight to Auberdine's leaders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren know how to read Orcish?",a="Delgren took the initiative to study Orcish, though others in his holy order ridiculed him. He believed an enemy's tongue could offer tactical insight, and that knowledge let him translate notes recovered from Ilkrud Magthrull.",al={"delgren reads orc","how does delgren know orcish","delgren translation"}},{q="What are the soulgems and why are they held by satyrs?",a="The soulgems are crimson focus stones that bind ancient Highborne spirits above ritual circles of imprisonment. Athrikus Narassin bargained for them or placed them in sanctuaries such as Night Run and Satyrnaar, where the spirits' misery fuels the cult's arcane power.",al={"althalaxx soulgems","why do satyrs have the gems","trapped highborne souls"}},{q="Where are Night Run and Satyrnaar located?",a="Night Run and Satyrnaar are satyr strongholds in northeastern Ashenvale's forested heights, east of Maestra's Post.",al={"where is night run","where is satyrnaar","satyr camp locations"},gp=true},{q="Why are the night elves reluctant to talk about the satyrs?",a="Delgren notices that his elven hosts avoid discussing the satyrs because they were once night elves. During the ancient War of the Ancients, they surrendered to demonic corruption and were warped into goat-legged fiends, an enduring source of grief and shame for the Kaldorei.",al={"why secretive about satyr","night elf satyr connection","satyr history elven"}},{q="How does freeing these souls help stop the Tower of Althalaxx cult?",a="Athrikus Narassin draws on the spiritual energy in the Highborne soulgems to power his rituals. Shattering the gems frees the trapped souls and starves those rituals of power, leaving him vulnerable to an assault at the tower.",al={"why shatter soulgems","athrikus power source","weakening athrikus"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Elissa that Delgren mentions speaking to?",a="Elissa Starbreeze is a prominent night elf Sentinel stationed in Auberdine, where she coordinates local defenses in Darkshore. Delgren plans to confer with her about the entrenched satyr threat to northern Kalimdor.",al={"elissa auberdine","who is elissa","delgren elissa"}},{q="Who are you sent against to free the Highborne souls?",a="You are sent deep into the corrupted ruins of Night Run and Satyrnaar against the satyrs who hold the soulgems. These demonic servants of the Burning Legion have allied with Athrikus Narassin and his dark cult, keeping the ancient Highborne souls imprisoned within floating red gems above their dark circles of imprisonment.",al={"who are you fighting","who guards the soulgems","satyrs in night run and satyrnaar"},it="target",add="866ee2a4"},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier send you instead of going himself?",a="Delgren the Purifier is stationed at Maestra's Post, coordinating the defense and intelligence against cultist and demonic incursions across the border. Infiltrating deep into fortified satyr strongholds like Night Run and Satyrnaar requires a seasoned adventurer who can slip past enemy lines and shatter the gems without pulling an entire garrison away from the outpost.",al={"why does delgren need me","why cant delgren go","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="706f1be3"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren the Purifier is a pragmatic holy crusader who studies his foes' language to uncover demonic corruption and cleanse the tormented dead.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you bear a solemn duty to free Highborne ancestors from satyr desecration. The task confronts the tragic remnants of your people's ancient past.",["class:Priest"]="Shattering the circles of imprisonment brings peace to spirits suffering centuries of demonic torment."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","athrikus","delgren","highborne","maestra's post","night run","satyrnaar","soulgems"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:maestra-s-post","subzone:night-run","subzone:satyrnaar","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1140},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (6)"}}
E["quest:1141"] = {t="quest",n="The Family and the Fishing Pole",z="darkshore",s="On Auberdine's docks, Gubber Blump waits with his heirloom Fishing Pole for a catch. Hostile murlocs keep the town's small fishing boats ashore, so he seeks help catching native Darkshore grouper from the coast.",h="On Auberdine's docks, Gubber Blump waits with his heirloom Fishing Pole for a catch.",sec={{t="A Dwarf Far From Ironforge",b="Gubber Blump takes pride in his family's skill with a fishing line. Night elves make up most of Auberdine, though dwarves and gnomes have settled around its docks and port. Gubber spends his days gazing over the Veiled Sea instead of digging into stone. He hopes to bring in the local catch.",sp=0},{t="Murloc Infestations and Darkshore Grouper",b="Darkshore grouper thrive along the coast and make versatile food. They put up a lively fight on the line. Local fishermen usually row small boats into deeper waters to catch them, but aggressive murlocs now prowl the coast. The boats stay ashore, and Gubber fears the creatures are eating the local fish. So he asks travelers to fish from shore.",sp=0},{t="The Blump Legacy",b="Gubber gives a Blump Family Fishing Pole to anyone who brings him a hearty catch. He believes that landing a batch of feisty groupers proves an angler worthy of his family's legendary fishers, including his cousin Graun Blump. For Gubber, handing over a family rod is the highest mark of respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gubber Blump?",a="Gubber Blump is a dwarf fisherman on Auberdine's docks in Darkshore. He comes from a proud family of anglers, teaches basic fishing techniques, and gives the family's signature rods to promising fishers.",al={"who is gubber","gubber blump lore","auberdine dwarf fisherman"},it="identity"},{q="Why aren't boats going out from Auberdine to fish?",a="Hostile murlocs prowl large stretches of the Darkshore coast, making it too dangerous to launch small fishing boats. Local anglers stay by the piers and shallows.",al={"why no boats","darkshore fishing boats","auberdine boat trouble"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Darkshore grouper?",a="A Darkshore grouper is a native saltwater fish found off Darkshore's coast. Anglers prize the lively fight it puts up and its use in hearty coastal recipes.",al={"darkshore grouper","grouper darkshore"}},{q="Who is Graun Blump?",a="Graun Blump is Gubber's cousin. Gubber says she has a full beard and a pungent smell, and counts her among the finest anglers their family has produced.",al={"graun blump","gubber cousin"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there dwarves in a night elf town like Auberdine?",a="After the Third War and the forging of the Alliance, dwarves and gnomes from Ironforge crossed the sea to Kalimdor. They came to trade, build maritime links, and help their new night elf allies with harbor infrastructure.",al={"why dwarves in auberdine","dwarves in darkshore"},it="arrival"},{q="What is the Blump Family Fishing Pole?",a="The Blump Family Fishing Pole is a sturdy rod used by the Blump clan. Gubber gives these treasured poles to travelers who prove their angling skill in Darkshore's waters.",al={"blump fishing pole","blump family rod","gubber reward pole"},it="power"},{q="Why does Gubber Blump want Darkshore grouper?",a="Gubber comes from a proud lineage of dwarf fishermen and genuinely loves the craft. He normally sails out onto the bay to catch Darkshore grouper, but the recent arrival of aggressive murlocs has halted boat traffic entirely. Worried that the murlocs are gorging themselves on the local stock, Gubber is eager to secure some grouper and see another promising angler carry on good fishing practices.",al={"gubber blump motive","why does gubber want fish","why catch grouper"},it="motive",add="27b30f0f"},{q="What is the Darkshore Grouper used for?",a="Darkshore grouper make for fine eating and can be prepared in a variety of local recipes. While Gubber admits that they make plenty of tasty dishes, he personally cares far more about the thrill of hooking and reeling them in than eating them.",al={"what are darkshore grouper for","darkshore grouper use","grouper purpose"},it="item",add="60ad423d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, finding another of your people devoted to fishing instead of subterranean smithing or brewing reminds you how varied dwarven pursuits can be.",["profession:Cooking"]="Darkshore grouper is a reliable, nutritious catch along northern Kalimdor's coast and a staple for meals at frontier camps.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find Auberdine's harbor bringing mainland races and night elves together against coastal dangers such as murlocs."},kw={"auberdine","blump family fishing pole","darkshore grouper","fishing","graun blump","gubber blump","murloc","veiled sea"},rel={"npc:gubber-blump","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc","quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle"},m={start="Gubber Blump",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=1141,ri={"Darkshore Grouper"}},src={"The Family and the Fishing Pole"}}
E["quest:1143"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Dark rites at the Tower of Althalaxx threaten northern Darkshore. Balthule Shadowstrike leads an Alliance assault on Athrikus Narassin, the ancient sorcerer who commands the cult from the tower’s peak.",h="Dark rites at the Tower of Althalaxx threaten northern Darkshore.",sec={{t="Breaching the Summit",b="In northern Darkshore, the ruined Tower of Althalaxx shelters demonic rites. Balthule Shadowstrike watches from nearby and sees the danger must be faced now. Athrikus Narassin, an ancient night elf warlock, dwells at the summit. Beneath the shattered roof, he directs the dark rituals.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Strike",b="Athrikus Narassin is guarded by loyal warlocks and magic more dangerous than that of the cultists on the slopes. You must cut through his inner circle and take his severed head as proof. Balthule warns the demonic forces may gather again. Yet Athrikus’s death leaves the cult without its commander and brings Darkshore a measure of safety.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athrikus Narassin?",a="Athrikus Narassin is an ancient night elf warlock who commands the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx. He directs dark summonings and demonic rites among the ruins of northern Darkshore.",al={"athrikus","who is athrikus","boss of althalaxx"},it="target"},{q="Where can Athrikus Narassin be found?",a="Athrikus Narassin dwells at the summit of the Tower of Althalaxx. Seasoned warlocks and summoned minions guard him.",al={"where is athrikus","athrikus location","top of althalaxx"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike, an Alliance scout camped near the base of the Tower of Althalaxx, asks you to slay Athrikus.",al={"quest giver","balthule","balthule shadowstrike"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Delgren mentioned in the quest?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a nearby Alliance ally. He sent you to coordinate with Balthule against the demonic cabal.",al={"delgren","delgren the purifier"},it="allies"},{q="What happens after Athrikus is defeated?",a="Athrikus Narassin’s death deals a critical blow to demonic operations in the area. Balthule warns that the dark forces may gather again.",al={"after athrikus","tower of althalaxx ending"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Tower of Althalaxx dangerous to Darkshore?",a="Cultists and warlocks in the tower practice fel sorcery and summon demons into night elven lands. They threaten the wilderness and nearby settlements.",al={"why clean tower","althalaxx threat"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want Athrikus Narassin killed?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike knows that Athrikus Narassin leads the cabal of cultists and warlocks occupying the ruined Tower of Althalaxx. By striking directly at Athrikus atop the spire, Balthule hopes to shatter their leadership and drive back the demonic forces creeping across northern Darkshore before their corrupt rites spread further.",al={"why kill athrikus","balthule motive","balthule shadowstrike quest reason"},it="motive",add="95b2d6f7"},{q="What is Athrikus Narassin's Head for?",a="Athrikus Narassin's head serves as irrefutable proof that the ancient warlock has truly been slain. Bringing it back to Balthule Shadowstrike assures him and his allies that the dark master of the tower can no longer command his followers or summon demonic forces into Darkshore.",al={"athrikus narassin head use","why bring athrikus head","athrikus head quest item"},it="item",add="6015f725"},{q="Why does Balthule send you to face Athrikus instead of going himself?",a="Athrikus resides at the very summit of the tower, surrounded by his deadliest warlocks. While Balthule considers waiting for Delgren the Purifier's reinforcements, Delgren placed his absolute faith in your proven combat prowess by sending you in the first place, leaving you as their best chance to strike swiftly before the cultists reinforce.",al={"why me balthule","why doesnt balthule fight athrikus","why send me alone"},it="why_me",add="9e544083"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, facing Athrikus Narassin recalls the arcane and demonic corruption that once devastated your people.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see in Athrikus’s potent demonic magic at Althalaxx’s summit the danger of unbound fel worship.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping secure northern Darkshore protects travel between Auberdine and the lands beyond."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","darkshore","demonic","narassin","shadowstrike","warlock"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","quest:494","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=1143,ri={"Athrikus Narassin's Head"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (8)"}}
E["quest:1167"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Before you face Athrikus Narassin, Delgren sends you north to speak with Balthule Shadowstrike. The scout has watched the Tower of Althalaxx and can tell you what has changed there.",h="Before you face Athrikus Narassin, Delgren sends you north to speak with Balthule Shadowstrike.",sec={{t="A Scout's Report",b="Delgren the Purifier sends you north to meet Balthule Shadowstrike, his sentinel partner. You have purified corrupted relics and weakened the cult's hold along Darkshore's border. Before you confront Athrikus, Delgren wants fresh intelligence from Balthule. The sentinel has kept watch from the ruins overlooking the tower.",sp=0},{t="Disturbances in the Spire",b="Balthule Shadowstrike reports strange disturbances in the tower's upper sanctum. Blinding flashes and agonizing screams now shake the ancient elven spire, with erratic lightning in its halls. What is happening inside threatens to make the approach to Athrikus more dangerous.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Delgren send me back to Balthule?",a="Delgren sends you to Balthule for fresh information before you confront Athrikus. Balthule has watched the Tower of Althalaxx and can report what he has seen there.",al={"why see balthule","talk to balthule","delgren orders"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike keeps an observation campsite on the hills just west of the Tower of Althalaxx. From there, he watches the ruins in northern Darkshore.",al={"balthule location","find balthule","where is balthule"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What recent events did Balthule witness at the tower?",a="Balthule saw a blinding flash from the tower's highest chamber. Then he heard wretched screams carry across the coast and saw erratic lightning bolts strike the ground.",al={"what happened at the tower","balthule screams","tower flash"}},{q="Who is Athrikus?",a="Athrikus Narassin is the dark sorcerer leading the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx. Delgren and Balthule are determined to stop his fell rituals.",al={"who is athrikus","athrikus narassin","tower boss"},it="identity"},{q="Is Delgren the Purifier a local night elf?",a="No. Delgren is a human paladin and warrior of the Holy Light, stationed on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale. He has joined night elf scouts to purge demonic corruption.",al={"who is delgren","delgren race","is delgren an elf"},it="identity"},{q="What kind of ruin is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient night elf spire along Darkshore's craggy northern cliffs. It was abandoned before fallen arcanists and demonic cultists claimed it for forbidden rites.",al={"althalaxx background","what is the tower","tower lore"},it="place"},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren the Purifier is dedicated to rooting out dark, corrupting magic and demonic influence. The cultists occupying the Tower of Althalaxx threaten the sanctity of Darkshore with their sinister rituals. Delgren wants Athrikus stopped before the sorcerer can unleash whatever horrors he is preparing, but he knows a reckless assault could be fatal without intelligence on the tower's latest defenses.",al={"delgren motive","why does delgren care","delgren purpose tower"},it="motive",add="cf915580"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Delgren and Balthule work together to protect northern Kalimdor. Human paladins and night elf scouts stand together there.",["class:Paladin"]="Delgren studies the danger before he acts. That is the discipline expected of a warrior of the Light.",["race:NightElf"]="Balthule Shadowstrike defends ancestral lands from sorcery. It recalls the reckless arcane excesses that ruined night elf civilization ten millennia ago."},kw={"althalaxx","athrikus","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","tower"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=1167},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (7)"}}
E["quest:1442"] = {t="quest",n="Seeking the Kor Gem",z="darkshore",s="You cross the sea to Darkshore seeking a Kor gem for Jordan Stilwell. Thundris Windweaver sends an Alliance paladin initiate into Blackfathom Deeps, where naga have corrupted the potent stone. Jordan needs it for his craft.",h="You cross the sea to Darkshore seeking a Kor gem for Jordan Stilwell.",sec={{t="A Trusted Alliance",b="Paladins in training travel across the sea to Darkshore for materials Jordan Stilwell needs. In Auberdine, the night elf Thundris Windweaver remembers the human blacksmith with respect. Night elves keep their distance, and some fallen humans have betrayed their trust. Yet Thundris believes paladins can still follow a righteous path. He tells them where ancient gems may be found.",sp=0},{t="Into the Deeps",b="Blackfathom Deeps lies beneath Ashenvale's foggy northwestern coast. Twilight's Hammer cultists and treacherous sea-dwellers dwell in its submerged halls. Naga priestesses channel foul magic through ancient Kor gems. The gem you seek lies deep within the temple complex, among its dark halls and dangerous inhabitants.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Stone",b="When you bring a corrupted Kor gem back to Thundris Windweaver, he must cleanse it before Jordan Stilwell can forge it into a holy weapon. The naga give the gem raw magical potency, but twist its enchantment toward evil. Thundris removes that corruption so the gem's power stays pure and stable for the sacred smithing ritual ahead.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Kor Gem?",a="Thundris Windweaver sends paladins to find the Kor Gem. He is a night elf in Auberdine's coastal port in Darkshore and acts on behalf of the weaponsmith Jordan Stilwell.",al={"quest giver seeking kor gem","who gives seeking the kor gem","thundris windweaver quest"},it="arrival"},{q="Where is the Kor Gem located?",a="The Kor Gem lies inside Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient underground temple on Ashenvale's northwestern coast. Naga priestesses among the ruins carry the gems.",al={"kor gem location","where to get kor gem","where is corrupted kor gem"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Jordan Stilwell need a Kor Gem?",a="Jordan Stilwell needs the Kor Gem's potent magic as material for crafting his refined weapon during the paladin trial The Test of Righteousness.",al={"why kor gem","what is kor gem for","stilwell gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Thundris have to purify the gem?",a="Naga imbue Kor gems with great arcane power, but their foul enchantments taint it. Thundris purifies the gem so its strength can safely serve in a weapon of the Light.",al={"why purify kor gem","corrupted kor gem cleansed","cleansing the gem"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Thundris mention a 'fallen kind'?",a="Thundris likely means human betrayals such as Prince Arthas Menethil's fall into darkness, which tarnished the Silver Hand's reputation across Azeroth. Even so, he judges each paladin on their own merit.",al={"who is the fallen one","thundris fallen kind","fallen paladin reference"},it="history"},{q="Do I need a group to get the Kor Gem?",a="Thundris warns you not to go alone. Elite naga deep within Blackfathom Deeps carry the gem, so a dedicated adventuring party is strongly advised.",al={"is kor gem soloable","can you solo kor gem","blackfathom deeps group"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver remembers Jordan Stilwell from long ago as a man of modest, honorable character. Although Kor gems are perilous and inherently steeped in dark magic, Thundris trusts that Stilwell's purpose is noble. Recognizing you as a champion walking a holy path, he agrees to help locate and cleanse the artifact so Stilwell can complete his work safely, ensuring its foul energies are stripped away before it is ever used.",al={"thundris motive","why does thundris help","why help stilwell"},it="motive",add="5bec2e5c"},{q="What is the Corrupted Kor Gem for?",a="The Corrupted Kor Gem is an arcane focus imbued with dark power by the naga dwelling in the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Jordan Stilwell requires a Kor gem as an essential component for forging his masterwork weapon. However, before it can serve a righteous weapon, the gemstone's vile naga corruption must be cleansed while preserving its raw inner potency for Stilwell's crafting ritual.",al={"what is kor gem for","corrupted kor gem use","purpose of kor gem"},it="item",add="c21b70e4"},{q="Who holds the Kor Gem in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The gem is held by the naga who have infested the sunken elven shrine of Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale. These serpentine creatures prize the Kor gems, imbuing them with foul, shadowy power to fuel their own sinister rites in the flooded depths.",al={"who has the kor gem","kor gem target","who drops kor gem"},it="target",add="35f248ef"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin of the Alliance, you face a trial of character and endurance. It tests your willingness to travel into Kalimdor's hostile depths and help forge a consecrated arm of the Light.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Thundris Windweaver build a fragile but growing bridge between the ancient Kaldorei and the newly allied followers of the Holy Light from the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, you see a human blacksmith rely on night elf wisdom and dwarven steel to craft arms against rising darkness."},kw={"auberdine","blackfathom deeps","darkshore","jordan stilwell","kor gem","naga","paladin","test of righteousness","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:1653","zone:blackfathom","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:naga"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1442,ri={"Corrupted Kor Gem"}},src={"Seeking the Kor Gem"}}
E["quest:1579"] = {t="quest",n="Gaffer Jacks",z="darkshore",s="Near Auberdine, Wizbang Cranktoggle needs his lost gaffer jacks. He lost a box of hardware overboard on his voyage from Ironforge, and the parts lie somewhere along Darkshore's coast.",h="Near Auberdine, Wizbang Cranktoggle needs his lost gaffer jacks.",sec={{t="A Cluttered Mind in a Quiet Haven",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle crossed the Great Sea from Ironforge seeking quiet in Darkshore. The gnome inventor drank too much on the voyage. In a drunken haze, he leaned over the rail and lost a crate of specialized metal parts called gaffer jacks in the water near Auberdine.",sp=0},{t="Tuning the Stintle Pegs",b="Wizbang says gaffer jacks are essential precision tools. Without them, he cannot tune his stintle pegs or continue his delicate tinkering. He will not wade into the cold surf himself, so he asks local anglers to cast along Darkshore's shore and fish up the scattered parts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are gaffer jacks?",a="Gaffer jacks are small gnomish mechanical fasteners and components. Wizbang Cranktoggle needs them to tune his stintle pegs.",al={"what is a gaffer jack","gaffer jack use","gaffer jacks item"},it="item"},{q="How did the gaffer jacks end up in the sea?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle drank too much during his voyage from the Eastern Kingdoms to Kalimdor. Drunk aboard ship, he dropped his supply box overboard near Darkshore.",al={"how did he lose them","why are they in the water","why fish for gaffer jacks"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine instead of Ironforge?",a="Wizbang went to Auberdine for its quiet. Ironforge's constant clatter and noisy workshops wore on him, especially while he nursed his hangovers.",al={"why is wizbang in auberdine","why did wizbang leave ironforge"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can the lost gaffer jacks be fished up?",a="Anglers can fish gaffer jacks from the open saltwater along Darkshore near Auberdine. They may turn up on ordinary casts, not only at schools of fish.",al={"where do i fish gaffer jacks","gaffer jacks location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after recovering the gaffer jacks?",a="After Wizbang gets his gaffer jacks back to tune his pegs, he says he also lost his electropellers in Darkshore's rivers and lakes. Those need fishing out too.",al={"what next after gaffer jacks","quest after gaffer jacks"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang need adventurers instead of retrieving them himself?",a="Wizbang has a throbbing hangover and no sea angling gear. He stays dry on the Auberdine docks and leaves the dredging to anyone with a fishing rod.",al={"why cant wizbang get them","why doesnt wizbang fish"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want the gaffer jacks recovered?",a="Wizbang traveled all the way from Ironforge to Darkshore seeking peace and quiet to work on his inventions. Unfortunately, his clumsy drunken mishap on the voyage left his essential supplies resting at the bottom of the sea. Without those gaffer jacks, his tinkertastic work comes to an immediate halt, as he cannot even tune his stintle pegs without them.",al={"why does wizbang need gaffer jacks","wizbang cranktoggle motive","why help wizbang cranktoggle"},it="motive",add="bd1e627b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know the restless eccentricity of tinkers. Wizbang's delicate components and heavy drinking might make even you cringe.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know how maddening it is to miss one unusual part needed to calibrate a delicate device.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Darkshore's woods are quiet and sacred. A loud, hungover gnome inventor is an odd sight for Auberdine's sentinels."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","electropellers","fishing","gaffer jacks","ironforge","stintle pegs","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","quest:1580","quest:1141","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1579,ri={"Gaffer Jack"}},src={"Gaffer Jacks"}}
E["quest:1580"] = {t="quest",n="Electropellers",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Wizbang Cranktoggle wants his lost electropellers back. A mishap with an explosive duck decoy scattered the prototype parts in freshwater streams.",h="In Darkshore, Wizbang Cranktoggle wants his lost electropellers back.",sec={{t="A Tipsy Invention",b="Wizbang Cranktoggle went inland one evening to find a place to test his latest invention. The gnome tinkerer, based in Auberdine, had built a self-propelled duck decoy that explodes. He drank too much and blacked out. Hours later, he woke in town with singed hair and an empty pack; his bag of electropellers had fallen into one of the coastal rivers.",sp=0},{t="Dredging the Waters",b="Wizbang asks local fishermen to dredge Darkshore's freshwater streams, for he will not brave the wilds himself. Anglers on the Wildbend River and Cliffspring River can snag the buoyant metal parts along with local fish. Once the components are back, Wizbang can resume his erratic waterfowl experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the electropellers?",a="Fish in Darkshore's freshwater rivers and lakes, including the Cliffspring River and Wildbend River. The electropellers are not in the ocean along the coast.",al={"where are electropellers","how to get electropellers","electropeller location"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is an eccentric gnomish engineer who lives in Auberdine. He makes bizarre, explosive inventions and relies on travelers to gather lost components and oddities for his experiments.",al={"who gives electropellers","wizbang cranktoggle"},it="identity"},{q="What was Wizbang trying to build?",a="Wizbang was building a self-propelled duck decoy that explodes. After drinking too much, he accidentally detonated an early prototype, scorching his hair and losing his bag of parts in the water.",al={"exploding duck decoy","wizbang project"},it="purpose"},{q="Can electropellers be found in fish schools?",a="No. Electropellers come from open freshwater casts, not special schools such as Lesser Oily Blackmouth nodes.",al={"fish schools electropellers","can i fish schools"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Complete Gaffer Jacks first. Wizbang assigns it earlier to test your angling luck in the local waters.",al={"prereq for electropellers","electropellers prerequisite"},gp=true},{q="Are electropellers dropped by monsters?",a="No. Enemies and ground containers do not yield electropellers. Retrieve them from rivers with a fishing pole.",al={"do mobs drop electropellers","who drops electropellers"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want you to recover the electropellers?",a="Wizbang lost his entire bag of components during a drunken misadventure testing inventions along the waterways of Darkshore. He woke up back in Auberdine with singed hair and an empty pack. Without those missing parts, his ongoing engineering research into self-propelled, exploding duck decoys is at a complete standstill.",al={"why does wizbang need electropellers","wizbang motive","why get electropellers"},it="motive",add="42aa198c"},{q="What is an Electropeller used for?",a="Electropellers are specialized mechanical components Wizbang designed for propulsion. Specifically, they serve as the drive mechanism inside his prototype self-propelled, exploding duck decoy, allowing the mechanical decoy to steer and motor through bodies of water before its volatile payload detonates.",al={"what are electropellers","electropeller use","electropeller purpose"},it="item",add="c9029636"},{q="Why does Wizbang ask you to fish for the electropellers instead of doing it himself?",a="Wizbang has already seen proof of your uncanny luck and fishing prowess when you dredged up gaffer jacks for him previously. Having recovered in Auberdine disoriented and singed from his drunken mishap, he prefers relying on a proven angler rather than scouring the wilds of Darkshore on his own.",al={"why me wizbang","why doesn't wizbang fish them up"},it="why_me",add="d23bdc75"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Wizbang's chaotic ambition to build exploding duck decoys. Losing expensive parts in an elf-guarded river is embarrassing.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see electropellers as curious examples of miniaturized gnomish propulsion. They drive mechanical decoys before violently combusting.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may regard Wizbang's loud, smoky inventions and river-littering mishaps with quiet disapproval. Darkshore's streams should remain natural."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring river","darkshore","duck decoy","electropellers","fishing","wildbend river","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"quest:1579","npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","quest:4762","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=1580,ri={"Electropeller"}},src={"Electropellers"}}
E["quest:2078"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Revenge",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast seeks revenge on the murlocs who plundered his wrecked ship. He sends you to wind up his mechanical first mate, the Threshwackonator 4100.",h="Along Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast seeks revenge on the murlocs who plundered his wrecked ship.",sec={{t="A Captain's Vendetta",b="Gelkak Gyromast is stranded on Darkshore, but he will not yield to the murlocs along the shore. He has gathered the parts for his plan and seeks revenge on their tribe and its chief. Rather than wade into the surf with his cutlass, the eccentric captain turns to engineering. He gives you a winding key and asks you to tend to his mechanical subordinate.",sp=0},{t="The First Mate's Mutiny",b="Gelkak's first mate is the Threshwackonator 4100, a clanking mechanical golem left in the shallows south of the wreck. The machine promises an easy slaughter of the murlocs, but it cannot be trusted. You wind it up and lead it back to Gelkak. Then it malfunctions and mistakes its rescuer and creator for hostile targets, forcing a battle on the beach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak's first mate?",a="Gelkak's first mate is the Threshwackonator 4100, an automated mechanical golem on the coast south of his stranded camp.",al={"first mate","gelkak first mate","who is the first mate"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gelkak want revenge?",a="Gelkak's ship was wrecked along Darkshore. The native Greymist murlocs rummaged through the wreckage and took part of his first mate's key. He means to use the golem against their tribe and its chief.",al={"why revenge","murloc revenge","gelkak motivation"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you bring the Threshwackonator back?",a="Use Gelkak's key to activate the Threshwackonator, then lead it back to him. What happens when it reaches the captain becomes clear during the escort.",al={"threshwackonator attack","robot malfunction","why does the golem attack"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What do I do with Gyromast's Key after finishing the quest?",a="Gyromast's Key activates the Threshwackonator. Once the work is done, the key has no further purpose.",al={"gyromast key use","keep gyromast key","can i delete key"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="Where did Gelkak get the Threshwackonator?",a="The Threshwackonator came with cargo and equipment salvaged from Gelkak's ill-fated voyage along northern Kalimdor. It was designed to give his crew heavy mechanical muscle.",al={"who built threshwackonator","threshwackonator origin"},it="origin"},{q="Does Gelkak give up after the golem is destroyed?",a="Gelkak's plans and response become clear when you bring his first mate back.",al={"what happens to gelkak","after gyromast revenge"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Why does Gelkak need you to fetch his first mate instead of going himself?",a="Gelkak is stranded on the beach of Darkshore after a disastrous shipwreck, completely obsessed with recovering his sunken ship's cargo and taking vengeance against the local Greymist murlocs. Having already relied on you to dive for the vital components of his mechanical first mate, he remains camped by his salvaged gear and commands you as a hired crewmate—or in his terms, a landlubber—to start up the contraption and guide it safely back to him.",al={"why me gyromast","why does gelkak need help","why cant gelkak get the golem himself"},it="why_me",add="a39a7119"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Gelkak's mechanical first mate shows how much a stranded captain relies on engineering equipment.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize the winding key as a familiar way to activate a mechanical automaton.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help clear malfunctioning machinery and aggressive murlocs from the coastline between Auberdine and the lands to the south."},kw={"darkshore","gelkak","golem","gyromast","key","murloc","threshwackonator","threshwackonator 4100"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2098","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2078},src={"Gyromast's Revenge"}}
E["quest:2098"] = {t="quest",n="Gyromast's Retrieval",z="darkshore",s="Gelkak Gyromast needs your help on Darkshore's coast. His mechanical first mate cannot work without a winding key, shattered on the rocks. Wildlife and murlocs carried off its three pieces.",h="Gelkak Gyromast needs your help on Darkshore's coast.",sec={{t="Castaway on Darkshore",b="On Darkshore, Gelkak Gyromast is a gnome pirate stranded far from the South Seas. He says aggressive threshadons attacked and sank his vessel just off the coast. The wreck cast him ashore among the flotsam, marooned and parted from his crew.",sp=0},{t="The Scavenged Key",b="Gelkak's first concern is his first mate, not provisions or gold. His companion needs a special key to operate, but the key broke into three pieces when Gelkak crashed on the rocky shoals. Reef crawlers on the beach, foreststriders near the woods, and Greymist murloc scavengers carried the shiny pieces away.",sp=0},{t="A Peculiar Companion",b="Gelkak speaks of his first mate with a sea captain's fierce loyalty. He says the companion must be put in working order, and the broken key is vital to winding it up again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gelkak Gyromast?",a="Gelkak Gyromast is a gnome pirate whose vessel predatory threshadons attacked and sank off Darkshore.",al={"gelkak gyromast","who is the gnome pirate","darkshore gnome pirate"},it="identity"},{q="What is the key used for?",a="The key is needed to reactivate and wind up Gelkak's mechanical first mate, which shut down during the shipwreck.",al={"why does gelkak need the key","gelkak key purpose","first mate key"},it="item"},{q="Where did the three pieces of the key go?",a="Foreststriders took the top piece, Greymist murlocs the middle piece, and coastal reef crawlers the bottom piece after the key broke on shore.",al={"where are the key pieces","who stole the key","broken key darkshore"},gp=true},{q="Why was a gnome pirate sailing near Darkshore?",a="Gelkak was sailing off northern Kalimdor in search of plunder when hostile threshadons ended his voyage.",al={"why is gelkak in darkshore","pirates in darkshore"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after the key is reassembled?",a="With all three pieces of his key, Gelkak can wind up his companion and continue with Gyromast's Revenge.",al={"what next after key","gyromast retrieval follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the murlocs holding the key piece?",a="Greymist murlocs scavenged the middle piece. Their tribe lives among wreckage from drowned ships along Darkshore's shoals.",al={"darkshore murlocs","greymist murloc key","shipwreck murlocs"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast want his key restored?",a="Gelkak Gyromast was shipwrecked off the coast of Darkshore when threshadons sank his vessel. Left stranded and surrounded by hostile wildlife, he desperately needs his mechanical first mate back in working order to defend himself and enact his revenge against the creatures that wrecked his voyage. Without the three shattered pieces of the winding key, his clockwork companion remains entirely inert.",al={"why gelkak wants key","gelkak gyromast motive","why help gelkak"},it="motive",add="460afe34"},{q="Why does Gelkak Gyromast need your help?",a="Gelkak is a marooned pirate with no crew left beside him and no friends among the local night elves. Having barely survived his ship sinking and washing ashore battered on the beach, he is in no shape to battle the vicious reef crawlers, foreststriders, and murlocs that made off with his broken key shards.",al={"why does gelkak need me","why can't gelkak get the key","why me gyromast"},it="why_me",add="234cb20d"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Gelkak's reliance on clockwork devices instead of flesh-and-blood shipmates. His pirate life is unusual among your kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the challenge of keeping clockwork contraptions working after a violent shipwreck in saltwater."},kw={"darkshore","first mate","foreststrider","gelkak gyromast","greymist","gyromast's retrieval","pirate","reef crawler","threshadon"},rel={"npc:gelkak-gyromast","quest:2078","zone:darkshore","topic:pirate","topic:murloc"},m={start="Gelkak Gyromast",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2098,ri={"Bottom of Gelkak's Key","Middle of Gelkak's Key","Top of Gelkak's Key"}},src={"Gyromast's Retrieval"}}
E["quest:2118"] = {t="quest",n="Plagued Lands",z="darkshore",s="Darkshore's wildlife is falling to a creeping sickness, and Tharnariun Treetender seeks a way to save it. He asks you to calm a rabid thistle bear with an enchanted relic and bring it back alive.",h="Darkshore's wildlife is falling to a creeping sickness, and Tharnariun Treetender seeks a way to save it.",sec={{t="A Blight on the Wilderness",b="A creeping sickness twists Darkshore’s beasts into maddened, violent creatures. Thistle bears suffer most, and their frenzy threatens travelers and the coast’s fragile balance. Night elf sentinels answer with steel, while druids seek to understand the sickness and heal its cause.",sp=0},{t="Tharnariun's Hope",b="Tharnariun Treetender will not kill the corrupted beasts before trying to save them. He made a trap called Tharnariun’s Hope. Set on the forest floor, its soothing light briefly calms a raging thistle bear. Pacified, the bear follows you back to Tharnariun’s outpost for study.",sp=0},{t="Tragic Medicine",b="When an infected bear reaches camp, Tharnariun tries to purge its sickness with restorative magic. His first attempt ends in disaster. The cleansing energies overwhelm the weakened animal, and it collapses and dies. The failure shows how deeply the dark plague has taken hold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Plagued Lands?",a="Tharnariun Treetender, a night elf druid in Auberdine, asks for your help. He seeks a cure for Darkshore’s afflicted wildlife.",al={"quest giver plagued lands","tharnariun darkshore quest","who starts plagued lands"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What is the objective of Plagued Lands?",a="Use Tharnariun’s Hope to trap and calm a Rabid Thistle Bear in Darkshore, then lead it back to Tharnariun alive.",al={"plagued lands goal","what to do in plagued lands","how to catch bear darkshore"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What happens to the bear when you bring it back?",a="Tharnariun tries to cleanse the bear with healing magic, but the sickness has advanced too far. The strain overwhelms it, and it dies after the treatment.",al={"does the bear die","tharnariun bear cure result","bear death plagued lands"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What item do you use to capture the bear?",a="Tharnariun provides Tharnariun’s Hope, an enchanted trap. Its calming light pacifies the enraged bear so it will follow you.",al={"plagued lands trap","tharnariun's hope item","bear cage darkshore"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What quest follows Plagued Lands?",a="Cleansing of the Infected follows Plagued Lands, then comes Tharnariun’s Hope.",al={"next quest after plagued lands","plagued lands chain","tharnariun follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the thistle bears rabid?",a="A creeping plague is spreading through Darkshore, poisoning local wildlife and driving thistle bears into mindless aggression.",al={"why are bears sick in darkshore","darkshore plague bears","darkshore corruption"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Tharnariun Treetender want you to capture a rabid thistle bear?",a="A dark sickness spreads through Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of the local wildlife. The thistle bears have suffered the worst of it, turning from noble woodland beasts into frenzied engines of destruction. Tharnariun Treetender believes he may have devised a cure for the affliction, but he needs a living, rabid subject brought directly to him so he can test his remedy and halt the corruption before it claims all the forest's creatures.",al={"why capture thistle bear","tharnariun motive plagued lands","why does tharnariun want a bear"},it="motive",add="bbb593c2"},{q="What are rabid thistle bears and why are you targeting them?",a="Thistle bears are native forest predators of Darkshore, typically revered as stalwart and noble beasts. However, an unnatural contagion has recently infected their ranks, driving them into a mad frenzy and warping their minds. You are sent after them not to slaughter them outright, but to lure and pacify a sick specimen with Tharnariun's trap so it can be safely examined in hopes of developing an antidote.",al={"what are rabid thistle bears","why target rabid thistle bears","rabid thistle bear darkshore"},it="target",add="1b7f183c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing Darkshore’s native flora and fauna fall to rabid madness affronts Cenarius and the balance of nature you are sworn to protect.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share Tharnariun’s grief as nature falls to corruption. The bear’s tragic loss shows how deeply the disease has spread through the land.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler crossing northern Kalimdor, you face untamed corruption pressing against the borders of settled lands."},kw={"cleansing of the infected","darkshore","plagued lands","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope","thistle bear"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=2118},src={"Plagued Lands"}}
E["quest:2138"] = {t="quest",n="Cleansing of the Infected",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Tharnariun Treetender asks you to stop the infected thistle bears. His attempt to cleanse one failed, and he fears the rabid beasts will harm other creatures and spread the sickness.",h="In Darkshore, Tharnariun Treetender asks you to stop the infected thistle bears.",sec={{t="A Bitter Necessity",b="Tharnariun Treetender has searched for a remedy to the sickness in Darkshore's wildlife. He tried to cleanse a captured bear, but the thistle bears remain diseased and violent. So he asks you to put them down before they maul other creatures or carry the sickness farther into the ancient woodlands.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Wilds",b="Tharnariun asks you to kill twenty rabid bears, though he knows this will not cure the plague. The killings buy time for Auberdine's defenders. Until someone finds and severs the source of the forest's corruption, the settlement has no other way to hold back the aggressive herds and the danger they bring.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tharnariun want the thistle bears killed instead of cured?",a="Tharnariun tried to cleanse a captured bear, but the cure failed and the beast died. Now the diseased bears threaten other creatures, so killing them is his last resort to slow the sickness's spread.",al={"why kill the bears","why not cure bears","tharnariun bear quest"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun is a night elf caretaker in Auberdine. He studies the ailments affecting Darkshore's plants and animals and works to preserve nature's balance against the spreading corruption.",al={"tharnariun role","who gives cleansing of the infected"},it="identity"},{q="Does slaying the rabid bears actually end the plague?",a="No. Tharnariun warns that killing the rabid bears will not stop the plague. It buys the forest and Auberdine's residents time by slowing the spread of infection and violence.",al={"does this fix darkshore","is the plague cured"}},{q="What comes after Cleansing of the Infected?",a="After you report back, Tharnariun asks you to prepare for more bloodshed and offers Tharnariun's Hope, which continues the effort to deal with the blighted wildlife.",al={"next quest after cleansing","what follows cleasning infected"},it="next_step"},{q="Where are the rabid thistle bears found?",a="Rabid thistle bears roam the coastal and inland forests of central Darkshore, among the misty pines south and east of Auberdine.",al={"rabid thistle bear location","where are bears darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What caused the thistle bears to go rabid?",a="A mysterious taint sweeping through northern Kalimdor's woodlands has corrupted the bears. It turned peaceful wildlife into frenzied, aggressive beasts that Tharnariun's attempted cure cannot heal.",al={"why are bears sick","bear sickness darkshore"},it="origin"},{q="What are rabid thistle bears and why must they be killed?",a="Thistle bears are native forest predators that usually live in harmony with the wildlands of Darkshore. However, a creeping, unnatural plague spreading through the woods has driven many of them rabid and violently deranged. In their tainted madness, these diseased beasts attack other wildlife, menace travelers near Auberdine, and ravage the woodland ecology. Because attempts to cure their affliction have failed, putting them down is the only way to contain the devastation.",al={"rabid thistle bears","who are rabid thistle bears","why kill rabid thistle bears"},it="target",add="acd0862d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you bear the weight of ordering corrupted beasts killed. Since the war, the sickness has reached deep into your ancestral homeland.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Tharnariun's command may pain you. It is an act of mercy and care for the forest, not ordinary hunting.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know culling diseased predators can protect the wider ecology, even when the cause remains unknown."},kw={"auberdine","cleansing","darkshore","infected","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun","treetender"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2118","quest:2139","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=2138},src={"Cleansing of the Infected"}}
E["quest:2139"] = {t="quest",n="Tharnariun's Hope",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Tharnariun Treetender's work against the wildlife sickness reaches a grim turn. Travelers have put down infected beasts across Darkshore, and now he sends an Alliance champion after the rabid Den Mother northeast of town.",h="In Auberdine, Tharnariun Treetender's work against the wildlife sickness reaches a grim turn.",sec={{t="A Tragic Necessity",b="Since the Third War, an unnatural sickness has made Darkshore's wild creatures rabid. Tharnariun Treetender is stationed in Auberdine, where he has asked travelers to put down infected beasts and ease the forest's suffering. Yet killing rabid thistle bears treats only a symptom. Tharnariun decides the source among the local bears must be removed: their matriarch, the Den Mother.",sp=0},{t="The Den Mother",b="The Den Mother lurks in a cavern northeast of Auberdine, near the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran. Once a guardian of the woodland fauna, she was consumed by the affliction spreading across northern Kalimdor. She kept bearing and raising litters of rabid cubs. Alliance heroes hunted her down in her den, ending her torment and stemming the tide of frenzied bears prowling the coastal highway.",sp=1},{t="The Grim Reality of Kalimdor",b="Tharnariun gives profound thanks after the Den Mother's death, though melancholy shadows his words. For the kaldorei, raising weapons against woodland creatures is agony. Dark forces press against their new home, and many despair or seek shelter. Auberdine's defenders accept the heavy burden of protecting their wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharnariun Treetender?",a="Tharnariun Treetender is a night elf caretaker stationed in Auberdine. Distraught by the blight and madness warping Darkshore's wildlife, he oversees efforts to study and track the suffering animals, then put them out of their misery.",al={"tharnariun","who gives tharnariun's hope","treetender auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Den Mother located?",a="The Den Mother dwells in a cave in the hills northeast of Auberdine, just east of the ruins of Bashal'Aran.",al={"where is den mother","den mother cave location","find den mother"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must the Den Mother be killed instead of cured?",a="The affliction ravaging Darkshore's wildlife grips the beasts and drives them into violent frenzies. With no immediate cure and the Den Mother raising rabid offspring, Tharnariun decides killing her is the only way to stop the sickness from spreading further.",al={"can den mother be saved","why kill den mother","cure den mother"},it="motive"},{q="What quests lead up to Tharnariun's Hope?",a="Three parts lead to Tharnariun's Hope. The chain begins with 'Plagued Lands', continues through 'Cleansing of the Infected', and ends with 'Tharnariun's Hope'.",al={"prerequisites for tharnariuns hope","quest chain tharnariun"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What is making the animals of Darkshore sick?",a="Tharnariun names no source. He knows only that a sickness is spreading across Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of those it touches. Thistle bears have been hit hardest.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","darkshore animal plague cause","what corrupted the bears"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Tharnariun mention people escaping to fortified lands?",a="Auberdine is an exposed coastal outpost beset by ghosts, corrupted wildlife, and hostile creatures. Night elf civilization struggles to rebuild after the Burning Legion's invasion, and some residents feel overwhelmed and hide or retreat toward safer Alliance bastions.",al={"fleeing auberdine","fortified alliance lands"},it="people"},{q="Who is the Den Mother?",a="The Den Mother is a massive, corrupted bear laired in a cave northeast near the ruins of Bashal'Aran. She is the source giving birth to or harboring the rabid thistle bears that plague the region. Slaying her cuts off the influx of diseased beasts menacing Auberdine.",al={"what is the den mother","who is den mother","den mother darkshore"},it="target",add="f873ab28"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, slaying woodland beasts, especially a matriarch bear, violates their deep reverence for nature. This duty is bitter and sorrowful.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold bears in high spiritual esteem through the teachings of Ursoc. Killing a corrupted Den Mother reminds you of nature's delicate balance and the tragedies of corruption.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you understand the tragedy of an apex predator driven mad by disease. You know culling an infected beast can be the truest act of mercy.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Auberdine and strengthen the Alliance's foothold along northern Kalimdor's coast. You defend night elf lands from growing wilderness threats."},kw={"auberdine","bashal'aran","cleansing of the infected","darkshore","den mother","rabid thistle bear","tharnariun treetender","tharnariun's hope"},rel={"npc:tharnariun-treetender","quest:2138","quest:2118","subzone:auberdine","quest:954","zone:darkshore","topic:alliance"},m={start="Tharnariun Treetender",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=2139},src={"Tharnariun's Hope (quest)"}}
E["quest:2178"] = {t="quest",n="Easy Strider Living",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong offers hunters her own recipe for strider stew if they bring her foreststrider meat.",h="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong offers hunters her own recipe for strider stew if they bring her...",sec={{t="A Taste of the Wild",b="Auberdine's coastal folk make use of the wildlife around them. Alanndarian Nightsong has her own recipe for hearty strider stew, made from the tall foreststriders that range through Darkshore's woods. She asks you to hunt the birds and bring back their meat before she shares her cooking.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Foreststriders",b="Foreststriders range through the woodlands and beaches north and south of Auberdine. Their sharp beaks and quick tempers make them dangerous when provoked, but their meat makes a rich stew. Bring fresh meat to Alanndarian, and she will share her recipe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong lives in Auberdine, in Darkshore. She offers to teach her strider stew recipe to travelers who prove their hunting skill.",al={"alanndarian","who is alanndarian nightsong","stew cook auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find the strider meat?",a="Hunt foreststriders across Darkshore for their meat. The large, flightless birds range along the shorelines and through wooded groves outside Auberdine.",al={"strider meat location","where are foreststriders","how to get strider meat"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="You hunt foreststriders and bring five cuts of meat to Alanndarian Nightsong. In return, she teaches you to prepare Strider Stew.",al={"why do easy strider living","quest purpose","easy strider living objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the foreststriders dangerous to hunt?",a="Foreststriders have sharp beaks and quick legs, and they grow aggressive when approached. Hunt with care.",al={"are striders hard to kill","foreststrider danger"},it="danger"},{q="Does this quest unlock a cooking recipe?",a="Yes. Bring Alanndarian the meat she asks for, and she teaches you the recipe for Strider Stew.",al={"do i get recipe","strider stew recipe","cooking reward"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You begin and end in Auberdine, and hunt in the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"quest zone","where is easy strider living"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want this done?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong has an empty cooking pot and an appetite for fresh strider stew. Before she is willing to part with her secret recipe, she insists on seeing whether you have the mettle to hunt the tallbirds yourself and bring back fresh cuts for her cooking fire.",al={"alanndarian motive","why does alanndarian want strider meat","why strider stew"},it="motive",add="64984ff6"},{q="What is the Strider Meat used for?",a="The succulent meat is the core ingredient in Alanndarian's savory strider stew. Bringing her five cuts fills her empty kettle and proves to her that you have earned the right to learn her secret wilderness recipe.",al={"what is strider meat for","why strider meat","strider meat use"},it="item",add="624f04e5"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook traveling through Darkshore, you can learn to prepare Strider Stew from local wildlife.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf in Kalimdor, you know the value of living off the land. Strider stew is a coastal staple in Auberdine.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can practice tracking and hunting swift foreststriders along Darkshore's misty paths."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cooking","darkshore","easy strider living","foreststrider","strider meat","strider stew"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=2178,ri={"Strider Meat"}},src={"Easy Strider Living"}}
E["quest:3524"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, sea creatures are washing ashore in growing numbers. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde studies the deaths from Auberdine for the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, where priestesses fear the strandings may be an ill omen.",h="Along Darkshore, sea creatures are washing ashore in growing numbers.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Omen",b="Great sea creatures have sometimes beached themselves on Darkshore. It is a tragic sight, but it has been occasional. Now they wash ashore in growing numbers along the coast. The Priestesses of Elune in the Temple of the Moon fear these deaths may bring ill omens to northern Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="The Temple of the Moon sends scholar Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde to the port town of Auberdine to learn why the great beasts come ashore. Based there, she gathers biological samples to send by hippogryph to Darnassus for close examination. Greymist murlocs swarm the carcasses in the surf, scavenging the remains. Without armed protection, researchers cannot reach the bones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are giant sea creatures washing up on Darkshore?",a="The Temple of the Moon is still investigating why giant sea creatures wash ashore on Darkshore. Such strandings happen now and then, but their sudden increase has led night elf scholars to fear a deeper disturbance or ill omen beneath the Great Sea.",al={"why beached creatures","sea creature strandings","dying sea beasts"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is an investigator sent from Darnassus by the Temple of the Moon. Based in Auberdine, she catalogs coastal anomalies and collects samples from beached leviathans to send to the priesthood for study.",al={"gwennyth","who is gwennyth bly'leggonde"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the creature south of Auberdine lie?",a="The creature's bones lie on the shoreline a short march south of the Auberdine docks. Greymist murlocs surround the great carcass in the surf and guard it.",al={"creature location","sea creature bones location","where is the beached beast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What will Darnassus do with the sea creature bones?",a="Hippogryphs carry the bones directly to Darnassus. Scholars and priestesses at the Temple of the Moon study the marrow, structure, and signs of decay to learn whether disease, foul magic, or unnatural predation drove the beast ashore.",al={"why collect bones","purpose of sea creature bones","darnassus bones"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Greymist murlocs gathered around the carcass?",a="The Greymist murlocs use the stranded giants as an easy source of food, tools, and bonecraft. They claim the carcasses, making an unarmed approach life-threatening for scholars.",al={"murlocs at whale","why murlocs around creature"},it="target"},{q="Does this investigation conclude after retrieving the first set of bones?",a="No. The carcass south of town is the first site. Gwennyth continues her research with further inquiries into other leviathans that have died along Darkshore's long, mist-shrouded coast.",al={"is this a chain","washed ashore follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want this done?",a="Gwennyth was dispatched by Darnassus's Temple of the Moon to investigate an alarming surge of giant sea beasts beaching themselves along Darkshore. She views this sudden spike in strandings as an ill omen for the region and urgently needs skeletal remains so scholars in the capital can determine what drives these majestic creatures ashore.",al={"gwennyth motive","why help gwennyth","why study beached creatures"},it="motive",add="d10a93c6"},{q="Why can't Gwennyth collect the sea creature bones herself?",a="While Gwennyth is a capable researcher for the Temple of the Moon, she lacks the martial might to fight her way past the aggressive Greymist murlocs swarming the shoreline. The local sentinels have their hands full protecting Auberdine itself, so she relies on visiting adventurers to retrieve specimens from infested waters.",al={"why does gwennyth need me","why cant gwennyth get bones","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="a35c5129"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The coastal strandings disturb Darkshore's balance. The Sisterhood of Elune intervenes directly from Darnassus.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you know the Sisterhood of Elune must read spiritual omens and natural imbalances. Gwennyth seeks to decipher those signs in the sea creature's remains.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can read the mass death of marine life as a warning of ecological discord along the Kalimdor coast, one that calls for watchful attention."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","greymist murlocs","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","washed ashore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=3524,ri={"Sea Creature Bones"}},src={"Washed Ashore"}}
E["quest:4681"] = {t="quest",n="Washed Ashore",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, dead sea creatures have drawn Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde into a troubling inquiry. She serves the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus and seeks the cause of the strandings and deaths.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, dead sea creatures have drawn Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde into a troubling inquiry.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Tide",b="Dead sea creatures line Darkshore's beaches and shallows, leaving the night elves of Auberdine puzzled. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde has already examined one stranded creature on the beach. Now she asks you to dive west of the docks, near a sunken vessel, and inspect the bones of a massive sea turtle. Those remains will help her report to the Temple of the Moon.",sp=0},{t="Flight from the World Tree",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde hopes to gather enough physical evidence for a formal report to the Priestesses of Elune in Darnassus. Her early findings suggest the sea creatures may be fleeing something in the open sea. The danger may lie in the waters around Teldrassil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are sea creatures washing ashore in Darkshore?",a="The cause remains unknown. Gwennyth needs samples from the stranded creatures for a report to the Temple of the Moon and to continue her research.",al={"why turtles dying","beached creatures darkshore","why beached whales"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher in Auberdine who reports to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. She is recording the wave of dead and beached sea creatures along Darkshore's coast.",al={"gwennyth","auberdine researcher","quest giver washed ashore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the skeletal sea turtle located?",a="The skeletal sea turtle lies on the ocean floor due west of Auberdine's docks, near the wreckage of a sunken vessel off Darkshore's coast.",al={"turtle remains location","where skeletal turtle","sea turtle bones"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What does the Temple of the Moon have to do with this?",a="The Temple of the Moon directs night elf ecological and spiritual matters. Gwennyth needs physical samples for a formal report to the priestesses about the strange die-off.",al={"why darnassus care","temple of the moon role","priestesses of elune involvement"},it="ties"},{q="Are there more beached creatures to find?",a="Yes. Gwennyth says beached creatures lie along the Darkshore coastline and asks you to search the sands for remains from other stranded behemoths.",al={"other beached sea creatures","more sea creature quests","darkshore beached behemoth"},gp=true},{q="What is the difference between the two 'Washed Ashore' quests?",a="The first Washed Ashore asks you to examine a creature stranded on a nearby beach. The follow-up sends you west of the docks to inspect a submerged skeletal sea turtle.",al={"washed ashore part 1 vs part 2","two washed ashore quests","washed ashore chain"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the sea turtle remains investigated?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is investigating the dead and beached sea creatures along Darkshore. She asks you to recover samples from the skeletal turtle west of Auberdine so she can file a report with the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"gwennyth bly'leggonde motive","why investigate the turtle","why does gwennyth want this"},it="motive",add="6f0a7268"},{q="What are the Sea Turtle Remains used for?",a="The remains serve as critical scientific and spiritual evidence for the night elves. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde and the Temple of the Moon intend to examine the bones to uncover signs of disease, corruption, or trauma. These samples allow researchers in Darnassus to piece together why large marine creatures are stranding themselves or dying off the coast, helping the priesthood understand the broader ecological threat facing the shores of northern Kalimdor.",al={"sea turtle remains purpose","what is sea turtle remains for","why sea turtle remains"},it="item",add="23091480"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may read the mass deaths and erratic flight of Darkshore's ancient sea creatures as signs of corruption or a disruption in nature's balance around Teldrassil.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you support the Priestesses of Elune at the Temple of the Moon. They oversee the spiritual and natural well-being of northern Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Auberdine as the gateway between Teldrassil and the mainland. Evidence that ocean life is fleeing your new home is a troubling omen."},kw={"auberdine","beached creature","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea turtle","sea turtle remains","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:940","quest:2519","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4681,ri={"Sea Turtle Remains"}},src={"Washed Ashore (2)"}}
E["quest:4722"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, a Beached Sea Turtle lies among the surf as murlocs scavenge its remains. Auberdine naturalists seek sound samples to send to Darnassus for study.",h="Along Darkshore, a Beached Sea Turtle lies among the surf as murlocs scavenge its remains.",sec={{t="A Stranded Leviathan",b="Dead sea turtles drift ashore along Darkshore’s coast, or beach themselves in confusion. Their remains soon draw scavengers. Greymist murlocs have made crude camps around this turtle’s skeletal frame and carve away its flesh and shell. Yet bone, shell, or tissue may remain intact in the wreckage.",sp=0},{t="Field Research for Darnassus",b="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde works in Auberdine as a field researcher, recording unusual marine life and disturbances along the coast. Night elves regard stranded beasts with reverence and scientific curiosity. Suitable remains are cataloged and prepared for shipment to scholars in Darnassus. They seek to learn why so many giants of the open sea wash ashore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many beached sea creatures in Darkshore?",a="Strong coastal currents and turbulent waters drive debris and dying sea beasts onto Darkshore’s sand. Night elf scholars suspect disturbances in the deep ocean are drawing marine life toward the shallows, so local naturalists study each corpse that washes ashore.",al={"why dead sea turtle","darkshore beached creatures","why stranded"},it="danger"},{q="Who wants the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher in Auberdine, gathers washed-up samples for naturalists and scholars in Darnassus.",al={"who do i turn this in to","gwennyth auberdine","where to turn in turtle remains"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="Greymist murlocs scavenge what washes onto the beaches. A giant turtle offers abundant meat, tough hide, and bone for tools and shelters.",al={"murlocs near turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camp"},it="threat"},{q="What happens to the samples once Gwennyth receives them?",a="Gwennyth packages viable tissue and skeletal samples for transport across the sea to Darnassus. Scholars and priestesses examine them to monitor the coastal ecosystem’s health and behavior.",al={"what does darnassus do with remains","turtle sample research"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this the only beached creature along the coast?",a="No. Darkshore’s long coast holds multiple beached sea turtles and stranded sea behemoths. Several yield research specimens for Auberdine’s scholars.",al={"other beached animals","more dead turtles","washed ashore creatures"},it="place"},{q="Are sea turtles sacred to the night elves?",a="Night elves revere Kalimdor’s native beasts as part of the natural balance under Elune and the wild gods. Sea turtles are not solitary divine avatars, but their unexpected deaths and beachings warn of grave ecological trouble.",al={"night elf turtles","druids and turtles"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gwennyth want the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is gathering specimens for scholars in Darnassus who are investigating Darkshore's blighted coastline. A rash of dead marine life has washed ashore, and by studying uncontaminated tissue from beached creatures before scavengers ruin them, researchers hope to uncover what sickness or disruption in the sea drove these great beasts ashore to die.",al={"why take sea turtle remains","why study turtle remains","gwennyth turtle motive"},it="motive",add="d6ac85f8"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know unexplained beachings of ancient sea creatures signal deeper disruption in Kalimdor’s waters. Researchers in Auberdine and Darnassus investigate each washed-up leviathan.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see stranded sea life and scavenging murlocs as signs of ecological imbalance along Darkshore. That calls for close observation and healing."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","darnassus","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:3524","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4722},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (1)"}}
E["quest:4723"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="At Mist's Edge, a giant sea thresher lies stranded as murlocs feed on its carcass. In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde gathers samples for night elf researchers in Darnassus, who seek to learn why deep-sea giants wash ashore.",h="At Mist's Edge, a giant sea thresher lies stranded as murlocs feed on its carcass.",sec={{t="A Giant on the Shallows",b="Along Mist's Edge, enormous thresher remains have joined the shipwrecks and debris washed in by the tide. The beast dwarfs the wildlife of Darkshore's shallows. Its size suggests it came from beyond the Veiled Sea, from waters far from the calm waters here. Murlocs swarm over the corpse, but they lack the strength and coordination to bring down such a creature. Something else killed the predator before the sea carried it ashore.",sp=0},{t="Studies in Darnassus",b="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde coordinates the salvage of bones and biological samples from Darkshore's stranded sea giants. Night elf researchers in Darnassus hope the remains will show whether illness, disturbances in the deep sea, or arcane corruption drives the giants onto the killing sands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of beast washed up on the shore?",a="A giant thresher washed ashore, far larger than the threshers usually seen near Darkshore's beaches.",al={"what creature is this","what is the dead monster","what animal is dead on the beach"},it="identity"},{q="Did the murlocs kill it?",a="No. Murlocs swarm the carcass to feed, but even in large groups they are too weak to hunt a deep-water beast of that size.",al={"did murlocs kill the thresher","did murlocs kill the sea creature"},it="history"},{q="Why are sea creatures stranding themselves along Darkshore?",a="The cause is unknown. Night elf researchers suspect ocean disturbances, disease, or ecological distress may drive deep-sea creatures into shallow surf, where they become stranded and die.",al={"why are threshers dying","why do creatures beach themselves"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher in Auberdine. She collects bones and biological samples from beached wildlife along Darkshore for study in Darnassus.",al={"who is gwennyth","who takes the bones in auberdine"},it="people"},{q="Where are the collected bones sent?",a="The collected bones go to scholars and naturalists in Darnassus, where they are examined for anatomical and magical clues.",al={"where do bones go","what does auberdine do with bones"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is this carcass located?",a="The carcass lies on the sandy shore of Mist's Edge, along Darkshore's western coast.",al={"carcass location","where is the beached sea creature"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, strandings along Darkshore signal trouble in the surrounding waters. Naturalists in Auberdine and Darnassus are investigating before more marine life perishes.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see the stranded giant as an alarming sign of disturbance in the Veiled Sea's natural balance."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","mist's edge","murloc","sea creature","thresher"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:mist-s-edge","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus","topic:murloc"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=4723},src={"Beached Sea Creature (1)"}}
E["quest:4725"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's shore, a broken carriage rests on the shell of a Beached Sea Turtle. Greymist murlocs gather around the great carcass.",h="Along Darkshore's shore, a broken carriage rests on the shell of a Beached Sea Turtle.",sec={{t="A Beast in Harness",b="You find a broken carriage strapped across a giant sea turtle's shell on Darkshore's misty shore. Many sea creatures have washed up along this coast, but this turtle carried a load. Its handlers drove it onto the beach. Now the carriage lies abandoned in the tide.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers of the Shallows",b="Greymist murlocs swarm the turtle's remains. They have made a den among the rotting meat and scavenged timber. A marked container lies among their refuse and the broken carriage frame. The turtle's former masters left it there.",sp=0},{t="Naga Supply Lines",b="After you bring the marked container to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine, its naga markings reveal the truth. The harness matches the supply carriages the naga use to carry weapons and war material from the ocean depths. The turtle's remains show that the naga are making incursions into northern Darkshore. The recovered container is sent to Darnassus for study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is there a carriage on the sea turtle's shell?",a="The naga harness giant sea turtles as pack animals and siege beasts. Their carriages carry supplies and weapons from the depths to Darkshore's coast.",al={"turtle carriage","why carriage on turtle","harnessed turtle"}},{q="What is inside the carriage?",a="A strangely marked box lies in the broken carriage. Its runes mark it as naga property, and scholars in Auberdine send it to Darnassus for scrutiny.",al={"turtle box","strangely marked box","box in turtle carriage"},it="item"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle?",a="Greymist murlocs live along the coast and scavenge shipwrecks and beached carcasses. They have claimed the turtle's remains for food and a den.",al={"murlocs around turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","why murlocs eating turtle"},it="threat"},{q="Who studies the beached creatures in Darkshore?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine oversees the investigation into the beached sea creatures. She catalogs the relics and strange materials found among their remains.",al={"who studies beached sea creatures","auberdine researcher","gwennyth bly'leggonde role"},it="people"},{q="How does this turtle differ from other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Unlike many creatures that wash ashore sick or distressed, this turtle was harnessed to carry cargo. The naga drove it onto the beach.",al={"other beached turtles","why this turtle different","turtle mystery darkshore"}},{q="What happens to the marked box after Auberdine?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde records the discovery in Auberdine and sends the naga box to Darnassus. Elven leaders there study the growing threat along their northern borders.",al={"where does box go","box sent to darnassus","what does auberdine do with box"},it="next_step"},{q="Why bring the marked box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Unlike other marine carcasses washing ashore along Darkshore, this turtle was clearly harnessed as a beast of burden. The abandoned carriage and its strangely marked cargo suggest an organized, hostile force rather than natural strandings. Taking the relic to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine allows the night elf researchers to study the markings, assess the creeping coastal threats, and forward their findings to Darnassus.",al={"why bring box to auberdine","why take turtle box to gwennyth","beached turtle box motive"},it="motive",add="4b167599"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see that naga supply beasts are washing up on Darkshore. Your ancestral enemies are reinforcing beachheads close to Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Auberdine's sentinels learn from beached creatures. Their findings track murloc infestations and organized naga raiding parties."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carriage","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","naga","sea turtle","strangely marked box"},rel={"quest:4722","npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:naga","topic:murloc","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4725},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (2)"}}
E["quest:4727"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore’s northern shore, a Beached Sea Turtle lies untouched by nearby Greymist murlocs. A sample goes to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine for the Temple of the Moon. Naturalists and priestesses seek to learn why great sea creatures wash ashore and scavengers leave them alone.",h="Along Darkshore’s northern shore, a Beached Sea Turtle lies untouched by nearby Greymist murlocs.",sec={{t="A Curious Absence",b="Greymist murlocs crowd Darkshore’s northern coast and scavenge food washed up from the Veiled Sea. Yet the great turtle’s bones lie mostly untouched. Those who study the shore wonder whether the murlocs missed it or avoid it for some unknown reason.",sp=0},{t="Study of the Shoreline",b="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde gathers samples from beached sea turtles for the Temple of the Moon. The night elf priestesses study disturbances in Darkshore’s waters. Skeletal fragments may help them learn whether sickness, magic, or dangerous sea predators are killing the ancient creatures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the beached sea turtle?",a="The remains of an ancient sea turtle have washed ashore in northern Darkshore. Its unusual presence and the absence of scavengers have drawn the night elves’ attention.",al={"turtle carcass","sea turtle skeleton","what is this turtle"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the murlocs avoiding the carcass?",a="Greymist murlocs usually scavenge beach carcasses, but they have left these remains alone. No one knows whether they missed the turtle or avoid it for an unknown reason. Gwennyth considers their absence worth remembering as the remains are studied.",al={"why aren't murlocs eating it","greymist murlocs turtle","why avoid carcass"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf researcher in Auberdine. She gathers samples of Darkshore’s beached sea life for the Temple of the Moon.",al={"gwennyth auberdine","who wants turtle remains","turtle quest turn in"},it="people"},{q="Why does the Temple of the Moon care about beached sea creatures?",a="The Temple of the Moon studies beached sea creatures because unusual numbers are dying along Darkshore. Its priestesses examine samples to learn what is harming the seas.",al={"temple of the moon turtle","why study turtles","elune marine life"},it="motive"},{q="Where is this particular sea turtle located?",a="The carcass lies on Darkshore’s northern coast, near territory inhabited by Greymist murloc tribes.",al={"where is the turtle","beached sea turtle location","turtle darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are there other beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Several beached sea creatures, including giant sea turtles, lie along Darkshore’s shores. Auberdine’s researchers are investigating why these ocean giants are dying.",al={"other beached creatures","more sea turtles","beached sea creature quests"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see unexplained deaths and scavengers avoiding sea creatures along Darkshore. These signs point to a growing imbalance in kaldorei lands.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you watch the coastline closely. Murlocs leaving the dead untouched may point to an unnatural taint in the waters.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you extend Elune’s care to all living things. You investigate deaths that disturb nature’s balance."},kw={"auberdine","beached","carcass","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","remains","sea turtle","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:murloc","quest:4722","quest:2519"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4727},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (3)"}}
E["quest:4728"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, a giant sea mammal lies washed ashore beside an abandoned dig site. Its carcass and scattered tools draw murlocs and travelers.",h="Along Darkshore, a giant sea mammal lies washed ashore beside an abandoned dig site.",sec={{t="A Halted Excavation",b="On Darkshore's sand lies a giant sea mammal, partly gutted and worn by the sea. A rusted wheelbarrow and discarded tools mark where an orderly study began. The researchers left before they could finish.",sp=0},{t="The League and the Murlocs",b="Dwarven field researchers from the Explorer's League were studying the carcass in Darkshore. Their work stopped when local murlocs swarmed the site to scavenge. In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde acts for the Temple of the Moon. She accepts salvaged bone samples to help study the unnatural wash-ups along the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is this creature lying on the beach?",a="The remains are those of a giant sea mammal washed ashore on Darkshore. No one has identified its species. Its size has drawn scavenging murlocs and dwarven researchers.",al={"beached sea creature identity","what is this carcass","what died here"},it="identity"},{q="Who left the tools and wheelbarrow behind?",a="Dwarven members of the Explorer's League left the tools. They began studying the beached creature, but hostile coastal murlocs drove them away before they could finish.",al={"who left the tools","abandoned wheelbarrow darkshore","who was digging here"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want these bones?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde collects samples for the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. The night elves are investigating the strange deaths of massive sea creatures washing ashore along Darkshore.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creature","auberdine sea bones"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are murlocs prowling around the carcass?",a="Murlocs came to scavenge the carcass for meat and blubber. They chased off the dwarven scholars and now defend the remains for themselves.",al={"murlocs around carcass","why are murlocs here","murloc scavengers"},it="danger"},{q="Is the Explorer's League officially allied with Auberdine here?",a="Yes. The Explorer's League is part of the Alliance and has a presence in Darkshore. It works with local night elf authorities and shares reports of its discoveries and coastal investigations.",al={"explorers league auberdine","dwarves in darkshore","explorers league alliance darkshore"},it="allies"},{q="Are there other beached creatures along the Darkshore coast?",a="Yes. Enormous marine beasts and skeletal remains have washed ashore along Darkshore's beaches. They point to widespread disturbance in the waters off Kalimdor.",al={"more beached creatures","other carcasses darkshore","multiple beached sea creatures"},it="place"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The abandoned tools belong to your kin in the Explorer's League. Native murlocs chased them from their dig site.",["race:NightElf"]="The Temple of the Moon is deeply concerned by the unnatural number of massive sea creatures dying and washing ashore on Darkshore's sacred coast.",["faction:Alliance"]="This discovery shows Darnassus and the Ironforge Explorer's League working together to record Kalimdor's mysteries."},kw={"auberdine","beached","bones","darkshore","explorers league","gwennyth","murloc","sea creature"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","quest:4723","quest:2519"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4728},src={"Beached Sea Creature (2)"}}
E["quest:4730"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, a great sea mammal lies half-devoured on the sand. Murlocs gather around it, and Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine seeks bone samples to learn why gentle sea beasts are dying on the shore.",h="Along Darkshore, a great sea mammal lies half-devoured on the sand.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Shoreline Discovery",b="Far north along Darkshore's lonely beaches, a great sea mammal lies rotting and half-eaten. Murlocs pick over its bones, more vicious than usual. These beasts were gentle in life, and their deaths trouble the coast as much as the blighted forests inland.",sp=0},{t="Uncharacteristic Stranding",b="Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde says these gentle mammals live in the waters around Teldrassil's base. Unlike aggressive threshers, they have never been known to drive themselves onto the rocks. The Temple of the Moon is gathering bone samples to learn what corruption or threat drives them from the deep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature washed up here?",a="The remains are those of a large, gentle sea mammal that usually lives in the deep waters around Teldrassil's base. These peaceful giants do not usually beach themselves.",al={"what animal is this","what is the beached creature","sea monster bones"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the sea creature beach itself?",a="No one knows why the sea creature beached itself. Priestess Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde says such strandings are unnatural for this species, and night elf researchers suspect a disturbance or corruption in the seas is disorienting them or driving them from their home waters.",al={"why did it beach","why are sea creatures dying","darkshore strandings"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a Temple of the Moon priestess stationed in Auberdine. She is coordinating an inquiry into the coastline, gathering bones to study the affliction harming local sea life.",al={"who turns in this quest","who is gwennyth","auberdine priestess"},it="people"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the corpse?",a="The murlocs have gathered around the corpse for an easy meal. This band is stronger and more aggressive than murlocs living closer to Auberdine.",al={"why murlocs here","murlocs near bones","beach murlocs"},it="hostile"},{q="Where does this creature normally live?",a="These sea mammals live in the open waters around Teldrassil's great boughs and roots. In ordinary times, they rarely approach the mainland shore.",al={"where do these live","sea mammal habitat","teldrassil sea creatures"},it="place"},{q="How does this relate to other beachings in Darkshore?",a="Several kinds of sea life have washed ashore along Darkshore, including carnivorous threshers and giant sea turtles. Threshers are naturally turbulent, but gentle mammals beaching themselves shows that the trouble affects species across the coastal ecosystem.",al={"other beached sea creatures","beached thresher","beached sea turtle"},it="conflict"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, these strandings wound their reverence for natural harmony. The waters around their new home of Teldrassil are growing troubled.",["class:Priest"]="The Temple of the Moon oversees this inquiry and seeks divine insight into the corruption troubling Kalimdor's waters.",["class:Druid"]="For the Cenarion Circle, any change in sea life is a dire omen of an unnatural blight poisoning coastal wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Protecting the shores around Auberdine helps secure Alliance shipping lanes between Darkshore, Teldrassil, and the eastern kingdoms."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","sea creature bones","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","quest:4723","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:2519","subzone:temple-of-the-moon"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=4730},src={"Beached Sea Creature (3)"}}
E["quest:4731"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, a Beached Sea Turtle lies dead beneath the carriage it once hauled. A box marked with strange runes rests in the wreckage.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, a Beached Sea Turtle lies dead beneath the carriage it once hauled.",sec={{t="A Beast of Burden",b="A dead sea turtle lies among the ancient bones along Darkshore's coast. Splintered carriage boards cling to its broad shell. It was driven onto the rocks while hauling cargo, not stranded by sickness or confusion. A container carved with unfamiliar, serpent-like marks lies in the wreckage, where scavengers feed on the remains.",sp=0},{t="The Naga Incursion",b="In Auberdine, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde recognizes the box's craftsmanship as naga work. The naga send great sea beasts ashore with provisions and weapons during their attacks from the water. The wreck lies along Darkshore's southern shore, and Gwennyth suspects the turtle carried supplies toward Ashenvale. Its end may mean the naga have reached farther across northern Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does this sea turtle have a carriage on its back?",a="The naga fitted the carriage to the turtle and used giant sea turtles as living pack animals. They carried supplies, weapons, and war materiel from the ocean depths onto land.",al={"turtle carriage","why turtle has cart","sea turtle harness"},it="item"},{q="Who is currently inhabiting the remains?",a="Powerful Greymist murlocs have taken over the giant shell since the turtle died. They use its hollowed remains as a fortified seaside shelter.",al={"who lives in turtle","greymist murlocs turtle","what is guarding turtle"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Strangely Marked Box go?",a="Bring the box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, an emissary of the Temple of the Moon stationed in Auberdine.",al={"where do i take the box","strangely marked box","turn in marked box"},it="next_step"},{q="What do the markings on the box mean?",a="The markings are naga script. They show that the box and carriage belonged to a naga supply convoy moving along the coast, likely toward Ashenvale before disaster struck.",al={"turtle box lore","who made the marked box","naga box"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon interested in beached turtles?",a="The priestesses of Elune are investigating threats to Darkshore's coast, both environmental and military. Recovered artifacts like this box go to Darnassus, where scholars can map hostile movements.",al={"why temple wants turtles","gwennyth darkshore mission"},it="motive"},{q="Where was the turtle traveling before it died?",a="From the carcass's place along the coast, Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde suspects the naga were directing the laden turtle south, possibly toward Ashenvale.",al={"turtle destination","where was turtle going"},sp=1,it="place"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you know the naga's use of sea life to carry war supplies outrages the kaldorei. These tracks help the Temple of the Moon follow threats toward Ashenvale.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you see a noble sea turtle forced to carry weapons of war, then left to rot among scavengers. The naga show little regard for wild beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help alert Auberdine and Darnassus to naga supply routes that threaten northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","beached sea turtle","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","naga","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","topic:naga","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4731},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (4)"}}
E["quest:4732"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Turtle",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore, Beached Sea Turtle remains wash ashore in growing numbers. Their bones give Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine specimens to study as Kalimdor's marine life dwindles.",h="Along Darkshore, Beached Sea Turtle remains wash ashore in growing numbers.",sec={{t="A Strand of Bones",b="Great sea creatures and turtles lie along Darkshore's shore. Many ancient turtles drift onto the shoals or crawl onto the sand to die. Greymist murlocs gather at the carcasses and strip away the flesh. Soon, only shell and bone remain, beside crude camps they make there.",sp=0},{t="Vanishing Waters",b="Before the Third War, sea turtles thrived in the sacred waters around Mount Hyjal and the roots of Nordrassil, the World Tree. After Nordrassil's sacrifice against the Burning Legion and Teldrassil's planting off Kalimdor's northern shore, their numbers collapsed.\n\nGwennyth Bly'Leggonde and other priestesses of Elune study the remains for the Temple of the Moon. They seek to learn whether dark magic, changing seas, or the loss of the turtles' ancient sanctuary drives them to their deaths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are sea turtles beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="The night elves do not know why sea turtles beach themselves. They once thrived in the waters beneath Nordrassil, the World Tree. Since Nordrassil's destruction in the Third War and the raising of Teldrassil, their numbers have plummeted, and many seem to end their lives along Darkshore's shoals by choice.",al={"why do turtles die here","darkshore turtle mystery","why beached"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde is a night elf scholar and representative of the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine. She catalogs and studies washed-up sea creatures to uncover why Darkshore's wildlife is suffering.",al={"who is gwennyth","where to turn in turtle remains","auberdine researcher"},it="identity"},{q="Why are murlocs gathered around the turtle remains?",a="Greymist murlocs scavenge the enormous carcasses for food and materials. They often make shoreline settlements beside beached sea turtles and other sea creatures, then strip the remains clean.",al={"why murlocs on turtle","greymist scavengers","murloc camps on beach"},it="why_here"},{q="What connection do these turtles have to Nordrassil?",a="Night elves say sea turtles were once common in the pristine waters around Mount Hyjal and Nordrassil, the World Tree. Nordrassil's violent destruction disrupted the natural balance, and sightings of the turtles fell sharply afterward.",al={"nordrassil connection","hyjal turtles","mount hyjal turtle link"},it="history"},{q="Does Teldrassil have anything to do with their decline?",a="The priesthood has seen sea turtles in ever-decreasing numbers since Teldrassil began to grow. The Temple of the Moon studies whether the new World Tree has altered coastal currents, disrupted migration, or bears an unnatural aura that affects ocean life.",al={"teldrassil effect on turtles","why did teldrassil change turtles"},it="threat"},{q="Are there multiple beached creatures along Darkshore?",a="Yes. Darkshore's long coastline holds many beached sea creatures and turtles. Each carcass offers bone and tissue samples for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde to study as she pieces together the ecological disaster unfolding along the shore.",al={"more beached quests","other beached turtles","beached sea creatures"}},{q="Why does Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde want the sea turtle remains?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde studies the remains on behalf of the Temple of the Moon in Auberdine. Sea turtles once flourished around the base of Mount Hyjal and Nordrassil, but ever since Teldrassil was planted, their numbers have plummeted and stranded carcasses have begun washing ashore along Darkshore. She collects these salvageable specimens hoping biological study will reveal why the creatures are perishing.",al={"why collect sea turtle remains","why does gwennyth want turtle bones","sea turtle remains purpose"},it="purpose",add="ad0e3c15"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, these ancient ocean dwellers stranded on shore signal nature out of balance after the battle at Mount Hyjal and Teldrassil's arrival.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the Temple of the Moon seeks to honor and understand the creatures that once played beneath Nordrassil's boughs.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you help the Sisterhood of Elune diagnose the spiritual sickness spreading through Kalimdor's waters by retrieving these remains."},kw={"auberdine","beached","darkshore","greymist","gwennyth bly'leggonde","murloc","nordrassil","sea turtle","teldrassil","temple of the moon"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","topic:nordrassil","quest:940","topic:murloc","quest:4722"},m={start="Beached Sea Turtle",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4732},src={"Beached Sea Turtle (5)"}}
E["quest:4733"] = {t="quest",n="Beached Sea Creature",z="darkshore",s="A colossal thresher lies stranded on Darkshore's rocky Twilight Shore. Its death and stranding deepen the sea troubles worrying the night elves.",h="A colossal thresher lies stranded on Darkshore's rocky Twilight Shore.",sec={{t="A Giant Cast Ashore",b="Along the Twilight Shore in southern Darkshore, driftwood and sea debris wash into the inlets. In one, you find the remains of an enormous thresher. Tides and scavengers have begun to pick it apart, yet its skeleton dwarfs the ordinary predators in these coastal shallows. The giant does not belong in these waters. Sickness or disorientation may have driven it onto the rocks, or a deeper disturbance may lie in the Veiled Sea.",sp=0},{t="The Temple's Vigil",b="In Auberdine, priestesses of the Temple of the Moon study the dead giants washing ashore. Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde oversees the gathering of skeletal samples to learn why deep-dwelling predators are dying. Colossal threshers once appeared near the roots of Teldrassil, but their numbers have steadily fallen. The priestesses fear the balance of life in the sea off Kalimdor's northern coast is unraveling.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of beast is this beached carcass?",a="The carcass is the skeleton of an immense predatory sea beast called a thresher. It is several times larger than the common threshers along Darkshore's coast.",al={"what is the beached sea creature","giant thresher darkshore","beached monster carcass"},it="identity"},{q="Where did this creature originally come from?",a="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde says creatures of this immense size once roamed the waters near Teldrassil's roots, but their numbers have steadily declined. This thresher is not native to Darkshore's immediate shallows.",al={"where do giant threshers live","thresher origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Temple of the Moon studying these carcasses?",a="The Temple of the Moon studies the carcasses to understand why sea beasts are washing ashore along Darkshore. By examining bones and remains, the priestesses hope to learn whether corruption, disease, or outside forces are driving deep-sea creatures onto land.",al={"why does gwennyth want bones","temple of the moon sea creatures","why study beached animals"},it="motive"},{q="Where should the bones be brought?",a="Bring the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde, a night elf researcher in Auberdine's harbor town.",al={"where to turn in sea creature bones","who gets the thresher bones"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Where on the coast is this carcass located?",a="The carcass lies in a rocky inlet along the Twilight Shore, on Darkshore's southern coast.",al={"where is the beached creature","thresher location darkshore","twilight shore skeleton"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Are there other creatures beaching themselves in Darkshore?",a="Yes. Several kinds of sea beasts and behemoths have washed ashore along Darkshore's coast, prompting researchers in Auberdine to investigate.",al={"other beached animals","beached sea creature questline"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The unexplained decline and beaching of sea life near Teldrassil troubles the Kaldorei. They look to Elune and the Temple of the Moon for meaning in such omens.",["class:Priest"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde studies the sea under the Temple of the Moon. She seeks balance and divine insight through close inquiry into its waters.",["class:Druid"]="The stranding of great sea predators signals an ecosystem in distress. The Cenarion Circle shares this concern throughout Darkshore."},kw={"auberdine","beached sea creature","darkshore","gwennyth bly'leggonde","sea creature bones","temple of the moon","thresher","twilight shore"},rel={"npc:gwennyth-bly-leggonde","zone:darkshore","subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:4723","quest:3524","quest:940","topic:elune"},m={start="Beached Sea Creature",["end"]="Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde",level="19",faction="Alliance",id=4733},src={"Beached Sea Creature (4)"}}
E["quest:4740"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Murkdeep!",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine's council wants Murkdeep dead for a Sentinel's death and ships lost off Darkshore. Find the Greymist chieftain south along the coast.",h="Auberdine's council wants Murkdeep dead for a Sentinel's death and ships lost off Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Mist-Shrouded Shoals",b="Greymist murlocs are usually a nuisance along Darkshore. Murkdeep has turned against Auberdine, and the wanted poster outside the inn names him as the killer of at least one night elf Sentinel. It also suspects him of sabotaging or wrecking two cargo vessels offshore. With ships lost and raids along the coast, the Auberdine Village Council has set a public bounty on their leader.",sp=0},{t="The Ambush at the Huts",b="Murkdeep lurks off the southern coast near murloc huts clustered around a bonfire. Trespassers face an organized defense as Greymist coastrunners and shore-crawlers surge from the surf to protect their settlement. Then Murkdeep emerges with his vanguard to strike the intruders.",sp=0},{t="Justice for the Fallen",b="Proof of Murkdeep's death answers the Sentinels' grim need. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea handles the council's bounty payout. With Greymist leadership broken, travelers and ships on Darkshore's foggy coast gain a reprieve from sabotage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I pick up the bounty on Murkdeep?",a="Find the wanted poster outside the inn in central Auberdine, in Darkshore.",al={"where to start wanted murkdeep","murkdeep quest start","auberdine wanted poster"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Auberdine council offering a bounty on Murkdeep?",a="The Auberdine council offers the bounty because Murkdeep killed at least one night elf Sentinel and is suspected of sinking two cargo vessels off Darkshore.",al={"why kill murkdeep","what did murkdeep do","murkdeep crimes"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Murkdeep?",a="Murkdeep is far south of Auberdine, along the beach by three murloc huts around a bonfire.",al={"murkdeep location","where is murkdeep","murkdeep camp"},gp=true},{q="Why isn't Murkdeep at the murloc camp when I arrive?",a="Murkdeep stays out of sight. Step between the huts near the bonfire, and Greymist murlocs surge from the ocean in waves. Murkdeep appears with the final wave, after the first defenders fall.",al={"murkdeep not there","murkdeep spawn","how to summon murkdeep"},gp=true},{q="Who turns in the quest once Murkdeep is dead?",a="Report Murkdeep's death to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea, on duty in Auberdine.",al={"who to turn in murkdeep","murkdeep turn in","glynda nalshea location"},gp=true},{q="Are the murlocs at this camp different from other murlocs in Darkshore?",a="Murkdeep commands the Greymist murlocs, including coastal scouts and warriors who defend their seaside encampment in coordinated waves.",al={"greymist murlocs","murkdeep tribe","what murlocs are with murkdeep"},gp=true},{q="Who is Murkdeep and why is he a target?",a="Murkdeep is an exceptionally dangerous murloc chieftain who guards the Greymist murloc huts along the Darkshore coast south of Auberdine. Unlike ordinary shore-dwelling pests, he is officially blamed for the death of at least one night elf Sentinel and suspected of orchestrating the sinking of two cargo ships off the coast. His lethality makes him a priority threat to Auberdine's maritime safety and coastal defense.",al={"who is murkdeep","why target murkdeep","what did murkdeep do"},it="target",add="715f24d2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf defending Darkshore, you avenge a fallen Sentinel and protect the lifeline Auberdine's docks provide.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Auberdine is a vital northern trade hub. The cargo ships Murkdeep is suspected of sinking deal a costly blow to Alliance logistics in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","greymist","murkdeep","murloc","sentinels","wanted poster"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc","topic:sentinels"},m={start="WANTED: Murkdeep!",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4740,ri={"Murkdeep"}},src={"WANTED: Murkdeep! (quest)"}}
E["quest:4761"] = {t="quest",n="Thundris Windweaver",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver hears that the Blackwood furbolgs have grown hostile. Terenthis sends you with news of their growing aggression, and Thundris seeks the cause of the corruption spreading through Darkshore.",h="In Auberdine, Thundris Windweaver hears that the Blackwood furbolgs have grown hostile.",sec={{t="A Report to the Elder",b="You bring Terenthis’s report to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine after scouting corrupted furbolg camps in Darkshore. Terenthis stays in the wilds to investigate the spreading corruption. As village elder, Thundris watches over daily life and weighs the spiritual and environmental dangers facing the kaldorei. Your report gives Auberdine’s leaders proof that the furbolgs’ troubles reach beyond territory: an unnatural malice is taking hold of them.",sp=0},{t="Corruption Along the Coast",b="Thundris has heard that the forest dwellers near Auberdine have grown hostile. Yet the furbolgs are not his only concern. Corruption spreads through Darkshore’s soil, plants, and waters. Thundris believes the land cannot heal until someone finds the source of the blight. So he turns to the waterways and calls on capable allies to trace the taint upstream.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver leads Auberdine as its elder and oversees the town’s governance and daily affairs. He works with sentinels and druids to understand and fight the corruption spreading through Darkshore.",al={"thundris windweaver","auberdine elder","who is thundris"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Terenthis send you to Thundris?",a="Terenthis sends you to brief Auberdine’s leaders after you scout the Blackwood furbolg camps. Thundris Windweaver has theories about the madness affecting wildlife and furbolgs, and needs firsthand news to coordinate a response.",al={"why go to thundris","terenthis report","auberdine report"},it="motive"},{q="What is happening to the furbolgs in Darkshore?",a="Corruption has made Darkshore’s furbolgs increasingly violent. Their hostility comes from a taint poisoning the land, not merely from disputes over territory.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","furbolg hostility","why are furbolgs mad"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Elder Windweaver suspects Darkshore’s waters may carry the source of the rot. He sends you to sample the Cliffspring River and find where the contamination begins.",al={"next quest","what after thundris","cliffspring river quest"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Auberdine is the kaldorei’s main port and foothold on the mainland coast. Bringing news to Elder Windweaver supports your people’s effort to preserve their sacred wilderness.",["class:Druid"]="The swift corruption of local furbolgs and forest dwellers signals a severe imbalance in the land. Cenarion allies and village elders cannot ignore it.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Auberdine safe from hostile woodland tribes protects Alliance supply lines and travelers crossing between Kalimdor and Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","furbolg","terenthis","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","quest:4762","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4761},src={"Thundris Windweaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:4762"] = {t="quest",n="The Cliffspring River",z="darkshore",s="Foul water now runs down the Cliffspring River toward Auberdine. Thundris Windweaver sends Alliance investigators to collect a sample from the pool beneath a road bridge waterfall. He suspects the corruption began beyond the riverbanks.",h="Foul water now runs down the Cliffspring River toward Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Tainted Waterway",b="From the eastern highlands, the Cliffspring River runs to the coastal shoals of Mist's Edge, just north of Auberdine. Now its waters carry an unnatural rot toward the night elf settlement. Thundris Windweaver fears the foul water will poison the shores and the town's supplies. So he sends scouts upriver to take samples from the waterfall pool beneath the road bridge.",sp=0},{t="The Root in Felwood",b="The Blackwood furbolgs have made camps along the river, and their agitation is plain. Thundris suspects they may be spreading the taint, but believes its true root lies elsewhere, in Felwood. He expects the water sample to confirm his suspicion.\n\nThe forest to the east was scarred during the Third War. To cleanse the water, the corrupted furbolgs must be confronted and the land's ancient sources purified.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I collect the water sample?",a="From Auberdine, head north to the Cliffspring River's mouth at Mist's Edge. Follow the river inland to the first waterfall beneath an overhead road bridge, then fill the sampling tube from the pool.",al={"where is the water sample","cliffspring river location","waterfall pool location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Cliffspring River turning foul?",a="Thundris suspects the Blackwood furbolgs along the river may be spreading the foulness, though he believes their corruption has a deeper root. He needs a water sample to investigate.",al={"why is river corrupted","what is poisoning darkshore water","cliffspring taint source"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and investigator in Auberdine. He studies Darkshore's spreading ecological decay and seeks the causes of regional corruption.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives cliffspring river quest"},it="identity"},{q="Are the furbolgs responsible for poisoning the river?",a="Thundris suspects the Blackwood furbolgs may be spreading the taint, but believes their corruption has a deeper source. The water sample will help him investigate.",al={"did furbolgs taint the water","blackwood furbolg corruption"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="How does this river impact Auberdine?",a="The Cliffspring River flows into Mist's Edge just north of Auberdine. Coastal currents may carry the foul runoff to the town's shoreline, threatening its fisheries, flora, and freshwater supply.",al={"threat to auberdine","why does auberdine care about cliffspring"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after testing the sample?",a="Thundris thanks you for the sample and prepares to investigate the corrupted Blackwood furbolgs further. He hopes to find a way to cleanse their taint.",al={"quest after cliffspring river","what follows cliffspring river"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver fears that the corruption spreading down the Cliffspring River will wash out into Mist's Edge and taint Auberdine itself. While he suspects the local Blackwood furbolgs have poisoned the river, he believes a deeper, older darkness is behind their madness. He needs raw evidence to diagnose the taint and formalize a plan of action before the settlement's waters are completely ruined.",al={"why thundris water sample","thundris windweaver motive","why clean cliffspring river"},it="motive",add="1995e089"},{q="What is the Cliffspring River Sample for?",a="The Cliffspring River Sample allows Thundris Windweaver to inspect the foulness creeping into Darkshore's waterways. Examining the tainted water gives him the physical proof he needs to test its properties, investigate its deeper origin, and prepare an eventual cure.",al={"cliffspring river sample use","what is the water sample for","why collect water sample"},it="item",add="1f8a1dfc"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you see clean woodland waters turned foul by lingering demonic taint. You are called to cleanse Darkshore's wounded nature.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Auberdine depends on Darkshore's coastline. If the spreading rot reaches Mist's Edge, it threatens Kaldorei homes and livelihoods."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","cliffspring","darkshore","felwood","river","taint","thundris","waterfall","windweaver"},rel={"quest:4761","quest:4763","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","subzone:mist-s-edge","zone:felwood","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=4762,ri={"Cliffspring River Sample"}},src={"The Cliffspring River"}}
E["quest:4763"] = {t="quest",n="The Blackwood Corrupted",z="darkshore",s="In northern Darkshore, the Blackwood Corrupted are caught in a dark influence. Evidence in the tainted waters of Cliffspring River leads Thundris Windweaver to send you against it. You gather their food and purify it with moonwell water, drawing the demonic handler into the open and breaking his hold on the northern camp.",h="In northern Darkshore, the Blackwood Corrupted are caught in a dark influence.",sec={{t="A Hidden Master",b="In Auberdine, the night elves have long wondered why the once-peaceful Blackwood furbolgs turned on their neighbors. Their search along Cliffspring River traced the rot to satyr meddling. These ancient servants of the Burning Legion manipulate the tribe with fel magic. Insidious talismans twist the furbolgs' minds and drive them into feral aggression.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Shackles",b="Thundris Windweaver prepares a remedy to draw the puppet master out. You gather grain, fruit, and nuts from the northern Blackwood settlement, then soak them in holy water from Auberdine's moonwell. The water purifies the tainted food. Set it by the central bonfire, and nearby furbolgs find brief respite from madness. Xabraxxis, the satyr corruptor, emerges in fury to defend his hold over the camp.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the Blackwood furbolgs aggressive?",a="The furbolgs' minds have been poisoned by demonic influence. Satyrs secretly planted themselves near the camps and channel foul magic through enchanted talismans. This twists the furbolgs' natural instincts into rabid violence.",al={"why furbolgs mad","why are furbolgs hostile","blackwood aggression"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Xabraxxis?",a="Xabraxxis is a satyr corruptor who oversees the northern Blackwood furbolg camp. He works from the shadows to keep the tribe gripped by fel madness, using a Talisman of Corruption to sustain his control.",al={"xabraxxis lore","who is the satyr","satyr boss darkshore"},it="target"},{q="Does cleansing their food cure the furbolgs forever?",a="No. Moonwell-infused food breaks the demonic haze only long enough for the furbolgs to know peace and draw out Xabraxxis. Slaying the satyr and claiming his talisman is a significant victory, but Thundris Windweaver says a permanent cure for the corrupted tribes will take more effort.",al={"is the cure permanent","did we save the furbolgs","are furbolgs cured"},sp=1},{q="Where did the idea to use moonwell water come from?",a="Moonwells are sacred pools blessed by the Goddess Elune. Their rejuvenating magic counters fel and undeath. Thundris Windweaver provides a cleansing bowl so the sanctified water can neutralize the demonic toxins woven into the furbolgs' food.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell cleansing bowl"},it="history"},{q="What happens when the food bowl is placed at the bonfire?",a="The nearby furbolgs briefly break free of their bloodlust. They gather peacefully around the blessed food and stop attacking. Enraged that his puppets are escaping their torment, Xabraxxis appears at once to punish the meddlers.",al={"bowl near bonfire","cleansing the furbolgs"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf researcher and investigator stationed in Auberdine. He coordinates efforts to uncover the causes of Darkshore's creeping ecological decay and the madness gripping local wildlife.",al={"thundris windweaver lore","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want this done?",a="Thundris Windweaver sees the furbolgs not merely as dangerous beasts, but as ancient allies driven mad by dark magic. The night elves believe that purging the demonic influence gripping the Blackwood tribe is crucial to restoring the balance of Darkshore's forests. By identifying the root of the corruption and stripping the satyrs of their power, Thundris hopes to save the furbolgs from permanent spiritual ruin.",al={"why help thundris","thundris windweaver goal","why purify the furbolgs"},it="motive",add="dd154993"},{q="What is the Talisman of Corruption for?",a="The Talisman of Corruption is a sinister demonic relic channeled by the satyr to subvert the natural will of the furbolgs. Through it, corruptors twist the minds of the Blackwood tribe, maintaining a relentless magical grip that drives them to madness and hostility. Thundris needs it seized and destroyed to break that hold and reclaim the forest.",al={"talisman of corruption purpose","what does the talisman of corruption do","satyr talisman"},it="item",add="3c287e3e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The furbolgs were long friends of the kaldorei. Seeing them fall under the sway of their ancestral enemies, the satyrs, is a bitter tragedy night elves are eager to set right.",["class:Druid"]="Restoring balance means cutting out the rot at its root. A satyr's fel talismans warp primal woodland creatures, making the Cenarion Circle's confrontation with Xabraxxis urgent.",["class:Priest"]="Channeling Elune's pure, restorative grace through moonwell water stands in stark contrast to the corrupting shadow and fel magic the satyr wields."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","furbolg","moonwell","satyr","talisman of corruption","thundris windweaver","xabraxxis"},rel={"quest:4762","quest:4761","topic:furbolg","topic:satyr","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=4763,ri={"Talisman of Corruption"}},src={"The Blackwood Corrupted"}}
E["quest:4811"] = {t="quest",n="The Red Crystal",z="darkshore",s="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea asks you to investigate a red crystal in Darkshore's eastern mountains. Moonkin are multiplying nearby and seem drawn to it, and the Sentinels need to know whether the crystal is real.",h="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea asks you to investigate a red crystal in Darkshore's eastern mountains.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Shift in the Wilds",b="Moonkin were once gentle, mystical creatures bound to Kalimdor's wilds. Now aggressive packs multiply along the slopes east of Auberdine. Some night elves still revere them, but Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea puts the town's safety first as danger grows. Reports point to a single spot among the eastern peaks.",sp=0},{t="The Eastern Mountain Anomaly",b="Scouts and wanderers speak of an unnatural red crystal jutting from a rocky hillside high above Darkshore. Rumors travel easily along the fogbound coast, so Glynda wants you to see the place for yourself. The crystal is real. The Sentinels still need to learn why moonkin gather there and whether it threatens the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the red crystal in Darkshore?",a="The red crystal is a glowing formation embedded in Darkshore's eastern mountains. The Sentinels know little of its origins, but local wildlife, especially moonkin, seem drawn to it.",al={"what is red crystal","darkshore crystal","red rock auberdine"},it="item"},{q="Who sends you to look for the red crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine sends you to investigate. She helps defend the settlement and wants confirmation of reports from the eastern mountains.",al={"who gives the red crystal quest","glynda nalshea quest","auberdine crystal quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why are moonkin behaving aggressively around the crystal?",a="Moonkin, once regarded as gentle and mystical, have grown territorial and volatile. Glynda suspects the crystal is tied to their changed behavior and growing numbers.",al={"why are moonkin mad","angry moonkin darkshore","moonkin hostile"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The crystal lies east of Auberdine, high on Darkshore's eastern mountain ridge, where moonkin prowl nearby.",al={"where to find red crystal","red crystal location","darkshore red crystal map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the crystal considered dangerous by the night elves?",a="Glynda is wary of the crystal. She does not know whether it is benign or sinister, but its effect on the wild beasts already concerns Auberdine's safety.",al={"is the crystal bad","is red crystal evil"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after you discover the crystal?",a="Telling Glynda the crystal is real confirms the reports. She then seeks to learn what it is, beginning efforts to cleanse and sample it with water from Auberdine's moonwell.",al={"what is after red crystal","as water cascades follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea want the red crystal found?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea is tasked with safeguarding Auberdine. While moonkin were once revered as gentle and mystical beings, their numbers east of the town are surging and they have turned increasingly aggressive. Rumors suggest the creatures are congregating around a mysterious red formation in the eastern mountains. Glynda needs to confirm whether the crystal actually exists so she can assess whether it poses a direct danger to Auberdine and determine why the wild moonkin are so strangely drawn to it.",al={"why glynda nal'shea wants red crystal","sentinel glynda motives","why find the red crystal"},it="motive",add="79e10640"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you may find the agitated moonkin troubling. Your people revere them as sacred wards of Elune and nature.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you have close spiritual ties to moonkin and Darkshore's natural order. The crystal's disruptive pull threatens the balance you care for.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you rely on Auberdine as a key coastal port on northern Kalimdor. A threat growing unchecked in the hills could isolate the haven from the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","moonkin","red crystal","sentinels"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4813","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4811},src={"The Red Crystal"}}
E["quest:4812"] = {t="quest",n="As Water Cascades",z="darkshore",s="At Auberdine, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea hopes moonwell water will reveal what lies beneath Darkshore's red crystal. Sacred water may pierce its opaque surface.",h="At Auberdine, Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea hopes moonwell water will reveal what lies beneath Darkshore's red...",sec={{t="Purifying the Unknown",b="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea seeks a safe way to study the red crystal high on Darkshore's eastern cliffs. Moonwell water bears divine, restorative magic, blessed by the night elves' devotion to Elune. Glynda believes water from Auberdine's moonwell may react with the strange stone and pierce its opaque shell without destroying it.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of Felwood",b="Felwood's corruption makes the eastern ridge a dangerous place to investigate. Demonic energies twisted the forest above Darkshore during the Third War, and Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea fears the red spire may be linked to that corruption. As sacred water trickles over the crystal's lattice, the humming stone briefly turns transparent. What lies within calls for a closer look.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I get the water for this quest?",a="Draw water from Auberdine's moonwell with the empty vial Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea provides. Auberdine is the night elf settlement.",al={"where is the moonwell","moonwell water location","fill empty water tube"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does moonwell water affect the crystal?",a="Moonwells hold consecrated water rich with magic, blessed by Elune. Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea expects its purifying essence to react with the stone's foreign energy and reveal its hidden composition.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell magic on crystal"},it="power"},{q="Where is the red crystal located?",a="The red crystal rests along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall, set into the rocky foothills between the shore and the highlands above.",al={"red crystal location","where is the crystal","red crystal darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Sentinel Glynda worried about Felwood?",a="Felwood lies east and above Darkshore, scarred by demonic corruption from the Third War. Since the crystal appeared near the boundary ridge, Glynda fears it may share that demonic origin.",al={"glynda felwood","connection to felwood"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you pour the water on the crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda expects potent moonwell water to reveal a clue to the crystal's composition. Its reaction becomes clear when you pour the water over it.",al={"pouring water result","what happens to the crystal"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who gives the quest As Water Cascades?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine gives you this work after the reconnaissance called The Red Crystal.",al={"quest giver","who starts as water cascades"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What is the Moonwell Water Tube for?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea provides the tube so you can collect purified water from Auberdine's moonwell and carry it to the mysterious red crystal. Moonwells hold potent, blessed magic capable of reacting with magical anomalies. By pouring the water over the strange stone, Glynda hopes its sacred energy will react with the structure and reveal clues about what it is made of—and whether it poses a danger to Darkshore.",al={"moonwell water tube purpose","why do i need moonwell water","moonwell water tube quest"},it="item",add="a7631f7f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you know moonwells as sacred fonts of life and solace. Their consecrated waters may reveal what lies within a strange formation, showing how Elune's grace helps untangle threats along your borders.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you watch over Darkshore's fragile ecosystem. Unnatural formations along the ridge below corrupted Felwood give you reason to distrust them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know the scouts based in Auberdine must keep the coast secure from corruption creeping down from the eastern highlands."},kw={"as water cascades","auberdine","darkshore","empty water tube","felwood","glynda nal'shea","moonwell","red crystal"},rel={"quest:4811","quest:4813","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","zone:felwood"},m={start="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",["end"]="Mysterious Red Crystal",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4812,ri={"Moonwell Water Tube"}},src={"As Water Cascades"}}
E["quest:4813"] = {t="quest",n="The Fragments Within",z="darkshore",s="At the eastern cliffs, you return to the red crystal with water from a moonwell. It may reveal what lies within, and you carry the finding back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",h="At the eastern cliffs, you return to the red crystal with water from a moonwell.",sec={{t="A Grim Revelation",b="Blessed moonwell water clears the cloudy face of the crimson crystal. Within its dense mineral lie several small bone fragments and half a humanoid jawbone. The crystal is so hard that even powerful spells would struggle to break it. Whatever entity or artifact left these remains, they have been preserved alone above the Darkshore coast.",sp=1},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Back in Auberdine, you tell Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea what you found. The discovery gives the local night elf leaders more cause for concern, but no clear answers. Glynda will present the findings to the town council. The crystal rests high on the eastern cliffs, far enough from town to bring her some comfort; it poses no immediate danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is trapped inside the red crystal?",a="Blessed moonwell water clears the red crystal enough to reveal several bone fragments and half a humanoid jawbone trapped inside.",al={"what is in the crystal","what are the fragments","what bones are inside"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Can the crystal be broken open to inspect the bones?",a="The crystal is exceptionally resilient, and even powerful magic would struggle to break it open. The bones' exact identity remains unknown.",al={"can you break the crystal","opening the red crystal"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Who do you report the findings to?",a="You report your findings to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in the port town of Auberdine.",al={"who turns in the fragments within","quest turn in","glynda nalshea"},it="next_step"},{q="What will the Sentinels do about the crystal?",a="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea plans to inform the council in Auberdine so its members can consider what to do. The crystal rests high in the eastern cliffs, so they do not see it as an urgent threat.",al={"what happens next with the crystal","auberdine council crystal"},sp=1,it="today"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know that humanoid bones trapped in strange crystal along the mountain borders of Ashenvale and Felwood call for vigilance from the Sentinels guarding Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see a curious anomaly in a mineral that resists natural wear and powerful magic alike. It lies beyond the usual balance of the wild."},kw={"auberdine","bone fragments","darkshore","glynda nal'shea","jawbone","moonwell water","mysterious red crystal"},rel={"quest:4812","quest:4811","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:felwood"},m={start="Mysterious Red Crystal",["end"]="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=4813},src={"The Fragments Within"}}
E["quest:5321"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeper Has Awakened",z="darkshore",s="Kerlonian Evershade struggles to stay awake on the road from Darkshore to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Newly roused from a long sleep, he carries the Horn of Awakening and needs help past furbolgs and cultists.",h="Kerlonian Evershade struggles to stay awake on the road from Darkshore to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Slumbering Mind",b="Kerlonian Evershade is a Druid of the Claw, newly awakened from sleep in the barrows. For millennia, druids communed with wild spirits through the Emerald Dream. The Third War called them to wake, but centuries of hibernation left Kerlonian struggling to stay conscious.\n\nHe set out south from Darkshore to meet Liladris Moonriver in Ashenvale, yet exhaustion soon overtook him. Sudden naps leave him helpless in the wilds, so he relies on a brass Horn of Awakening and passing allies to keep moving.",sp=0},{t="Peril Along the Road",b="The road from Darkshore into Ashenvale is dangerous for Kerlonian. In Twilight Vale, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs stalk the road. Farther south in Ashenvale, members of the Dark Strand cult lie in ambush. Sleep may lay Kerlonian down wherever he stands, so you need to keep watch and rouse him with the horn.",sp=0},{t="Arrival at the Outpost",b="Kerlonian Evershade reaches Maestra's Post after surviving the ambushes, then slips away to find a patch of grass for his interrupted nap. Liladris Moonriver, his contact, greets him with fond exasperation and little surprise at his dazed state. The waking world still jars many druids after the timeless quiet of the Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Kerlonian keep falling asleep?",a="Kerlonian Evershade keeps falling asleep because he only recently woke from centuries of hibernation in the Emerald Dream. The waking world leaves many druids disoriented and lethargic, and he struggles to stay awake without being roused.",al={"why is kerlonian sleeping","why is he so sleepy","druid falling asleep"},it="why_here"},{q="How do you wake Kerlonian up when he naps?",a="You can wake Kerlonian with the Horn of Awakening, found in a chest beside him when the journey begins. When he falls asleep along the trail, blow the horn to rouse him and let him continue.",al={"how to wake kerlonian","kerlonian horn","horn of awakening use"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is waiting for Kerlonian at Maestra's Post?",a="Liladris Moonriver is waiting for Kerlonian at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. She knows his chronic sleepiness and is relieved to see him arrive safely.",al={"who is liladris","who is kerlonian meeting"},it="target"},{q="What enemies attack along the way?",a="Blackwood furbolgs attack near Twilight Vale. Farther south in Ashenvale, excavators, adepts, and cultists of the Dark Strand strike from the shadows.",al={"ambushes during escort","what attacks kerlonian","twilight vale ambush"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the title 'The sleeper has awakened' come from?",a="“The sleeper has awakened” is a greeting spoken by Druids of the Claw when called into service during the Third War. The words point to Kerlonian's nature as an awakened shapeshifter.",al={"sleeper has awakened quote","druid voiceline"},it="origin"},{q="What happens to the horn if you take too long?",a="The Horn of Awakening vanishes from your possessions after a limited time. If the journey takes too long or must begin again after a failure, gather a replacement from the chest at Kerlonian's resting spot.",al={"horn expired","horn of awakening disappeared"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kerlonian Evershade need an escort to Maestra's Post?",a="Kerlonian is traveling south to reunite with Liladris Moonriver at Maestra's Post, but his long slumber in the Emerald Dream has left him chronically exhausted and disoriented. Unable to stay awake for long stretches and unfamiliar with the treacherous road into Ashenvale, he cannot safely make the journey alone without someone to guide him and stir him whenever he dozes off.",al={"why escort kerlonian","kerlonian evershade purpose","why go to maestras post"},it="motive",add="be04fcfa"},{q="What is the Horn of Awakening?",a="The Horn of Awakening is Kerlonian's personal enchanted instrument, kept stored in a chest by his campsite. Because awakening from the Emerald Dream has left him battling overwhelming fatigue, the horn's sharp call cuts through his lingering, magically heavy drowsiness to shake him awake whenever he collapses into a roadside slumber.",al={"horn of awakening lore","what does horn of awakening do","kerlonian horn"},it="item",add="9356c39d"},{q="Why does Kerlonian ask you for help instead of the night elf sentinels?",a="Kerlonian has stopped far from any fortified night elf outpost, isolated in the wilds of southern Darkshore. With Sentinel patrols stretched thin guarding against regional threats, no guards are stationed nearby to attend to a dozing druid. As a traveling adventurer passing through, you are his only immediate hope for a guide and protector on the road toward Ashenvale.",al={"why does kerlonian need me","why ask adventurer kerlonian","why not sentinels kerlonian"},it="why_me",add="b8969ed3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know deep communion with the Emerald Dream can take a heavy toll. Long hibernation can leave the waking mind slow to regain full consciousness.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share in the upheaval of Kerlonian's people. Thousands of druids answered the horn during the Third War and now adjust to daylight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help keep communication open between Auberdine and the outlying sentry posts by helping travelers pass safely between Darkshore and northern Ashenvale."},kw={"ashenvale","dark strand","darkshore","druid of the claw","evershade","horn of awakening","kerlonian","liladris","maestra's post","twilight vale"},rel={"npc:kerlonian-evershade","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:twilight-vale","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","quest:2561"},m={start="Kerlonian Evershade",["end"]="Liladris Moonriver",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=5321,ri={"Horn of Awakening"}},src={"The Sleeper Has Awakened (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5713"] = {t="quest",n="One Shot. One Kill.",z="darkshore",s="On the road to Auberdine, Sentinel Aynasha is ambushed and cannot carry her message onward. Poisoned by Marosh the Devious and his furbolg trackers, she must mix an antidote before she can travel.",h="On the road to Auberdine, Sentinel Aynasha is ambushed and cannot carry her message onward.",sec={{t="Ambush on the Forest Road",b="Sentinel Aynasha carries important communications toward Auberdine when hostile furbolgs intercept her on a trail in northern Kalimdor. Marosh the Devious leads them. Their venom leaves the scout unsteady and unable to continue on foot.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Aynasha knows how to make natural remedies, but the antidote takes time to mix and take effect. Marosh's trackers are closing in, so she needs travelers to guard her as she works. Though her strength is failing, she keeps her bow steady and fires into the brush to hold the attackers back.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="After Marosh is slain and the assault ends, the antidote restores enough strength for Aynasha to continue to Auberdine. She asks her protectors to carry word of the aggressive furbolgs threatening regional supply routes to Sentinel Onaeya at Maestra's Post, south in Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Aynasha?",a="Sentinel Aynasha is a night elf scout carrying important messages between Darkshore and Ashenvale. Skilled with a bow and woodland survival, she is poisoned in an ambush while on duty.",al={"sentinel aynasha","aynasha","who is aynasha"},it="identity"},{q="Who attacked Sentinel Aynasha?",a="A pack of hostile furbolgs led by Marosh the Devious attacks Sentinel Aynasha. They poison her in the clash, leaving her unable to move freely.",al={"who attacked her","marosh the devious","marosh","who poisoned her"},it="threat"},{q="Where was Sentinel Aynasha traveling?",a="Aynasha is traveling to Auberdine with an important dispatch when Marosh and his trackers trap her on the road.",al={"where was aynasha going","aynasha destination"},it="place"},{q="Why must you report to Sentinel Onaeya?",a="Aynasha needs to reach Auberdine with her message, so she asks you to go south to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale and alert Sentinel Onaeya to the furbolg hostility.",al={"sentinel onaeya","why maestra's post","onaeya"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in the area hostile?",a="Many furbolg tribes across Darkshore and Ashenvale have fallen to demonic taint and madness since the Third War. They attack traveling Sentinels and wayside travelers without distinction.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","furbolg hostility","corrupted furbolg"},it="hostile"},{q="Does Aynasha fight during the ambush?",a="Yes. The venom leaves Aynasha barely able to stand, but she fires her bow to cover her defender while preparing the antidote.",al={"does aynasha help","aynasha bow","does she fight"},gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Aynasha need your protection?",a="Aynasha carries an urgent message bound for Auberdine, but an ambush by local furbolgs left her struck by a debilitating poison. She is barely able to stand, much less complete her journey on her own. She needs you to stand guard and keep the attackers at bay long enough for her to concoct and administer an antidote so she can recover and see her mission through.",al={"why help aynasha","aynasha motive","why does aynasha need help"},it="motive",add="39e047c2"},{q="Who is attacking Sentinel Aynasha?",a="The ambush is led by Marosh the Devious and his pack of furbolg trackers. The corrupted furbolgs stalking these borders prey on vulnerable travelers along the road, and they struck Aynasha to cut down an isolated night elf messenger.",al={"who leads the ambush","who is marosh","aynasha attackers"},it="target",add="85f1ffa2"},{q="Why can't Aynasha fight off the furbolgs herself?",a="Although Aynasha is a skilled Sentinel archer and will support you with her bow, the venom coursing through her veins leaves her severely weakened and barely able to stand. She cannot manage close combat while simultaneously focusing on preparing her antidote, leaving her life entirely in your hands.",al={"why me aynasha","why does aynasha need me","why cant aynasha fight"},it="why_me",add="69f547c2"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you protect a fellow Sentinel and the important communications moving between outposts in Ashenvale and northern Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep woodland paths clear of aggressive furbolgs and safe for travel between Ashenvale and Alliance strongholds to the north.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see Aynasha's resolve in the shots she continues to fire into the brush while the venom weakens her."},kw={"ambush","antidote","aynasha","darkshore","furbolg","maestra's post","marosh","onaeya","sentinel"},rel={"npc:sentinel-aynasha","npc:sentinel-onaeya","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:furbolg","topic:elune"},m={start="Sentinel Aynasha",["end"]="Sentinel Onaeya",faction="Alliance",id=5713},src={"One Shot. One Kill."}}
E["quest:6122"] = {t="quest",n="The Principal Source",z="darkshore",s="At Cliffspring Falls, sick deer have drawn the Cenarion Circle to the water. Dendrite Starblaze sends young druids from Moonglade to gather a sample for Auberdine naturalist Alanndarian Nightsong.",h="At Cliffspring Falls, sick deer have drawn the Cenarion Circle to the water.",sec={{t="A Vital Waterway Corrupted",b="Cliffspring Falls feeds northern Darkshore with fresh water. When deer began to suffer a lingering sickness, the Cenarion Circle looked to the river for its cause. Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade suspects the water is tainted. He sends novice druids to gather a sample at the cavern mouth beneath the falls.",sp=0},{t="Shadows at the Falls",b="Vicious naga dwell inside Cliffspring River Cave, near the falls' headwaters. Their presence endangers anyone who comes to study the blight. The Cenarion Circle needs a sample from the cave mouth to learn what is making the wilderness sick.",sp=0},{t="A Deeper Malady",b="In Auberdine, Alanndarian Nightsong finds that the water sample confirms the Circle's fears. The corrupted falls are poisoning the riverbanks, yet sick deer have also been seen beyond the water's direct path.\n\nThe sample may help begin an antidote. Alanndarian suspects a wider corruption is spreading through Darkshore's water table.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="Cliffspring Falls supplies fresh water to northern Darkshore. Its headwaters feed local streams and rivers, so contamination can spread through the surrounding land and wildlife.",al={"why cliffspring falls matters","cliffspring river importance","darkshore water source"},it="place"},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore falling ill?",a="The deer drink from Cliffspring Falls and the streams it feeds. The water is tainted at its source, and the pollutant is making woodland creatures sick.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sick deer","what poisoned the deer"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is an elder druid trainer in Moonglade. He guides young druids, watches for disturbances across Kalimdor, and coordinates the Cenarion Circle's response to natural crises.",al={"dendrite starblaze lore","who gave me this quest","starblaze moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf naturalist in Auberdine. Concerned by the corruption and suffering wildlife in Darkshore, she asked the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade for help studying the affliction and finding a cure.",al={"who is alanndarian nightsong","nightsong auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why are naga at Cliffspring Falls?",a="Naga from the Darkshore coast have moved inland and occupied the cave system behind Cliffspring Falls. Their presence endangers anyone trying to reach the headwaters and investigate the water.",al={"naga in cliffspring cave","why are naga here","cliffspring falls naga"},it="threat"},{q="What ability does this quest help druids learn?",a="The investigation is part of the Power over Poison trial. By studying the wildlife sickness and working with Alanndarian Nightsong on an antidote, druid initiates learn to cure poisons.",al={"what spell does this give","druid poison quest","cure poison chain"},it="power"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze want this done?",a="As an emissary of the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade, Dendrite Starblaze is bound to protect the natural balance of Kalimdor. Alanndarian Nightsong reached out from Auberdine seeking aid against a virulent sickness poisoning Darkshore's wildlife. Dendrite suspects the contamination originates at Cliffspring Falls, the region's main freshwater source, and must confirm its source to help create a cure.",al={"dendrite motive","why does dendrite send me","why investigate cliffspring falls"},it="motive",add="df1ca1a8"},{q="What is the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler for?",a="The sampler holds corrupted water drawn directly from the cave mouth at Cliffspring Falls. Delivering it to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine allows her to analyze the precise nature of the poison afflicting Darkshore's wildlife and begin concocting an effective cure.",al={"filled cliffspring falls sampler use","what is the water sample for","why collect cliffspring water"},it="item",add="87aa05d6"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you instead of handling it himself?",a="Dendrite serves as a key liaison for the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade, coordinating broader druidic efforts across Kalimdor. Investigating the source and collaborating with Alanndarian on the ground in Darkshore offers an essential field trial for an advancing druid learning to wield power over poison.",al={"why me dendrite","why does dendrite need druids","why send an initiate"},it="why_me",add="00d3706a"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you face the decay at Cliffspring Falls and help prepare remedies. This trial teaches you how to cure poisons in the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Auberdine, you see Cliffspring Falls' corruption threaten your ancestral forests and the creatures that live there."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring falls","cure poison","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","naga","power over poison"},rel={"quest:6125","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:alanndarian-nightsong","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:cenarion-circle","quest:947"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6122,ri={"Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler"}},src={"The Principal Source (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6123"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering the Cure",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, sick deer need a salve, and Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine shows a young druid how to make one. The remedy calls for water and healing plants gathered nearby.",h="In Darkshore, sick deer need a salve, and Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine shows a young druid how to make...",sec={{t="A Remedy for Darkshore's Wildlife",b="Alanndarian Nightsong seeks a cure for Darkshore's sick deer. A contaminated water source has harmed the local wildlife, so sampled Cliffspring water will form the salve's base. Natural ingredients with healing power must complete the mixture. The deer cannot recover alone, and the Cenarion Circle needs a remedy soon.",sp=0},{t="Roots and Lunar Blooms",b="Earthroot and Lunar Fungus lend healing power to the salve. Earthroot grows in rocky soil, where a practiced herbalist's eye helps find it. Lunar Fungus blooms in caves east of Auberdine. The moonkin there have grown territorial and agitated, making the gathering more dangerous.",sp=0},{t="The Path to Poison Cleansing",b="Alanndarian Nightsong teaches the initiate how much care it takes to brew a remedy for a specific toxin. Each step in gathering and preparing the ingredients demands care. The lesson prepares the druid to cleanse poisons with nature magic, without a separate brew for each one.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Gathering the Cure?",a="A druid initiate gathers Earthroot and Lunar Fungus for Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine. The ingredients make a curative salve for Darkshore's sick deer, while the work teaches how remedies can counter poisons.",al={"why do this quest","gathering the cure goal","what is gathering the cure for"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Lunar Fungus grow?",a="Lunar Fungus grows in caves in the hills directly east of Auberdine. Wild moonkin there have grown territorial and aggressive.",al={"where is lunar fungus","lunar fungus location","how to find lunar fungus"},gp=true},{q="Do I need to be an herbalist to get Earthroot?",a="You do not need Herbalism to obtain Earthroot, though it grows in wild herb patches. Without the skill, you need to trade with an herbalist or get the herb from someone else for Alanndarian's recipe.",al={"need herbalism for earthroot","can non herbalists get earthroot","earthroot without profession"},gp=true},{q="Who is Alanndarian Nightsong?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong is a night elf in Auberdine who called on the Cenarion Circle for aid. She watches over Darkshore's plants and animals and guides young druids through their first trials to cleanse and protect the wilds.",al={"who is alanndarian","alanndarian nightsong lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="Darkshore's deer drank water tainted by a contaminated spring. The poison leaves them suffering, unable to recover without a curative salve.",al={"why are deer poisoned","sick deer darkshore","what poisoned the deer"},it="origin"},{q="How does this quest help me learn Cure Poison?",a="The training teaches initiates the care needed to prepare herbal antidotes for individual poisons. The Cenarion Circle uses that lesson to prepare druids to channel nature magic that can neutralize poison.",al={"cure poison quest druid","learn cure poison","power over poison chain"},it="power"},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want this done?",a="As a druid watching over Darkshore from Auberdine, Alanndarian cannot stand idly by while the native wildlife suffers. The local deer have succumbed to a debilitating affliction and cannot recover on their own. Crafting an effective curative salve is her immediate priority to halt their agony and restore balance to the corrupted woods.",al={"alanndarian motive","why help sick deer","why does alanndarian care"},it="motive",add="0cfb14cd"},{q="What is the Earthroot for?",a="Alanndarian uses the earthroot to imbue her curative salve with restorative properties. Mixed into the water sample drawn from Cliffspring Falls, which serves as the salve's base, the natural medicinal essence of the herb counteracts the toxins sickening the Darkshore deer.",al={"why earthroot","what does earthroot do","earthroot salve"},it="item",add="e3b496ec"},{q="What is the Lunar Fungus for?",a="The lunar fungus provides the necessary potency for the salve. Its potent natural bloom amplifies the mixture's curative strength, ensuring the remedy is powerful enough to purge the deep-seated poison affecting the afflicted deer.",al={"why lunar fungus","lunar fungus purpose","fungus for salve"},it="item",add="74e6ce3c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you learn how ordinary remedies work against natural toxins. That knowledge prepares you to channel curative power without relying on tools.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you have the trained eye Alanndarian values for finding Earthroot in the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you share the kaldorei duty to protect Darkshore's sacred groves and wildlife, in reverence for Elune and the spirits of the wild."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cure poison","darkshore","druid quest","earthroot","gathering the cure","lunar fungus","moonkin caves"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","quest:6125","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6123,ri={"Earthroot","Lunar Fungus"}},src={"Gathering the Cure (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6124"] = {t="quest",n="Curing the Sick",z="darkshore",s="Across Darkshore, deer are falling sick, and Curing the Sick brings you a way to help them. Alanndarian Nightsong gives you salve for the poisoned animals before you report to the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade.",h="Across Darkshore, deer are falling sick, and Curing the Sick brings you a way to help them.",sec={{t="A Plague in the Woodlands",b="Deer are falling sick across Darkshore, from the Cliffspring River south to the border of Ashenvale. They wander the misty woods, weakened by toxins in the soil and streams. After you gather the needed reagents, Alanndarian Nightsong gives you freshly brewed animal salve to treat them.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Unveiled in Moonglade",b="After you treat ten deer, you report to Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade. Auberdine gains some relief, but Dendrite sees the herds’ sickness as a sign of deeper corruption spreading across northern Kalimdor. He warns that leaders in Darnassus debate while the rot advances. The Cenarion Circle must stay alert to its reach across the continent.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are the deer in Darkshore sick?",a="Corruption in Darkshore’s soil and water is making the deer sick, from the Cliffspring River south to Ashenvale. They graze on tainted plants and drink the affected water, growing weak and diseased.",al={"why are deer sick","darkshore sickly deer","what poisoned the deer"},it="threat"},{q="Who prepares the curative salve used on the deer?",a="Alanndarian Nightsong prepares the curative animal salve in Auberdine from reagents you gather. Her batch has ten doses for the suffering animals, while she and the townsfolk try to make more.",al={"who makes the cure","alanndarian salve","curative animal salve maker"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze care about the deer?",a="Dendrite Starblaze oversees druid training for the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade. Caring for the deer tests a druid’s duty and confirms that dangerous corruption is spreading through Kalimdor’s wilderness.",al={"why dendrite moonglade","cenarion circle interest in deer","dendrite starblaze role"},it="purpose"},{q="What political tension does Dendrite Starblaze hint at?",a="Dendrite says some night elf authorities in Darnassus recognize the growing rot, while others ignore its warning signs. He urges you to face the hard truths about the natural world.",al={"darnassus tension","who ignores the corruption","darnassus blinders"},it="conflict"},{q="Where can the sickly deer be found?",a="Sickly deer roam across Darkshore, from south of the Cliffspring River, just north of Auberdine, to the border of Ashenvale.",al={"sickly deer location","where are the deer","darkshore deer location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does a druid learn from completing this task?",a="You learn to cleanse poison through practical work. Treating suffering forest animals with a physical cure joins botanical remedies with spiritual mastery over poison.",al={"what does this teach druids","cure poison training druid","lesson of curing the sick"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Alanndarian Nightsong want the deer cured?",a="Alanndarian sees Darkshore's wildlife suffering under an insidious and spreading affliction. While she remains behind in Auberdine to rally the villagers and brew more medicine, she needs an able druid to act immediately in the field. Tending to the afflicted deer halts their suffering before the sickness wipes out local herds entirely.",al={"alanndarian motive","why cure the deer alanndarian","alanndarian nightsong darkshore deer"},it="motive",add="5b53be21"},{q="Why does Alanndarian ask you instead of having the Auberdine guards cure the deer?",a="Auberdine's townspeople and Sentinels are tied up defending the settlement and working with Alanndarian to produce more salve. Furthermore, calming wild, feverish animals requires the steady hand and empathy of an initiate of the Cenarion Circle. As a druid in training, you are uniquely suited to minister directly to the beasts of the wild.",al={"why ask me alanndarian","why not auberdine sentinels","why send a druid to cure deer"},it="why_me",add="73042015"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you prove your commitment to preserving balance and prepare to purge poisons with druidic magic.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Darkshore as the edge of your people’s settled lands. Sickness among its deer is an ominous sign for the kaldorei."},kw={"alanndarian nightsong","auberdine","cenarion circle","cliffspring river","curative animal salve","curing the sick","darkshore","dendrite starblaze","poison","sickly deer"},rel={"npc:alanndarian-nightsong","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6125","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:5921","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid"},m={start="Alanndarian Nightsong",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=6124,ri={"Sickly Deer"}},src={"Curing the Sick (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:6341"] = {t="quest",n="The Bounty of Teldrassil",z="darkshore",s="Nessa Shadowsong is comparing Teldrassil's fish with the mainland catch. She sends samples from Rut'theran Village to Auberdine to learn whether the island fish are larger and more plentiful.",h="Nessa Shadowsong is comparing Teldrassil's fish with the mainland catch.",sec={{t="A Fisherman's Study",b="Nessa Shadowsong asks you to carry fish bones and scales to Laird in Auberdine. Fishers in Rut'theran Village bring in large, plentiful catches. Nessa wants to learn whether the mainland waters yield the same kind of fish. The samples let Laird compare the island catch with fish from the coast of Darkshore.",sp=0},{t="Arranging Passage",b="Nessa Shadowsong sends you to Vesprystus, the hippogryph master in Rut'theran Village, with the collection for Auberdine. Give him the samples, and he arranges your passage across the water to Darkshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Nessa trying to investigate?",a="Nessa Shadowsong wants to compare the large, plentiful fish caught around Rut'theran Village with fish from the mainland coast of Darkshore. She sends bones and scales for Laird to compare.",al={"nessa goal","why compare fish","bounty of teldrassil purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is receiving the fish samples in Auberdine?",a="Laird, a fish vendor in Auberdine, receives the collection from Nessa Shadowsong.",al={"who gets nessa collection","laird darkshore","auberdine fish vendor"},it="target"},{q="Why take the parcel to Vesprystus instead of traveling directly to Auberdine?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master in Rut'theran Village. Nessa sends you to him with the collection so he can arrange passage across the water to Darkshore.",al={"why vesprystus","who is vesprystus","hippogryph master ruttheran"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Rut'theran Village located in relation to Teldrassil?",a="Rut'theran Village sits at the southern base of Teldrassil, at sea level. An emerald portal connects it to Darnassus, and its harbor serves ships and hippogryphs traveling to and from the great tree.",al={"rut'theran location","where is nessa shadowsong","how to reach ruttheran"},it="place"},{q="What happens after giving the collection to Vesprystus?",a="After Vesprystus accepts the collection, he offers Flight to Auberdine. A hippogryph carries you across the strait to Darkshore.",al={"flight to auberdine next","after bounty of teldrassil","what does vesprystus do"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this part of leaving the starting zone for Night Elves?",a="Yes. This chain introduces young night elf adventurers to flight paths and guides them from Teldrassil to Darkshore, where they continue their journeys.",al={"leaving teldrassil","level 10 night elf quest","moving to darkshore"},gp=true},{q="Why does Nessa Shadowsong need you to deliver the collection?",a="Nessa Shadowsong is tending to her duties and research among the docks of Rut'theran Village. With travelers regularly departing the island, handing her parcel of specimens to an able adventurer heading toward Darkshore is far simpler than abandoning her work to arrange transport across the sea herself.",al={"why me nessa","why does nessa need help","why send an adventurer to vesprystus"},it="why_me",add="4163d491"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elf travelers, the journey leads from the heights of Teldrassil to the mainland shores of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the route between Rut'theran and Auberdine links the night elf capital with the rest of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","bounty of teldrassil","darkshore","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","vesprystus"},rel={"quest:6344","quest:6342","npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Nessa Shadowsong",["end"]="Vesprystus",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6341},src={"The Bounty of Teldrassil"}}
E["quest:6342"] = {t="quest",n="Flight to Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="You carry unusual fish specimens from Teldrassil to Auberdine for Laird. Vesprystus sends you from Rut'theran Village by hippogryph.",h="You carry unusual fish specimens from Teldrassil to Auberdine for Laird.",sec={{t="Taking Wing to Darkshore",b="From Rut'theran Village, you fly by hippogryph toward Darkshore with fish specimens for Nessa Shadowsong. The village is a sanctuary at the edge of the wider world for young adventurers leaving Teldrassil. A ferry also crosses the strait between the island and mainland Kalimdor, while night elves travel by bonded hippogryph.",sp=0},{t="Curious Catches",b="At Auberdine's docks, Laird examines Nessa's findings. The scales are as large as fists, and the jawbone is nearly twice the size of mainland specimens. Waters around the base of the World Tree seem to yield altered or abnormally large life. The strange catches may be tied to Teldrassil's potent, restless nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this flight?",a="You carry unusual fish specimens caught around Rut'theran Village to Laird in Auberdine on a hippogryph flight between the settlements.",al={"why do i fly to auberdine","flight to auberdine quest goal","why fly"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the parcel, and what is inside it?",a="Nessa Shadowsong, a fisherwoman, sends the parcel. It contains fish specimens from Rut'theran Village's waters, including massive scales and an oversized jawbone.",al={"nessa's collection","what is in the package","who sent package"},it="item"},{q="Why are the fish from Teldrassil so large?",a="Laird finds scales as big as a fist and a jawbone nearly twice normal size. Waters around Teldrassil's World Tree seem to foster magnified wildlife compared with mainland Darkshore.",al={"why are fish big","rut'theran fish size","huge scales"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Vesprystus?",a="Vesprystus is the hippogryph master at Rut'theran Village. He tends the night elven mounts and arranges flights across the water to mainland Kalimdor.",al={"vesprystus lore","who is the hippogryph master"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Laird?",a="Laird is a night elf fisherman in Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore. He studies local aquatic life and compares mainland catches with those near Teldrassil.",al={"laird lore","who is laird","laird darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Can you travel between Rut'theran and Auberdine without flying?",a="Yes. A regular ferry runs between the docks at Rut'theran Village and the pier at Auberdine, offering an alternative to the hippogryph flight.",al={"boat to auberdine","ferry to darkshore","other way to auberdine"},gp=true},{q="Why does Vesprystus send you to Auberdine?",a="As Rut'theran Village's hippogryph master, Vesprystus oversees vital travel between Teldrassil and the mainland of Kalimdor. While he holds Nessa Shadowsong's parcel of unusual fish specimens intended for Laird in Auberdine, his primary concern is introducing travelers to the night elves' flight network. By sending you across the waters on the back of a hippogryph, he ensures you establish a connection with Auberdine's flight master, opening rapid transit across Darkshore for your future journeys.",al={"why does vesprystus want this done","vesprystus motive","why send parcel auberdine"},it="motive",add="ddbceafb"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you fly by hippogryph to Auberdine, a rite of passage for young kaldorei leaving Teldrassil for the ancestral mainland.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can take hippogryphs between coastal outposts across northern Kalimdor and the capital."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","flight path","flight to auberdine","hippogryph","laird","nessa shadowsong","rut'theran village","teldrassil","vesprystus"},rel={"npc:vesprystus","npc:laird","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:6341","quest:6343","quest:940"},m={start="Vesprystus",["end"]="Laird",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6342},src={"Flight to Auberdine"}}
E["quest:6343"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Nessa",z="darkshore",s="Laird sends you from Auberdine to Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village with his findings. This introductory errand teaches young travelers to cross between Kalimdor and Teldrassil.",h="Laird sends you from Auberdine to Nessa Shadowsong in Rut'theran Village with his findings.",sec={{t="A Messenger Across the Sea",b="Laird sends you back across the water with his written observations. Fish caught off Darkshore differ sharply from those near Teldrassil. He suspects the great World Tree changes the life in these waters. You can hire a flight from Caylais Moonfeather, the hippogryph master, or take the regular ferry from Auberdine's pier to Rut'theran Village.",sp=0},{t="Curious Bounties",b="At Rut'theran Village, Nessa Shadowsong receives Laird's reply and is fascinated by the difference in marine life. Fish near the World Tree grow so large that local fishermen benefit at once, though the Kaldorei do not know why. Nessa plans to share the findings with her fellow villagers. For now, she harvests the abundant sea life and watches for whatever forces may be responsible.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts and completes this quest?",a="Laird, the fisherman in Auberdine on the Darkshore coast, sends you to Nessa Shadowsong at Rut'theran Village, at the base of Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","who gives quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the fastest way back to Rut'theran Village?",a="You can fly with Caylais Moonfeather, the hippogryph master in Auberdine, or take the regular passenger ferry from the long pier to Rut'theran Village.",al={"how to get back","travel to ruttheran","ferry or hippogryph"},gp=true},{q="Why is Laird studying the fish?",a="Laird studies the fish because catches along Darkshore differ greatly from those around Teldrassil. He suspects the World Tree's growth and unique energies alter the surrounding wildlife.",al={"why study fish","fish difference","laird response lore"},it="motive"},{q="Does Nessa find out why the fish are so strange?",a="Nessa does not learn why the fish are so strange right away. She notes the difference and agrees it deserves further study. She shares the report with the villagers and enjoys the abundant catches for now.",al={"why are fish big","teldrassil fish mystery"},it="next_step"},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="'Flight to Auberdine' comes before this journey. It carries Nessa's original letter from Rut'theran Village to Laird in Darkshore.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","flight to auberdine"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest chain?",a="The chain introduces Teldrassil's mysterious influence on local wildlife. It teaches young night elf adventurers how to cross between their island home and the Kalimdor mainland by ship and flight master.",al={"why do this quest","travel quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Laird want this letter delivered to Nessa?",a="Laird wants Nessa Shadowsong to know right away about the dramatic disparity between the sea life along the Darkshore mainland and the waters of Teldrassil. He suspects that Teldrassil itself is exerting an unusual influence over the surrounding marine wildlife, and sharing his observations helps the villagers understand the strange bounty they are harvesting.",al={"why send response to nessa","laird response purpose","why does laird want this done"},it="motive",add="c6069b83"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf leaving Teldrassil's boughs for the first time, you take part in your first official errand between the island haven and the ancient mainland of Darkshore.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you pass between Auberdine and Rut'theran Village. The maritime gateway links northern Kalimdor's night elf settlements with Alliance interests across Azeroth."},kw={"auberdine","caylais moonfeather","darkshore","laird","nessa shadowsong","return to nessa","rut'theran village","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:6342","npc:laird","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},m={start="Laird",["end"]="Nessa Shadowsong",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6343},src={"Return to Nessa"}}
E["quest:729"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="In southern Darkshore, hostile stone golems overrun a dig site, and Archaeologist Hollee seeks help in Auberdine. She fears for Prospector Remtravel, her senior colleague, whose research often blinds him to mortal danger.",h="In southern Darkshore, hostile stone golems overrun a dig site, and Archaeologist Hollee seeks help in...",sec={{t="A Perilous Dig",b="Archaeologist Hollee came across the sea with the Explorers' League. Master Greywhisker sent her to apprentice under Prospector Remtravel, whose discoveries had made him renowned in Ironforge's academic circles. The League sent them to study ancient ruins along Darkshore's untamed coast. As they dug through what seemed to be the remains of a great civilization, violent stone golems burst from the earth and overran the site.",sp=0},{t="Oblivious to Doom",b="In panic, Hollee fled through the night to Auberdine, the night elf port, to seek help. Remtravel barely noticed the danger. Absorbed in his relics, the elderly prospector stayed among the rubble as lumbering constructs surrounded his camp. South of Auberdine, anyone who reaches him finds him grumbling about missing stone brushes and misplaced fossils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a celebrated dwarven researcher with the Explorers' League of Ironforge. His discoveries made him famous in dwarven academic circles, but valuable relics can leave him blind to danger nearby.",al={"remtravel","prospector remtravel lore","who is the prospector"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine?",a="Master Greywhisker assigned Hollee to assist Remtravel. When dangerous golems rose at their dig site, she fled north in panic to Auberdine to seek help with a rescue.",al={"archaeologist hollee","hollee auberdine","why did hollee run"},it="why_here"},{q="What were the dwarves excavating in Darkshore?",a="The dwarves were excavating what seemed to be the remains of a great ancient civilization beneath Darkshore. Before golems overran the site, Remtravel had uncovered a mysterious fossil and stone artifacts.",al={"what was remtravel digging","darkshore dig site","remtravel fossil"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Prospector Remtravel be found?",a="Prospector Remtravel is at the excavation site in southern Darkshore, among ancient ruins south of Auberdine. Dangerous golems surround his camp as he searches for his stone brush and fossil.",al={"where is remtravel","remtravel location","find prospector remtravel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who sent this expedition to Darkshore?",a="The Explorers' League sent the expedition from Ironforge under Master Greywhisker's orders. Greywhisker assigned Hollee to apprentice under Remtravel and study Darkshore's ancient ruins.",al={"who sent hollee","master greywhisker","explorers league darkshore"},it="origin"},{q="Is Remtravel in actual danger?",a="Yes. Hostile golems prowl the ruins around Remtravel, but he is blind to the danger. He is focused on cataloging his findings and wonders where his tools and assistant have gone.",al={"is remtravel dead","remtravel alive","help remtravel"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Archaeologist Hollee want this done?",a="Hollee was thrilled to study under Prospector Remtravel, a famed researcher from the Ironforge Explorers' League. However, when hostile golems erupted from the dig site, Remtravel's deep distraction left him oblivious to the danger. Hollee fled to Auberdine for reinforcements, terrified that her mentor will be killed if someone does not pull him out of the ruins.",al={"why does hollee need help","hollee motive","why look for remtravel"},it="motive",add="90475777"},{q="Why does Hollee ask you to check on Remtravel instead of going herself?",a="Hollee barely escaped the dig site with her life when the stone golems arose. Terrified and lacking the martial prowess to fight through the hostile constructs alone, she must stay safely in Auberdine and rely on capable, passing adventurers to venture back into the fray and check on her mentor.",al={"why me hollee","why doesnt hollee go back","why doesn't auberdine help"},it="why_me",add="1b9bcac6"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see Remtravel's obsessive curiosity at work: he risks life and limb over an uncatalogued fossil.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see Ironforge researchers studying the unfamiliar ancient lands of their night elf allies in Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","explorers league","fossil","golems","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:730","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Prospector Remtravel",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=729},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector"}}
E["quest:731"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="At Darkshore's southern ruins, Prospector Remtravel presses on with his dig, hoping to find a prize for the Explorers' League. Hostile troggs and his forgetfulness make the search perilous, and word of his safety must reach his assistant in Auberdine.",h="At Darkshore's southern ruins, Prospector Remtravel presses on with his dig, hoping to find a prize for the...",sec={{t="A Perilous Excavation",b="Far south in Darkshore, Remtravel's Dig lies among ancient ruins. Dwarven excavators searching there uncovered troggs, who drove out the workers and besieged their camp. Remtravel will not return to Auberdine empty-handed. He wanders into danger to recover a fossil, hoping to justify the expedition's costs to the Explorers' League.",sp=0},{t="Muddled Memories and Trogg Ambushes",b="Keeping Remtravel safe at the excavation is dangerous and frustrating. He circles the site, mistakes brushes for fossils, and blunders past scaffolding and abandoned tents. Each stop draws aggressive troggs from the quarry's shadowed recesses. After travelers clear wave after wave of the subterranean brutes, Remtravel remembers where his prize is: he already gave the fossil to Hollee. He happily returns to work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a senior field researcher for the dwarven Explorers' League. Stationed in Darkshore, he was sent to excavate ancient coastal ruins, though his extreme absent-mindedness often puts his life in danger.",al={"remtravel","who is the prospector","absent minded prospector guy"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Remtravel still at the dig site?",a="Remtravel refuses to return to Darnassus without tangible proof of his work. He wants to recover a mysterious fossil to present to the Explorers' League before abandoning the camp.",al={"why stay at dig","why is remtravel there","why hasn't he fled"},it="why_here"},{q="Where did the troggs come from?",a="Remtravel's team dug deep into the earth and breached underground pockets inhabited by troggs. The primitive creatures surged up and overran the machinery, tents, and workers.",al={"why are there troggs in darkshore","darkshore troggs","dig site troggs"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Hollee?",a="Archaeologist Hollee is Remtravel's colleague and assistant in Auberdine. Distraught over her mentor's long absence and familiar with his forgetfulness, she asks travelers to find him and ensure he returns safely.",al={"hollee","archaeologist hollee","remtravel assistant"},it="people"},{q="What happens after finding the fossil?",a="After helping Remtravel search the dig, report on his safety to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine.",al={"quest continuation","what next","after remtravel escort"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Prospector Remtravel want to find the fossil?",a="Remtravel is under pressure from the Explorers' League chapter in Darnassus to prove he has actually been making progress at the dig site. Despite being terribly confused and absent-minded, he knows he needs to show tangible results—specifically the mysterious fossil and written findings—to justify his expedition and satisfy his superiors.",al={"remtravel motive","why search fossil","why find fossil remtravel"},it="motive",add="6ea255c4"},{q="Why does Remtravel need your help to search the excavation?",a="The excavation site has been overrun by hostile troggs, and Remtravel is a scatterbrained researcher, not a seasoned warrior. He is completely fixated on retrieving his lost artifacts and notes, leaving him entirely vulnerable to ambush as he wanders through the dig site without someone armed watching his back.",al={"why does remtravel need an escort","why remtravel needs protection","why not search alone remtravel"},it="why_me",add="4634f683"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Remtravel shows the Explorers' League's fierce passion and stubbornness. His dedication to ancient titan-lore blinds him to the danger around him.",["race:NightElf"]="For you as a night elf, dwarven digging in Darkshore may confirm your people's wariness: Remtravel's excavation uncovered a horde of violent troggs beneath sacred ground.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping Remtravel and preserving his findings supports scholarly and diplomatic ties between the dwarven Explorers' League and the night elves of Teldrassil."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","excavation","explorers' league","fossil","hollee","remtravel","troggs"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","npc:archaeologist-hollee","quest:729","topic:explorers-league","topic:trogg","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Prospector Remtravel",["end"]="Archaeologist Hollee",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=731},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (2)"}}
E["quest:741"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="From Darkshore, Hollee sends Remtravel’s fossil to Darnassus while she stays to watch the wandering prospector. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker takes a keen interest in the find.",h="From Darkshore, Hollee sends Remtravel’s fossil to Darnassus while she stays to watch the wandering...",sec={{t="A Courier to the Capital",b="Prospector Remtravel has found a curious fossil on Darkshore’s coast. He would rather keep digging than follow protocol. So Archaeologist Hollee stays with him among the shore’s dangerous beasts and hostile cultists. She asks you to carry the specimen to Darnassus, where a dwarven scholarly delegation is kept.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Stake in Kalimdor",b="Dwarves from Ironforge have crossed the Great Sea under the Explorers’ League banner. They seek ancient relics and lost history in Kalimdor’s soil. In Darnassus, Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker marvels at Remtravel’s knack for finding ancient treasures. Night elves see their forests as living sanctuaries, while the League sees ancient lands as ground to study and decipher.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="Prospector Remtravel found an unidentified petrified specimen on Darkshore’s coast. Its age and strange nature make it a prized find for Explorers’ League scholars in Darnassus.",al={"mysterious fossil","what fossil is this","remtravel fossil"},it="item"},{q="Why does Hollee stay behind in Darkshore?",a="Archaeologist Hollee stays to watch Prospector Remtravel. He wanders off and ignores danger while excavating, so she will not leave him alone in the wilds while she carries his discoveries to Darnassus.",al={"why doesn't hollee go","hollee staying","why hollee stays"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker is a senior representative of Ironforge’s Explorers’ League. He oversees archaeological work in northern Kalimdor from Darnassus, where he studies relics brought back by dwarven diggers.",al={"greywhisker","who is greywhisker","chief greywhisker"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the Explorers' League operating in Darnassus?",a="King Magni Bronzebeard chartered the Explorers’ League to uncover the origins of the dwarven race and ancient history across Azeroth. Friendly ties with the night elves let dwarven scholars base expeditions in Darnassus and study Kalimdor’s forgotten lands.",al={"dwarves in darnassus","explorers league darnassus","why are dwarves here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this fossil end up after Darnassus?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker inspects the fossil in Darnassus. Finds of this scale are meant to be cataloged or sent through League channels toward the great museum in Ironforge.",al={"where does fossil go","fossil next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Where did Remtravel find the specimen?",a="Remtravel uncovered the specimen on Darkshore’s wild coast, among shipwrecks, ancient ruins, and fossilized sea life from before the Great Sundering.",al={"where was fossil found","remtravel dig site"},it="place"},{q="Why does Archaeologist Hollee want the fossil delivered to Darnassus?",a="Prospector Remtravel wants his discovery examined right away, but someone needs to bring it to their superiors. Hollee is determined not to abandon Darkshore while Remtravel remains behind in the wilderness, so she relies on you to ferry the priceless find directly to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus on their behalf.",al={"why send fossil to darnassus","hollee motive","why deliver fossil"},it="motive",add="c70c2c67"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, carrying Remtravel’s fossil serves the Explorers’ League’s chief aim: uncovering the world’s deep past and showing the worth of dwarven perseverance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, seeing dwarven excavators bring ancient remnants from Darkshore’s sacred soil can be jarring. Cooperation with the League preserves Alliance bonds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help connect its people across great distances. Dwarven researchers rely on travelers to carry finds safely from Darkshore’s remote shores to Darnassus."},kw={"archaeologist","darkshore","darnassus","explorers league","fossil","greywhisker","hollee","remtravel"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-hollee","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","npc:prospector-remtravel","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Archaeologist Hollee",["end"]="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=741},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (3)"}}
E["quest:8721"] = {t="quest",n="Starweave the Elder",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Elder Starweave welcomes visitors during the Lunar Festival. Travelers honor Kalimdor's ancestral spirits and seek her wisdom and blessing.",h="In Auberdine, Elder Starweave welcomes visitors during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Auberdine",b="During the Lunar Festival, ancestral spirits appear across Azeroth beneath pillars of celestial light. Elder Starweave joins the night elves in Auberdine, a harbor on Darkshore's coast. Travelers come to honor her and seek guidance from ages past.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Heavens",b="Elder Starweave looks to the heavens above Kalimdor. She tells visitors that the stars hold answers to mortal doubts and worldly riddles. Those who seek her counsel are urged to look skyward for truth and receive ancestral favor, along with tidings of other wandering spirits across the wild frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave receives visitors in Auberdine, the coastal night elf town in Darkshore. A beam of moonlight shines down from the heavens where she stands.",al={"starweave location","where is elder starweave","elder starweave darkshore"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The yearly Lunar Festival honors ancestral elders across Azeroth. Travelers receive recognition, festive currency, and ancestral goodwill.",al={"why do elder starweave","starweave the elder purpose","what does starweave do"}},{q="Who is Elder Starweave?",a="Elder Starweave is an ancient night elven spirit who honors the Lunar Festival. She offers wisdom about the constellations and points pilgrims toward other revered elders, including Elder Bladeswift.",al={"who is starweave","starweave lore","elder starweave backstory"}},{q="Can Horde players visit Elder Starweave?",a="Yes. Festival elders welcome respectful travelers of either faction. Since Elder Starweave is in Auberdine, an Alliance harbor, Horde travelers must be wary of the town's night elven guards.",al={"can horde talk to starweave","horde elder starweave","starweave hostile horde"}},{q="What does Elder Starweave tell travelers?",a="Elder Starweave tells visitors that the stars hold answers to mortal riddles. She asks whether the wise and fortunate might look upward to find truth.",al={"starweave dialogue","what does elder starweave say"}},{q="Which elder does Starweave point to?",a="Elder Starweave shares Elder Bladeswift's location and tidings, guiding travelers onward across northern Kalimdor.",al={"who does starweave mention","elder after starweave","next elder darkshore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, honoring Elder Starweave in Auberdine connects you with the ancient spirits of your forebears and the revered mysteries of Elune and the stars.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold ancestral spirits and celestial balance in deep reverence. Communion with Elder Starweave reflects those beliefs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you must carefully make your way into Auberdine's Alliance-held docks to pay your respects without provoking the local sentinels."},kw={"ancestor","auberdine","darkshore","elder bladeswift","elder starweave","lunar festival","starweave"},rel={"npc:elder-starweave","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Starweave",id=8721},src={"Starweave the Elder"}}
E["quest:942"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, a strange fossil draws you across the Great Sea to the Wetlands. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sends you to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor, hoping he can unlock its secrets.",h="In Darkshore, a strange fossil draws you across the Great Sea to the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sees a likeness between the strange fossil from Darkshore and a relic shown at an Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. Archaeologist Flagongut presented that relic and believed such fossils held powers waiting to be unlocked. Greywhisker thinks Flagongut is the only dwarf who can discern what makes this Kalimdor find so extraordinary.",sp=0},{t="A Voyage Across the Sea",b="You carry the mysterious fossil from Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms. Flagongut was last seen lodging at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, waiting for an armed escort to the Whelgar Excavation Site. When you bring him the fossil, the Darkshore survey reaches across continents as part of a wider archaeological inquiry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Greywhisker send me all the way to Menethil Harbor?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker remembers Archaeologist Flagongut displaying an identical relic at an annual Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. He believes Flagongut knows how to unlock its hidden power, so he sends you to Flagongut's last known location at Menethil Harbor.",al={"why go to menethil","greywhisker fossil errand","why wetlands"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an Explorers' League researcher stationed in the Wetlands. He is staying at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor while preparing for an expedition to the perilous Whelgar Excavation Site.",al={"who is flagongut","archaeologist flagongut lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the mysterious fossil?",a="The mysterious fossil is an ancient specimen retrieved from Darkshore. Flagongut once claimed that an identical specimen he studied held latent magical or historical power waiting to be unlocked.",al={"what is the fossil","mysterious fossil origin","remtravel fossil"},it="item"},{q="What does Flagongut say when you deliver the fossil?",a="Flagongut is astonished that a relic identical to his own research sample came from distant Kalimdor. The discovery confirms that ancient history links the two landmasses.",al={"flagongut reaction","handing in the fossil"}},{q="Where does Flagongut want to go next?",a="Flagongut is waiting in Menethil Harbor for an escort inland to the Whelgar Excavation Site, a major dig in the Wetlands.",al={"where is flagongut going","flagongut excavation"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this quest fit into the Absent Minded Prospector storyline?",a="After you escort and rescue Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore, you examine his excavated relic with Greywhisker. The inquiry then moves from northern Kalimdor to Explorers' League experts in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"absent minded prospector part 4","quest chain context"},it="history"},{q="Why does Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker want this done?",a="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker recognizes that the mysterious fossil Remtravel uncovered bears a striking resemblance to a peculiar relic presented at an Explorers' League conference in Ironforge. Its discoverer, Archaeologist Flagongut, believed the relic possessed a latent power waiting to be unlocked. Greywhisker hopes Flagongut can study this new specimen and unlock ancient secrets of the past.",al={"why send fossil","greywhisker motive","why does greywhisker want the fossil examined"},it="motive",add="5b36a0d8"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see how far the Explorers' League reaches. Its fieldwork in remote Kalimdor connects with fellow scholars based in Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you travel by Alliance shipping routes from Kalimdor across the sea to Menethil Harbor. The routes keep League branches connected."},kw={"absent minded prospector","archaeologist flagongut","chief archaeologist greywhisker","darkshore","deepwater tavern","explorers' league","menethil harbor","mysterious fossil"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:chief-archaeologist-greywhisker","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:deepwater-tavern","topic:explorers-league","zone:darkshore","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker",["end"]="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=942},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (4)"}}
E["quest:943"] = {t="quest",n="The Absent Minded Prospector",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Remtravel's dig sends his search across the Great Sea. In Menethil Harbor, Archaeologist Flagongut hopes to join Remtravel's finds with his own fossil and the lost Stone of Relu, revealing the relics' hidden powers.",h="In Darkshore, Remtravel's dig sends his search across the Great Sea.",sec={{t="Cross-Continental Archaeology",b="You once helped the distracted Prospector Remtravel during an escort through northern Darkshore. Now the search crosses the Great Sea to the Wetlands marshes. Prospector Whelgar keeps Flagongut's original fossil at his excavation site. After reviewing the finds, Archaeologist Flagongut believes the Stone of Relu can unlock the mysterious powers within the fossils.",sp=0},{t="Lost to the Marshes",b="Before Flagongut could meet Whelgar, mottled raptors ambushed his caravan on the road and swallowed the Stone of Relu. To piece together the mystery, Flagongut needs you to hunt the beasts, recover the stone, and retrieve his original fossil from Whelgar's camp. With both fossils and the key assembled, the dwarven researchers hope to learn the relics' true origin and power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is a Darkshore quest ending in the Wetlands?",a="The Explorers' League works across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker sent Remtravel's fossil from Darkshore across the sea to Archaeologist Flagongut in the Wetlands. Their shared research joins the two dig sites.",al={"why wetlands darkshore quest","menethil harbor connection","why send to wetlands"},it="place"},{q="What is the Stone of Relu?",a="The Stone of Relu is an ancient relic recovered by Archaeologist Flagongut. He believes it can serve as a cipher or catalyst, unlocking dormant magical secrets preserved in fossils excavated in Darkshore and the Wetlands.",al={"stone of relu","what is relu stone","relu artifact"},it="item"},{q="Who is Archaeologist Flagongut?",a="Archaeologist Flagongut is an operative of the dwarven Explorers' League, based in Menethil Harbor. He studies ancient relics from nearby excavations and hopes to unlock the hidden power in fossils found by Prospectors Remtravel and Whelgar.",al={"flagongut","who is flagongut"},it="identity"},{q="Who has the original fossil?",a="Prospector Whelgar holds Flagongut's original fossil at his excavation site in the Wetlands. You have already delivered Remtravel's Darkshore fossil to Flagongut.",al={"where is the fossil","who has remtravel fossil","whelgar fossil"}},{q="Why do raptors have the Stone of Relu?",a="While traveling along the Wetlands road to consult Prospector Whelgar, Flagongut was ambushed by mottled raptors. In the chaos, one of the beasts swallowed the stone whole.",al={"raptor swallowed relic","why raptors have stone"},it="target"},{q="What do the dwarves expect the fossils to do?",a="Flagongut believes the fossils hold hidden power and secrets of the past. He believes the Stone of Relu is the key to unlocking them.",al={"fossil power","what does the fossil do"},it="motive"},{q="What is Flagongut's Fossil for?",a="Flagongut's Fossil is one of the ancient specimens recovered by the dwarven excavators, alongside the piece uncovered by Prospector Remtravel in Darkshore. Archaeologist Flagongut believes these ancient relics hold dormant magical power and forgotten secrets, which he hopes to finally unlock and decipher using the resonant power of the Stone of Relu.",al={"flagonguts fossil","flagongut fossil use","what is flagonguts fossil"},it="item",add="1568e7b3"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the Explorers' League at work, linking distant dig sites across continents to piece together dwarven heritage and the mysteries of the Titans.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you may help bridge the sea between the night elven lands of Darkshore and the dwarven settlements around Menethil Harbor, alongside Alliance couriers."},kw={"darkshore","explorers league","flagongut","fossil","menethil","remtravel","stone of relu","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"npc:archaeologist-flagongut","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Archaeologist Flagongut",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=943,ri={"Flagongut's Fossil","Stone of Relu"}},src={"The Absent Minded Prospector (5)"}}
E["quest:944"] = {t="quest",n="The Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Onu fears the Twilight's Hammer cult has reached the fallen ancient horror. He sends Alliance scouts to investigate.",h="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Onu fears the Twilight's Hammer cult has reached the fallen...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Presence",b="Onu sees corruption linger along Darkshore, driving wildlife from its homes. The naga on the coast trouble him, but signs of the Twilight's Hammer trouble him more. Its followers worship primal lords who ruled the world before their overthrow in ages past.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Lord",b="South of Onu, a grim excavation surrounds a colossal creature pierced by a great stone weapon. Onu gives you a Phial of Scrying and asks you to enter the pit and learn whether cultists have gathered there. The behemoth has been dead for eons, yet corruptive power still clings to its bones. The Twilight's Hammer may seek to claim it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this mission?",a="Onu, an ancient of lore, sends you from his place along the road in southern Darkshore, near the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"quest giver","who gives the masters glaive quest","start npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="In southern Darkshore, a monstrous ancient lord fell eons ago, pierced through the skull by a titanic stone glaive. Its vast petrified skeleton remains buried in the earth.",al={"what is masters glaive","lore of masters glaive","giant skull in darkshore"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult interested in the site?",a="The Twilight's Hammer worships the old, dark powers of ancient Azeroth. Slivers of primeval power remain in the long-dead creature's remains, and the cultists seek to harness them.",al={"twilight cult darkshore","why are twilight cultists here","twilights hammer masters glaive"},it="why_here"},{q="How do I report back to Onu?",a="After exploring the excavation pit, use the Phial of Scrying from your bags to call forth a Scrying Bowl on the ground. Through it, you can speak to Onu by magic without returning to him.",al={"where to turn in quest","how to use scrying phial","scrying bowl"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What follows this scout mission?",a="Once the Scrying Bowl confirms the cultists are there, Onu sends you to their encampment in The Twilight Camp to learn more about their activities.",al={"next quest","followup to masters glaive"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Onu send you to investigate the Master's Glaive?",a="Onu is deeply unsettled by the presence of the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore. As an ancient ancient of lore watching over the woodlands, he knows this nihilistic cult venerates the defeated Old Gods of the earth. The Master's Glaive marks the ancient resting place of one such fallen monstrosity, and Onu fears that even in death, remnants of the entity's lingering dark power could be unearthed and wielded by the cultists.",al={"why does onu want this","onu motive masters glaive","why scout masters glaive"},it="motive",add="fcbe4ca5"},{q="Who are you sent to investigate at the Master's Glaive?",a="You are sent to reconnoiter the Twilight's Hammer cultists lurking around the massive monument. These zealots revere primordial, ancient powers that once ruled Azeroth. They have gathered in the cavernous pit of the Master's Glaive to tap into whatever eldritch essence or remnant strength still radiates from the petrified skull of the ancient being slain there.",al={"masters glaive target","who am i looking for at masters glaive","who is at masters glaive"},it="target",add="821e537b"},{q="Why does Onu need you to scout the Master's Glaive instead of going himself?",a="Onu is a massive, rooted ancient of lore who cannot easily slip unnoticed into the deep ravine of the Master's Glaive. Furthermore, Darkshore's night elf forces are stretched thin dealing with the encroaching naga along the coast and corruption across the wild. A nimble, capable traveler armed with a Phial of Scrying can quietly scout the cultists' encampment and magically report back without drawing unwanted attention.",al={"why me onu","why send me masters glaive","why doesnt onu scout masters glaive"},it="why_me",add="dfa4afd6"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the Master's Glaive as a reminder of terrors older than your people. Mad cultists trespassing on Darkshore's sacred soil is an intolerable defilement.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you answer Onu's call to learn how the ancient taint buried deep in the earth disturbs the land and its wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep the Twilight's Hammer from awakening ancient horrors that could overrun northern Kalimdor's struggling settlements."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","old lord","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:948","quest:949","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore","topic:naga"},m={start="Onu",["end"]="Scrying Bowl",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=944},src={"The Master's Glaive (quest)"}}
E["quest:947"] = {t="quest",n="Cave Mushrooms",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Cave Mushrooms are needed for a potion Barithras Moonshade prepares in Auberdine. He asks you to gather rare fungi behind Cliffspring Falls and investigate warnings from the Grove of the Ancients.",h="In Darkshore, Cave Mushrooms are needed for a potion Barithras Moonshade prepares in Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Recipe Behind the Falls",b="Barithras Moonshade needs scaber stalks and a death cap for a potent mixture. Both grow in a damp cavern behind Cliffspring Falls in northeastern Darkshore. Gathering them is more dangerous than picking ordinary woodland herbs.",sp=0},{t="The Ancients' Warning",b="The tree guardians at the Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras away from the cavern. They sense a foul presence in the mountain caves. Moonshade sends you to learn whether the elders’ fears of a creeping evil in northern Darkshore are well founded.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this task begin?",a="Barithras Moonshade gives you the assignment in Auberdine, the night elf settlement on Darkshore’s central coast.",al={"where to pick up cave mushrooms","barithras moonshade location","cave mushrooms quest start"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where are the mushrooms located?",a="The mushrooms grow in a cavern behind Cliffspring Falls, along the mountain face northeast of Auberdine.",al={"where are scaber stalks","death cap location","cave behind waterfall darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why won't Barithras Moonshade retrieve the mushrooms himself?",a="The Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras to stay clear of the falls. The great ancients sense that an unnatural, rising evil has taken refuge in the cave.",al={"why barithras won't go","why barithras stays in auberdine"},it="why_me"},{q="What specific mushrooms are needed?",a="Moonshade needs five scaber stalks and one dangerous death cap mushroom for his potion.",al={"required mushrooms","which fungi for moonshade"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What does this errand lead to next?",a="After you verify the presence in the cave and deliver the fungi, you travel south to Onu, the ancient protector at the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after cave mushrooms","onu follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the Ancients concerned about Cliffspring Falls?",a="The Grove of the Ancients warned Barithras that a rising evil may lurk in the cave behind the falls. He asks you to gather mushrooms and investigate the warning.",al={"ancients warning cliffspring falls","why scout cave"},sp=1},{q="Why does Barithras Moonshade want this done?",a="Barithras Moonshade is an herbalist concocting a potent new potion that demands rare fungi found only in the cavern behind Cliffspring Falls. Beyond his alchemical work, however, he carries a deeper concern: the Grove of the Ancients warned him that a rising evil lurks within that very cave. By sending you to harvest the ingredients, he also hopes to learn whether the Ancients' grim omens are true.",al={"why does barithras want cave mushrooms","barithras moonshade motive","why collect mushrooms for barithras"},it="motive",add="a048db56"},{q="What is the Death Cap for?",a="The Death Cap is an exceptionally rare and potent toxic fungus native to the cavern behind Cliffspring Falls. Barithras Moonshade requires a pristine specimen as a key reagent in a specialized potion he is crafting in Auberdine.",al={"what is death cap used for","death cap mushroom purpose","why does barithras need death cap"},it="item",add="991c4c10"},{q="What is the Scaber Stalk for?",a="Scaber Stalks are rare mushrooms that flourish in the damp, shadowy cave behind Cliffspring Falls. Barithras Moonshade needs five of them to blend into his ongoing alchemical concoctions alongside the potent Death Cap.",al={"what are scaber stalks for","scaber stalk mushroom purpose","why does barithras need scaber stalks"},it="item",add="be6516db"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you may value the hunt for death caps and scaber stalks. These fungi grow in dark caverns rather than lush woodland soil.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the Grove of the Ancients is deeply attuned to Darkshore’s natural balance. Any disturbance beneath the falls concerns the Kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Auberdine is the Alliance’s main stronghold on the Kalimdor coast. Evil spreading in the eastern mountains threatens the whole shore."},kw={"auberdine","barithras moonshade","cave mushrooms","cliffspring falls","darkshore","death cap","grove of the ancients","onu","scaber stalks"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","subzone:cliffspring-falls","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=947,ri={"Death Cap","Scaber Stalk"}},src={"Cave Mushrooms"}}
E["quest:948"] = {t="quest",n="Onu",z="darkshore",s="Barithras Moonshade sends you south from Auberdine to consult Onu. Your findings at Cliffspring Falls have caught the notice of one of Darkshore’s oldest guardians.",h="Barithras Moonshade sends you south from Auberdine to consult Onu.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Ancients",b="Barithras Moonshade sees more than strange fungi in the samples you brought to Auberdine. The caves beneath Cliffspring Falls are tainted, and word of them has reached Onu, an Ancient of Lore in the Grove of the Ancients south of town. Darkshore’s waterways may be corrupted beyond anything a naturalist can explain. Onu seeks counsel, and even an Ancient’s patience cannot hide the weight of his summons.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Grove",b="The road south from Auberdine turns inland, away from the coastal ruins and toward the mountain slopes. The Grove of the Ancients shelters an old refuge of nature, apart from the decay along the shore. Onu waits among stone barrows and kindred spirits. He is ready to guide allies toward the blights stirring at the edge of the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Onu?",a="An Ancient of Lore, Onu gathers and preserves knowledge. He watches over the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore and offers wisdom to those defending the land.",al={"who is onu","onu identity","what is onu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Onu want to speak with me?",a="You gathered fungal samples for Barithras Moonshade from the caves beneath Cliffspring Falls. What you found alarmed the naturalists, and Onu wants to speak with you about the spreading corruption.",al={"why onu summons","reason for talk","why go to onu"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients lies south of Auberdine, along the eastern mountain foothills. Follow the main road south through Darkshore, then head east toward the mountain slopes to reach Onu.",al={"onu location","where is grove of the ancients","how to find onu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of creature is an Ancient of Lore?",a="Ancients of Lore are old treant beings allied with the night elves and the Cenarion Circle. They are revered for their wisdom and memory, and preserve nature’s magic and history.",al={"ancient of lore","what creature is onu","treant vs ancient"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Onu's summons considered urgent?",a="Ancients are deliberate and rarely hurry. Barithras Moonshade says Onu’s call for counsel means the threat to Darkshore is severe.",al={"why urgent","is onu worried","barithras warning"},it="danger"},{q="What comes after meeting with Onu?",a="After you meet Onu at the Grove of the Ancients, he asks you to investigate a darker threat farther south along the coast: the excavation around the Master’s Glaive.",al={"next quest after onu","what happens next","where does onu send you"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Barithras Moonshade send me to Onu?",a="Barithras knows that the Ancients of Lore possess deep wisdom regarding the land's corruption, and Onu has taken direct notice of what you found within the cave at Cliffspring Falls. Because an Ancient rarely reaches out unless Darkshore faces a profound and urgent threat, Barithras urges you to heed the summons immediately.",al={"barithras motive","why send to onu","why does barithras want this done"},it="motive",add="be40e913"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the Ancients of Lore as sacred partners who have guided your people since before the Sundering. Answering Onu’s call helps preserve Darkshore.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you revere the Ancients as keepers of nature’s wisdom. Investigating the strange growths in the caves at Onu’s request fits the Cenarion Circle’s work.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler helping defend Darkshore, you can seek insight into Kalimdor’s northern wilderness from the region’s Ancients."},kw={"ancient of lore","auberdine","barithras moonshade","cliffwater falls","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu"},rel={"npc:barithras-moonshade","quest:947","zone:darkshore","quest:952"},m={start="Barithras Moonshade",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=948},src={"Onu (quest)"}}
E["quest:949"] = {t="quest",n="The Twilight Camp",z="darkshore",s="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, cultists gather while Alliance scouts seek their purpose. A scrying bowl has revealed their ritual site. Now you enter the excavation to learn what the Twilight's Hammer seeks beneath the earth.",h="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, cultists gather while Alliance scouts seek their purpose.",sec={{t="Probing the Dig",b="The Twilight's Hammer has made the Master's Glaive a threat. A scrying bowl revealed the cultists' fortifications. You enter their camp to learn their designs before the Alliance can prepare its defenses.",sp=0},{t="The Illustrated Tome",b="In the cultists' northern camp, an ancient tome lies filled with unsettling art. Printed by hand, its pages reveal that the Twilight's Hammer studies the colossal entity buried beneath the earth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of The Twilight Camp quest?",a="You enter the Twilight's Hammer camp near the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore to find a clue to the cult's motives: a hand-printed ritual book.",al={"twilight camp quest objective","what do i do twilight camp"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends you to investigate the camp?",a="The Scrying Bowl at the overlook above the Master's Glaive sends you to investigate. You continue the inquiry begun for the ancient protector Onu.",al={"who gives twilight camp","twilight camp quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the clue found in the camp?",a="The Twilight Tome lies in the northern part of the encampment. Other tomes can unleash warding magic against intruders.",al={"where is the book","twilight tome location","find clue twilight camp"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer at the Master's Glaive?",a="The cultists seek the dark powers of the Old Gods and their servants. Around the massive petrified carcass pinned by the giant stone blade, they dig to study or awaken whatever ancient evil remains there.",al={"why are cultists at masters glaive","twilights hammer darkshore purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after finding the tome?",a="Finding the tome leads to Return to Onu. You carry the writings north to the ancient treant in the Grove of the Ancients.",al={"next quest after twilight camp","where to go after twilight tome"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Scrying Bowl direct you to investigate the camp?",a="Onu's scrying bowl reveals that Twilight's Hammer cultists have gathered around the Master's Glaive, where an ancient 'old lord' fell long ago. Their purpose there is not known, but Onu is sure it must be dark. Before he and the defenders of the grove can make a plan, they need something from the camp that reveals what the cult intends.",al={"why investigate the twilight camp","scrying bowl purpose","why search twilight camp"},it="motive",add="8554815a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you see the Twilight's Hammer defile sacred Kalimdor beneath Darkshore's ancient groves.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you help Cenarion wardens uncover the cult's research and keep it from corrupting ancient entities buried beneath the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help stop the cult's strange excavations from destabilizing northern Kalimdor."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","onu","scrying bowl","twilight camp","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Scrying Bowl",["end"]="Twilight Tome",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=949},src={"The Twilight Camp"}}
E["quest:950"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Onu",z="darkshore",s="You bring a torn page from the Twilight Tome to Onu in Darkshore. The cultists' writing is all you could bear to take from their book.",h="You bring a torn page from the Twilight Tome to Onu in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Glimpse into Madness",b="The Twilight Tome overwhelms anyone who tries to read it. Its words swim across the page, and its ornate scrollwork twists into grotesque figures. You tear out a page of scribbles before the strain brings on vertigo.",sp=0},{t="Ancient Suspicions",b="Onu, the Ancient of Lore, recognizes a strange aura in the page you bring him. Its chaotic, primal magic points to ancient, shadowy forces buried beneath the earth. Though the writing is hard to decipher, it shows the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore pursues more than banditry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the page taken from the Twilight Tome?",a="Insane Scribbles is a torn page from the Twilight Tome, the cult's sacred book. Its shifting script brings severe mental distress.",al={"insane scribbles","what are the scribbles","twilight tome page"},it="item"},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore in the Grove of the Ancients in southern Darkshore. He is an elder guardian and scholar who guides night elves and Alliance allies against corruption in the forest.",al={"who is onu","onu darkshore","treant onu"},it="identity"},{q="What does Onu learn from the scribbles?",a="Onu senses chaotic, primal energy in the page and the influence of ancient, malevolent entities. The writings suggest the Twilight's Hammer cultists are pursuing relic sites and buried powers across Darkshore.",al={"what did onu find","meaning of scribbles"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore?",a="The Twilight's Hammer came to Darkshore to excavate ruined elven sites and uncover traces of ancient power linked to primeval darkness and the Old Gods. Chaos in the land helps hide their rites.",al={"cultists in darkshore","why twilight hammer here"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Onu turns his attention to the ancient elven ruins of Mathystra to the north. He directs adventurers to secure the relics before the cultists can seize them.",al={"what quest is next","next after return to onu"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does reading the tome cause dizziness?",a="Dark, maddening magic fills the Twilight Tome. Its glyphs bewilder mortal minds, causing hallucinations and swoons that keep outsiders from understanding its secrets.",al={"why dizziness tome","twilight tome effects"},it="power"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the cultists' desecration of Darkshore's shores as a threat to the balance guarded by the Ancients of Lore. Onu's warnings strike close to home for the kaldorei.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you recognize the scribbles' chaotic, unnatural resonance as an affront to the natural order you protect alongside treants like Onu.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help investigate cult activity along Darkshore's coast and keep night elf settlements like Auberdine safe from hidden threats."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","insane scribbles","old ones","onu","twilight tome","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:949","quest:948","quest:951","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Twilight Tome",["end"]="Onu",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=950},src={"Return to Onu"}}
E["quest:951"] = {t="quest",n="Mathystra Relics",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's northeastern coast, Mathystra Relics may reveal how the Twilight's Hammer bends ancient elven magic. Onu, an Ancient of Lore in the Grove of the Ancients, seeks them to learn what the cult intends.",h="Along Darkshore's northeastern coast, Mathystra Relics may reveal how the Twilight's Hammer bends ancient...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="After you recovered a tainted parchment from Twilight's Hammer cultists near the Master's Glaive, Onu deciphered its meaning. The writing was not the cult's own. It was a cursed fragment of ancient night elven script, tainted by the Twilight's Hammer. The zealots are using forgotten elven magic to awaken or summon their ancient masters into the mortal world.",sp=1},{t="The Fallen Bastion",b="Onu sends you to the Ruins of Mathystra on Darkshore's northeastern shore. Before the Sundering, Mathystra was a shining bastion of highborne civilization. The city fell to rubble, weeds and naga, yet its old enchantments endure in shattered urns and relics scattered among the stone foundations.",sp=0},{t="Divining Dark Designs",b="You gather surviving relics from the grassy debris so the defenders of Darkshore can learn which arts the cult means to use. Onu studies the magic left in each piece. He must uncover the cult's plans before the Twilight's Hammer bends ancient kaldorei sorcery to free its subterranean masters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Mathystra Relics?",a="The Mathystra Relics are fragments of enchanted pottery, urns and artifacts from the ruins. They were made during the height of ancient night elven civilization before the Great Sundering, and still hold lingering magic.",al={"what are the relics","mathystra relic lore","elven relics mathystra"},it="item"},{q="Why does Onu want these relics?",a="Onu wants the relics because the Twilight's Hammer is using ancient elven magic to bring its dark masters back into the world. By studying intact pieces from Mathystra, he hopes to learn how the cult will wield that power.",al={"why does onu want relics","purpose of mathystra relics"},it="motive"},{q="Where were the Ruins of Mathystra located?",a="The Ruins of Mathystra lie along Darkshore's northeastern coast, north of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran and just past the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"where is mathystra","mathystra location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the Twilight's Hammer trying to bring back?",a="The Twilight's Hammer seeks to bring back its ancient, malevolent masters. Onu warns that the cult is using ancient elven magic to return them to Azeroth.",al={"who are twilight hammer masters","cult masters darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="What was Mathystra before it became a ruin?",a="Mathystra was once a great night elven city and bastion, thousands of years ago. The Great Sundering left it in ruins, and wilderness, ghosts and vile beach-dwelling creatures such as the naga overran it.",al={"history of mathystra","what was mathystra"},it="history"},{q="Who gives the quest 'Mathystra Relics'?",a="Onu gives you the Mathystra Relics task. He is an ancient treant rooted in the Grove of the Ancients in south-central Darkshore, after your investigation of the Master's Glaive.",al={"who starts mathystra relics","quest giver mathystra relics"},gp=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see relics of your people's pre-Sundering glory dug from the dirt. Their fall is a somber reminder, and the Twilight's Hammer's use of your ancestors' potent arts is an alarming warning.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you aid Onu, one of nature's greatest elder sentinels. You help safeguard Darkshore's ancient history from dark cultists.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help keep northern Kalimdor safe from dark forces beneath the earth by preventing the Twilight's Hammer from weaponizing ancient magic."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","mathystra","onu","relics","ruins of mathystra","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-mathystra","quest:948","quest:952","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:944","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:950","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=951,ri={"Mathystra Relic"}},src={"Mathystra Relics"}}
E["quest:953"] = {t="quest",n="The Fall of Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="At Ameth'Aran in Darkshore, you search the ruins and read their ancient stone tablets for Sentinel Tysha Moonblade. Their words tell how the Highborne city fell in the Sundering, preserving history largely lost in the War of the Ancients for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",h="At Ameth'Aran in Darkshore, you search the ruins and read their ancient stone tablets for Sentinel Tysha...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Highborne",b="Ameth'Aran was home to Queen Azshara's elite sorcerers, who wielded powerful arcane magic. When the Well of Eternity was destroyed ten thousand years ago, the city fell to broken marble and cracked pillars. The Highborne who died there still haunt the ruins as restless, anguished spirits.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering Lost Chronicles",b="Few written accounts survived the Great Sundering intact. The War of the Ancients drove night elves into a struggle for survival, and much of their history was lost. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade surveyed Ameth'Aran and found two large engraved tablets, the Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran.\n\nGhostly Highborne specters drove Tysha from the ruins. Their readings can carry the disaster's history to the scholars of the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin in central Darkshore. Ten thousand years ago, it was a city where Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility wielded and studied powerful arcane magic. The Great Sundering brought its fall.",al={"ametharan lore","what was ameth aran","who lived in ameth aran"},it="place"},{q="Why are there ghosts in Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran's ghosts are the spirits of Highborne who lived and died there. The sudden catastrophe shattered the Well of Eternity and fragmented Kalimdor, binding them to the ruins in eternal torment.",al={"why are there spirits in ameth aran","ameth aran ghosts","restless highborne"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Sentinel Tysha Moonblade?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade is a night elf sentinel stationed along the road in Darkshore. She scouts ancient sites and recovers lost historical records for the Circle of Ancients in Auberdine.",al={"tysha moonblade","who gives fall of ameth aran"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Circle of Ancients want these tablets read?",a="The Circle of Ancients wants the tablets read because the Well of Eternity's destruction plunged Kalimdor into immense upheaval. Countless libraries and monuments were obliterated, and few written records survived the War of the Ancients. The tablets preserve rare firsthand Highborne accounts of the Sundering.",al={"why read the tablets","circle of ancients tablets","lay of ameth aran meaning"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the tablets located?",a="The Lay of Ameth'Aran and the Fall of Ameth'Aran are etched into two large standing stone monuments among Ameth'Aran's ruined courtyards. The wandering ghosts of the city's former residents surround them.",al={"where are the ameth aran tablets","tablet locations","how to read ameth aran"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Highborne of Ameth'Aran during the Sundering?",a="When the Well of Eternity imploded at the climax of the War of the Ancients, massive tremors and arcane backlash tore Kalimdor apart. Ameth'Aran collapsed, burying its citizens and leaving their ghosts in the rubble.",al={"how did ameth aran fall","ameth aran destruction"},it="history"},{q="Why does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade want this done?",a="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade was dispatched on behalf of the Circle of Ancients to survey the ancient ruins. Records from the era of the War of the Ancients and the Sundering are exceedingly rare due to the cataclysms of that age. Gathering the history carved upon the tablets allows her to provide a full accounting to the druids and elders in Auberdine.",al={"tysha moonblade motive","why does tysha need this","why study ameth'aran tablets"},it="motive",add="4f4506ec"},{q="Why does Sentinel Tysha Moonblade need your help?",a="Tysha previously ventured into Ameth'Aran to examine the tablets herself, but she was ambushed and driven off by the vengeful Highborne spirits haunting the ruins. Unable to safely transcribe the inscriptions on her own while under constant spectral attack, she requires a capable adventurer to breach the ruins and decipher the text in her stead.",al={"why cant tysha read the tablets","why does tysha need me","why doesn't tysha go herself"},it="why_me",add="2329a43d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Ameth'Aran's ruins as a grim reminder of your ancestors' hubris under Queen Azshara. Unchecked arcane sorcery brought catastrophic consequences.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can read the tablets as a glimpse of pre-Sundering elven spellcraft at its height. They also tell of the ruin that followed when that power spiraled out of control.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help the Sentinels preserve Darkshore's history for the night elf leaders guiding the Alliance on Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","azshara","circle of ancients","darkshore","highborne","sundering","tablets","tysha moonblade"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","zone:darkshore","topic:highborne","topic:war-of-the-ancients","subzone:auberdine"},m={start="Sentinel Tysha Moonblade",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=953},src={"The Fall of Ameth'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:954"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="An eerie blue aura burns above a shrine in Bashal'Aran, where satyrs and grells will not go. Thundris Windweaver, Auberdine's elder, asks you to find its source.",h="An eerie blue aura burns above a shrine in Bashal'Aran, where satyrs and grells will not go.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Ruins",b="Bashal'Aran once flourished under the ancient Kaldorei Empire. Now demonic taint fills its broken marble halls and overgrown arches. Twisted satyrs and corrupt grells feed on the ruins' lingering magic, growing more malicious by the day. Yet Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine has noticed a mystery: atop a western bluff, a blue aura shines above a shrine that no demon will approach.",sp=0},{t="The Wounded Shade",b="At the raised shrine, you find Asterion, an ancient spirit, at the heart of the blue light. The shade has kept a lonely vigil for centuries. Amid howling beasts and vile fiends, even a traveling stranger brings respite from decades of isolation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the blue aura located?",a="The blue aura shines above a shrine atop a small raised bluff on Bashal'Aran's western edge, just east of Auberdine in Darkshore. The shrine rises slightly above the crumbling walls around it.",al={"find blue aura","where is asterion","bashal'aran shrine location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the satyrs avoid the shrine?",a="No one knows why the satyrs and grells avoid the shrine. A strange blue aura fills the place, and Thundris Windweaver sends you to find its source.",al={"why demons afraid","why satyrs stay away"},it="threat"},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Thundris Windweaver, a night elf druid and Auberdine's elder, sends you after noticing unnatural demonic movements in the eastern ruins.",al={"who gives quest","quest giver","thundris windweaver location"},gp=true},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient kaldorei ruin in the forests of Darkshore, sacked during the ancient Sundering. Grells and satyrs now infest it, drawn by its dormant ley powers.",al={"what happened to bashal'aran","history of bashal'aran"},it="history"},{q="Why does Thundris Windweaver want me to investigate Bashal'Aran?",a="Thundris Windweaver watches the ancient ruins of Bashal'Aran with growing dread. Corrupted sprites and satyrs swarm the grounds, drawing upon lingering arcane energies to magnify their demonic power. Yet among this infestation, a single shrine wrapped in a curious blue aura remains utterly untouched by the demons. Thundris needs to understand what power keeps them at bay—and whether it might hold the key to pushing back the corruption encroaching upon Darkshore.",al={"why investigate bashal'aran","thundris motive","why send me to bashal'aran"},it="motive",add="2cba9e48"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Bashal'Aran recalls what your ancient kin lost in the Sundering. Their lingering shades keep lonely vigils as demonic corruption presses in.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance wanderer, you help Auberdine's scouts push into Darkshore's contested ruins and keep demonic threats from reaching the coast."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","blue aura","darkshore","grell","kaldorei ruins","satyr","thundris windweaver"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:4761","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",["end"]="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=954},src={"Bashal'Aran (quest)"}}
E["quest:955"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Magic still binds Asterion beneath Bashal'Aran's broken stones. The ancient night elf seeks release from his ghostly form and suspects the grells have touched the seal that holds him. He asks travelers to gather their earrings and trace its lingering magic.",h="Magic still binds Asterion beneath Bashal'Aran's broken stones.",sec={{t="A Centuries-Old Torment",b="For centuries, Asterion has waited among Bashal'Aran's shattered marble. The ancient night elf spirit remains caught between life and true death beneath Darkshore's canopy. Arcane craft binds him to the ruined settlement, and he cannot break free alone. Solitude and despair have worn down his mind.",sp=0},{t="Traces in the Wild",b="Asterion believes an ancient seal hidden in the ruins may hold the key to his release. He cannot search the brush and fallen stones himself. The feral grells of Bashal'Aran forage there and steal small baubles, so he asks travelers to gather their earrings. He hopes the trinkets' lingering magic will lead him to the seal that torments his soul.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf ghost bound to Bashal'Aran's ruins in Darkshore. A mystical seal has held him in torment for centuries, and he longs to be free of his spectral state.",al={"asterion lore","who is the ghost in bashal'aran","asterion quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Asterion want grell earrings?",a="Asterion believes the grells have touched the seal that binds him. Their earrings may carry traces of its magic and help him find it.",al={"why grell earrings","grell earring purpose","earrings quest darkshore"},it="item"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran lies in Darkshore's forested coast, an ancient night elf ruin from before the Great Sundering. Wild grells, satyrs, and spectral remnants of its fallen inhabitants roam there.",al={"what is bashal'aran","bashal'aran history","ruins of bashal'aran"},it="place"},{q="What happens after collecting the earrings?",a="After travelers gather the earrings, Asterion examines them. He senses the grells brushed against the seal in what he considers recent times, though they do not carry it. This lets him narrow down its location in the ruins.",al={"what do the earrings show","did the grells have the seal","grell earring result"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Asterion trapped here?",a="An ancient magical seal bound Asterion to Bashal'Aran centuries ago. It anchors his spirit to the ruins and keeps him from finding peaceful rest.",al={"who bound asterion","how is asterion bound","asterion's seal"},it="history"},{q="What are grells?",a="Grells are small, malicious woodland creatures native to Kalimdor's forests. They have sharp claws, favor trinkets, and often infest old ruins and attack travelers.",al={"what is a grell","grells lore","darkshore grells"},it="target"},{q="Why does Asterion want this done?",a="Asterion is trapped in an agonizing spectral form, anchored to the ruins of Bashal'Aran by an ancient magical seal. Centurylong confinement has slowly eroded his sanity, and he yearns for release from this torment. By inspecting the earrings carried by the local creatures, he hopes to magically scry the precise location of the ward that binds him so it can ultimately be destroyed.",al={"asterion motive","why help asterion","why does asterion want earrings"},it="motive",add="99bf1a9e"},{q="Why does Asterion need your help instead of acting himself?",a="Asterion is an insubstantial ghost bound directly to the ruins by powerful sorcery. Incapable of venturing far beyond his immediate resting place or physically fighting the grells and sprites himself, he relies entirely on passing mortals to hunt the creatures and gather their trinkets for his divinations.",al={"why does asterion need me","why can't asterion get the earrings","why can't asterion leave"},it="why_me",add="a8a71265"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei, you may see Asterion as a reminder of the ancient civilization lost in the Sundering and of souls bound in ruin for millennia.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize Asterion's use of enchanted trinkets to trace lingering magic as an ancient Highborne practice of arcane divination.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help pacify Darkshore's treacherous northern reaches by clearing the chaotic grells around Bashal'Aran."},kw={"asterion","bashal'aran","binding","darkshore","ghost","grell","grell earring","seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","zone:darkshore","quest:954","quest:99141"},m={start="Asterion",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=955,ri={"Grell Earring"}},src={"Bashal'Aran (2)"}}
E["quest:956"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Among the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, Asterion seeks release from his prison. He has traced the binding magic to the satyrs who command the grells. Now he asks travelers to recover the Ancient Moonstone Seal.",h="Among the ruined pillars of Bashal'Aran, Asterion seeks release from his prison.",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Stone",b="For more than a thousand years, Asterion has been bound within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. The marble pillars mark the bounds of his prison. His strength and ancient magic cannot carry him beyond them. A cursed relic holds him there.\n\nThrough the centuries, Asterion has watched Darkshore's canopy. He wonders if the worn stone around him might ever set him free.",sp=0},{t="Satyrs and the Moonstone Seal",b="Nearby grells bore traces of the magic binding Asterion. From them, he reasoned that the Ancient Moonstone Seal was the enchantment's source. The satyrs who command the grells hold the seal now. These demonic night elves roam the ancient groves and keep watch over the relic. Asterion needs travelers to recover the seal so its binding power can be broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is an ancient night elf spirit trapped among Bashal'Aran's ruined pillars. Ancient magic has bound him for more than a thousand years, keeping him from leaving his stone prison or passing on.",al={"who is asterion","asterion lore","ghost in bashal aran"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the satyrs have the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="The satyrs command the wild grells of northern Darkshore. Asterion sensed traces of his binding magic in the grells, then deduced that the satyrs held the Ancient Moonstone Seal, the source of his captivity.",al={"why do satyrs have seal","satyr moonstone seal","ancient moonstone seal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens once the seal is recovered?",a="When Asterion takes the recovered Ancient Moonstone Seal, the relic that bound him for centuries, it can be broken. Then he will be free to walk the forests again.",al={"what does seal do","recovering the seal"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elf ruin on the misty shores of northern Darkshore. Once a magnificent settlement or holy enclave, it now lies broken, plagued by grells, satyrs, and trapped spirits from an earlier age.",al={"bashal aran lore","what is bashal aran"},it="place"},{q="How long has Asterion been trapped here?",a="Asterion has been imprisoned for more than a thousand years. Neither strength nor magic can break the boundary, and through the centuries he has wondered if he will ever be free.",al={"how old is asterion","how long trapped"},it="history"},{q="Can Asterion simply walk away from the shrine?",a="No. The Ancient Moonstone Seal maintains a barrier around the shrine, and the stone pillars keep Asterion's spirit from crossing beyond them.",al={"can asterion leave","why is ghost trapped"}},{q="Why does Asterion want the seal recovered?",a="Asterion is desperate for freedom. The ancient relic serves as the binding anchor of his eternal prison, holding his spirit trapped within the ruined shrine. For over a thousand years, he has stared past the stone pillars, unable to break their hold through strength or sorcery. Recovering the artifact is the only way to destroy it and finally allow him to walk the forests freely once more.",al={"why does asterion want this done","asterion motive","why help asterion"},it="motive",add="31aed888"},{q="What is the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is a magical relic that acts as the key to Asterion's captivity. It creates an intangible barrier between the pillars of Bashal'Aran, functioning like an eternal cell that no spell or physical strength of his can shatter. As long as the seal endures in the hands of the nearby corrupt forces, Asterion remains bound to the shrine.",al={"what is the ancient moonstone seal","what does the moonstone seal do","ancient moonstone seal purpose"},it="item",add="5f1ff286"},{q="Why are you sent against the local satyrs?",a="The satyrs command the vile grells swarming the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Because the lesser grells bore traces of the seal's enchantment, Asterion deduced that their masters must have claimed the artifact itself. Corrupt and drawn to ancient magical relics, the satyrs hold the seal within their encampment, making them your target.",al={"who are the satyrs in bashal'aran","why fight the satyrs","who has the seal"},it="target",add="c7650517"},{q="Why can't Asterion retrieve the seal himself?",a="Asterion cannot leave the confines of the shrine. The magic of the seal keeps him utterly bound within its perimeter, treating the stone pillars as impassable bars. He possesses neither the strength nor the sorcery to breach his confinement, leaving him completely reliant on an outsider to venture into the satyr camps on his behalf.",al={"why does asterion need me","why cant asterion get the seal","why me asterion"},it="why_me",add="341831b6"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, Bashal'Aran recalls your people's ancient past. Lingering ancestors remain chained to the earth by satyrs, whose kind embody the demonic betrayal of the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="As a Druid, you know the satyrs' influence still corrupts Darkshore's wildlife. It also disturbs ancient spirits who should rest peacefully in nature's cycle.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure Kalimdor's northern coast by cleansing Darkshore's ruins of satyr corruption. That work also helps the Kaldorei lay their tragic past to rest."},kw={"ancient moonstone seal","asterion","bashal'aran","darkshore","grell","kaldorei","night elf ghost","satyr"},rel={"npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:satyr","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=956,ri={"Ancient Moonstone Seal"}},src={"Bashal'Aran (3)"}}
E["quest:957"] = {t="quest",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="At Bashal'Aran, Asterion's spirit remains bound by an ancient seal. You carry the seal south to Ameth'Aran, where an old flame may break his bonds.",h="At Bashal'Aran, Asterion's spirit remains bound by an ancient seal.",sec={{t="A Prison of Ancient Sorcery",b="Asterion's spirit remains chained in death at Bashal'Aran by an Ancient Moonstone Seal. Highborne sorcerers forged it before the Great Sundering, and no ordinary strength can break its power. Only an ancient flame still burning among Ameth'Aran's fallen stones to the south can destroy it.",sp=0},{t="Twin Ruins of Darkshore",b="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister settlements of the kaldorei under Queen Azshara, when the Well of Eternity anchored their empire. Now both are overgrown, haunted ruins, where ghosts linger and arcane power remains volatile. In a stone gazebo at Ameth'Aran, a mystical brazier burns with cyan fire. Only this flame can consume Asterion's binding relic.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance Awakens",b="Asterion is free once the seal is destroyed, and sees a shattered Kalimdor far changed from the golden age he remembers. Yet freedom brings no peace. He senses that Athrikus, his former Highborne master and jailor, still endures. Despair turns to a cold hunger for revenge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Asterion?",a="Asterion is a night elf spirit trapped in Bashal'Aran's ruins. He dates back ten thousand years, to Queen Azshara's reign, and a seal forged by one of the most powerful Highborne binds him there.",al={"asterion","who is the ghost","npc asterion"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I destroy the Ancient Moonstone Seal?",a="Carry the Ancient Moonstone Seal south to Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran's twin ruin. In a stone gazebo, a large cubical brazier burns with ancient greenish-blue fire that can destroy it.",al={"where is the flame","ancient flame location","destroy seal"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the relationship between Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities in the ancient night elf empire before the Sundering. Both were devastated ten thousand years ago, leaving haunted stone pillars, lingering arcane power, and restless spirits.",al={"twin ruins","ametharan connection","bashalaran ametharan"},it="place"},{q="Who imprisoned Asterion?",a="Asterion says one of the most powerful Highborne made the seal that binds him. His former master is revealed as the story continues.",al={"who imprisoned asterion","who is athrikus","asterion master"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="What era does Asterion remember?",a="Asterion remembers the age when the original Well of Eternity still existed, Queen Azshara ruled the empire, and Highborne nobles held their majestic courts before the Sundering.",al={"asterion past","well of eternity era","how old is asterion"},it="history"},{q="Does freeing Asterion lay his spirit to rest?",a="Destroying the seal is meant to break Asterion's prison. What freedom means to him becomes clear when you return.",al={"does asterion pass on","what happens to asterion","asterion after free"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Asterion want the Ancient Moonstone Seal destroyed?",a="The Ancient Moonstone Seal is the anchor binding Asterion's spirit in torment within the ruins of Bashal'Aran. Crafted millennia ago by powerful Highborne sorcery, it keeps him imprisoned and blind to the world beyond. Destroying it in the mystical ancient flame of Ameth'Aran is the only way to shatter his ethereal chains, granting him freedom and the clarity to witness what has become of Kalimdor.",al={"why destroy moonstone seal","asterion motive","why does asterion want to break the seal"},it="motive",add="8275c861"},{q="Why does Asterion need you to take the seal to Ameth'Aran?",a="Bound by the ancient Highborne magic anchoring him to Bashal'Aran, Asterion cannot leave the immediate ruins, let alone travel south to Ameth'Aran. He needs a traveler to carry the seal into the ancient flame.",al={"why cant asterion destroy the seal","why does asterion need me","why send an adventurer to destroy the seal"},it="why_me",add="51df5ddd"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of modern Kalimdor, you meet your people's pre-Sundering past and the lingering corruption of Queen Azshara's Highborne nobility when Asterion is freed.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you glimpse the raw arcane power of ancient Highborne sorcerers in the enchantments binding Asterion and the flames that endure at Ameth'Aran.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help clear ancient curses in Darkshore and secure the borders for new night elf settlements expanding from Auberdine."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus","azshara","bashal'aran","darkshore","highborne","moonstone seal"},rel={"npc:asterion","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:highborne","quest:954","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Asterion",level="13",faction="Alliance",id=957},src={"Bashal'Aran (4)"}}
E["quest:960"] = {t="quest",n="Onu is meditating",z="darkshore",s="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Onu enters a deep trance as a threat grows. The ancient of lore weighs the alliance and motives of the Twilight's Hammer cult and the naga. If you lose your scrying phial, speak to him for another.",h="At the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, Onu enters a deep trance as a threat grows.",sec={{t="A Mind in Deep Contemplation",b="In the Grove of the Ancients, Onu holds Kalimdor's history in his ancient memory. Ominous reports of dark excavations at the Master's Glaive draw his vast consciousness inward. He considers what brings the fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists and the naga to the petrified remains of an ancient behemoth. As you carry out his reconnaissance, Onu remains within reach and can replace a scrying phial misplaced in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Scrying the Depths",b="Onu uses nature-attuned divination to watch the ruins without risking his physical presence. He entrusts you with a scrying phial, which conjures a scrying bowl at the excavation site and lets him commune from afar. The journey south through Darkshore is perilous, with hostile wildlife and cultist patrols, so mishaps can happen.\n\nOnu's trance is an attentive vigil, not unbroken slumber. He readily offers another vial of sacred waters so you can continue the investigation of the Master's Glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Onu meditating?",a="Onu meditates over the disturbing presence of the Twilight's Hammer cult and the naga at the Master's Glaive. He seeks to perceive their motives and guide you as you investigate the site.",al={"why is onu meditating","onu trance","what is onu doing"},it="motive"},{q="What is the purpose of this interaction?",a="This interaction is a safety measure for adventurers at The Master's Glaive. If you lose your Phial of Scrying, speaking with Onu provides a replacement so you can complete the ritual.",al={"lost phial of scrying","get another phial","onu replacement quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Onu located?",a="Onu is rooted in the Grove of the Ancients in central-southern Darkshore, just off the main road.",al={"onu location","where to find onu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do I do with the Phial of Scrying?",a="Carry the phial to the Master's Glaive and use it to create a scrying bowl. Onu can then communicate with you through the bowl.",al={"how to use phial of scrying","scrying bowl darkshore","phial of scrying purpose"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is an ancient excavation site in southern Darkshore. There, the colossal petrified skull of a forgotten entity lies pierced by a gargantuan blade. Cultists and naga have gathered there for unknown, malevolent purposes.",al={"what is masters glaive","monument in south darkshore"},it="place"},{q="Can Horde players interact with Onu here?",a="Onu is allied strictly with the night elves and the Alliance. Horde adventurers near the Grove of the Ancients will find him and his protectors hostile or uncooperative.",al={"is onu alliance only","horde onu meditating"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why does Onu need your help instead of investigating himself?",a="Onu remains in the Grove of the Ancients to meditate on the Twilight's Hammer and naga. He relies on travelers to investigate the Master's Glaive and contact him through a scrying bowl.",al={"why send me","why doesn't onu go","why onu needs you"},it="why_me",add="72a6a09e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you revere ancients of lore like Onu, stewards of Kalimdor's balance. Their ageless wisdom helps you understand disturbances in Darkshore's wilds.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you share a profound bond with nature and ancients of lore. Scrying rituals reflect the Cenarion Circle's way of surveying tainted ground from a distance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, securing Darkshore from cultists and aquatic invaders matters as you journey between Teldrassil and Ashenvale."},kw={"darkshore","grove of the ancients","master's glaive","meditating","onu","phial of scrying","scrying bowl","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","quest:950","quest:948","subzone:master-s-glaive","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Onu",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=960},src={"Onu is meditating"}}
E["quest:963"] = {t="quest",n="For Love Eternal",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Cerellean Whiteclaw asks you to ease Anaya Dawnrunner's torment in Ameth'Aran. His grief has lasted since the city fell.",h="In Auberdine, Cerellean Whiteclaw asks you to ease Anaya Dawnrunner's torment in Ameth'Aran.",sec={{t="A Slumber Full of Grief",b="Ten thousand years ago, the War of the Ancients tore Kalimdor apart around the Well of Eternity. Ameth'Aran fell, and Anaya Dawnrunner was lost to Cerellean Whiteclaw. Grief-stricken, Cerellean joined Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage in the druids' long hibernation. He hoped the ages spent walking the Emerald Dream would quiet his heart, but his sorrow endured.",sp=0},{t="The Ghost of Ameth'Aran",b="When he awoke, Cerellean wandered Darkshore in a stupor. At last he came to the melancholy ruins of Ameth'Aran, where he saw Anaya's tortured ghost. He cannot raise a weapon against the woman he loved. So he asks passing travelers to destroy her tormented form, retrieve her pendant, and bring peace to her troubled soul.",sp=0},{t="Parting Across the Veil",b="When Anaya's pendant reaches Auberdine, her spectral remnant appears before Cerellean for the last time. Freed from the anguish binding her to the ruins, Anaya gives him a brief farewell and fades away. By the seaside, the grieving druid weeps, yet finds bittersweet solace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cerellean Whiteclaw?",a="Cerellean Whiteclaw is a night elf druid resting in Auberdine. After losing Anaya in the Sundering ten thousand years ago, he entered the druids' long hibernation with Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage. His sorrow endured through the ages.",al={"cerellean whiteclaw","who gives for love eternal","cerellean lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner was a night elf who lived in Ameth'Aran before the Great Sundering. She died when the city fell after the War of the Ancients. Her ghost remains trapped in its ruins.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","who is anaya","anaya darkshore"},it="target"},{q="Where is Anaya's spirit located?",a="Anaya's spirit wanders the ancient, ghost-infested ruins of Ameth'Aran in southern Darkshore, east of the main road.",al={"anaya location","where is anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why couldn't Cerellean free Anaya himself?",a="Cerellean cannot bear to raise his hand or cast a spell against Anaya's apparition. Ten thousand years have passed, yet he cannot strike at her while she suffers.",al={"why doesn't cerellean kill anaya","why cerellean asks for help"},it="why_me"},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran was an ancient night elven settlement destroyed in the Sundering that followed the War of the Ancients. Its ruins in Darkshore still hold lingering ghosts and arcane echoes.",al={"ameth'aran history","fall of ameth'aran","what is ameth'aran"},it="history"},{q="What happens when you return Anaya's pendant?",a="You bring Anaya's pendant to Cerellean in Auberdine after freeing her troubled spirit. What follows is revealed when you return.",al={"quest turn in anaya","cerellean ending","for love eternal ending"},sp=1},{q="Why does Cerellean Whiteclaw want Anaya's spirit freed?",a="Cerellean believed his love, Anaya, had perished millennia ago when Ameth'Aran was shattered during the Sundering. Discovering her restless, tormented ghost wandering the ruins broke his heart. Knowing she suffers bound to this realm, he cannot endure the thought of her remaining in anguish, yet he cannot bear to raise a hand against her himself.",al={"why does cerellean want this done","cerellean motive","why destroy anaya spirit"},it="motive",add="dc23d6a3"},{q="What is Anaya's Pendant for?",a="Anaya's Pendant is the keepsake Cerellean asks you to bring back after freeing her troubled spirit in Ameth'Aran.",al={"anayas pendant use","what does anayas pendant do","purpose of anayas pendant"},it="item",add="ed60ea9d"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see the personal cost borne by those who slept for thousands of years beside Shan'do Stormrage. Cerellean woke to a world still marked by ancient losses.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Darkshore, you see the lasting scars of the Great Sundering and the fall of your ancient cities in Cerellean's story.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you see how your night elven allies carry grief across millennia as they adjust to the waking world."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","anaya's pendant","auberdine","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","for love eternal","sundering"},rel={"npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Cerellean Whiteclaw",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=963,ri={"Anaya's Pendant"}},src={"For Love Eternal"}}
E["quest:965"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="North of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze fears trouble at an ancient ruin. She sent Balthule Shadowstrike to watch the Tower of Althalaxx, but his report has not come.",h="North of Auberdine, Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze fears trouble at an ancient ruin.",sec={{t="A Scout Unaccounted For",b="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze keeps watch for danger around Auberdine. Suspicious activity near the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore caught her attention, so she sent Balthule Shadowstrike to watch the ancient ruin. Days have passed without word. Elissa asks you to travel north, find Balthule, and make sure he has not met an untimely end.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Upon the Ruin",b="The road north from Auberdine passes ancient Kaldorei ruins and crosses the Cliffspring River before it reaches the tower. Balthule survived his first watch, though he could send no word back to Auberdine. You find him in the surrounding woods. There, he confirms Elissa's fears: dark and troubling events are underway inside the crumbling stone spire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze?",a="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze is a night elf Sentinel stationed in Auberdine. She protects the settlement from dangers across Darkshore and watches for threats such as the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"elissa starbreeze","who gives quest","auberdine questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is the scout Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze sent to watch strange activity around the Tower of Althalaxx. He keeps watch outside the ruin for signs of hostile forces.",al={"balthule","who is the scout","shadowstrike"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Tower of Althalaxx located?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx stands in northeastern Darkshore. From Auberdine, head east and follow the northern road past Bashal'Aran, then cross the bridge over the Cliffspring River until the spire comes into view.",al={"tower of althalaxx location","where is the tower","how to find althalaxx"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was a scout sent to the tower in the first place?",a="Elissa sent Balthule to watch strange activity around the Tower of Althalaxx as part of her duty to protect Auberdine.",al={"why watch the tower","what is wrong at althalaxx","why sent balthule"},it="origin"},{q="Why hasn't Balthule returned to Auberdine?",a="Elissa has not received Balthule's report, so she asks you to check on him. Balthule can explain his situation when you find him.",al={"why balthule missing","is balthule trapped","why did balthule stay"},it="threat"},{q="Does this quest chain continue?",a="Yes. Finding Balthule Shadowstrike begins a multi-part investigation into the dark forces occupying the Tower of Althalaxx and their ambitions in Darkshore.",al={"is this a chain","what quest comes next","althalaxx chain"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze want this done?",a="As a Sentinel charged with the defense of Auberdine, Elissa Starbreeze is responsible for safeguarding Darkshore from encroaching threats. She dispatched Balthule Shadowstrike to investigate suspicious occurrences near the Tower of Althalaxx, but he is long overdue. Fearing he has fallen into unexpected peril, she needs someone to locate him and confirm his safety.",al={"why find balthule","elissa starbreeze motive","why send me to tower of althalaxx"},it="motive",add="895f5562"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Althalaxx's ruins recall the fallen highborne of ancient Kalimdor. Corruption festers in their stones, and guarding Auberdine against it is a vital duty for the sentinels.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on Auberdine as the Alliance's main gateway into northern Kalimdor. Its surrounding roads and borders need protection."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule shadowstrike","darkshore","elissa starbreeze","scout","sentinel","tower"},rel={"npc:sentinel-elissa-starbreeze","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:954"},m={start="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze",["end"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=965},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["quest:966"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Warlocks gather at the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, drawing Balthule Shadowstrike's watchful eye. He asks travelers to recover scraps of parchment from the fanatics camped outside the ruins, hoping to learn who they are and what they seek.",h="Warlocks gather at the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore, drawing Balthule Shadowstrike's watchful eye.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Shallows",b="Balthule Shadowstrike watches the misty shore of northern Darkshore and keeps the ancient Tower of Althalaxx in sight. Auberdine sent him to watch the ruin and warn Delgren the Purifier if danger grows. Yet leaving his post to report might let the dark spellcasters among the stones slip from view. So Balthule asks passing travelers to scout the camps around the tower.",sp=0},{t="Deciphering the Cult",b="The lesser followers at the ruined grounds carry scraps of scrolls and notes. Several worn parchments tell Balthule their name: the Cult of the Dark Strand. He has never heard of the sect, and now knows more than a band of rogue warlocks is at work. Delgren needs warning at once.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance scout stationed on the road near the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Auberdine's leaders sent him to watch the suspicious gatherings and report to Delgren the Purifier.",al={"balthule shadowstrike lore","who is balthule","balthule darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven ruin in northern Darkshore. Sinister warlocks and their cultist thralls have occupied the grounds around it and its interior, performing dark rituals beyond Auberdine's watch.",al={"tower of althalaxx","what is althalaxx","darkshore ruined tower"},it="place"},{q="Who are the cultists surrounding the tower?",a="The cultists around the tower belong to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a secretive band of warlocks and zealots gathered at the ancient elven ruins to pursue dark summoning rituals.",al={"who are the warlocks","cult of the dark strand","dark strand fanatics"},it="target"},{q="Why does Balthule warn against entering the tower?",a="Balthule warns that the warlocks inside the upper tower are far more powerful and dangerous than the fanatics camped among the ruins. He advises gathering intelligence from the perimeter before trying to storm the stronghold.",al={"can i go into the tower","tower warlocks dangerous","inside the tower"},it="danger"},{q="What do the worn parchments reveal?",a="Scraps carried by the cult's fanatics reveal the group's name: the Cult of the Dark Strand. Balthule learns that the occupants are an organized sect whose presence threatens the region.",al={"what is on the parchments","worn parchment lore","cult notes"},it="item"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale who works to cleanse demonic and corrupt influences. He suspects malicious activity is taking root at the Tower of Althalaxx and relies on scouts like Balthule for intelligence.",al={"delgren","who is delgren","delgren the purifier"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want this done?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike fears that dark forces are gathering in secret right on Darkshore's borders. While Delgren suspected warlocks were congregating at the ancient ruins, neither of them knows who they are or what foul ritual they intend to enact. Balthule needs enough written evidence to piece together their identity and motives before taking decisive action to protect the region.",al={"why balthule wants parchments","balthule motive","why investigate althalaxx"},it="motive",add="bc625320"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike send you instead of going himself?",a="Balthule is stationed on a solitary reconnaissance watch outside the ruins. He cannot leave his post to scour the surrounding cultist camps or return to Auberdine to report, terrified that any absence might cause him to miss critical enemy movements. By having you confront the outer cultists and retrieve their writings, he can maintain continuous surveillance over the tower.",al={"why does balthule need help","why not balthule","why balthule asks you"},it="why_me",add="151da73d"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can aid Delgren the Purifier's crusade against fel and demonic corruption by helping uncover a dark cult in northern Darkshore.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can see how covens beyond Alliance and Horde authority seize ancient ruins for their summonings.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the dark cultists' desecration of the Tower of Althalaxx as another defilement of ancient elven heritage along Kalimdor's shores."},kw={"althalaxx","auberdine","balthule","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","fanatics","parchment","purifier","shadowstrike","warlocks"},rel={"npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","quest:965","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:light"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=966,ri={"Worn Parchment"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (2)"}}
E["quest:967"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="At the Tower of Althalaxx, Dark Strand cultists gather, and Balthule Shadowstrike needs help. He sends a warning with an Alliance courier to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale for his mentor, Delgren the Purifier.",h="At the Tower of Althalaxx, Dark Strand cultists gather, and Balthule Shadowstrike needs help.",sec={{t="A Plea for Reinforcements",b="Balthule Shadowstrike sees that one scout cannot face the Dark Strand threat alone. After clashing with cultists near the Tower of Althalaxx, he writes a report for his master, Delgren the Purifier, and gives it to an Alliance messenger. The cult's summoners grow bolder. Balthule needs seasoned leaders to direct a response.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Ashenvale",b="Balthule's dispatch sends you south along Darkshore's coastal road, then across the wooded border into Ashenvale. Delgren the Purifier is stationed at Maestra's Post beside the western road. The human paladin works to cleanse demons and undead from the woodland. Night elven customs once seemed strange to him, but he has earned the Sentinels' deep respect as an indispensable ally.",sp=0},{t="A Holy Warrior Awakened",b="Delgren the Purifier receives Balthule's urgent letter and reads it with grim resolve. Devoted to the Holy Light, he sees dark cultists, corrupted souls, and demonic fiends in the ancient woods as an intolerable blight. The letter reports the Dark Strand's entrenched foothold in the ruined highborne tower. Delgren prepares to take charge and strike back.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale. Devoted to the Holy Light, he brings martial and spiritual skill to the night elf Sentinels' fight against demons and undead in their ancestral forests.",al={"delgren the purifier","who is delgren","delgren lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Balthule Shadowstrike sending a messenger to Ashenvale?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is a scout outside the Tower of Althalaxx, where he studies the Dark Strand cult. As its dark rituals and numbers grow, he sends his findings to his mentor Delgren so they can organize a strike.",al={"why send letter to delgren","balthule letter reason"},it="motive"},{q="What is the relationship between Balthule and Delgren?",a="Delgren is Balthule's master. The human paladin taught the night elf the art of battle and the teachings of the Holy Light. Their bond is close despite their cultural differences.",al={"balthule and delgren","how do balthule and delgren know each other"},it="ties"},{q="Where is Maestra's Post?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost in western Ashenvale beside the main road south from Darkshore. Travelers pass it on their way into the forest.",al={"maestras post location","where is maestras post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Dark Strand cult doing at the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Dark Strand cult operates from the ruined highborne Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Its members practice dark arts and consort with demonic powers. They threaten to spread corruption along the shoreline.",al={"dark strand cult althalaxx","tower of althalaxx cultists"},it="threat"},{q="How does Delgren view his alliance with the night elves?",a="Delgren found night elven manners and ways unfamiliar when he arrived in Kalimdor. Fighting common evils beside them has earned the Sentinels his deep respect.",al={"delgren night elves","human paladin night elves"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Balthule choose you as his messenger instead of going himself?",a="Balthule must remain stationed near the Tower of Althalaxx to keep a watchful eye on the Dark Strand cultists and monitor their escalating threat. With the journey stretching across the entire length of Darkshore into Ashenvale, he needs a capable and well-armed traveler who can survive the dangerous roads and guarantee the urgent warning safely reaches Delgren's hands.",al={"why send me to delgren","why balthule messenger","why can't balthule deliver the letter"},it="why_me",add="4ad41352"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can look to Delgren as an example of your holy calling in unfamiliar lands. The human crusader wields the Light and has earned the trust of Kalimdor's reclusive night elves.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see your Sentinels building a practical partnership with eastern allies who have come to purge demonic remnants from your woods.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how Balthule in Darkshore and Delgren in Ashenvale keep the scattered Alliance garrisons of northern Kalimdor in contact."},kw={"ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","dark strand","darkshore","delgren the purifier","holy light","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","topic:light","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=967},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (3)"}}
E["quest:968"] = {t="quest",n="Tools of the Highborne",z="darkshore",s="Thundris Windweaver sends you from Auberdine to Ameth'Aran. Highborne spirits still haunt the ruins with enchanted relics in their hands, and he wants them taken away.",h="Thundris Windweaver sends you from Auberdine to Ameth'Aran.",sec={{t="Echoes in the Ruins",b="Ameth'Aran lies south of Auberdine and east of the coastal highway. Its stone foundations are overgrown. Ten thousand years ago, it was a stronghold of the Highborne, the privileged aristocracy of the ancient night elven empire.\n\nTheir unchecked arcane magic helped bring about the Sundering, which shattered the settlement. Yet its inhabitants never truly left. Sentinels patrolling Darkshore report Highborne ghosts in the sunken plazas, still clutching the enchanted tools and trinkets they held in life.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Arcane Past",b="For the kaldorei, arcane magic recalls a danger that nearly destroyed life on Azeroth. Thundris Windweaver fears that the Highborne implements could invite corruption if they remain in ghostly hands. So he sends you to wrest the relics from the restless spirits. He intends to have them destroyed before their tainted magic can fuel another disaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Highborne relics?",a="The relics lie in Ameth'Aran, south of Auberdine and east of Darkshore's main path. Wandering spirits carry them through the ruined stone courtyards.",al={"where are the relics","ameth'aran location","where to find relics"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who is Thundris Windweaver?",a="Thundris Windweaver is a night elf scholar and elder who lives in Auberdine. He works with the local Sentinels to guard Darkshore against lingering magical taints and ancient curses left by the Sundering.",al={"thundris windweaver","who gives tools of the highborne"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thundris want these relics destroyed?",a="Thundris fears the relics' arcane power could awaken dormant evils. Night elf society rejects arcane magic because reckless Highborne sorcery caused the Great Sundering.",al={"why destroy the relics","purpose of tools of the highborne"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of spirits haunt Ameth'Aran?",a="The spirits are Highborne aristocrats who died during the War of the Ancients. They still cling to their pride, power, and magical artifacts, reenacting their faded lives among the ruins.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","what are the spirits"},it="target"},{q="Why are the Highborne still bound to the ruins?",a="Thundris does not know why the Highborne remain bound to Ameth'Aran. The Sentinels have told him only that the spirits persist among the ruins and still wield their ancient magical implements.",al={"why are they ghosts","highborne curse"},it="history"},{q="What happens to the relics after you turn them in?",a="Thundris Windweaver takes custody of the relics and plans to dismantle and destroy them. He wants to ensure their dormant arcane taint can never be harnessed or released again.",al={"what does thundris do with relics","relic fate"},it="next_step"},{q="What are the Highborne Relics?",a="These relics are ancient magical implements preserved from before the Great Sundering, once wielded by the elite sorcerers of Queen Azshara's court. Even after ten thousand years, they retain the lingering taint of the arcane reckless dabbling that tore ancient Kalimdor apart. Left in the hands of lingering ghosts, they remain conduits of dormant, dangerous power.",al={"what are highborne relics","what is highborne relic","highborne relic lore"},it="item",add="df86da6d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, the ghosts of Ameth'Aran recall your ancestors' hubris and the Sundering that shattered their empire.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize the relics as rare, pristine examples of Highborne craftsmanship from before the Sundering. Still, the kaldorei seek to destroy them.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you help clear corrupted arcane remnants from Ameth'Aran and ease the spiritual wounds disturbing Darkshore's natural tranquility.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help the night elves secure their haunted lands and strengthen the Alliance's presence and solidarity in the ancient forests of northern Kalimdor."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","highborne","relics","sundering","thundris windweaver"},rel={"subzone:ameth-aran","quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","topic:highborne","zone:darkshore","topic:sentinels"},m={start="Thundris Windweaver",level="12",faction="Alliance",id=958,ri={"Highborne Relic (Classic)"}},src={"Tools of the Highborne"}}
E["quest:973"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="At the Tower of Althalaxx, dark cultists lead Delgren the Purifier to Ilkrud Magthrull. He sends you south through Darkshore into Ashenvale to slay the orc warlock at Fire Scar Shrine and recover his tome.",h="At the Tower of Althalaxx, dark cultists lead Delgren the Purifier to Ilkrud Magthrull.",sec={{t="A Hunt Into Ashenvale",b="Delgren the Purifier traces the dark cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx to Ilkrud Magthrull, an orc warlock. Ilkrud works from Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Delgren fears his magic could spread through the elven woodlands, so he sends you to kill the warlock and take his tome. He hopes its contents will reveal his master's designs.",sp=0},{t="The Warlock's Lair",b="At Fire Scar Shrine, Ilkrud keeps company with a summoned succubus and guardian felslayers. Red pillars mark the rocky ascent to the shrine. Once Ilkrud is dead, Delgren can study his tome. Its knowledge and commands connect to the rituals at Althalaxx.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion at Maestra's Post, a night elf outpost on the border between Darkshore and Ashenvale. He directs efforts against demonic corruption and cultists in the region.",al={"delgren","delgren lore","who starts quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ilkrud Magthrull?",a="Ilkrud Magthrull is an orc warlock who has made his lair at Fire Scar Shrine in southwestern Ashenvale. Delgren first considered him a minor annoyance, but his ties to the dark rites at the Tower of Althalaxx make him a critical target.",al={"ilkrud","who is ilkrud magthrull","orc warlock ashenvale"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Fire Scar Shrine located?",a="Fire Scar Shrine lies in southwestern Ashenvale, south of the Shrine of Aessina and west of Astranaar. Demons infest the corrupted enclave, and two red pillars flank the path to Ilkrud's altar.",al={"fire scar shrine location","where is ilkrud","how to reach ilkrud"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Delgren need Ilkrud Magthrull's tome?",a="Ilkrud's tome holds his dark rituals and communications. Delgren hopes to decipher them and discover the plot linking the warlock to the cultists around the Tower of Althalaxx.",al={"why tome","what is in ilkrud's tome","purpose of tome"},it="item"},{q="How does this quest connect Darkshore to Ashenvale?",a="The investigation begins at the Tower of Althalaxx on Darkshore's northern coast. As the mystery deepens, the cultists' network leads south through Darkshore into Ashenvale's contested forests.",al={"darkshore to ashenvale quest","althalaxx chain connection"}},{q="What happens after recovering the tome?",a="Delgren studies the tome to uncover the schemes behind the cultists at the Tower of Althalaxx. His findings lead to the final confrontations in the chain.",al={"next quest","what follows althalaxx 5"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Delgren the Purifier want this done?",a="Delgren the Purifier is dedicated to rooting out demonic corruption in the region. While he previously viewed Ilkrud Magthrull as little more than a minor annoyance, the warlock's sinister research and active presence at the corrupted Fire Scar Shrine make him a growing menace that Delgren can no longer ignore.",al={"delgren motive","why kill ilkrud magthrull","delgren the purifier goal"},it="motive",add="b25de95c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you travel from Darkshore into Ashenvale's demon-tainted reaches to confront a growing menace.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you join Delgren the Purifier in fighting fel summoners and taking their corrupt tomes. You answer the Holy Light's call against demonic corruption.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you face Ilkrud Magthrull, a fellow practitioner of the dark arts. He guards his unholy texts with summoned succubi and voidwalkers.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you defend Ashenvale's ancient forests from the defilement at Fire Scar Shrine by bringing Ilkrud down."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","delgren","fire scar shrine","ilkrud","maestra","magthrull","tome","warlock"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","subzone:fire-scar-shrine","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","subzone:shrine-of-aessina","subzone:astranaar"},m={start="Delgren the Purifier",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=973,ri={"Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome"}},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (5)"}}
E["quest:97926"] = {t="quest",n="Making Do",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine waits for word from Stormwind, but no aid is coming. Making Do carries Alexston's Reply across the sea to Elder Thundris Windweaver.",h="Auberdine waits for word from Stormwind, but no aid is coming.",sec={{t="A Courier Across the Sea",b="You carry Alexston's Reply across the sea to Elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. The letter brings no troops or relief. Stormwind's representative explains that the kingdom's treasury is nearly empty. What wealth remains must stretch across its own struggling territories.",sp=0},{t="Left to Their Own Fate",b="Thundris Windweaver receives the reply with regret and thanks you for the long journey. Stormwind cannot help, and Darnassus has offered no aid either. Auberdine and its people must rely on themselves. Their fate rests in their own hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the quest Making Do?",a="You carry Baros Alexston's reply from Stormwind across the sea to Elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine. Stormwind cannot afford to send aid to Darkshore.",al={"what is making do","making do quest","auberdine stormwind quest"}},{q="Why does Stormwind refuse to aid Auberdine?",a="Stormwind's coffers are badly depleted, and its remaining resources are stretched thin across its own lands. The kingdom cannot afford to help Auberdine.",al={"why did stormwind say no","stormwind coffers thin","why won't stormwind help auberdine"}},{q="How does Thundris Windweaver react to the news?",a="Thundris Windweaver receives the letter with sadness and accepts that Auberdine must rely on itself. Neither Stormwind nor Darnassus is providing support.",al={"thundris reaction to stormwind","how does thundris react"}},{q="Who sent Alexston's Reply?",a="Baros Alexston sent the reply from Stormwind. He expresses sympathy for Auberdine while explaining that the kingdom cannot afford to help.",al={"who is alexston","alexstons reply sender"}},{q="Is Darnassus helping Auberdine?",a="Thundris Windweaver says neither Stormwind nor Darnassus has helped Auberdine. The settlement must rely on itself.",al={"darnassus aid auberdine","why didn't darnassus help"}},{q="Where is Alexston's Reply delivered?",a="Alexston's Reply is delivered to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, the port town on Darkshore's coast.",al={"where does this quest end","making do turn in location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see how distance and Stormwind's strained treasury leave Auberdine without financial support.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see that neither your human allies across the sea nor Darnassus nearby is helping Auberdine with its local struggles.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see how Stormwind's depleted coffers and hardship across its lands prevent the kingdom from funding aid overseas."},kw={"alexston","alexston's reply","auberdine","coffers","darkshore","making do","stormwind","thundris windweaver"},rel={"quest:4761","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:darnassus"},m={id=97926},src={"In-game quest text: Making Do"},fv=true}
E["quest:981"] = {t="quest",n="The Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Beneath the tower's shadow, the Cult of the Dark Strand has been broken. Word of victory travels south to Delgren the Purifier in Ashenvale, closing the campaign against the cult in Darkshore.",h="Beneath the tower's shadow, the Cult of the Dark Strand has been broken.",sec={{t="A Threat Severed",b="For weeks, the Cult of the Dark Strand held the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Tracking its movements, gathering intelligence, and meeting it in violent skirmishes dismantled its work. The cult's sorcerers are slain, and its dark rituals are broken. The immediate danger of demonic infiltration in Darkshore has ended.",sp=0},{t="Report to Maestra's Post",b="After the cult leader's death, Balthule Shadowstrike sends you south to Maestra's Post beneath the Ashenvale canopy. Delgren the Purifier waits there. A devoted warrior of the Holy Light, he oversaw the fight against the tower's wicked occupants. Your report of the cult's collapse eases the regional defenders' minds. Delgren gives you his lasting blessing and gratitude.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="You travel from near the Tower of Althalaxx to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale and report your victory to Delgren the Purifier. Your report closes the long campaign against the tower's cult.",al={"tower of althalaxx objective","turn in tower of althalaxx","where to turn in quest 981"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Delgren the Purifier?",a="Delgren the Purifier is an Alliance champion stationed at Maestra's Post in northern Ashenvale. He wields the Holy Light and is devoted to purging corruption and fighting demonic threats such as the Cult of the Dark Strand across northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is delgren","delgren lore","delgren the purifier"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?",a="Balthule Shadowstrike is an Alliance operative near the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore. He works with Delgren, watches the cult's movements, and guides adventurers as they dismantle the cabal from within.",al={"balthule","balthule lore","who is balthule shadowstrike"},it="identity"},{q="What was the Cult of the Dark Strand doing at the tower?",a="The Cult of the Dark Strand occupied the ancient ruins of the Tower of Althalaxx to perform dark rituals, summon demonic entities, and spread its influence across Darkshore's coastal lands.",al={"cult of the dark strand","what happened at althalaxx","tower of althalaxx lore"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Maestra's Post located?",a="Maestra's Post is an Alliance outpost in northwestern Ashenvale, just south of the Darkshore border crossing along the main road.",al={"maestra's post location","where is maestras post","delgren location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the Cult of the Dark Strand completely destroyed?",a="The cult's leadership at the Tower of Althalaxx has been executed, and its primary ritual is broken. Scattered cultists and remnants still haunt isolated corners of Kalimdor, but the cult's organized threat in Darkshore has been shattered.",al={"is the cult gone","dark strand destroyed","did we kill the cult"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Balthule Shadowstrike want this done?",a="With the Cult of the Dark Strand shattered and their leadership broken, Balthule wants you to carry word of the victory back to Delgren the Purifier. Delgren initiated the campaign against the cultists lurking at the tower, and Balthule believes your efforts deserve proper recognition and the paladin's promised reward.",al={"why send me back to delgren","balthule motive","why report to delgren"},it="motive",add="b456cfd7"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, reporting to Delgren the Purifier carries special meaning. You share his holy mission to cleanse the world of demonic corruption and wicked cults.",["faction:Alliance"]="The cult's defeat protects the overland road between Darkshore and Ashenvale. Alliance scouts and travelers can pass without fear of demonic ambushes.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the cleansing of the Tower of Althalaxx remove a foul blight from the ancient Highborne ruins scattered through your sacred coastal forests."},kw={"althalaxx","ashenvale","balthule","cult","dark strand","darkshore","delgren","maestra's post"},rel={"npc:delgren-the-purifier","npc:balthule-shadowstrike","subzone:maestra-s-post","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Balthule Shadowstrike",["end"]="Delgren the Purifier",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=981},src={"The Tower of Althalaxx (9)"}}
E["quest:982"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Ocean, Vast Sea",z="darkshore",s="North of Auberdine, two night elf vessels lie beneath the waves. Murlocs ambushed the Silver Dawning and Mist Veil as they sailed into port, and the surviving crews seek a way to mourn their lost captains.",h="North of Auberdine, two night elf vessels lie beneath the waves.",sec={{t="Tragedy off the Coast",b="Murlocs overwhelmed the Silver Dawning and Mist Veil as they neared Auberdine. Both ships sank in the shallows north of the settlement. Their surviving crews reached shore, but the loss of the vessels and their captains still weighs on the port.",sp=0},{t="Recovering Lost Memories",b="Gorbold Steelhand, a dwarf in Auberdine, seeks to honor the fallen night elf captains. Murlocs now occupy the underwater wrecks, though the captains' lockboxes remain in the flooded holds. Their logs and personal effects could help the surviving sailors mourn their commanders and lay their spirits to rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the sunken ships located?",a="Both wrecks lie underwater off Darkshore, north of the Auberdine docks.",al={"where are the shipwrecks","wreck location","where to find silver dawning"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil?",a="Murlocs ambushed the Silver Dawning and Mist Veil as they sailed toward Auberdine. Their crews were overrun, both captains died, and the ships sank to the ocean floor.",al={"how did ships sink","why did ships wreck","what sank mist veil"},it="history"},{q="Who is Gorbold Steelhand?",a="Gorbold Steelhand is a dwarf in Auberdine. He looks out for the surviving sailors and asks that the fallen captains' belongings be recovered.",al={"who gives deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand lore"},it="identity"},{q="What is inside the lockboxes?",a="The lockboxes hold the fallen night elf captains' logs and personal effects, cherished by the sailors who survived the wrecks.",al={"what are in the lockboxes","captains lockbox contents"},it="item"},{q="Why do the survivors care so much about these effects?",a="The captains were respected night elf mariners. Their logs and possessions offer their surviving crews comfort and may help put their spirits to rest.",al={"why recover lockboxes","why help the captains"},it="motive"},{q="What creatures inhabit the shipwrecks now?",a="Murlocs have overtaken the wrecks, treating the hulls as trophies and prowling the surrounding waters.",al={"what is guarding the ships","mobs at the shipwrecks"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the captains' belongings matter as a matter of ancestral honor. They served Auberdine's maritime trade.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can recognize Gorbold Steelhand's instinct to honor fallen comrades and support sailors in foreign ports.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how the grieving crew reflects the maritime cooperation between dwarfs and night elves along the Kalimdor coast."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","deep ocean vast sea","gorbold steelhand","lockbox","mist veil","murloc","shipwreck","silver dawning"},rel={"npc:gorbold-steelhand","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","topic:murloc"},m={start="Gorbold Steelhand",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=982,ri={"Mist Veil's Lockbox","Silver Dawning's Lockbox"}},src={"Deep Ocean, Vast Sea"}}
E["quest:983"] = {t="quest",n="Buzzbox 827",z="darkshore",s="Along Darkshore's coast, repairs are needed at Buzzbox 827. Wizbang Cranktoggle built it as the first link in a chain of voice relays, each made to use parts from local wildlife. Restoring it lets Wizbang test his network from Auberdine.",h="Along Darkshore's coast, repairs are needed at Buzzbox 827.",sec={{t="Gnomish Innovation on Ancient Shores",b="In Auberdine, gnomish engineer Wizbang Cranktoggle is linking Darkshore's wild coast with a chain of voice relays called Buzzboxes. Their levers and gears carry speech across great distances, a sharp contrast with the ancient ruins and somber forests around them. The machines break down often, so each needs constant care to keep working.",sp=0},{t="Ecological Maintenance",b="Buzzbox 827 lies on the shore just south of Auberdine. Wizbang built each relay to use parts from nearby wildlife, so repairs do not depend on carrying refined iron gears and copper pins through the wilderness. This unit takes the sturdy, jointed legs of local tide and reef crawlers. Put the legs in its receiver hopper, and the machine assembles itself and carries Wizbang's voice through its speakers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Buzzbox?",a="A Buzzbox is a long-distance voice machine invented by the gnome Wizbang Cranktoggle. Its levers and inner workings carry voices across Darkshore, letting people speak over great distances.",al={"what does a buzzbox do","buzzbox purpose","gnome box darkshore"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does a metal machine need crab legs to run?",a="Wizbang designed each Buzzbox to use parts from nearby wildlife as replacements. Buzzbox 827 sits near the beach crawlers, so travelers can repair it with their limbs instead of rare machined metal.",al={"why crawler legs","crawler leg repair","why feed it legs"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Buzzbox 827 located?",a="Buzzbox 827 is on the Darkshore shoreline, just south of Auberdine.",al={"buzzbox 827 location","where is buzzbox 827","find buzzbox 827"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Wizbang Cranktoggle?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is a gnome tinkerer staying upstairs at the Auberdine inn. He is building a communication network across Darkshore, though his prototypes often fail.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle","who made buzzbox","auberdine gnome"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Crawler Legs for the repair?",a="Pygmy Tide Crawlers and Young Reef Crawlers scuttle through the sands and shallows of the Darkshore beach just south of Auberdine. Their legs can repair the Buzzbox.",al={"crawler leg location","how to get crawler legs","pygmy tide crawler"},gp=true},{q="What happens once Buzzbox 827 is repaired?",a="Feed the Crawler Legs into the hopper, and the machine churns them into place, hums to life, and carries Wizbang's voice from Auberdine. Pleased with the result, he asks you to go farther down the coast and repair Buzzbox 411.",al={"after buzzbox 827","buzzbox questline next","buzzbox 827 completion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Wizbang Cranktoggle want Buzzbox 827 repaired?",a="Wizbang Cranktoggle is testing his latest invention: an experimental communication network across Darkshore that allows people to speak to each other across long distances. Unfortunately, his buzzboxes require constant maintenance and break down frequently. Getting Buzzbox 827 operational is the first step in proving that his network actually works.",al={"wizbang cranktoggle motive","why fix buzzbox 827","why does wizbang need this done"},it="motive",add="aa80bf26"},{q="What are the Crawler Legs used for?",a="Wizbang designed each buzzbox to rely on parts harvested from nearby native wildlife. Buzzbox 827 specifically requires six crawler legs to replace worn or broken mechanical components within its holding mechanism. Once inserted, the device's inner gears grind and slot the legs into place to restore power and transmission.",al={"what are crawler legs for","crawler leg buzzbox","why crawler legs"},it="item",add="2c1df07a"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see Wizbang's improvisation at work. He uses local chitin and arthropod limbs instead of forged brass gears, trading durability for parts that are easy to scavenge.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can recognize Wizbang's ambition in his attempt to bring connected communication to an ancient, untamed land without telephones or radios.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may find the clanking, smoking Buzzboxes an eyesore on Kalimdor's sacred, somber shores. The night elves of Auberdine tolerate the tinker's experiments."},kw={"auberdine","buzzbox 827","crawler legs","darkshore","gnomish engineering","reef crawler","tide crawler","wizbang cranktoggle"},rel={"npc:wizbang-cranktoggle","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wizbang Cranktoggle",["end"]="Buzzbox 827",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=983,ri={"Crawler Leg"}},src={"Buzzbox 827 (quest)"}}
E["quest:984"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Terenthis asks scouts to learn whether furbolg corruption has reached Darkshore. Madness has taken hold among furbolgs in Teldrassil, and the night elf druid now sends them to inspect mainland settlements across the sea.",h="In Auberdine, Terenthis asks scouts to learn whether furbolg corruption has reached Darkshore.",sec={{t="Shadows Across the Sea",b="Night elves across northern Kalimdor have long lived peacefully with the furbolg tribes. Since the Third War, strange corruption has unhinged furbolg minds in Teldrassil. They have kidnapped and attacked their former allies. Terenthis, the druid in Auberdine, fears the affliction has spread to mainland tribes along Darkshore’s coast.",sp=0},{t="A Gathering Storm",b="A furbolg camp near the ruins of Ameth'Aran shows the same corruption found in northern Teldrassil. The furbolgs there act erratically and attack without cause. The camp lies close to Auberdine, so its hostile inhabitants now threaten the Alliance settlement.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in Auberdine. Reports of maddened furbolgs attacking and capturing night elves across Teldrassil have led him to watch for threats throughout Darkshore.",al={"terenthis questgiver","who gives how big a threat","terenthis auberdine"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Darkshore turning hostile?",a="Terenthis has seen hints of corruption in Darkshore and suspects the furbolgs may be affected, as some on Teldrassil were. He asks for their camps to be investigated because he has not established signs across the region.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","corrupt furbolgs darkshore","furbolg corruption"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the corrupt furbolg camp located?",a="The encampment lies inland in central Darkshore, just north of the ancient highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran and southeast of Auberdine.",al={"camp location","where is the furbolg camp","how big a threat location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does this relate to events on Teldrassil?",a="In Teldrassil, corrupted furbolgs kidnapped and injured night elf sentinels and civilians. Terenthis points to those recent rescues as he seeks to learn whether mainland Darkshore faces the same crisis.",al={"teldrassil connection","teldrassil furbolgs","why does terenthis mention teldrassil"},it="history"},{q="What happens after reporting back to Terenthis?",a="If you find signs of corruption, tell Terenthis in Auberdine. He responds when you return.",al={"next quest","what follows how big a threat","quest continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are night elves so concerned about furbolg camps near Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is the Alliance's main port and supply route on the mainland. Hostile, deeply corrupted tribes close to town could threaten trade roads, scouts and the settlement itself.",al={"threat to auberdine","why care about furbolgs"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Terenthis want this done?",a="Terenthis took a personal vow to prevent further bloodshed after his night elf brethren had to be rescued from corrupted furbolgs over on Teldrassil. He has already noticed faint hints of corruption touching Darkshore, and he fears the contagion could spread undetected through the local furbolg tribes. By sending you to scout their camps, he hopes to gauge whether the danger is already at Auberdine's doorstep before more lives are lost.",al={"terenthis motive","why investigate furbolgs darkshore","why does terenthis care"},it="motive",add="0269df0a"},{q="Who are you sent to investigate?",a="You are dispatched to scout the local furbolg tribes inhabiting Darkshore. While many furbolg clans once lived peacefully or reclusively alongside the night elves, dark influences have begun warping their minds and driving them to madness. Terenthis sends you to inspect their settlements to confirm whether this affliction has taken root among the tribes living dangerously close to Auberdine.",al={"who am i investigating","what furbolg camp","who is the target"},it="target",add="1e1a0eb0"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you see ancient allies like the furbolgs fall to irrational darkness soon after the Third War. Their corruption threatens sacred lands and old bonds.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know furbolgs share deep bonds with nature and ancient wilderness spirits. Their sudden corruption is a grave concern for those who heal Kalimdor's balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you depend on Auberdine as the Alliance's main gateway to mainland northern Kalimdor. Its safety matters to the region's security and supply routes."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","corruption","darkshore","furbolg","teldrassil","terenthis","threat"},rel={"npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","quest:940"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=984},src={"How Big a Threat?"}}
E["quest:985"] = {t="quest",n="How Big a Threat?",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Terenthis sends you against the Blackwood furbolgs south of Auberdine. Their corrupted camp threatens the settlement, and the Sentinels seek to cull its pathfinders and windtalkers.",h="In Darkshore, Terenthis sends you against the Blackwood furbolgs south of Auberdine.",sec={{t="A Necessary Cull",b="The Sentinels see the Blackwood furbolgs as an immediate danger to Darkshore’s refugees and defenders. After you scout south of Auberdine, Terenthis sends you to strike their camp. Kill Blackwood Pathfinders and Windtalkers to hinder their attack before it reaches the settlement.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy of the Corrupted",b="Night elves have long counted furbolgs as spiritual kin and allies of the wilderness. Fel moss and demonic taint have spread across northern Kalimdor, driving the Blackwood tribe mad. No known remedy can restore their minds. So Auberdine’s defenders face a grim choice: stop the furbolgs before innocent people die.",sp=0},{t="Grimclaw's Arrival",b="After you report the cull to Terenthis, Grimclaw, a white bear, rushes into Auberdine toward the night elf. The bear’s arrival brings urgent new developments in the struggle against the wildlife and corruption ravaging the coast. Auberdine’s defenses face their next challenge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Terenthis want the Blackwood furbolgs killed?",a="The Blackwood tribe south of Auberdine has been corrupted and turned violent and irrational. Their camp threatens the settlement, and with no known cure, Terenthis orders a strike to protect Auberdine.",al={"why kill blackwood furbolgs","reason for furbolg cull","terenthis furbolg quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Blackwood furbolg camp located?",a="The Blackwood furbolg camp lies just south of Auberdine in Darkshore’s coastal forest. The tribe has gathered among the corrupted trees.",al={"blackwood furbolg location","where are pathfinders and windtalkers","furbolg camp darkshore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is a white bear tied to investigations into the wilderness of Darkshore.",al={"white bear auberdine","grimclaw the bear"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="What is causing the furbolgs to go mad?",a="Fel moss and lingering demonic corruption left after the Third War have poisoned the furbolgs. These dark forces warp mind and body, driving peaceful tribes to uncontrollable aggression.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","darkshore furbolg corruption","what corrupted blackwood"},it="conflict"},{q="Why are night elves reluctant to kill furbolgs?",a="Night elves and furbolgs have shared friendship and reverence for nature for thousands of years. Killing the furbolgs grieves the night elves, but the corruption leaves them no alternative.",al={"night elves and furbolgs","why mourn furbolgs"},it="people"},{q="What is the difference between the first and second 'How Big a Threat?' quests?",a="The first sends you to find and observe the Blackwood camp. The second sends you to thin its ranks by killing pathfinders and windtalkers after the danger is confirmed.",al={"how big a threat parts","how big a threat difference"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Blackwood pathfinders and windtalkers?",a="They are members of the Blackwood furbolg tribe who have established an encampment south of Auberdine. Driven mad and aggressive by the spreading forest corruption, their scouts and shamans represent an immediate, escalating danger to the night elf settlement. Until a cure for their affliction is discovered, Terenthis considers culling their ranks the only way to safeguard his people.",al={"blackwood pathfinders","blackwood windtalkers","who are we killing"},it="target",add="0dbe6a0f"},{q="Why does Terenthis send an adventurer instead of the Auberdine sentinels?",a="Terenthis turns to a traveler who has already proven adept at scouting the Blackwood camp. He asks whether that same traveler is prepared to confront the tribe in combat and reduce the threat to Auberdine.",al={"why send me","why not use guards","why terenthis needs me"},it="why_me",add="a17cffed"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may grieve the culling of the Blackwood. Centuries of kinship with the furbolgs have been shattered by the demonic blight left after the Third War.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you feel the tragedy keenly. The furbolgs’ plight reflects the forest’s suffering beneath the taint of fel moss.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Auberdine is the Alliance’s port anchor in Darkshore. Clearing nearby hostile encampments helps secure the region."},kw={"auberdine","blackwood","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","pathfinder","terenthis","windtalker"},rel={"npc:terenthis","quest:984","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=985},src={"How Big a Threat? (2)"}}
E["quest:986"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="In Auberdine, Terenthis prepares a way to search for Volcor, missing in Darkshore. He can weave a cloak of camouflage, but first needs pelts from the coast's fiercest moonstalkers.",h="In Auberdine, Terenthis prepares a way to search for Volcor, missing in Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Search into the Wilds",b="In Auberdine, Terenthis fears for Volcor and his companion Grimclaw as danger closes around Darkshore's coast. Aggressive predators and corrupted wildlife roam the southern wilds. Terenthis will not send an unprotected scout into that danger, so he plans a cloak woven with wild illusions.",sp=0},{t="Pelts of the Pride",b="Ordinary hides cannot fool Darkshore's beasts. Terenthis needs fine pelts from mature moonstalker sires or matriarchs. The great cats roam the woodlands south of Auberdine, near the Wildbend River and toward Ashenvale's forested border.",sp=0},{t="Delicate Magic",b="Moonstalker fur and nature enchantments let the wearer pass through hostile territory while searching for Volcor. Terenthis warns that the illusion is delicate. Strenuous activity or combat breaks the enchantment and leaves the searcher exposed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or tracker missing in the wilds of southern Darkshore. His companion Grimclaw and Terenthis in Auberdine seek to find him.",al={"who is volcor","volcor lore","lost master volcor"},it="identity"},{q="Who offers this task?",a="Terenthis, a night elf in Auberdine, offers to make the cloak after adventurers help with earlier local concerns.",al={"quest giver","where to get a lost master","terenthis location"},it="people"},{q="Where are moonstalker sires and matriarchs found?",a="Mature moonstalker sires and matriarchs roam southern Darkshore, near the Wildbend River and farther south toward the Ashenvale border.",al={"fine moonstalker pelt locations","where to find moonstalkers","wildbend river cats"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the cloak meant to do?",a="Terenthis plans to enchant a cloak that conceals its wearer from Darkshore's hostile beasts, allowing a search for Volcor without constantly drawing attacks.",al={"what does the cloak do","terenthis cloak","cloak enchantment"},it="power"},{q="Why does Terenthis need specific pelts?",a="Terenthis needs five fine pelts from moonstalker sires or matriarchs to make the cloak.",al={"why sires and matriarchs","why fine pelts"},it="item"},{q="Does the camouflage cloak have limitations?",a="Yes. Terenthis warns that the enchantment is fragile. Speaking to others is permitted, but strenuous activity or combat quickly breaks the illusion.",al={"does the illusion break","cloak restrictions"},it="power"},{q="Why does Terenthis want this done?",a="Terenthis is deeply concerned for his fellow night elf Volcor, who went missing in the perilous wilds of southern Darkshore, and for the loyal bear Grimclaw, who came to Auberdine seeking help for his master. Terenthis refuses to send you into such dangerous territory unprotected, so he insists on preparing a magical camouflage cloak first to ensure you can safely locate Volcor without being mauled by the coast's predators.",al={"why help volcor","terenthis motive","why does terenthis want pelts"},it="motive",add="bc18541c"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, finding Volcor reflects your duty to protect your kindred and wild companions across Darkshore.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the bond between Volcor and Grimclaw, and the skill it takes to track and hunt Darkshore's matriarchs and sires.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can appreciate how Terenthis turns moonstalkers' wild essence into protective camouflage."},kw={"a lost master","auberdine","darkshore","fine moonstalker pelt","grimclaw","moonstalker","terenthis","volcor","wildbend river"},rel={"npc:terenthis","npc:volcor","subzone:auberdine","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=986,ri={"Fine Moonstalker Pelt"}},src={"A Lost Master"}}
E["quest:993"] = {t="quest",n="A Lost Master",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, you follow Grimclaw’s trail to find the missing scout Volcor. Terenthis has made an Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak from fine moonstalker pelts for the search.",h="In Darkshore, you follow Grimclaw’s trail to find the missing scout Volcor.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Woods",b="Terenthis waits in Auberdine with the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak he has woven. South of the settlement, Grimclaw waits on the road for help sent by Terenthis. The loyal bear belongs to the missing night elf scout Volcor. Give Grimclaw a familiar greeting, and he leads you from the road toward the cave where Volcor is hiding.",sp=0},{t="Hiding in the Dark",b="Volcor lies wounded in a cavern after corrupted furbolgs attacked him. He uses stealth and Grimclaw’s wits to keep from being overrun. The enchanted cloak offers concealment and hope as Volcor plans his escape. Yet his wounds leave him in danger on the journey back to Auberdine.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout from Darkshore who went missing near hostile furbolg encampments. After a confrontation left him badly wounded, he crawled into a nearby cave while his bear companion, Grimclaw, went for help.",al={"volcor lore","who is the lost master"},it="identity"},{q="How do you find Volcor's hiding spot?",a="Grimclaw waits beside the road south of Auberdine. Wave to show you are the helper Terenthis sent, and Grimclaw runs toward the secluded cave where Volcor is hiding.",al={"where is volcor","find volcor cave","how to follow grimclaw"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak?",a="Terenthis enchanted a cloak made from fine moonstalker pelts to grant brief, potent magical stealth. Its magic lets you pass Darkshore’s creatures as you search for Volcor, and you give the cloak to him.",al={"moonstalker cloak","cloak magic"},it="item"},{q="Who attacked Volcor?",a="Corrupted furbolg tribes roaming Darkshore ambushed and wounded Volcor. He escaped immediate slaughter, but his injuries kept him from returning to Auberdine alone.",al={"who hurt volcor","why is volcor bleeding"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding Volcor?",a="After Volcor receives the enchanted cloak, he catches his breath and asks for your help escaping the wilderness. You can guide him out carefully through stealth or cut through the furbolgs by force.",al={"volcor next quest","after a lost master"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Terenthis want to find Volcor so urgently?",a="Terenthis fears that time is slipping away for his fellow night elf. Volcor was ambushed by corrupted furbolgs, and with only the loyal bear Grimclaw returning to plead for help, Terenthis knows Volcor cannot survive alone in hiding for long. Having completed the enchanted cloak to mask his scent and presence, Terenthis needs you to reach Volcor before the furbolgs hunt him down or his injuries claim him.",al={"terenthis motive","why save volcor","why does terenthis care about volcor"},it="motive",add="49342a22"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see the bond between scouts and their animal companions in Grimclaw’s steadfast search for help for his master, Volcor.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see the intelligence and devotion of Kalimdor’s well-trained beasts in the way Grimclaw finds help for Volcor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Auberdine depends on scouts like Volcor to watch the growing corruption among Darkshore’s furbolg tribes, making his rescue vital to the outpost."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","furbolg","grimclaw","moonstalker cloak","nightsaber","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","quest:986","topic:furbolg","zone:darkshore"},m={start="Terenthis",["end"]="Volcor",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=993},src={"A Lost Master (2)"}}
E["quest:994"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Force",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Volcor fights through the wild to reach safety. He finds Grimclaw by the road, and you bring word of his escape to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="In Darkshore, Volcor fights through the wild to reach safety.",sec={{t="A Direct Way Out",b="Volcor is stranded in Darkshore’s perilous wilderness, with danger closing around him. He chooses to fight the hostile creatures instead of slipping away unseen. His skill clears a path to the main road and safety.",sp=0},{t="Reunion on the Road",b="Volcor reaches the road and meets Grimclaw, his bear companion, who waited by the path. Safe at last, Volcor prepares for his next journey and asks you to report to Terenthis in Auberdine. His escape reaches the night elf leadership and draws Sentinel Selarin’s attention to troubles in southern Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout or woodsman in Darkshore who went missing with his companion Grimclaw. After you find him while searching for Terenthis, he needs help escaping hostile wildlife and dangerous terrain.",al={"volcor identity","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Grimclaw?",a="Grimclaw is Volcor’s loyal bear companion. While Volcor was trapped, Grimclaw waited apart from him near the road, where they could meet again.",al={"grimclaw","volcor bear","volcor pet"}},{q="Why does Terenthis care about Volcor's return?",a="Terenthis coordinates scout movements and local defenses from Auberdine. Finding lost allies and judging threats along the coast helps the night elves hold Darkshore.",al={"terenthis volcor","why help volcor","terenthis quest"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="You report Volcor’s safe passage to Terenthis in Auberdine. The next stage leads to Trek to Ashenvale.",al={"after escape through force","what comes next","next quest after volcor"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is there an alternate way to finish Volcor's escort?",a="Yes. You can fight your way out with Volcor or guide him quietly past danger using stealth.",al={"escape through force alternate","escape through stealth","volcor choices"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest lead in the broader storyline?",a="Volcor’s safe return links Darkshore’s local conflicts to the defense of night elf lands and opens assignments in Ashenvale.",al={"volcor storyline","darkshore to ashenvale questline"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Volcor want to fight his way out?",a="Volcor has spent too long trapped and endangered in the wilds of Darkshore away from his companion, Grimclaw. Having resolved to break out directly rather than sneak away, he is determined to carve a path through whatever hostiles block the path down to the road. His sole focus is reaching safety and reuniting with his loyal bear before reporting back toward Auberdine.",al={"volcor motive","why escape through force","why does volcor want this"},it="motive",add="8bb9ddbb"},{q="Why does Volcor need your help to escape?",a="Volcor is separated from Grimclaw and surrounded by hostile threats in the wilderness. Alone and exposed, breaking through the wilderness by brute force carries immense risk. With you lending martial support, his chances of surviving the gauntlet down to the safety of the main road are far higher than trying to cut his way out single-handedly.",al={"why does volcor need me","why can't volcor escape alone","why help volcor"},it="why_me",add="365007a7"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you help protect the Kaldorei’s hold on Darkshore, where wild beasts, corruption, and outside invaders threaten their ancestral woodlands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you strengthen the bond between the young Alliance and the Night Elves by helping secure Kalimdor’s northern frontier."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","escort","grimclaw","selarin","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","npc:sentinel-selarin","quest:990","subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=994},src={"Escape Through Force"}}
E["quest:995"] = {t="quest",n="Escape Through Stealth",z="darkshore",s="In Darkshore, Volcor needs your help escaping a furbolg den. Guide the trapped night elf scout past hostile beasts, then report to Terenthis in Auberdine.",h="In Darkshore, Volcor needs your help escaping a furbolg den.",sec={{t="The Trapped Scout",b="Volcor, a night elf scout, was sent to investigate Darkshore's growing threats. Now he is trapped inside a furbolg cave, cut off from the main roads and outnumbered. He needs your help to escape before the furbolgs discover him.",sp=0},{t="A Careful Flight",b="Volcor takes a careful path through the cave instead of charging its corrupted denizens. Once outside, he runs ahead on foot. He asks you to meet him in Auberdine, where he can travel faster alone.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Auberdine",b="Back in Auberdine, you bring news of Volcor's rescue to Terenthis, a night elf leader who works to protect the troubled coast. Volcor's safe return shows that discipline and teamwork can resist the darkness spreading through Darkshore and the wilderness beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Volcor?",a="Volcor is a night elf scout sent by his superiors to investigate Darkshore's wilderness. He became trapped in a furbolg cave until an Alliance adventurer rescued him.",al={"volcor lore","who is volcor","volcor darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Volcor run off alone once outside the cave?",a="Volcor says he can travel faster alone once clear of the cave's narrow passages. He asks you to meet him in Auberdine instead of traveling together along the open roads.",al={"why does volcor leave","volcor splits up"}},{q="Who is Terenthis?",a="Terenthis is a night elf leader in Auberdine. He coordinates local scouting and organizes responses to the corruption and hostile denizens threatening Darkshore.",al={"terenthis auberdine","who is terenthis"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this rescue take place?",a="The rescue begins inside a furbolg cave in Darkshore's wild, contested forests, far from Auberdine.",al={"volcor cave location","where is volcor cave"},it="place"},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="After Volcor is safely accounted for and Terenthis has heard your report, your journey continues south toward Ashenvale with Trek to Ashenvale.",al={"what comes after escape through stealth","next quest after volcor"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the alternative to stealth in this rescue?",a="Volcor offers another approach: instead of slipping out quietly, adventurers can fight their way through in a separate escort option.",al={"escape through force","volcor other quest","stealth vs force"},gp=true},{q="Why does Volcor want to escape through stealth?",a="Trapped deep within a hostile furbolg den, Volcor's primary concern is surviving long enough to return to Auberdine and report back to Terenthis. Slipping past the corrupted furbolgs without raising an alarm offers him the cleanest path out of the den without risking an overwhelming fight in tight quarters.",al={"why escape through stealth","volcor motive stealth","why sneak out with volcor"},it="motive",add="b4a3f8fd"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, helping Volcor supports the scouts watching Kalimdor's troubled forests as corruption spreads from barrows and dens.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can appreciate Volcor's choice to bypass an entrenched enemy instead of risking a reckless frontal fight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance ally, helping Volcor escape shows the night elf leadership in Auberdine that non-kaldorei allies can be trusted with delicate work in the wilderness."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","darkshore","escort","furbolg","stealth","terenthis","volcor"},rel={"npc:volcor","npc:terenthis","zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","quest:990","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Volcor",["end"]="Terenthis",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=995},src={"Escape Through Stealth"}}
E["subzone:ameth-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Ameth'Aran",z="darkshore",s="Broken colonnades rise from Ameth'Aran in southern Darkshore, where restless ghosts haunt the stones. Once a great Highborne city, it fell when the Well of Eternity collapsed and shattered the ancient world.",h="Broken colonnades rise from Ameth'Aran in southern Darkshore, where restless ghosts haunt the stones.",sec={{t="A City of Sorcerers",b="Before the Great Sundering, Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran were twin centers of Highborne influence along the ancient coastline. Queen Azshara favored Ameth'Aran, where its ruling nobles pursued unrestrained arcane experiments. Their sorcerer, Athrikus Narassin, governed from afar in the Tower of Althalaxx. The city flourished until the Well of Eternity collapsed and tore the Kaldorei Empire apart.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal and Eternal Torment",b="As the world began to tear apart, Athrikus Narassin returned to Ameth'Aran and promised salvation through powerful shielding magic. Instead, he stole his subjects' life force to feed his soul gems. He disguised the betrayal as a promise of eternal preservation. Dark magic and a great cataclysm shattered Ameth'Aran, and anguished Highborne specters still stalk its grounds, unable to rest ten thousand years after their murder.",sp=1,bt={"q965.3"}}},faq={{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran?",a="In the Kaldorei Empire's final days, Ameth'Aran already lay in ruins. Then the Well of Eternity shattered during the Great Sundering and destroyed the city ten thousand years ago. The spirits of Highborne who died there still haunt the ruins.",al={"why is ametharan ruined","ameth aran history","fall of ametharan"},it="history"},{q="Who are the ghosts wandering the ruins?",a="The ghosts are restless Highborne elves who lived and practiced arcane magic in Ameth'Aran before the Great Sundering. Unable to rest, they wander the broken stones in unending agony and fury.",al={"ghosts in ameth aran","ametharan specters","highborne ghosts darkshore"},it="residents"},{q="Who was Anaya Dawnrunner?",a="Anaya Dawnrunner lived in Ameth'Aran and was beloved by Cerellean Whiteclaw. She died when the city fell during the Sundering. Her ghost remained bound to the ruins until Cerellean sought outside aid to release her soul.",al={"anaya dawnrunner","cerellean lover","ameth aran lost love"},sp=1},{q="What are the stone tablets found in the ruins?",a="The stone tablets bear Ameth'Aran's history and an account of its fall. Sentinel Tysha Moonblade tried to decipher them for a historical report to the Cenarion Circle, but hostile ghosts forced her to rely on passing travelers.",al={"ametharan tablets","runestones in ameth aran","fall of ametharan tablets"}},{q="What is Ameth'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran is an ancient ruined night elf settlement in southern Darkshore, situated southeast of Auberdine. Before the Sundering, it stood as a magnificent twin city alongside Bashal'Aran, where Queen Azshara's favored Highborne practiced their arcane craft.",al={"what is ametharan","about ameth'aran","ameth aran ruins"},it="place",add="5cae2414"},{q="Why is Ameth'Aran ruined?",a="Ameth'Aran fell during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, when the shattering of the Well of Eternity tore the ancient kaldorei world apart. The broken settlement remains haunted by restless Highborne spirits.",al={"why is ameth'aran destroyed","how was ameth'aran ruined","ameth aran fall"},sp=1,it="ruin",add="bf7a1160"},{q="Is Ameth'Aran dangerous?",a="Yes. The ruins are haunted by restless Highborne ghosts who violently defend their former home against the living. Sentinel scouts like Tysha Moonblade have been driven out by their wrath, and any traveler seeking the ancient tablets must tread carefully among the spectral apparitions.",al={"is ameth aran safe","ameth'aran danger","threats in ameth aran"},it="danger",add="1468cad3"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Ameth'Aran as a grim monument to the Highborne caste's hubris and treachery, which brought about the Sundering.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see these ruins as an unhealed scar on Darkshore. Tormented spirits linger here and disrupt the natural balance of the wilds."},kw={"ameth'aran","anaya dawnrunner","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","cerellean whiteclaw","darkshore","highborne","tysha moonblade"},rel={"quest:953","quest:963","quest:954","zone:darkshore","npc:cerellean-whiteclaw","npc:sentinel-tysha-moonblade","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:highborne"},src={"Ameth'Aran"}}
E["subzone:auberdine"] = {t="subzone",n="Auberdine",z="darkshore",s="Ships crowd Auberdine's docks, carrying travelers between Darkshore, Teldrassil, and the Eastern Kingdoms. The night elven town is the Alliance's main port in northern Kalimdor, between the Veiled Sea and pine-covered bluffs.",h="Ships crowd Auberdine's docks, carrying travelers between Darkshore, Teldrassil, and the Eastern Kingdoms.",sec={{t="Gateway to Northern Kalimdor",b="Auberdine stands on the Veiled Sea, the only major settlement still thriving in Darkshore. Ships sail to Stormwind Harbor and, by way of Southshore, to Menethil Harbor. Ferries cross to Rut'theran Village beneath the boughs of the World Tree. Unlike Teldrassil's secluded treetop cities, Auberdine welcomes travelers from across the sea. Lamps light its stone streets, where dwarves and gnomes mingle with merchants among low, arched timber houses.",sp=0},{t="A Beleaguered Haven",b="Elder Thundris Windweaver and the Auberdine Village Council govern the town. They coordinate Darkshore's defense with the local Sentinels. Auberdine is a vital trade hub, though Darnassus rarely speaks its name; memory there dwells on the great cities lost to the Sundering. Trouble presses from every side. Aggressive murlocs raid fishing boats along the strand, corrupted Blackwood furbolgs push from the south, and foul magic drifting down from Felwood agitates the wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the ships in Auberdine go?",a="Auberdine's docks connect northern Kalimdor with the wider Alliance world. A ferry crosses to Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil's base. Ocean-going ships cross the Great Sea to Stormwind Harbor and, by way of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",al={"auberdine boats","where do boats go","auberdine travel"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who rules Auberdine?",a="Elder Thundris Windweaver and the Auberdine Village Council govern Auberdine. The Sentinels oversee its defense, led locally by Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea.",al={"auberdine leader","who is in charge","village council"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there dwarves and humans living in a night elf town?",a="Auberdine is the Alliance's chief port in northern Kalimdor, so foreign traders, craftsmen, and travelers arrive there first. Dwarves keep a smithy to serve visiting ships and travelers. The town is unusually diverse beside traditional night elf settlements.",al={"non elves in auberdine","why dwarves here"},it="people"},{q="Why do night elves from Darnassus look down on Auberdine?",a="Thundris Windweaver calls Auberdine a humble place whose name is not spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most kaldorei remember the cities lost to the Sundering, including the thriving Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran, and Auberdine remains in their shadow.",al={"darnassus auberdine rivalry","auberdine outcasts"},it="fame"},{q="What is Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is a tranquil coastal port settlement on the misty shores of Darkshore, serving as the primary gateway between northern Kalimdor and the wider Alliance. Built along the Veiled Sea, it features classic night elven wooden architecture, glowing streetlamps, and expansive docks. It welcomes travelers arriving by ship from Menethil Harbor or traveling by ferry to Teldrassil, offering shelter, trade, and fellowship amidst the shadowed wilderness.",al={"what is this town","tell me about auberdine","auberdine overview"},it="place",add="a08cc347"},{q="What happened at Auberdine?",a="Following the Great Sundering that shattered the ancient Kaldorei Empire and created Darkshore's coastline, numerous attempts to resettle the desolate region failed. Auberdine became the sole settlement to endure and thrive along these haunted shores. After the night elves aligned with the Grand Alliance, the quiet fishing community expanded its harbors to become the essential maritime nexus connecting the night elven homeland to the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"auberdine history","past of auberdine","what is auberdine's past"},it="history",add="36b132df"},{q="Is Auberdine dangerous?",a="Within its perimeter, Auberdine remains secure thanks to vigilant night elven Sentinels stationed along the roads and docks. However, the surrounding wilderness is beset by mounting perils. Corrupted furbolgs lurk to the south, agitated wildlife roams the forests, and aggressive murlocs prowl the shallows, actively threatening local fishermen and coastal shipping lanes.",al={"is it safe here","threats to auberdine","is auberdine under attack"},it="danger",add="ba4d867a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei venturing out from Teldrassil, you reach Auberdine as your first true mainland hub. Here, ancient tradition meets the unfamiliar ways and industry of younger Alliance allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you rely on this port to carry people and supplies into northern Kalimdor, linking Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","docks","kaldorei","lighthouse","port","sentinels","thundris windweaver"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:rut-theran-village","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:4761","zone:darnassus","topic:sentinels","quest:4740","topic:alliance"},src={"Auberdine"}}
E["subzone:bashal-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Bashal'Aran",z="darkshore",s="In northern Darkshore, Bashal'Aran's ruins draw satyrs and grells to lingering magic. A lone elven ghost remains bound by a curse centuries old.",h="In northern Darkshore, Bashal'Aran's ruins draw satyrs and grells to lingering magic.",sec={{t="A Shattered Twin City",b="Before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne in Bashal'Aran and its twin, Ameth'Aran. The mage Athrikus Narassin governed both towns. Their splendid markets and temples honored Elune.\n\nWhen the Well of Eternity collapsed, the cataclysm destroyed both settlements. For reasons lost to time, Athrikus used his arcane mastery to bind his second-in-command, the mage Asterion, inside a moonstone seal in Bashal'Aran. Asterion's body perished, but his ghost remained shackled to the ruined shrine.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Infestation",b="Deth'ryll satyrs and grells claim Bashal'Aran's crumbled stones. Drawn by magic lingering in the ancient masonry, they feed on its energy to strengthen their foul arts. They swarm the broken courtyards and terrorize travelers on Darkshore's forest paths.\n\nYet the creatures keep clear of the central shrine, where Asterion endures his endless vigil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Bashal'Aran before it was destroyed?",a="Before its destruction, Bashal'Aran was a magnificent Kaldorei city where Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne aristocrats. The mage-lord Athrikus Narassin governed it alongside its twin, Ameth'Aran.",al={"bashal'aran history","who built bashal'aran","what was this ruin"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is the ghost wandering the shrine?",a="Asterion's ghost wanders the shrine, where he remains imprisoned beyond mortal death. His governor, Athrikus Narassin, mysteriously betrayed him and bound him there with a moonstone seal.",al={"who is asterion","bashal'aran ghost","why is there a ghost"},it="residents"},{q="Why are satyrs inhabiting the ruins?",a="Satyrs and grells came to Bashal'Aran, drawn by arcane energy left by the ancient Highborne. They feed on its lingering magic to strengthen their dark demonic arts.",al={"why are there satyrs here","deth'ryll satyr lore","grells at bashal'aran"},it="threat"},{q="How does Bashal'Aran relate to Ameth'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran and Ameth'Aran were sister cities governed together under Queen Azshara. Before the Sundering shattered both settlements, Asterion often journeyed between them to tend to the people's needs.",al={"ameth'aran connection","twin cities darkshore","ameth'aran bashal'aran"},it="ties"},{q="What is Bashal'Aran?",a="Bashal'Aran is an ancient night elven ruin situated in northern Darkshore. Long ago, before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor, it was a prosperous Highborne city adorned with bustling bazaars and grand temples dedicated to Elune. Alongside its twin city Ameth'Aran to the south, it stood as a testament to the heights of early night elven civilization. Today, it lies broken and haunted, choked by wild overgrowth and lingering arcane remnants.",al={"what is bashal'aran","bashal'aran overview","about bashal'aran"},it="place",add="9019c4fd"},{q="What happened to Bashal'Aran?",a="In the days of the Kaldorei Empire, Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne here under the governorship of Athrikus Narassin and his lieutenant Asterion. When the first Well of Eternity imploded during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the city was utterly ruined. At an unknown time, Athrikus used a moonstone seal to magically bind Asterion to a shrine. While Asterion perished, his spectral form remained eternally trapped among the ruins long after his people vanished.",al={"history of bashal'aran","bashal'aran lore","what happened at bashal'aran"},it="history",add="3b163f6e"},{q="Is Bashal'Aran dangerous?",a="Yes. The shattered stonework is overrun by hostile grells and vile Deth'ryll satyrs. These demonic creatures are drawn to the potent arcane energies still seeping from the ancient Highborne stones, feeding on the remnants to fuel and swell their own dark magic. While they fear and avoid the sanctified shrine where the ghost Asterion lingers, any traveler venturing into the surrounding ruins will be attacked on sight.",al={"is bashal'aran safe","danger in bashal'aran","enemies in bashal'aran"},it="danger",add="0673c761"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, Bashal'Aran recalls the arcane hubris that doomed the ancient Kaldorei Empire and left its ruins open to demonic corruption.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, Asterion's moonstone seal shows how Highborne spellcraft can bind a spirit beyond mortal death."},kw={"ameth'aran","asterion","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","darkshore","deth'ryll","grell","highborne","satyr"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","npc:asterion","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:satyr","topic:elune","topic:alliance"},src={"Bashal'Aran"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Den",z="darkshore",s="In southern Darkshore, Blackwood Den has fallen to the Blackwood furbolgs’ corruption. Their cave and camps, once a peaceful home near Ashenvale, now echo with madness. Volcor, a night elf scout, is trapped inside and awaits aid from Auberdine.",h="In southern Darkshore, Blackwood Den has fallen to the Blackwood furbolgs’ corruption.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Stronghold",b="Near the southern border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, Blackwood furbolgs hold a rocky cave and crude camps. Corruption has taken hold of the tribe, and its members attack outsiders. Deep inside the cave, the night elf Volcor is pinned down and in danger. Scouts and travelers from Auberdine are needed to help him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Blackwood Den?",a="Blackwood Den is a furbolg settlement and cave complex in far southern Darkshore, near Ashenvale. The corrupted Blackwood tribe makes its home there.",al={"what is blackwood den","blackwood hold","where is blackwood den"},it="place"},{q="Who is inside the cave at Blackwood Den?",a="Volcor, a night elf, is trapped inside the cave behind enemy lines. Travelers who find him must work with allies in Auberdine to help him escape the den safely.",al={"who is trapped in the cave","who is volcor","elf in blackwood den"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="Corruption spreading across Darkshore and Kalimdor after the Third War has driven the Blackwood furbolgs mad. They attack outsiders on sight.",al={"why are blackwood furbolgs aggressive","are blackwood furbolgs evil","corrupted furbolgs darkshore"},it="hostile"},{q="What happened at Blackwood Den?",a="Blackwood Den was once a regular settlement of the Blackwood furbolg tribe in southern Darkshore. However, along with much of the local wildlife and indigenous tribes, the furbolgs here fell victim to a dark corruption spreading through the land. Twisted from their formerly peaceful ways, they turned fiercely aggressive, establishing fortified camps and trapping outsiders who dared to tread near their hollows.",al={"blackwood den history","what happened at blackwood den","blackwood den story"},it="history",add="9f3b6295"},{q="Who lives in Blackwood Den?",a="The den and its surrounding camps are held by the corrupted Blackwood furbolgs, who aggressively guard their territory against any intruders. Deep inside the cave, an unfortunate night elf named Volcor has found himself trapped, cornered by the hostile furbolgs and awaiting rescue from anyone brave enough to fight through the den.",al={"who lives in blackwood den","blackwood den inhabitants","who holds blackwood den"},it="residents",add="d219a6ba"},{q="Is Blackwood Den dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very perilous. The Blackwood furbolgs inhabit several clustered camps right outside the cave entrance and throughout the den itself. Corrupted and violent, they attack any outsiders on sight in packs, making any attempt to venture inside—especially to reach the trapped night elf Volcor—a deadly undertaking without careful preparation.",al={"is blackwood den dangerous","blackwood den dangers","how dangerous is blackwood den"},it="danger",add="3aa28176"},{q="Why is it called Blackwood Den?",a="The den takes its name from the Blackwood furbolg tribe that makes its home here. Nestled in the southern reaches of Darkshore near the border with Ashenvale, the cave and surrounding camps serve as the central hollow and sanctuary for this corrupted clan.",al={"why is it called blackwood den","blackwood den name meaning","where does blackwood den get its name"},it="name",add="f77a0955"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, the Blackwood tribe’s corruption is a tragedy. Rescuing Volcor is an urgent duty to protect their people along the southern road.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may mourn the furbolgs, once steadfast protectors of the wilderness. The madness at Blackwood Den is another painful sign of Kalimdor’s tainted nature."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackwood den","blackwood hold","darkshore","furbolg","volcor"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:auberdine","npc:volcor","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf"},src={"Blackwood Den"}}
E["subzone:cliffspring-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Cliffspring Falls",z="darkshore",s="At Cliffspring Falls, water pours from Darkshore’s eastern cliffs into the forest below. The falls feed the Cliffspring River and once supplied nearby night elf settlements. Now a foul taint spreads through the river basin.",h="At Cliffspring Falls, water pours from Darkshore’s eastern cliffs into the forest below.",sec={{t="A Tainted Source",b="Cliffspring Falls rises from caves high in Darkshore’s eastern bluffs and feeds the Cliffspring River. The river winds west through the woods before emptying into the sea. Its clear waters once gave nearby night elf settlements their purest drinking water.\n\nNow the water runs murky and foul, carrying sickness and decay through the river basin. Naturalists who investigate the falls find naga and cultists overrunning the caves. They plot in the shadows as demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood threatens to seep through the highland bedrock.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Cliffspring Falls?",a="Cliffspring Falls pours from caves in eastern Darkshore and feeds the Cliffspring River. Its waters once supplied nearby settlements with their main source of fresh drinking water.",al={"cliffspring falls","cliffwater falls","what is cliffspring falls"},it="place"},{q="Why is the water coming from the falls corrupted?",a="Demonic taint may be seeping through the mountains from Felwood. Twilight’s Hammer cultists and naga also occupy the caves that feed the falls.",al={"why is water tainted","cliffspring river corruption","corrupted water"}},{q="Who occupies the caverns behind the falls?",a="Naga and Twilight’s Hammer cultists occupy the flooded caves above and behind the waterfall.",al={"who is in the caves","cliffspring cave mobs","who lives in cliffspring falls"},it="residents"},{q="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?",a="The Cliffspring River crosses northern Darkshore, and its waters are a principal source of fresh water. Their poisoning threatens wildlife, ancient groves, and night elf homes.",al={"why does darkshore care","cliffspring importance"},it="power"},{q="What happened to Cliffspring Falls?",a="Cliffspring Falls was once a pristine mountain cascade providing clean drinking water across northern Darkshore. Following the devastation of the Third War, dark powers crept into the surrounding wilds. Corruption took hold of the cavern at the river's headwaters, turning the pure mountain flow foul and attracting malevolent entities to its hidden depths.",al={"cliffspring falls history","what happened at cliffspring falls","why did cliffspring falls change"},it="history",add="b072a170"},{q="Is Cliffspring Falls dangerous?",a="The falls and the caverns behind them are extremely hazardous. Hostile naga crawl through the waterways, while fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists lurk deep inside the cave network conducting foul rituals. Beyond the deadly inhabitants, the tainted water itself poses a grave hazard to anyone who dares drink from it.",al={"cliffspring falls danger","is cliffspring falls safe","threats at cliffspring falls"},it="danger",add="894b4715"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf of Auberdine, you know the taint in Cliffspring Falls pollutes waters vital to Darkshore’s ancient forests. It threatens the forest’s health and spirit.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the Cenarion Circle, you watch the river closely and work to find and cleanse the unnatural rot threatening the wilderness."},kw={"auberdine","cliffspring falls","cliffspring river","cliffwater falls","darkshore","felwood","naga","twilight's hammer","water corruption"},rel={"quest:6122","quest:4762","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","zone:felwood","topic:alliance"},src={"Cliffspring Falls"}}
E["subzone:grove-of-the-ancients"] = {t="subzone",n="Grove of the Ancients",z="darkshore",s="Nature spirits and kaldorei gather in the Grove of the Ancients, where Onu, an Ancient of Lore, keeps watch. Old temple ruins stand beside the Wildbend River in southeastern Darkshore.",h="Nature spirits and kaldorei gather in the Grove of the Ancients, where Onu, an Ancient of Lore, keeps watch.",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Wildbend",b="Old temple stones ring the Grove of the Ancients in southeastern Darkshore. The Wildbend River runs through its heart, offering refuge from a troubled coastline. Nature spirits and kaldorei gather here as the Circle of Ancients. Together, they tend to the forest’s balance.",sp=0},{t="Keepers and Watchers",b="Onu, an Ancient of Lore, watches the land’s changing fortunes and offers wisdom to travelers. Wandering merchants and slumbering druids rest beneath the boughs. To the southeast, territorial furbolg camps hold their ground. Alliance sentinels and druids watch the southern reaches of Darkshore from this frontier outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients lies in southeastern Darkshore, against the mountain foothills near the Wildbend River.",al={"grove of ancients location","where is grove of the ancients","onu location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Onu?",a="Onu is an Ancient of Lore who lives in the grove. He watches over the southeastern woods and advises druids and travelers working to mend Darkshore’s balance.",al={"who is onu","ancient in grove of ancients","tree guy darkshore"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Circle of Ancients?",a="The Circle of Ancients is an assembly of great nature spirits and ancient treants who gather at the grove to commune, share knowledge, and discuss the welfare of the wild lands.",al={"circle of ancients","ancients meeting darkshore"}},{q="Are there dangers near the grove?",a="Hostile wildlife and territorial furbolg camps lie across the river and to the southeast of the grove.",al={"grove threats","is grove safe","monsters near grove"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The Grove of the Ancients is a sacred night elven ruin situated along the Wildbend River in southeastern Darkshore. Built around the crumbling remnants of an ancient temple, it serves as a secluded sanctuary where the Circle of Ancients gathers, watched over by revered tree guardians and slumbering keepers of nature.",al={"grove of the ancients","what is grove of ancients","about grove of the ancients"},it="place",add="b540280c"},{q="Why is the Grove of the Ancients called that?",a="The sanctuary takes its name from both the massive, sentient Ancients who reside here and the ancient night elven legacy embedded in its soil. As a meeting ground for the Circle of Ancients and home to the venerable Ancient of Lore, Onu, it stands as an enduring monument to the primeval guardians of the forest.",al={"why grove of ancients","how did it get its name","grove of ancients name meaning"},it="name",add="a4149ac4"},{q="Why is the Grove of the Ancients in ruins?",a="The stone structures scattered across the grove are the remains of an ancient night elven temple that fell into decay over millennia. While the architecture has long surrendered to the elements and encroaching woodland, the land remains deeply sacred and actively tended by nature spirits rather than rebuilt in stone.",al={"why is grove of the ancients ruined","grove of ancients temple ruins","who destroyed the grove"},it="ruin",add="f8aa7b2c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can seek wisdom from Onu, the Ancient of Lore, and the spirits of the forest at this revered sanctuary.",["race:NightElf"]="Ancient temple ruins and nature spirits surround the grove, a solemn reminder of the kaldorei’s long harmony with the land."},kw={"ancient of lore","circle of ancients","darkshore","grove of the ancients","onu","wildbend river"},rel={"quest:952","zone:darkshore","subzone:wildbend-river","topic:druid","subzone:auberdine","topic:furbolg"},src={"Grove of the Ancients"}}
E["subzone:long-wash"] = {t="subzone",n="Long Wash",z="darkshore",s="Murlocs now threaten the shore of Long Wash, south of Auberdine and toward Ameth'Aran beneath Darkshore's gray sky.",h="Murlocs now threaten the shore of Long Wash, south of Auberdine and toward Ameth'Aran beneath Darkshore's...",sec={{t="A Gloomy Shoreline",b="Long Wash is Darkshore's shortest stretch of distinct coast, despite its name. Beneath the region's perpetual overcast skies, damp sand lies strewn with flotsam, driftwood, and sea creatures washed up by the Veiled Sea. Crabs comb the surf, but travelers heading south from Auberdine must watch for murloc tribes camped at the water's edge. The murlocs attack anyone who enters the ground where they scavenge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Long Wash located?",a="Long Wash follows Darkshore's coast just south of Auberdine, reaching roughly west of the ruins of Ameth'Aran.",al={"long wash location","where is long wash","how to find long wash"},it="place"},{q="Why is it called the Long Wash?",a="A wash is an old word for shore swept by ocean waves. Though called Long Wash, it is Darkshore's shortest distinct beach.",al={"why long wash","long wash meaning","what does wash mean"},it="name"},{q="What threats can be found along the Long Wash?",a="Aggressive murloc clans gather along Long Wash, alongside territorial tide crawlers and other beach wildlife.",al={"dangers in long wash","long wash mobs","what lives in long wash"},it="danger"},{q="Why are there so many dead creatures on the beach?",a="The rough surf of the Veiled Sea washes debris, ship drift, and dying marine life onto Long Wash's damp sands. Corruption is also encroaching on Darkshore's coastal waters.",al={"dead animals long wash","beached creatures darkshore beach","flotsam on the shore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the murlocs along Long Wash are another sign of an unsettling imbalance creeping right up to their main port's doorstep."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","long wash","murloc","tide crawler","veiled sea"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Long Wash"}}
E["subzone:master-s-glaive"] = {t="subzone",n="Master's Glaive",z="darkshore",s="In southwestern Darkshore, Twilight's Hammer cultists now swarm around the Master's Glaive. Night elves once revered this ancient site, where a colossal weapon and a petrified skull recall a forgotten clash.",h="In southwestern Darkshore, Twilight's Hammer cultists now swarm around the Master's Glaive.",sec={{t="A Monument of an Ancient Clash",b="At the Master's Glaive, an adamantine blade pierces a colossal petrified skull. No record names the creature or the hand that drove the blade home. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell here. For generations, night elves believed only the titans could wield a weapon so vast. The blade and skull remain as a monument to that forgotten clash.",sp=0},{t="Dark Excavations",b="For generations, night elves held the Master's Glaive in solemn reverence. Now Twilight's Hammer fanatics camp around the sunken carcass, digging trenches and uncovering petrified ribs. Whispers beneath the stone draw them to study the remains and commune with the malevolent power that clings to them. They seek to revive or harness whatever fell essence sleeps within the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the massive weapon stuck in the skull?",a="No one knows for certain. The colossal adamantine blade is the Master's Glaive, driven into the skull in some forgotten age. Night elves believed only the titans could wield a weapon of such size.",al={"what is the sword","masters glaive sword","who put the sword there"},it="item"},{q="What creature's skull is buried here?",a="The creature's name is lost. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell here. Twilight's Hammer believes the petrified remains belong to a servant of the Old Gods.",al={"what died here","who is buried at masters glaive"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult gathered here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult worships the Old Gods. Its members have overrun the Master's Glaive to excavate the petrified remains. Lingering dark power draws them, and they hope to restore the fallen creature to life.",al={"why are cultists here","twilight hammer darkshore","what are cultists digging"},it="motive"},{q="Who knows about the history of this site?",a="Onu, the Ancient of Lore in Darkshore, recognizes the site as the resting place of an ancient lord of the earth. He bids investigators look into it.",al={"who studies the glaive"}},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="The Master's Glaive is an ancient, monumental site nestled in southwestern Darkshore. The landmark is dominated by a colossal petrified skull, impaled through the crown by an immense adamantine blade. What was once treated as a reverent holy site by the night elves is now a sinister excavation shrouded in dark worship.",al={"what is masters glaive","masters glaive darkshore","what is this place"},it="place",add="ce9b9209"},{q="What happened at the Master's Glaive?",a="No record tells the full story. Onu, the Ancient of Lore, says only that an old, old lord of the earth fell here, slain by a blade so vast that the night elves believed only the titans could have wielded it. Its petrified skull still lies where it fell, the glaive buried in its crown.",al={"masters glaive history","what battle happened here","soggoth history"},it="history",add="0f8799c2"},{q="Who controls the Master's Glaive?",a="The site has fallen under the sway of the Twilight's Hammer cult. Fanatical cultists swarming the basin conduct excavations around the petrified remains, driven by mad prophecies to unearth and awaken the fallen creature.",al={"who lives at masters glaive","who is at masters glaive","masters glaive cultists"},it="residents",add="1f2acdb9"},{q="Is the Master's Glaive dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Zealous Twilight's Hammer cultists actively guard the excavations and will attack any intruders on sight. Beyond the fanatic mortals, the lingering malevolence radiating from the dormant remains makes the basin a perilous place for the unwary.",al={"is masters glaive dangerous","is it safe here","masters glaive threat"},it="danger",add="f9a41c7d"},{q="Why is it called the Master's Glaive?",a="The location is named for the colossal weapon embedded in the earth. The massive blade, driven into the skull of a long-fallen creature in some forgotten age, came to be remembered in legends as the Master's Glaive.",al={"why is it called masters glaive","masters glaive name origin","where does the name come from"},it="name",add="5be20272"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the strange petrified monument was a solemn holy place for generations. Twilight's Hammer has defiled Darkshore's sacred grounds."},kw={"darkshore","master's glaive","old god","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:944","zone:darkshore","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:titan","topic:night-elf"},src={"Master's Glaive"}}
E["subzone:mist-s-edge"] = {t="subzone",n="Mist's Edge",z="darkshore",s="North of Auberdine, Mist's Edge follows Darkshore's western shore under ocean fog. Gray beaches hold wrecks, the remains of great sea creatures, crabs, and murlocs.",h="North of Auberdine, Mist's Edge follows Darkshore's western shore under ocean fog.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Shore",b="Along Darkshore's western edge, Mist's Edge is a shore of damp sand and rocky tidepools beneath coastal fog. Shattered vessels and drift timber lie among the remains of huge sea creatures. Crabs forage along the beach, while murloc tribes make their homes in the surf.",sp=0},{t="Wrecks and Scavengers",b="Lost vessels leave wreckage and discarded cargo along these sands. Night elf sentinels and scavengers watch the coast. Yet murloc encampments menace travelers making their way along the shore from Auberdine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mist's Edge?",a="North from Auberdine, Mist's Edge follows Darkshore's western shore beneath ocean fog, past shipwrecks and beached sea creatures.",al={"mists edge","darkshore beach","what is mists edge"},it="place"},{q="What threats wander this coast?",a="Hostile crabs and aggressive murloc packs roam the shoreline. Murlocs live in primitive camps beside the water.",al={"mists edge monsters","what attacks you on the beach","darkshore coast dangers"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks and skeletons here?",a="Harsh currents, hidden reefs, and heavy mist make the waters off Darkshore dangerous to navigate, driving ships onto the rocks. Ocean currents also carry the remains of massive leviathans and other sea creatures ashore.",al={"darkshore beached whales","shipwrecks mists edge","giant bones darkshore"},it="history"},{q="Is Mist's Edge dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers must stay vigilant along these bleak sands. The shore is crawling with aggressive coastal crabs, while aggressive tribes of murlocs build camps along the water and attack anyone trespassing near their fishing grounds. Between the prowling scavengers feeding on beached sea carcasses and the lurking murlocs, wandering the coast alone poses a constant threat.",al={"is mists edge safe","danger mists edge","how dangerous is mists edge"},it="danger",add="e5f03abb"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves of Auberdine, Mist's Edge marks a maritime boundary and an untamed border troubled by invading murlocs and foul scavengers."},kw={"auberdine","beach","coast","crabs","darkshore","mist's edge","murloc","shipwreck"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:auberdine","topic:murloc"},src={"Mist's Edge"}}
E["subzone:moonspray"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonspray",z="darkshore",s="Moonspray carries travelers across the sea between Darkshore and Teldrassil. The Alliance ship sails between mainland Kalimdor and the great World Tree.",h="Moonspray carries travelers across the sea between Darkshore and Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Vital Island Ferry",b="Moonspray carries travelers between Auberdine and Rut'theran Village. Across the Veiled Sea, it bears adventurers, couriers, and provisions from Darkshore's coast to the night elf sanctuary at Teldrassil's crown.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moonspray travel?",a="Moonspray sails between Auberdine on Darkshore's coast and Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil.",al={"moonspray route","where does moonspray go","moonspray destination"},it="place"},{q="Who owns and operates this ship?",a="The night elves own Moonspray, which sails with the Kaldorei Fleet under the Alliance banner.",al={"who sails the moonspray","kaldorei fleet moonspray","is moonspray alliance"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is this ferry route important?",a="Teldrassil rises from an island off Kalimdor's northwestern coast. Ships like Moonspray carry troops, provisions, and travelers across the water to the mainland.",al={"why take moonspray","teldrassil boat"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Moonspray?",a="The Moonspray is a graceful night elven transport vessel belonging to the Kaldorei Fleet. It plies the waters between the docks of Auberdine on the Darkshore coast and Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, serving as a vital naval ferry that connects the great world tree to the Kalimdor mainland.",al={"what is moonspray","moonspray ship","moonspray darkshore"},it="place",add="de38a5e0"},{q="What is the history of the Moonspray?",a="Constructed as part of the night elves' naval transport fleet, the Moonspray was chartered to bridge the gap across the sea after the growth of Teldrassil. Since the establishment of Auberdine and Rut'theran Village, it has steadily carried travelers, supplies, and messengers back and forth to keep the secluded capital connected to the shores of Kalimdor.",al={"moonspray history","what happened to moonspray","history of the moonspray"},it="history",add="6febef79"},{q="Is the Moonspray dangerous?",a="Not for travelers of the Alliance. The Moonspray is a peaceful civilian and supply ferry operated safely by night elf mariners. However, any members of the Horde attempting to board will find themselves in hostile territory, facing swift retaliation from both the crew and the night elf guards stationed at the harbor docks.",al={"is moonspray dangerous","moonspray danger","threats on moonspray"},it="danger",add="9638ce15"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Teldrassil to explore the wider world, you may make your first mainland journey aboard Moonspray.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Moonspray links its main coastal hub in northern Kalimdor with Darnassus, the isolated capital."},kw={"auberdine","boat","darkshore","ferry","kaldorei fleet","moonspray","rut'theran village","teldrassil","transport"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:rut-theran-village","zone:darkshore","quest:940"},src={"Moonspray"}}
E["subzone:remtravel-s-excavation"] = {t="subzone",n="Remtravel's Excavation",z="darkshore",s="Prospector Remtravel's dig in southern Darkshore has broken into ancient ruins.",h="Prospector Remtravel's dig in southern Darkshore has broken into ancient ruins.",sec={{t="A Quarry Overrun",b="Prospector Remtravel came to southern Darkshore in search of relics from the distant past. He set up a large dig, far from Auberdine's safety. As his team cut through old layers of earth, they uncovered Gravelflint troggs and hulking stone golems. The creatures overran the quarry and scattered the miners. Now Remtravel scrambles to recover his most promising finds.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Fossil",b="Before chaos swept the excavation, the miners uncovered a rare fossil with curious mystic properties. In the panic of the trogg attack, the absent-minded prospector misplaced it among the sprawling dirt pits. Recovering the relic means venturing back into the dig. Vicious troggs and ancient automatons awakened by the pickaxes remain there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Remtravel's Excavation?",a="Prospector Remtravel established this archaeological dig in southern Darkshore while searching for ancient fossils and subterranean relics.",al={"what is this place","darkshore dig site","remtravel site"},it="place"},{q="Why are there troggs here?",a="Dwarven miners dug too deeply and broke into underground caverns. Their work awakened the Gravelflint troggs and dormant stone golems.",al={"why troggs in darkshore","gravelflint troggs","where did troggs come from"},it="hostile"},{q="Who is Prospector Remtravel?",a="Prospector Remtravel is a dwarven archaeologist leading the excavation. He has a keen eye for artifacts, but lost track of a key fossil when the dig came under attack.",al={"who is remtravel","prospector remtravel lore"},it="leader"},{q="What kind of relic was discovered here?",a="Shortly before the troggs surged from below, Remtravel uncovered an unusual fossil with strange mystic properties.",al={"what did they find","remtravel fossil","mystic fossil"},it="item"},{q="What happened at Remtravel's Excavation?",a="Prospector Remtravel established this archaeological dig in Darkshore and unearthed an unusual fossil possessed of mystic properties. However, his delving broke into subterranean chambers, awakening hostile Gravelflint troggs and massive ancient golems. Overwhelmed by these emerging creatures, the expedition lost control of the site, and the absent-minded dwarf misplaced his prized relic amidst the chaos.",al={"remtravels excavation history","what happened at the dig site","history of remtravel excavation"},it="history",add="6ff3d594"},{q="Who runs Remtravel's Excavation?",a="The excavation was established and led by the renowned dwarven archaeologist Prospector Remtravel. In his absence, however, no peaceful workers remain on site. Hostile Gravelflint troggs and animated stone golems have overrun the trenches, driving out the researchers and seizing control of the diggings.",al={"who controls remtravel excavation","who lives in remtravel excavation","remtravel excavation inhabitants"},it="residents",add="37fcd3a2"},{q="Why was Remtravel's Excavation abandoned?",a="The expedition had to abandon active work when their digging broke open buried caverns, unleashing a swarm of aggressive Gravelflint troggs alongside unearthed stone golems. The diggers could not hold the grounds against such brute strength, forcing them to flee and leave their equipment behind.",al={"why is remtravel excavation abandoned","why did remtravel leave the dig site","what ruined remtravels excavation"},it="ruin",add="3a095efd"},{q="Is Remtravel's Excavation dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for anyone without proper combat training. The open pits and trenches are teeming with feral Gravelflint troggs and colossal, unearthed golems that attack any intruders on sight.",al={"how dangerous is remtravels excavation","is it safe at remtravel excavation","dangers of remtravel excavation"},it="danger",add="f43c459f"},{q="Why is it called Remtravel's Excavation?",a="The dig site takes its name from Prospector Remtravel, the famed dwarven archaeologist who spearheaded the operation in Darkshore to uncover ancient relics.",al={"remtravel excavation name origin","why is it named remtravel","who named remtravels excavation"},it="name",add="92ab137b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the Explorers' League seeks the secrets of the past. Digging in foreign lands can uncover dangerous troggs along with them.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may view Alliance dwarves' deep digging with skepticism, especially when it awakens wild troggs on Darkshore's ancient soil."},kw={"darkshore","excavation","fossil","golem","gravelflint","prospector","remtravel","trogg"},rel={"npc:prospector-remtravel","zone:darkshore","topic:trogg"},src={"Remtravel's Excavation"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-mathystra"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Mathystra",z="darkshore",s="Stormscale naga hold Mathystra's broken halls on Darkshore's northern coast. Ghost Sabers haunt the ruins of this ancient night elven city, shattered in the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago.",h="Stormscale naga hold Mathystra's broken halls on Darkshore's northern coast.",sec={{t="A City Cast into the Sea",b="Mathystra once sheltered Highborne nobles on Darkshore's northern coast. When the Well of Eternity collapsed in the Great Sundering, great waves broke the city. They toppled its marble arches and swept much of its stonework into the sea. The surviving night elves left for smaller woodland villages farther south. Sunken courtyards and cracked foundations still face the battered coast.",sp=0},{t="The Stormscale Vipers and Ghost Sabers",b="Stormscale naga guard Mathystra's broken halls and drive away travelers who venture north past the Tower of Althalaxx. Ancient Highborne relics lie half-buried among flagstones, sand, and seafoam. Young night elves sometimes brave the naga to recover remnants of their heritage. Meanwhile, spectral Ghost Sabers stalk the broken streets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What used to be here before the ruins?",a="Mathystra was a thriving night elven city built at the height of the ancient Highborne empire. The Well of Eternity's collapse in the Great Sundering shattered the city and drowned much of it ten thousand years ago, cleaving Kalimdor apart.",al={"mathystra history","who built mathystra","what was mathystra"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Ruins of Mathystra right now?",a="Stormscale naga occupy the ruins, rising from the sea to claim the sunken pavilions and coastlines. They attack land-dwellers who enter their territory.",al={"who lives in mathystra","mathystra mobs","who is at mathystra"},it="residents"},{q="What are Ghost Sabers?",a="Ghost Sabers are ethereal, translucent felines haunting Mathystra's ruined stonework. Hunters seek them along the coast, and disturbing ancient figurines there can draw the spirits from the shadows.",al={"ghost saber mathystra","glowing cat darkshore","ghost sabers"}},{q="Why do night elves visit these ruins today?",a="Young night elves and scholars sometimes enter the ruins to recover Highborne relics left behind after the Sundering. Stormscale naga make the search perilous.",al={"mathystra relics","why go to mathystra"}},{q="What are the Ruins of Mathystra?",a="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city, resting along the northern coast of Darkshore just beyond the Tower of Althalaxx. Once a magnificent center of Highborne civilization, all that remains today are weathered stone foundations, shattered pillars, and long-buried relics swallowed by the wilderness.",al={"what is mathystra","ruins of mathystra lore","about ruins of mathystra"},it="place",add="b3a23ce3"},{q="Why was Mathystra ruined and abandoned?",a="Mathystra was devastated ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, when the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity tore ancient Kalimdor apart. The city was decimated by the cataclysm, and surviving night elves chose to abandon the shattered ruins entirely, settling instead in coastal havens further south.",al={"why is mathystra ruined","what destroyed mathystra","how was mathystra destroyed"},it="ruin",add="f1593a2d"},{q="Are the Ruins of Mathystra dangerous?",a="Yes, you should tread carefully among the stones. The ruins are fiercely held by the Stormscale naga, who violently defend their claiming of the coast against any outsiders. In addition to these serpent trespassers, ethereal Ghost Sabers and remnants of ancient Highborne magic linger across the rubble.",al={"is mathystra safe","threats in mathystra","ruins of mathystra danger"},it="danger",add="2087f816"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can see Mathystra as a warning of the ancient Highborne's hubris. Their reckless sorcery brought cataclysm upon their coastal settlements.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you may find Ghost Sabers prowling Mathystra's rubble. These translucent beasts are tied to the spirit world, and beastmasters seek them as striking companions."},kw={"darkshore","ghost saber","great sundering","highborne","mathystra","naga","ruins of mathystra","stormscale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:tower-of-althalaxx","topic:naga","topic:highborne","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ruins of Mathystra"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-althalaxx"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Althalaxx",z="darkshore",s="Dark sorcery stirs at the Tower of Althalaxx on northern Darkshore's coast. Athrikus Narassin once withdrew there, and now demonic cultists and warlocks shelter within its ancient Highborne walls.",h="Dark sorcery stirs at the Tower of Althalaxx on northern Darkshore's coast.",sec={{t="A Highborne Retreat",b="Queen Azshara settled favored Highborne servants in Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran ten thousand years ago. She placed the powerful sorcerer Athrikus Narassin in authority over them. As Athrikus turned from civic governance, he withdrew to the nearby Tower of Althalaxx. The Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, yet the tower endured on Darkshore's desolate coast, a quiet ruin of forgotten elven magic.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Strand",b="Warlocks and dark cultists stir the Tower of Althalaxx with malignant sorcery. Calling themselves the Cult of the Dark Strand, they have gathered there with allied satyrs under Athrikus Narassin's leadership. Their rites channel demonic magic and torment the lingering spirits of the ancient dead. Through these rites, they serve sinister designs tied directly to the demonic Shadow Council.",sp=1,bt={"q965.3"}}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="On northern Darkshore's coast, the Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven mage tower from Queen Azshara's reign. Dark sorcerers and cultists occupy it now.",al={"tower of althalaxx","althalaxx tower","what is althalaxx"},it="place"},{q="Who originally built and lived in the tower?",a="Queen Azshara placed Athrikus Narassin, a powerful Highborne sorcerer, in authority over Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. He withdrew to the tower as he grew distant from civic governance.",al={"who lived here","athrikus narassin","who built the tower"},it="history"},{q="Who are the cultists occupying the tower now?",a="Warlocks, cultists, and satyrs of the Cult of the Dark Strand occupy the tower. They practice dark rites among its ruins.",al={"who are the cultists","cult of the dark strand","althalaxx enemies"},it="residents"},{q="Why are there ghosts and tortured spirits here?",a="The cultists torment the long-dead elven spirits of ancient Darkshore with dark rituals and soul-binding magic. They use the spirits' agony in spells.",al={"why are there ghosts","tortured spirits althalaxx"}},{q="Is the Tower of Althalaxx dangerous?",a="The tower is extremely dangerous. It swarms with fanatical warlocks and cultists of the Cult of the Dark Strand, who serve demonic masters under the direction of the Shadow Council. In addition to these dark spellcasters and their satyr allies, the grounds are haunted by tortured spirits and wraiths bound by foul sorcery.",al={"is tower of althalaxx safe","tower of althalaxx danger","threats at tower of althalaxx"},it="danger",add="1aaea03f"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, the tower recalls Highborne corruption and demonic folly on ancestral lands. It calls for swift intervention from Darnassus.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can read the Cult of the Dark Strand's dark rites as proof of the Shadow Council's far-reaching influence and lingering presence in Kalimdor."},kw={"althalaxx","ameth'aran","athrikus narassin","bashal'aran","dark strand","darkshore","highborne","satyr","shadow council"},rel={"quest:965","zone:darkshore","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:954","topic:highborne","topic:shadow-council","topic:satyr","topic:alliance"},src={"Tower of Althalaxx"}}
E["subzone:twilight-shore-darkshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Shore (Darkshore)",z="darkshore",s="Murloc tribes and hungry sea creatures crowd Twilight Shore in southern Darkshore. Its rugged coast runs from the Long Wash to Ashenvale, where misty beaches meet cliffs, islets, and dangerous surf.",h="Murloc tribes and hungry sea creatures crowd Twilight Shore in southern Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Coastline",b="Twilight Shore runs south from the Long Wash, past the ruins of Ameth'Aran, toward Ashenvale. Gray beaches give way to sharp cliffs and rocky islands. Threshadons and sea crawlers prowl the waters, while aggressive murloc camps line the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Shore located?",a="Twilight Shore follows Darkshore's southern coast, beginning south of the Long Wash, roughly west of Ameth'Aran's ruins, and reaching the rocky border of Ashenvale.",al={"twilight shore location","where is twilight shore","twilight shore map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats can be found along the Twilight Shore?",a="Aggressive murloc tribes crowd the shore. In the cold surf, threshadons, lurkers, and giant crabs prey on unwary travelers.",al={"twilight shore mobs","dangers at twilight shore","what is at twilight shore"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the terrain so rugged here?",a="The Veiled Sea's relentless pounding has broken the coast into sharp cliffs, rocky shoals, and small offshore islands. Farther north, the beaches are flatter and more open.",al={"why are there cliffs","twilight shore geography"}},{q="What is the Twilight Shore?",a="The Twilight Shore is a rugged stretch of coastline along southern Darkshore, running from the edge of the Long Wash down toward the border of Ashenvale. Unlike the flatter sandy reaches farther north, this coast is jagged and unforgiving, marked by jutting sea cliffs, rocky islets, and misty gray beaches battered by cold ocean waters.",al={"twilight shore lore","what is twilight shore","about twilight shore"},it="place",add="4cda5a2c"},{q="Is the Twilight Shore dangerous?",a="Yes, it is among the most hazardous stretches of shoreline in the region. Swarms of aggressive murlocs claim the rocky banks and outcroppings, while the surf is prowled by starving threshadons eager to snap at swimmers. Traveling near the churning surf or clambering along its isolated bluffs leaves you vulnerable to ambush from both land and sea.",al={"is twilight shore safe","how dangerous is twilight shore","twilight shore dangers"},it="danger",add="2a509b88"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you reach the lonely, mist-shrouded border between Darkshore's haunted ruins and Ashenvale's ancestral forests."},kw={"ashenvale","coast","darkshore","long wash","murlocs","threshadons","twilight shore"},rel={"zone:darkshore","subzone:long-wash","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:murloc"},src={"Twilight Shore (Darkshore)"}}
E["subzone:twilight-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Twilight Vale",z="darkshore",s="In Twilight Vale, beasts and furbolgs prowl the dark woods between Darkshore and Ashenvale. The southern forest marks a perilous passage from Darkshore’s tainted coast to Ashenvale’s sacred canopies.",h="In Twilight Vale, beasts and furbolgs prowl the dark woods between Darkshore and Ashenvale.",sec={{t="A Perilous Threshold",b="Twilight Vale runs south from Ameth'Aran to the Ashenvale border, where dusk hangs over Darkshore’s southern woods. Corruption has spread deep among the wildlife. Rabid bears roam beside feral nightsabers, and hostile furbolg tribes stalk the trees.\n\nSentinels and travelers urge you to stay on the main road. A few paces into the woods can bring a swift, deadly ambush.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Twilight Vale located?",a="Twilight Vale lies in southern Darkshore, just south of the highborne ruins of Ameth'Aran, and reaches the pass into Ashenvale.",al={"twilight vale location","where is twilight vale","twilight vale map"},it="place"},{q="What threats wander this forest?",a="Rabid bears, aggressive nightsabers, and corrupted furbolgs roam the vale and attack those who enter their territory.",al={"twilight vale monsters","what is in twilight vale","danger twilight vale"},it="threat"},{q="Is it safe to travel through the vale?",a="The main dirt road is far safer than the underbrush. Stray from it, and feral beasts may cross your path.",al={"is twilight vale safe","safe path darkshore to ashenvale"},it="danger"},{q="Why is the wildlife in the vale corrupted?",a="Darkshore has suffered since the Third War, and sundering magic lingers across northern Kalimdor. Tainted water and dark magical residue have maddened wildlife and made peaceful furbolgs violent.",al={"why are bears rabid in darkshore","furbolg corruption twilight vale"},it="origin"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you mourn the corruption of the southern woods’ native beasts and the fall of furbolg neighbors near Ashenvale’s threshold.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid traveling between Darkshore and Ashenvale, you see the sickness afflicting the vale’s creatures and the urgent need to cleanse the land."},kw={"ameth'aran","ashenvale","darkshore","furbolgs","nightsabers","rabid bears","twilight vale"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:ashenvale","subzone:ameth-aran","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:alliance"},src={"Twilight Vale"}}
E["subzone:wildbend-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wildbend River",z="darkshore",s="Near the Grove of the Ancients, Wildbend River carries demonic poison toward the sea. Its waters cross southern Darkshore from the corrupted heights of Felwood and threaten the wilderness.",h="Near the Grove of the Ancients, Wildbend River carries demonic poison toward the sea.",sec={{t="A Toxic Mountain Stream",b="Wildbend River carries corruption through southern Darkshore. It runs west past the Grove of the Ancients and empties into the sea. The stream begins as Felwood's Bloodvenom River, then tumbles through rocky ridges with foul runoff. Night elves watch its banks for twisted wildlife and spreading demonic blight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Wildbend River corrupted?",a="Wildbend River begins high in Felwood's mountains, where it is called the Bloodvenom River. Demonic magic saturated Felwood during the Third War, and foul runoff spills down the cliffs into Darkshore.",al={"why is water tainted","wildbend river poison","darkshore dirty water"},it="ruin"},{q="Where does the river flow?",a="Wildbend River descends from the eastern ridges between Felwood and Darkshore. It winds through southern Darkshore near the Grove of the Ancients, then empties into the Veiled Sea.",al={"where is wildbend river","wildbend path","wildbend river location"},it="place"},{q="Does the river affect the Grove of the Ancients?",a="Wildbend River passes close to the Grove of the Ancients and threatens the ancient protectors rooted there. Night elves work tirelessly to contain the blight and keep poisoned water from rotting the sacred groves.",al={"grove of the ancients water","is grove of ancients corrupted"}},{q="What is the Wildbend River?",a="The Wildbend River is a corrupted waterway winding through southern Darkshore, near the Grove of the Ancients. It originates high in the corrupted highlands of Felwood, tumbling down the mountains as a continuation of the Bloodvenom River before carving its way toward the sea.",al={"what is wildbend river","wildbend river","about wildbend river"},it="place",add="842d63ec"},{q="Is the Wildbend River dangerous?",a="Yes, its waters are deeply foul and treacherous. Because the river is the downstream continuation of Felwood's Bloodvenom River, demonic corruption cascades straight from the tainted highlands into Darkshore, polluting the surrounding landscape and threatening the sacred groves nearby.",al={"wildbend river dangerous","dangers of wildbend river","is wildbend safe"},it="danger",add="96fc4b9b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf warden, you often watch the riverbanks as polluted water from Felwood threatens Darkshore's ancient roots.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you study the ecological aftermath of the Third War and watch how deeply Felwood's corruption reaches plants and animals downstream."},kw={"bloodvenom river","darkshore","felwood","grove of the ancients","tainted water","wildbend river"},rel={"zone:darkshore","zone:felwood","subzone:bloodvenom-river","quest:952"},src={"Wildbend River"}}
E["zone:darkshore"] = {t="zone",n="Darkshore",z="darkshore",s="Auberdine links Darkshore to night elf lands and the wider Alliance. Travelers reach this cold, misty coast in northwestern Kalimdor from Teldrassil or the Eastern Kingdoms. Ancient ruins and troubled wildlife mark the land, while cultists, naga, and a creeping rot threaten it.",h="Auberdine links Darkshore to night elf lands and the wider Alliance.",sec={{t="A Land of Mist and Memory",b="Darkshore lies beneath the western shadows of Mount Hyjal and Felwood. Pine groves give way to fog and cold, rocky shores. Millennia ago, the Kaldorei cities of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran flourished here. The Great Sundering shattered them, leaving pillars and arches half-drowned or tangled in roots. Highborne spirits haunt the ruins, while scavenging murlocs and invading naga roam among them.",sp=0},{t="The Haven of Auberdine",b="After the Third War and the planting of Teldrassil, the night elves made Auberdine a busy haven on this wild coast. Ships arrive from Rut'theran Village, Stormwind Harbor, and Menethil Harbor in the distant Wetlands by way of Southshore. Auberdine links night elf lands to the rest of the Alliance. Sentinels patrol the trade road south to Ashenvale, but their small garrison cannot watch the deep wilds beyond it.",sp=0},{t="Poisoned Waters and Whispering Depths",b="A slow, malignant rot has reached Darkshore beneath the eastern mountains. Corrupted runoff from Felwood flows to sources such as Cliffspring Falls, poisoning the water and driving bears, stags, and the furbolgs of Blackwood Den into violent madness.\n\nThe Dark Strand cultists perform foul rites at the Tower of Althalaxx. Twilight's Hammer gathers around the ancient and terrifying monument called the Master's Glaive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darkshore?",a="Alliance travelers can sail to Auberdine from Rut'theran Village at the base of Teldrassil, Stormwind Harbor, or Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands by way of Southshore. Horde travelers heading north must cross Ashenvale on foot, taking the main road northeast from Zoram'gar Outpost over the border.",al={"getting to darkshore","how to reach auberdine","darkshore boat"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is wrong with the local wildlife and furbolgs?",a="Water flowing from Felwood's tainted heights, including the Cliffspring River, carries demonic pollution into Darkshore's water table. The foul water has driven native furbolg tribes feral and left local deer and predators diseased and aggressive.",al={"why are animals sick","furbolg corruption","darkshore taint"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran?",a="Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran were prosperous Kaldorei twin cities, destroyed ten thousand years ago in the Great Sundering. Their ruler, Athrikus Narassin, claimed he would save his people from the cataclysm, but bound their souls into gems to use as eternal power sources for himself. Weeping ghosts fill the ruins.",al={"ameth'aran history","bashal'aran lore","ruins in darkshore"},sp=1,it="ruin",bt={"q965.3"}},{q="What is the Master's Glaive?",a="In southern Darkshore, the Master's Glaive is a huge petrified skull pierced by an enormous stone weapon. This ancient relic is linked to the primordial Old Gods and their servants. Dangerous Twilight's Hammer cultists are drawn to it.",al={"what is the masters glaive","giant skull darkshore","masters glaive monster"},it="place"},{q="Who is the giant tree in the Grove of the Ancients?",a="The giant tree in the Grove of the Ancients is Onu, a wise and venerable Ancient of Lore. In his quiet grove south of Auberdine, he considers Twilight's Hammer's troubling advance and helps travelers investigate disturbances in the forest.",al={"ancient of lore darkshore","who is onu","tree person darkshore"},it="identity"},{q="Who lives in the Tower of Althalaxx?",a="The Dark Strand, a vicious cult that practices dark sorcery and summons demons, occupies the Tower of Althalaxx. Its members ambush unwary travelers along the northern coastal woods.",al={"tower of althalaxx","darkshore tower cultists","althalaxx cult"},it="residents"},{q="What is Darkshore?",a="Darkshore is a long, foggy strip of rocky coast running along northwestern Kalimdor. Sheltered beneath mountains to the east and the Veiled Sea to the west, it features shadowed woods, rainswept beaches, and crumbling elven ruins. It serves as the night elves' primary gateway between their island home of Teldrassil and the mainland.",al={"tell me about darkshore","what kind of zone is darkshore","darkshore overview"},it="place",add="7cfc9767",nx={8,9}},{q="Why does it look so ruined and gloomy?",a="Much of Darkshore was shattered ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, reducing grand Kaldorei cities to rubble. Today, an ever-present sea mist, stormy winds, and creeping magical pollution trickling down from tainted mountain rivers give the coast its persistent, mournful atmosphere.",al={"why is darkshore gloomy","why is darkshore ruined","darkshore destroyed"},it="ruin",add="0d623756"},{q="Who lives here now?",a="Night elves maintain the settlement of Auberdine alongside visiting Alliance traders, including dwarves and humans. Outside the town, the wilderness is occupied by hostile naga, troggs, corrupted furbolgs, and remnants of the dark cults that lurk among the ancient stones.",al={"who inhabits darkshore","darkshore population","who lives in darkshore"},it="residents",add="d345bcc9"},{q="What is Auberdine?",a="Auberdine is a quiet coastal settlement and the primary Alliance port in northern Kalimdor. Featuring low wooden elven halls, earthen paths, and a prominent harbor lighthouse, it connects Darnassus across the water to the mainland and the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"auberdine town","tell me about auberdine","what is the town in darkshore"},it="place",add="137b9ce8",nx={11,12}},{q="Who runs Auberdine?",a="Auberdine's civic affairs are led by the elder Thundris Windweaver, supported by the Auberdine Village Council. The town's military guard is handled by the Sentinels, with officers like Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea coordinating local patrols and defense.",al={"auberdine leader","who is in charge of auberdine","auberdine village council"},it="leader",add="f41ff152"},{q="Why is it built on the coast?",a="After night elves returned following the Third War, they chose this spot to revive maritime travel and supply lines. The port provides a vital ferry link to Rut'theran Village at Teldrassil and hosts long-distance trading vessels sailing from Menethil Harbor in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"why build auberdine on the beach","auberdine port purpose","why coast auberdine"},it="purpose",add="5f65caea"},{q="Who's in charge here?",a="The night elves claim Darkshore as part of their burgeoning kingdom. Elder Thundris Windweaver oversees civil matters from Auberdine, while the night elf Sentinels maintain military command along the coastal road and regional borders.",al={"who rules darkshore","who controls darkshore","darkshore leadership"},it="in_charge",add="451a86e7",nx={14,15}},{q="Who are the Sentinels?",a="The Sentinels are the traditional standing army of the Kaldorei, composed primarily of elite night elf warrior women. They patrol the roadways, guard settlements like Auberdine, and defend elven territory from encroaching monsters and invaders.",al={"sentinel army","night elf sentinels","what are the sentinels"},it="people",add="f5d3cc9f"},{q="Do they answer to Darnassus?",a="Yes. Darkshore's defenders owe allegiance to the Kaldorei leadership residing in Darnassus atop Teldrassil, even though the capital's high authorities sometimes view the rugged frontier town of Auberdine as a remote outpost of outcasts and misfits.",al={"do sentinels serve darnassus","darnassus authority darkshore","does auberdine answer to darnassus"},it="ties",add="435217d7"},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks on the beach?",a="Darkshore is notorious for brutal weather, heavy rain, dense sea mist, and jagged shallows. Wicked winds stir sudden waves that drive vessels onto the rocks, leaving shallow waters littered with hulls that failed to navigate the passage to Auberdine.",al={"darkshore shipwrecks","why are ships wrecked here","sunken boats darkshore"},it="history",add="709b4618"},{q="Why are the Highborne haunting these ruins?",a="Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne were the sorcerous nobility of Queen Azshara who ruled twin cities like Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. When the Great Sundering shattered their empire, their ruler trapped their souls in binding gems, leaving their tormented spirits to haunt the stone pillars for eternity.",al={"why are highborne ghosts here","ameth'aran ghosts","who were the highborne"},it="history",add="9d4c460f"},{q="What corrupted the Blackwood tribe?",a="Though once friendly neighbors to the night elves, the Blackwood furbolgs have been driven into an insatiable madness by dark corruption. Rivers running down from the tainted heights of Felwood carry poisoned water across Darkshore, twisting the minds of beasts and furbolgs alike.",al={"blackwood furbolgs crazy","why are furbolgs mad darkshore","furbolg taint source"},it="threat",add="c8232ccb"},{q="Who are the Twilight's Hammer and why are they camped here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer is a nihilistic apocalyptic cult dedicated to the dark entities known as the Old Gods. They have gathered at the Master's Glaive in southern Darkshore, conducting rituals and excavations around ancient subterranean remains buried beneath the earth.",al={"twilight hammer darkshore","cultists darkshore","why are twilight cultists here"},it="threat",add="a33e07d8"},{q="Why is Darkshore dangerous?",a="Beyond Auberdine's immediate borders, the coast is fraught with perils. Feral beasts and enraged furbolgs stalk the trees, naga and murlocs infest the beaches, and shadowy cults like the Dark Strand and Twilight's Hammer ambush travelers from hidden outposts.",al={"is darkshore safe","darkshore threats","dangers of darkshore"},it="danger",add="b665bd5a"},{q="Why is it called Darkshore?",a="The coast earned its name from the thick, shadowed woods and the somber, unusual mist that blankets the entire shoreline, obscuring daylight and casting the beaches in perpetual gloom.",al={"why darkshore named","name origin darkshore","why is it called darkshore"},it="name",add="9cbaedb5"},{q="How did I end up in Darkshore?",a="You likely arrived through Auberdine, the bustling coastal port and trade hub that connects northern Kalimdor to the wider world. If you journeyed from the boughs of Teldrassil, a ferry carried you across the mist-shrouded waters from Rut'theran Village to the mainland docks. Travelers venturing from the Eastern Kingdoms often take the long voyage aboard the great sailing ships from Menethil Harbor. Alternatively, hardy wanderers trekking overland from the deep forests of Ashenvale follow the patrolled Sentinel road northward onto the rocky, mist-blanketed shore.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to darkshore","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add="c5ede25e"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Darkshore?",a="The night elves in Auberdine desperately need help containing a spreading malaise across the coast. A foul corruption trickling from the Felwood heights has poisoned the rivers and water table, driving the local wildlife and peaceful Blackwood furbolgs into violent madness. Beyond the woods, ancient Highborne ruins like Ameth'Aran are stirring with restless ghosts, naga and murlocs encroach upon the rocky beaches, and sinister Twilight's Hammer cultists gather around the ancient monument of the Master's Glaive. The Auberdine Village Council and the Sentinels rely on travelers like you to restore balance.",al={"why am i here","what should i do in darkshore","what is my purpose here"},it="purpose",add="c840edc2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid answering calls from Moonglade, you reach Darkshore's front line. You diagnose tainted waterways and brew cleansers for sick forest creatures.",["race:NightElf"]="As a young night elf leaving Teldrassil, you take your first step onto mainland Kalimdor. Ancient ruins and spreading corruption scar the wild.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Auberdine is the primary trade nexus in northern Kalimdor. It keeps a direct sea link between Stormwind and Ironforge, and Darnassus, the night elf capital.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Darkshore is a remote Alliance stronghold under heavy patrol, just north of Horde camps in Ashenvale. Hostile sentinels and dangerous cults prowl its treacherous coast."},kw={"ameth'aran","auberdine","bashal'aran","blackwood den","cliffspring falls","darkshore","master's glaive","onu","tower of althalaxx"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","subzone:ameth-aran","subzone:master-s-glaive","quest:952","quest:965","quest:6122","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:ashenvale"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Darkshore (Classic)","Darkshore"}}
